<<及物動詞>>
1 
a. 忍受,容忍
I cannot ~ him. 
我對他忍無可忍
b. 忍受<做…>
He cannot ~ to stay [staying] in one position for long. 
他無法忍受長久1．be faithful to；obey； keep to；adhere to嚴守；遵守；堅持
*If you join the club，you must abide by its rules．你參加這個俱樂部就得遵守其規章。
*I expect him to abide by his decision to help us．我希望他能堅持他幫助我們的決定。
*Both sides should strictly abide by the contract．雙方應恪守本合同。
*Californians and New Englanders abide by the same federal laws．加利福尼亞人和新英格蘭人遵守同樣的聯邦法律。
2．fulfil履行
*Having made our decision， we must abide by it．我們既已作出決定，就應該照著辦。
*She will abide by her promise．她會履行諾言的。
3．suffer the consequences of承擔…的後果
*You two will have to abide by the inevitable．你們兩個人不得不承受那無可倖免的事。
*He said he'd abide by all possible consequences．他說他將承擔一切可能的後果。
*You must abide by the results of your mistakes．你必須承擔由你的錯誤所造成的後果。a.bid.ing
