<<不及物動詞>>
1 將數目加起來,作加法演算
2 增加[…][to]
The fine day ~ed to our pleasure. 
晴朗的天氣增添了我們的樂趣
add up
(1) → v.t. 2a
(2) 合計; 符合預期的數目
(3)(口語)合理,有道理
This doesn't ~ up. 
這不合情理
add up to?
(1) (加起來) 總計為…
The figures ~ up to 594. 
這些數字總計為五百九十四
(2)(口語)總而言之就是…,其含義是…,等於…
His statements all ~ up to an admission of guilt. 
他的陳述等於認罪
to add to ?
除…之外 (加上)add as an extra or extras追加
*Would you please add these names on to your list？請把這幾個名字補加到你的名單裡好嗎？
*Add the other items on at the bottom of the page．把別的項目加在這頁的下端。make greater；increase增加
*We can add another room to the house．這所房子我們還可以加蓋一個房間。
*Two added to five makes seven．2加5等於7。
*This adds to their difficulties．這增加了他們的困難。
*I don't want to add to your troubles．我不想給你增加麻煩。1．put together加起來
*Add these figures up and see what the total is．把這些數字加起來，看看總數是多少。
*The numbers wouldn't add up．這些數字加起來與總數不符。
2．assess； help估計；權衡；有所幫助
*They added up all the advantages and disadvantages and tried to come to a decision．他們權衡了所有的利弊得失，試圖做出決定。
*Doing morning exercise every day will add up．天天做早操有益於健康。
3．make sense；present a reasonable picture有意義；合情合理His excuse just doesn't add up．他的借口簡直沒有道理。
*Nothing he does seems to add up．他的所作所為似乎沒有意義。
*His story didn't add up．他的故事不合情理。1．amount to；make a total of合計，總共
*The money he spent added up to more than ＄ 1，000．他花的錢合計超過了1000美元。
*The bills add up to exactly ￡1，000．這些賬單加起來正好1000英鎊。
*Eight and ten add up to eighteen．8加10等於18。
2．mean；signify意味著；意思是
*The evidence all adds up to a case of murder．全部證據都表明這是一件謀殺案。
*The rain，the mosquitoes and the crowded cabin all added up to a spoiled vacation．下雨、蚊子和擁擠的小屋，意味著這假期過得糟透了。
*His long answer just adds up to a refusal．他的冗長的回答實際上意味著拒絕。add.
