2 a. 同意<做…>, <對於做…> 意見一致
We ~d to start at once. 
我們同意立即出發
b. <對於…一事> 意見一致,一致認為…,同意
We ~d [It was ~d] that we should travel first-class. 
我們一致同意乘頭等 (車、船) 旅行
c. <對於…一事> 意見一致,同意,一致認為…[with]
I ~d with him that some active measure should be adopted. 
我與他一致認為應該採取某種積極措施
agree to differ [disagree] 
互相容忍歧見1．have the same opinion about就…取得相同的意見
*Musicians rarely agree on the way a piece of music should be played．對於一支曲子應該怎樣演奏，音樂家們很少有相同的意見。
*The two sides agreed on a cease fire．雙方達成了停火協議。
2．decide on決定
*We agreed on leaving there the next day．我們一致同意第 2天離開那裡。
*We've agreed on fighting the evil in society．我們決定同社會上的邪惡作鬥爭。approve；say 「yes」to；consent同意；贊同；接受（想法、計劃、建議等）
*Do you agree to my plan？你贊同我的計劃嗎？
*The committee has agreed to his arrangement．委員會已同意了他的安排。1．have the same opinion as；approve of同意
*I can't agree with you on this matter．在這個問題上我不同意你的意見。
*I don't agree with a single word that you have said．你剛才說的話，我一點也不贊成。
2．suit；be good for適合；適宜
*The climate there does not agree with her．那裡的氣候對她不適宜。
*Rich food doesn't agree with her．油膩的食品不合她的胃口。
3．coincide with；be the same as 相一致；相等
*The bill does not agree with your estimate．賬單與你原來的估計不符。
*His explanation agrees with the facts．他的解釋同事實是相符的。
4．approve of贊成
*I don't agree with people drinking brandy all day long．我不贊成人們成天喝白蘭地。a.gree.a.ble
