穿著一身白衣1．by oneself；independently自己；獨立地
*He has completed the task all alow．他獨立完成了這項任務。
2．being the only one；without others獨自地；孤零零地
*The small cabin stands on the hillside all alone．那房子孤零零地座落在山坡上。
*She sat in her room reading all alone．她獨自坐在房裡看書。1． for the whole length of一路；沿途
*We saw green hills and forests all along the way．沿途所見，皆是青青的小山和森林。
2．all the time；from the beginning一直；自始至終
*The manager said he suspected the man of stealing the paper all along．經理說他一直都懷疑是那個人偷了文件。
*You've been nice to me all along，and I appreciate it very much．您一貫對我好，我非常感激。pass gently into sleep入睡；睡熟
*They both stretched their weary limbs，and fell fast asleep．他們倆伸開疲倦的腿睡著了。1． all of a sudden；suddenly；unexpectedly突然；出乎預料
*All at once they found themselves surrounded by the enemy．他們突然發現自己被敵人包圍了。
*All at once she decided she wasn't going．She didn't explain why．她突然決定不去了，她沒有講明理由。
*All at once we heard a shot and the soldier fell to the ground．突然我們聽到槍聲，接著士兵就倒下去了。
2．at the same time；together同時；一起
*When he heard the news， he was happy and sad all at once and didn't know what to do．聽到這消息，他悲喜交集，不知所措。
*She couldn't tell them more about the accident．Everything just seemed to have happened all at once．她不可能向他們講述更多的事情，一切都似乎是同時發生的。
3．without delay馬上；即刻
*We just can't decide such an important thing all at once．我們只是不能馬上決定這樣一件重要的事情。1．all except除…外；都
*All but three of the girls have passed the examination．除了 3個女生，其餘的學生都通過了考試。
*The shipwrecked people were rescued all but one．船隻失事，遇難者除一人以外全部得救。
2．almost；very nearly幾乎
*He was all but bankrupt and couldn't help us．他幾乎破產了，不能幫助我們。
*The girl was all but run over by the car．那女孩差點被那輛小汽車壓過去。all clear
