c.『法律』答辯 (書) 
in answer (to) ?
應…而,回答…而,為答覆…而
in ~ to your query
為答覆你的質疑
know all the answers
(口語)無事不知,機警而博識
He thinks he knows all the ~s. 
他認為他什麼都懂reply rudely回嘴；頂嘴
*Don't answer back like that．別那樣頂嘴！
*The child often answered his grandmother back．這孩子經常與祖母頂嘴。1． be responsible for；take the responsibility for對…負責
*You must answer for any missing articles after the party．你必須對聚會後遺失的任何物品負責。
*Parents should answer for their children's behaviour．父母應對自己孩子的行為負責。
2．guarantee 保證；擔保
*I can answer for his honesty．我可以保證他是誠實的。
*I will answer for the truth of his statements．我擔保他說的話是真實的。
3．be punished or blamed for因…而受罰；因…而受責備
*He will have to answer for his crimes．他必須因他的罪行而受到懲罰。
*Someday you will answer for your foolish behaviour．總有一天你將因你的愚蠢行為而受到懲罰。
4．serve for起…作用
*That night the table answered for a bed for me．那天晚上那張桌子成了我的床。
5．speak for代表…講話
*Stop answering for John，let him speak．不要替約翰說，讓他自己講。
*I can't answer for the other members of the committee．我不能代表其他委員的意見。1．correspond to；be in accordance with符合；相符；一致
*We all hope that the result will answer to our expectation．我們都希望結果和我們預料的一樣。
*That answers precisely to our needs．那正符合我們的需要。
*A man answering to the police description was arrested in London last night．那個與警察描述的特徵相符的人，昨晚已在倫敦被捕。
2．be responsible to對…負責
*You'll have to answer to me if any harm comes to these children．要是這些孩子受到什麼傷害，我將唯你是問。
*He said he was ready to answer to those who worked under his direction．他說他願意對在他領導下工作的人負責。
3．respond to；reply to對…做出反應；聽從
*The illness doesn't answer to medical treatment．這病治療無效。
*Young people should answer to the nation's call to go where they are most needed．青年人應該聽從國家號召，到最需要的地方去。1．respond to對…做出反應；響應
*We answered up to the appeal quickly．我們迅速響應了這個呼籲。
*At the roll call，the men answered up to their names．點名時，士兵們應答迅速。
2．have a ready reply to對…對答如流
*The little boy answered up to all the questions except two．除了兩個問題外，這個孩子對答如流。an.swer.a.ble
