<<不及物動詞>>
1 辯論,談論; 爭論
~ in a circle 
依循環論證法辯論
Don't ~!. 
別爭論!
I ~d on her behalf. 
我替她辯論
2 
a. 討論 [有關…之事] ; 議論,爭論[with][about, over]
He ~d with his friend about the best method. 
他與朋友討論最好的方法
Your father knows best. Don't ~ with him. 
你爸知道得最清楚,不要跟他辯
b. [為贊成…而] 辯論,辯護 [for,in favor of] ; [為反對…而] 辯論,辯駁[against]
He ~d for [against] the passage of the bill. 
他贊成[反對]通過這議案
I ~d for justice. 
我為正義辯論discuss；quarrel about爭論；爭辯
*They are always arguing about unimportant matters．他們總是為一些小事爭論不休。
*My students argued over the ocrrectness of the answer．我的學生們互相爭論著答案的正確性。express an opinion against反駁
*The next speaker will argue against this plan．下一個演講者將會反駁這項計劃。1．argue continuously連續爭論
*They sometimes argue away for hours．他們有時一爭論就是幾小時。
2．dismiss with a plausible argument以似是而非的理由駁回；不考慮
*He tried to argue the matter away．他想方設法要把這件事辯解過去。
*You can't argue away this problem．你不能不考慮這個問題。defeat sb．in an argument駁倒
*The speaker was wellinformed，but I argued him down at last．演講者博聞強記，但是我最終把他駁倒了。
*They argued him down fiercely．他們經過激烈的辯論把他說得啞口無言。debate in favour of；give reasons in support of為…爭辯；支持；贊成
*I'll try to argue the matter for you， but he's very obstinate．在這個問題上我會為你說話的，但他卻是個固執的人。
*It is necessary that we should argue the problem for them．我們有必要為他們辯論這件事。talk about sth． thoroughly until a decision is reached深入地辯論某事，直到辯出結果
*The committee argued the matter out，and at last agreed to take no action．委員會深入地研究了此事，最後決定不採取行動。
*They intend to argue the whole problem out tomorrow night．他們打算在明天晚上把整個問題辯出個結果來。persuade sb． agamst doing sth． by showing reasons說服某人不要做某事
*The parents argued their son out of leaving his present job．父母說服兒子不要放棄目前的工作。
*He was argued out of his opposition．他被說服得不再反對了。ar.gu.ment
