*She is quite at ease in speaking English．她英文說得十分流暢。

at ease
『軍』
1 稍息之姿勢
2 (指口令) 稍息in the wrong； mistaken出錯
*If my memory is not at fault， you are Mr．Smith．要是我沒記錯的話，你就是史密斯先生。
*Who is at fault in the car crash？這次撞車是誰的過錯？at the beginning；originally起初
*At first，she was ill at ease，but in a few minutes she felt relaxed．起初她有點不自在，可是幾分鐘後她就感覺輕鬆了。taking a quick look at一瞥
*He saw at first glance that she was filled with anger．他一眼就看出她在生氣。directly 直接地
*He got the information at first hand from the ambassador．他是直接從大使那裡得到這消息的。
*He has been to China to study conditions there at first hand．他曾多到中國直接研究那裡的情況。after a first quick look； when first seen乍一看
*At first sight， the problem seemed insoluble．乍看起來，這問題似乎無法解決。
*He fell in love with her at first sight．他對她一見鍾情。1．coming soon； almost here即將到來；為期不遠
*The Midautumn Festival is at hand．中秋節快要到了。
*He wished more than ever to have his father at hand．他比任何時候都希望父親就在他跟前。
2．easy to reach； nearby近在手邊；在近處
*It is very convenient to have a dictionary at hand when reading． 閱讀時手頭有一本詞典是很方便的。
*He lives close at hand．他住得很近。1．in reality；basically實際上；基本上
*He seems polite， but he's dishonest at heart．他似乎很有禮貌，但實際上是個不誠實的人。
*His manners are cold， but he is at heart a kind man．他的言談舉止有些冷淡，但實際上他心地善良。
2．deep down在內心
*She has your interests at heart．她常把你的利益放在心上。
*She did not at heart want to do it．她心裡並不想做那件事。
*I am sick at heart．我心中苦悶。1．in the house；in the place where one lives or comes from在家；在家鄉；在國內
*There's no one at home．家裡沒人。
*He was very famous at home and abroad．他在國內外都很有名。
*Americans abroad are protected by the government like Americans at home．海外的美國人如同在國內一樣，受到政府的保護。
2．comfortable； at ease安逸；自在
*She feels at home．她覺得很自如，像在家裡一樣。
*Please make yourself at home．請隨便一些。
3．familiar； skillful熟悉；精通
*Would you be at home driving a truck？你開卡車內行嗎？
*Tom has read many books about physics and is at home in that subject．湯姆讀過很多關於物理學的書，因此他精通這門學科。1．now and then不時地
*The music came from the building at intervals．音樂聲從樓裡不時傳來。
2．happening regularly after equal periods of time or appearing at equal distance（時間、距離）間隔
*The trees are planted at intervals of six feet．每隔6英尺栽一棵樹。
*Leaders should come to hear the masses'views at intervals．領導們應常常來聽聽群眾的意見。1．under consideration； in dispute 在爭論中
*The point at issue is who is best qualified for the post．爭論之焦點是誰擔任這項工作最稱職。
2．in disagreement不和；意見不一致
*The father is at issue with his son．父子意見不和。1．free； not confined； at liberty自由地；未被捕；逍遙法外
*The criminal is still at large．那個罪犯依然逍遙法外。
*It is disturbing to think that a dangerous wild animal is still at large in the quiet countryside．在寧靜的鄉村裡有一隻危險的野獸依然肆意逍遙，想起來未免令人忐忑不安。
2．as a whole；altogether普遍的；一般的；整體的
*The country at large is hoping for political and economic reforms．全國人民普遍希望進行政治和經濟改革。
*He was elected congressman at large．他被全體選民選為議員。
*All peoples at large are for peace．各國民眾全都贊成和平。
3．fully； completely詳盡地
*Please explain the passage at large．請詳細地講解這篇短文。
*There is no time to discuss the subject at large at this meeting．這次會上，我們沒有時間充分討論這個問題。finally； in the end最後；最終
*At last they climbed over the mountain．他們終於翻過了這座大山。anyhow； at the lowest estimate至少；起碼
*The dictionary costs at least yuan．這本詞典至少要花50元。
*I had not seen him for at least a week．我至少有一周沒看見他了。1．finally； at last最後；終於
*He succeeded at length．他終於成功了。
*At length there was a step forward in the negotiations．談判終於有了進展。
*He came at length．他終於來了。
2．in great detail詳盡地
*The two foreign ministers discussed the situation in this area at great length．兩位外長詳細討論了這一地區的局勢。
*The teacher explained the text at length，教師詳細地解釋了課文。1．at leisure；unoccupied 閒著；無事
*I'll be at liberty after midday．我午後有空。
2．free； unconfined不受約束；有行動或處理某事的自由
*You are at liberty to use the laboratory．你可以自由地使用這個實驗室。
*The prisoners were set at liberty．犯人被釋放了。1．very soon； immediately立刻
*The telegram must be sent at once．電報必須立即發出。
*I recognized him at once．我立刻就認出了他。
2．both； equally同樣；兼
*He is at once a statesman and a writer．他既是一位政治家，也是一位作家。
*He was at once happy and sad．他悲喜交集。
*The book is at once interesting and instructive．這本書既有趣又有教育意義。at one
1 和諧的
2 同意的; 一致的once曾經；在某一時間（常指過去）
*This kind of wine was very popular at one time， but now it is considered too strong．這種酒曾經很受歡迎，但是現在被認為度數太高了。
*At one time we met frequently．曾經有一個時期我們經常會面。in one's best state在最佳狀態；在全盛時期
*He is at his best with friends．他同朋友們在一起時最開心。
*The peach blossoms are at their best now．桃花正在盛開。
*She is at her best in the morning．她早上情緒最佳。close by； very near at hand在手邊；在手旁
*Having our own kitchen has one advantage；everything is at our elbow．有一間我們自己的廚房就有好處，每樣東西都近在手邊。
*He always keeps an encyclopedia at his elbow for reference．他手邊總是放著一本百科全書，以備參考。at one's own risk自行冒險
*Touch that at your peril． The parcel contains high explosives．你碰它就要自負後果。包裹裡裝有烈性炸藥。
*He made the experiment at his peril．他冒險做這個試驗。not knowing what to do next；quite at a loss不知所措；智窮技盡
*The soldier was at his wit's end when facing the danger．面對危險，那個士兵不知如何是好。
*He had approached every friend and acquaintance for help in vain and he was at his wit's end．他曾向每位朋友和熟人求助，但毫無結果，那時他真是一籌莫展。in harmony； in a state of friendship or quiet處於和平（和睦）狀態；處於平靜狀態
*If only the world were at peace．全世界都和睦相處就好了。
*We are fortunately at peace with all the world today．我們今天有幸能和世界各國和平共處。
*After taking the medicine， she felt at peace with herself．吃過藥之後，她感到平靜多了。now； during this period of time現在
*At present he is a professor of physics．他現在是物理學教授。
*I can't think of any fit person just at present．我現在一下想不出什麼適合的人。
*We don't need any more at present．現在我們不再需要什麼了。aimlessly； without any plan胡亂地；漫無目的地
*He asked questions at random．他胡亂問些問題。
*He took a book at random off the shelf．他隨意從書架上拿下一本書。1．not moving靜止
*The sea is at rest．大海很平靜。
2．quiet安靜
*The girl is never really at rest．那個女孩總是手腳不停。
3．settled解決
*The question is now at rest．問題現已解決。available to use freely可以自由支配（使用）
*After twenty hours of classes each week， the students have a lot of free time at their disposal．每週上20節課之後，學生們有大量自由支配的時間。
*Jack put his car at her disposal．傑克的車她可隨便使用。
*The money is at the disposal of the committee．這筆錢由委員會自由支配。1．ready to obey sb．聽從某人的命令
*The dog went for the man at its master's command．主子一聲令下，狗就向那人撲去。
2．at sb．'s service受某人支配
*She has a large vocabulary at her command．她掌握大量的詞彙。at the time that doesn't give sb．trouble在某人方便的時候
*Please come at your convenience．請在你方便的時候來。near；following closely緊跟在…後面
*He kept at my heels．他緊緊跟著我。
*Famine often follows at the heels of war．戰爭之後常常跟著饑荒。subject to sb．'s power or control 受某人支配或控制
*He is now at your mercy．他現在由你控制。
*The ship was at the mercy of wind and waves in the storm．在風暴中，那條船任憑風浪吹打。ready for sb．'s use or command聽任某人使用；聽任某人差遣
*I am at your service at any time．我隨時為你效勞。
*My bike is at your service．我的自行車你隨便用好了。1．on the open sea在海上
*The ship spent 40 days at sea． 這條船在海上航行了40天。
2．lost in mind； not understanding；puzzled；not knowing what to do茫然；迷惑；不知所措
*You are still all at sea． He is an outandout scoundrel．你還蒙在鼓裡，他是一個十足的流氓。
*The job was new to him， and for a few days he was all at sea． 他剛開始幹這活，有好幾天他都糊里糊塗的。
*He is quite at sea as to what measures should be taken to settle the problem．他全然不知該採取什麼措施來解決這個問題。
*She was quite at sea in regard to that matter．說到那件事，她實在茫然。at risk； in danger； in a position to be lost or gained勝敗未定；處於成敗（存亡、輸贏）關頭；在危險中
*The life of the wounded pilot is at stake，受傷的飛行員生死未卜。
*He put all his money at stake in this business．他孤注一擲，把錢全部投在這項經營上。
*My honor is at stake， so I cannot let the matter rest．這危及我的名譽，所以我不能不管。
*The team played hard because the championship was at stake．這支球隊打得非常賣力，因為冠軍賽已進入決定性的階段。having a meal在吃飯
*They were at table when I called．我拜訪時，他們正在吃飯。at the starting point of在…開頭
*They sang a song at the beginning of the meeting．會議開始時他們唱了一首歌。at the end of在…結束時
*She went home at the conclusion of the ceremony．典禮一結束她就回家了。at the expense of以…為代價；以…為犧牲
*He succeeded only at the cost of his health．他成功了，但身體卻垮了。
*He saved the lives of his friends at the cost of his own．他犧牲自己而挽救了朋友的生命。1．with the loss of； at the sacrifice of失去；犧牲
*He devoted his time to football at the expense of his studies．他全然不顧學習，把全部時間都用於踢球。
*He became a brilliant scholar，but only at the expense of his health．他成了一個卓越的學者，卻犧牲了自己的健康。
*Don't try to benefit at the expense of others．不要干損人利已的事。
2．at the cost of花費；支付
*We were all entertained at the director's expense．我們全由導演請客。
*They built the railroad at the expense of two hundred million dollars．他們花了2億美元修築這條鐵路。
*He has been at the expense of her education．他一直支付她的教育經費。at the bottom of在…底部（腳下）
*A temple stands at the foot of the mountain．山腳下有一座寺廟。
*See explanatory notes at the foot of this page．參看本頁下端的註解。1．at the present time； now此刻；目前（用於現在時態中）
*I know the address well enough，but I can't think of it at the moment．我清楚地記得這個地址，可是這會兒怎麼也想不起來了。
2．then那時；那一刻（用於過去時態中）
*I was busy at the moment．我那時很忙。
*I was willing to lend him the book，but I hadn't it with me at the moment．我是願意借給他那本書的，可是當時書不在我手邊。1．at the speed of以…的速度
*The car was running at the rate of 100 kmph． 汽車以100公里的時速行駛。
2．at a charge or payment fixed according to a standard scale以…的比率；以…的價格
*I bought the oranges at the rate of seven jiao a jin．我以7角錢一斤的價格買了這些桔子。at the proper or suitable time在適當的時候
*You must learn to do the right thing at the right time．應該學會在適當的時候做適當的事情。with the danger of； with the possibility of（loss，etc．）冒…之險；不顧…
*He was determined to get there even at the risk of his life．他決心到那裡去，即使是冒生命危險也在所不惜。
*At the risk of being bankrupt， he invested all his money in the company．冒著破產的危險，他把所有的錢都投到公司去了。1．at the same moment； together 同時；一起
*I know he is untrustful，but at the same time，I must admit he is a good worker．我知道，他不可信。但是同時我必須承認他是個好工人。
*Don't all speak at the same time．大家不要同時說話。
2．in spite of the fact；even though；however儘管如此；雖然；但是
*It will cost a lot of money． At the same time，I think we shall need it and it will certainly be useful．這將花費好多錢，但是我認為我們需要它而且它一定會有用途的。on seeing一看到…就
*The boy ran towards his mother at the sight of a dog．那個男孩一看見狗就朝母親跑去。sometimes；occasionally間或；有時
*At times I saw her walking alone by the lake．我有時看到她獨自在湖邊散步。
*At times I make mistakes when I speak English．我說英語有時有錯。in the state of armed struggle在交戰中
*The two countries were at war for 8 years．這兩個國家打了 8年仗。as one pleases or likes隨意地
*Gone for ever are the days when imperialism could trample small nations under foot at will．帝國主義任意把小國踩在腳下的日子已一去不復返了。
*No one can do anything at will．誰也不能為所欲為。
*He comes and goes at will．他來去自由。working； engaged in在工作；從事於
*He is at work on a new book．他在寫一本新書。at-
