~.lywhen one has free time在空餘之時
*I am quite at leisure if you want me to do anything for you．你要是需要我幫忙，我完全有空。
*Please look through the manuscript at you leisure．請在閒暇的時候把這份稿子看一下。1．at the maximum至多
*At best， they can cover only half the journey this week．他們這個星期至多只能走完一半的路程。
2．in the most favourable case充其量
*I can give you one hundred dollars at best．我充其量只能給你100美元。and no later最遲；至遲
*We must be there by 10 at（the）latest．我們必須最遲10點鐘趕到那裡。
*In a few days at（the）latest I will return．我最多幾天就返回。
*I will give you a definite answer on Friday at the latest．我最遲在星期五給你確切的答覆。not more than至多
*He is at most 30 years old．他至多30歲。
*It was a minor offense at most．那頂多也不過是個小錯。even in the worst circumstances壞到極點；作為最壞的可能性
*We'll lose some money at worst．我們至多損失一些錢罷了。
*She keeps cheerful，even when things are at their worst．即使在最糟的情況下，她也保持心情愉快。Au
