他以第一流的詩人而聞名 [而著稱] 
2 be+doing; 構成進行
a. 正在做…,正在…中
She is writing now. 
她現在正在寫字
b. 
常帶責難之意] 老是 [一天到晚] 在做…
He is always smoking. 
他一天到晚吸煙
c. 想要做…,正在著手做…
He is coming to see us this morning. 
他今晨要來看我們
I must be going. 
我必須走了
→ be GOing to do.
d. [be 動詞構成進行式] 正在做… (的時候) 
"Be serious !"-"I am being serious.". 
「要認真!」「我 (是很) 認真啊」
You are being too kind to him, aren't you?. 
你對他太客氣了吧?
3 [be+to do] 
a. 將要做…,預定做…
We are to meet at 5. 
我們預定在五點鐘見面
He was to have arrived at 5. 
他原定在五點鐘到達 (但還沒有到) 
b. 有義務做…,必須做…
I am to inform you that. 
?.我謹通知你…
You are not to speak in this room. 
你不可以在這個房間裡說話
c. 可以做…
No one was to be seen. 
一個人都看不見
d. 注定…
He was nevebe on the point of； be ready to即將；就要
*We were about to leave when you telephoned．你打電話來時，我們正要動身。be without money沒有錢
*He couldn't take his sister to the movie last night for the simple reason that he was broke．他昨晚不能帶他妹妹去看電影，原因很簡單，他沒有錢。have one's name down in a register for在名冊中登記
*He is down for promotion．他已列入晉級名單。
*We are down for a new council house．我們已登記了市建房屋。1．be in favour of贊成；擁護
*I'm for the Conservatives， but she's for the Socialists．我擁護保守黨人，但她卻擁護社會黨人。
2．be going to ； be heading for要去；動身去
*I'm for the hills this year．今年我要到山區去。1．enter for參加（競爭）
*He will be in for the match．他將參加這場比賽。
2．be due for； be in line for必定會遇到（遭到）；即將獲得
*You'll be in for trouble if you don't take my advice．如果不聽我的勸告，你非遇到麻煩不可。
*He is in for promotion．他即將獲得晉陞。be party to； be fully involved in參與；完全捲入
*He is in on the whole sordid business．他參與了整個這場骯髒的勾當。
*They were de finitely in on the consiracy．他們肯定完全參與了這一陰謀。
*I'm sure she's in on their plans．我肯定她跟他們同謀。be in favour with； be friendly with 得某人歡心；與某人友好相處
*He is in with her at the moment．他現在深得她的歡心。
*She's well in with those people．她跟那些人友好相處。1．go away； leave離開
*Mr．Smith has been off to Paris．史密斯先生已經離開去巴黎了。
2．be cancelled被取消
*The trip was off because of the bad weather．這次旅行因天氣不好而被取消了。
3．stay away from work； finish work下班；完工；休假
*She is off work at eight o'clock tonight．他今晚8點鐘下班。
4．have gone bad變壞；變質
*The meat is off． Don't eat it．肉變質了，不要再吃了。
5． have become loose鬆開
*There's a button off your coar．你的外衣掉了一個扣子。
6． be prevented from eating， etc．戒某種食品
*He's been off alcohol since his illness．他自病後就戒酒了。
7． dislike厭惡
*I'm off eggs just now；I ate so many last week．我現在厭惡雞蛋，上周吃得太多了。Be Prepared
隨時做好準備
