4 熊捕食時以前腿勒緊獵物之行動remember； consider記住；考慮
*You must bear in mind that contradictions exist everywhere．應當記住，矛盾是普遍存在的。
*We should bear our family in mind when we make our decisions．我們作決定時必須考慮到家庭。bear leader
(昔時) 陪伴富家或貴族子弟旅遊的家庭教師1．have some connection with；be related to與…有關；涉及
*These were vital decisions that bore on the happiness of everybody．這些是關係到每一個人幸福的重要決定。
*How does his remark bear on the matter？他的話同這件事有什麼關係？
2．affect sb．（usu． in a bad way）對…有影響；對…施加壓力
*The shortage of oil bears on the life of the people．石油短缺影響了人民生活。
*We have to bring some pressure to bear on him．我們必須對他加點壓力。prove or support the truth of證實；證明
*What you say bears out my argument．你的話證實了我的論點的正確性。
*If I tell the judge that I am innocent， can you bear me out？要是我告訴法官我是無辜的，你能為我作證嗎？
*I hope you will bear out what I tell you．我希望你能證實我告訴你的話。be somewhat like與…相像
*He bears same resemblance to his father．他有些像他的父親。Bear River
熊河
(發源於美國猶他州之東北部,長約350哩,向北流經懷俄明州再向西北經愛達荷州,最後南流入猶他州之大鹽湖)1．have courage；not lose heart （在困難情況下）堅強；不氣餒
*She bore up well against that trouble．她堅強地度過了那次難關。
*She bears up in face of difficulties．在困難面前她不氣餒。
*The young girl bore up well after her failure of first jumps．在幾次試跳失敗之後，那位姑娘表現得十分堅強。
2．support sb． in time of trouble （在困難時）幫助
*He couldn't have liced through the crisis without John to bear him up．要是沒有約翰的幫助，他是很難度過那次難關的。
3．remain strong without being broken支撐得住
*The bridge will bear up well under a tank．即使一輛坦克開上去，這座橋也能承受得了。show patience towards； tolerate容忍；忍耐
*It is hard to bear with criticism．耐心聽取批評是件不容易的事情。
*He can't bear with faultfinding people．他不能容忍吹毛求疵的人。
*There's no bearing with such rude fellows．對這些粗魯的傢伙決不寬容。bear's-ear
