beat up
(1) → v.t. A 5 a
(2) 痛打,毒打; 出其不意地襲擊<人>
(3)(口語) (擊鼓) 召集,徵集
~ up recrefuse to come to the point when speaking about a subject講話繞圈子；不著正題
*Don't beat about the bush． Come straight to the point．不要繞圈子，直截了當地說吧。
*Instead of answering my question he began to beat about the bush．他不回答我的問題而是在不著邊際地兜圈子。1．force or persuade sb． to lower his price迫使或勸說（某人）降價；還價
*At first he asked for fifty pounds，but I beat him down to fortyfive．起初他要50鎊，後來我把價殺到45鎊。
*Can we beat down the price？我們能還價嗎？
2．crush；pour down摧毀；傾瀉於；照射
*All their defenses were beaten down by the tanks．他們所有的防禦工事都被坦克摧毀了。
*The heavy rain beat down the crops．大雨傾盆，猛打著莊稼。
3．shine brightly or hotly烈日照射
*In summer the sun beats down on the roof，so that the upper rooms become unbearably hot．夏天烈日直射屋頂，因此樓上的房間酷熱難忍。
*The crowds stood there for over an hour， with the sun beating down on them．群眾站在那裡一個多小時，烈日一直照在他們身上。
4．deject使沮喪
*He was thoroughly beaten down and wretched．他十分沮喪和痛苦。beat generation
<<名詞>>1．beat severely痛打
*He told the police that he had been beaten up by two masked men．他告訴警察說兩個蒙面人把他痛打了一頓。
*They not only robbed the man of his money， but beat him up．他們不僅搶了那人的錢，而且還把他毒打了一頓。
2．mix thoroughly攪拌
*She beat up me egg in the flour．她把雞蛋同麵粉攪拌勻。
*He is beating up cream．他正在攪拌奶油。
3．go against the wind逆風而行
*The ship was beating up the channel．船在海峽裡逆風而行。
4．seek eagerly；gather together 熱切地尋找；召集
*She tried to beat up some support for the campaign she was leading．她努力為自己所領導的運動尋求支持。
*They will do their best to beat up customers for their company．他們將盡力為其公司招徠生意。
5．disturb as by a sudden visit驚擾
*Don't beat up the rabbit．不要驚跑那隻兔子。
*The enemy were unaware of our closing in until two shots beat them up．敵人沒有覺察到我們已經逼近，直到兩聲槍響震驚了他們。beat-beat
