beside oneself 
→ oneself.at the end of one's control…得發狂；…得要命
*She was beside herself with joy when she got the letter．收到那封信，她欣喜若狂，高興得要命。
*He was beside himself with grief．他極度悲傷。
*Jane has been almost beside herself with toothache，but she will not go to a dentist．簡牙痛得要命，可她就是不去看牙醫。having nothing to do with離題；與本題無關
*That question was beside the mark and need not be answered．那個問題與本題無關，沒有必要回答。
*What you have said is beside the point．你所說的與題無關。be.sides
