blow
[blo; blou]
<<不及物動詞>>
(blew[blu; blu:]; blown[blon; bloun])
(文語)開花 (bloom)（of the wind）cause to move吹走；吹跑
*The wind was so strong that people were nearly blown away．風刮得很大，幾乎把人都捲走了。cause to fall by blowing；knock down吹倒；摧毀
*The lamppost was blown down by the gale last night．昨晚電線桿被狂風吹倒了。
*The storm blew down many trees．這場風暴刮倒了許多樹。
*The building was blown down during the war．這幢大樓是在戰爭中被炸毀的。blow molding
吹氣製造法
(做玻璃器皿等)remove by explosion or force of wind吹掉；炸掉
*The wind blew off the roots of many trees．大風把許多樹連根拔掉。1．explode and stop functioning；burst（said generally of tires）爆炸；爆裂（通常指輪胎）
*Don't pump too much air into the tire，otherwise you blow it out．氣別打得太足，否則輪胎會炸掉的。
*We arrived late because the front tire blew out on the way．我們遲到了，因為車的前胎在路上爆了。
2．stop burning by blowing吹熄
*She blew out the candle．她吹滅了蠟燭。
3．stop blowing（風）停止
*The storm blew itself out after five days．5天後，暴風雨停了。
4．（cause a fuse，a bulb，etc．to）melt（使保險絲、燈泡等）燒斷
*A short circuit suddenly blew out the fuse．短路突然把保險絲燒斷了。
*An abnormally high lightning current blew out many television sets in the high building．一股超強的閃電電流燒壞了這座高層建築內的許多電視機。1．pass；vanish結束；（麻煩、不和等）消失
*The whole affair has caused a lot of trouble，but after it's blown over，no one will talk about it any more．那件事引起了很多糾紛，但過後便沒人再提它了。
*I believe your troubles will soon blow over．我相信你的困難不久就會克服掉的。
*They had frequent quarrels，but they soon blew over．他們之間常有爭吵，但一下子就過去了。
2．stop blowiug（風）息
*The storm has blown over．暴風雨停了。1．destroy by explosion炸毀；爆炸
*There were thousands of passengers in the train when it blew up．那列火車爆炸時，上面有幾千名乘客。
*The enemy blew up all the bridges in this area．敵人炸毀了這個地區所有的橋樑。
*A chemical factory blew up in the city yesterday．昨天，這個城裡的一家化工廠發生了爆炸。
2．become suddenly angry突然發怒
*He blew up at me when I told him that I couldn't do it．當我告訴他我不能做這件事時，他對我大發雷霆。
*I'm sorry I blew up at you this morning．很抱歉，今天上午我跟你發了脾氣。
3．fill with air；inflate打氣
*I'll have these tires blown up．我要給這些輪胎打打氣。
4．exaggerate；inflate誇大；吹噓；吹捧
*This whole affair has been blown up．整個這件事已經被誇大了。
*Don't blow this thing up more than necessary．別過分誇大這件事。
*He blows up his boss with flattery．他對他的老闆阿諛奉承。
5．increase in size；enlarge放大
*These prints would look very good blown up．這些圖片放大後會非常好看。
*He has blown the print up．他已經放大了這張像片。
6．scold scverely怒斥
*The headmaster blew the boys up about the broken window．校長斥責這些孩子打壞了窗戶。
*The boss blew Mary up for being late without a good excuse．由於瑪麗遲到，又沒有適當的理由，老闆把她訓了一頓。
*The teacher blew him up for not doing his homework．老師嚴厲地批評他未做家庭作業。inform against；betray；impair the value of告發；出賣；使…受損害；使…丟臉
*He blew upon his comrades．他出賣了同志。
*Her reputation is blown upon．她威性掃地。blow-by-blow
