『物理』束縛電子1．going in the direction of 開往；駛向
*The ship is bound for Wuhan．這船是開往武漢的。
2．intending to go to準備到…去
*Where are they bound for？他們要到哪裡去？
*They are bound for Northeast China to clear the wild land．他們正準備去東北開墾荒原。bound form
<<可數名詞>>
『語言』附著語式
(只能與其他形式連用而不能獨立成字的部分,如英文之字首 un-,字尾 -ness 等是; cf. free form)1．under the obligation；obliged有義務的；受到約束的
*We are bound to help them overcome the difficulties．我們有義務幫助他們克服困難。
2．sure to；determined to 一定的；決心要
*Are you bound to stay at the office so late？你必須在辦公室呆到這麼晚嗎？
*The girl is bound to win a prize medal．這女孩決心要獲得獎章。
*Under the leadership of the Party，the Chinese people are bound to win the victory．在黨的領導下，中國人民必定取得勝利。
*He is bound to succeed in doing the experiment．他一定會試驗成功。
3．destined for駛往
*She stood on the seaside，watching the ships bound to distant lands．她站在海邊，目送船舶駛向遙遠的國度。busy with；deeply concerned with 熱心於；關注於
*They are bound up in the difficult task．他們的全部身心都投入這項艱難的工作中了。
*He is bound up in his wife and children．他埋頭於自己的小家庭。have a very close connection with 同…密切相關
*The affair was bound up with their interests．這件事同他們的利益密切相關。
*The welfare of the individual is bound up with the welfare of the community．個人福利與社會福利息息相關。bound.a.ry
