[brˏk; brɑik)
(brokє[brok; brouk]; bro.kˏn[`brokn; 'broukn]]
<<及物動詞>>
A
1 切斷
a. 將<物>毀壞 (成二個以上或細片) ,打破,打碎,弄破
Who broke the mirror?. 
是誰打破了鏡子?
She broke the cup in two [into pieces]. 
她把杯子打破成兩半 [碎片] 
b. 折斷 <樹枝等> ,扯 [揪,扭,擰] 斷
~ one's pencil 
弄斷鉛筆心
The boy broke a branch off [from the tree]. 
這男孩扯斷 [從樹上扯下] 樹枝
c. 折斷 <骨> ,折斷…的骨,扭傷…的關節,使…的關節脫臼
~ one's leg [arm] 
折斷腿[手臂]
d. 割破,割傷,劃破,擦破<皮膚>
~ the skin 
擦破皮膚
e. 弄壞,損壞 <鍾、表等> ; 使…失靈
2 
a. 打破 <沉默、單調、有規則 (之狀態) 等> ,擾亂 <和平、安寧等> 
~ a person's sleep 
擾亂某人的睡眠
The shot broke the peace of the morning. 
槍聲打破了早晨的沉寂
Only the whir of the air conditioner broke the silence in the office. 
打破辦公室內寂靜的,只有空氣調節機呼呼的轉動聲
b. 使 <步伐等> 亂
~ step < 
部隊> (在行進中) 走亂步伐
~ ranks 
搞亂隊伍
3 中斷 <正在繼續之物> ,遮斷
~ an electric current 
切斷電流
~ diplomatic relations with 
? 與…斷絕外交關係
~ one's journey 
中止旅程
~ a strike 
破壞罷工,迫使罷工者結束罷工
He broke short the conversation. 
他突然停止了談話
4 a. 開闢<道路>
~ a trail [path] through the woods 
在樹林中開出一條小徑
b. 開墾<土地>,耕<地>; 破 <土> 
~ ground 
耕地; 破土
c. 開拓 <新領域等> ,打開 <局面等> 
~ new [fresh] ground ( 
研究、事業等) 啟步踏入新的領域,開闢新天地
d. <魚>跳出<水面>
I saw a fish ~ the water of the pond. 
我看到一條魚跳出池塘水面
e. 推開,打開,撬開<物>
~ a crate (open) 
撬開板條箱
~ a door open 
撬[打]開門
5 
a. 分開,拆散,分離,卸開 <整體之物、完整之物> 
~ a set 
拆開成套之物 (零售) 
b. 將 <大鈔> 換零 (change) 
~ a hundred dollar bill 
把一百美元鈔票換成1．come apart；come into pieces破裂；裂開
*The wings of the plane broke away in midair，so the plane crashed．機翼在半空中裂開，所以飛機失事了。
2．escape；rebel 逃跑；反叛
*The criminal broke away from the policemen．罪犯從警察手中逃走了。
*I imagine he will try to break away．我想他會設法逃跑。
3．end one's connection with脫離（社團、政黨等）；斷絕關係
*The state has broken away from the union．這個州已經脫離了聯邦政府。
*He broke away from his family and went abroad．他與家庭斷絕了關係，到國外去了。
4．get rid of；abandon 放棄；解除
*You should break away from such bad habits．你應該改掉這樣的壞習慣。
*We must break away from convention and adopt as many advanced techniques as possible．我們必須打破常規，盡量採用先進技術。1．destroy；reduce sth．to pieces 毀掉；打破
*The police broke the door down．警察破門而入。
2．crush；defeat鎮壓；制服
*They broke down all opposition．他們壓倒了所有的對手。
3．stop functioning（generally of motors and similar mechanical objects）壞了；出毛病（尤指發動機、機器等）
*The car broke down on the way to the airport．車子在去機場的路上拋錨了。
*The lift broke down，so we had to walk up the stairs．電梯壞了，我們只好走上樓去。
4．fail to carry out（plans，negotiations，etc．）；come to nothing失敗（指無結果中斷計劃、談判等）；堅持不下去
*The plan was good，but it broke down，because people were unwilling to cooperate．計劃是好的，但由於人們不願合作，還是失敗了。
*I expect the negotiations to break down soon．我預料談判不久就會中斷。
5．burst into tears；lose control 禁不住痛哭；（身體、精神）垮了
*When he heard his sentence，the man broke dewn．聽到判決，那人不禁號啕大哭。
*Your health will break down if you work too hard．太勞累的話，你身體會垮的。
*He tried to cope with the everincreasing burden of his work，but finally he broke down and had to take a complete rest．他設法應付日益加重的工作負擔，但最後身體垮了，不得不全休。
6．separate into parts；take apart；analyse 分解；分析
*Water can be broken down into hydrogen and oxygen．水可以分解為氫和氧。
*I want you to break this data down．我想請你分析一下這個資料。1．enter by force，usn．unlawfully 闖入
*A thief broke in during the night and stole all his money．盜賊夜間闖了進來，偷走了他所有的錢。
*Many students broke in the door of the burning laboratory．許多學生破門進入失火的實驗室。
2．interrupt 插嘴
*Don't break in when your teacher is speaking．當你的老師說話的時候不要插嘴。
*While I was explaining my point of view，he broke in to argue with me．正當我在解釋我的觀點時，他插進來和我爭論。
3．train；tame 訓練
*The horse has been well broken in．這匹馬受過良好的訓練。
*That PLA man is much noted for his skill in breaking in horses．那個解放軍戰士以善於馴馬而出名。
4．help adjust；adjust through usage sth．which is new and stiff 使適應新工作；使新物品逐漸合用
*I'll give you an easy job just to break you in to the work．先讓你幹點容易的事情，以便適應工作。
*Our new teachers are breaking in well．我們的新教師正在逐漸適應工作。
*He is broken in to the new work．他已經適應了新的工作。
*These new shoes are hurting me．I'll be glad when they are broken in．這雙新鞋穿上緊腳不舒服，等穿到合腳時我會很高興的。1．divide 分成
*Alice broke the chocolate into pieces，one for each person．愛麗絲把巧克力分成小塊，每人一塊。
2．enter by force 闖入
*The policeman found that the house had been broken into and a quantity of jewellery stolen．警察發現有人闖入室內，盜走一批珠寶。
*The thieves planned to break into the bank．小偷預謀闖進這家銀行。
3．burst into；begin suddenly 突然…起來
*Jack broke into laughter．傑克突然大笑起來。
*At this point even the interpreter broke into weeping．到這時連翻譯都哭泣起來了。
4．interrupt 打斷
*Don't break into their conversation；they are discussing something important．不要打斷他們的談話，他們正在討論重要的事情。
5．open and consume（sth．in reserve）；occupy 啟開和動用（儲存物品）；侵佔；佔用
*He has broken into the money he has saved for long．他已動用他長期積蓄的錢。
*They were so hungry that they couldn't help breaking into their emergency supplies of food and water．他們餓極了，不得不動用應急食物和飲水。
*I can't take on any extra work；my spare time has been broken into far too much as it is．我不能再承擔任何額外的工作，就現在這樣我的業餘時間已經佔用得過多了。
*Housework has broken into a lot of my time．家務事已佔用了我很多時間。escape；become free or loose 擺脫；脫開
*The criminal broke loose from the police and ran into the woods．罪犯掙脫警察，逃進了樹林。
*During the storm，the boat broke loose from its mooring．颳風暴時，船脫開了纜繩。break of day
破曉; 黎明
At break of day the hikers were already on the trail. 
黎明時分,那些徒步旅行者已經上路1．separate by breaking 弄碎；折掉
*He broke off a piece of chocolate and offered it to me．他掰開一塊巧克力遞給了我。
*He broke off a branch and gave it to me．他折了一根樹枝，把它遞給了我。
2．（relationship，agreement）end or terminate suddenly（關係、協議等）突然結束；解除
*The two countries broke off their relations last month．這兩個國家上個月中斷了外交關係。
*Unfortunately the negotiations have been broken off and are not expected to be resumed．不幸的是，談判已中斷，而且不能指望再恢復了。
*The girl broke off her engagement last week．這個女孩上周解除了婚約。
3．stop speaking；cease suddenly 中止（談話）；突然停止
*We had to break off our discussion because it was getting late．時間晚了，我們不得不中斷討論。
*Jack broke off telling the story to answer the telephone．傑克中斷了正在講的故事，去接一個電話。
*The conference broke off at noon．中午休會。
*Bill broke off in the middle of his speech because of shouts of protest from the audience．彼爾在聽眾的一片抗議聲中中斷了發言。
4．stop working for a short time 工間休息
*Let's break off for ten minutes．我們休息10分鐘吧。
*The whole cast broke off for coffee in the middle of the rehearsal．在排練當中全體演員休息了一會喝咖啡。
5．abandon；interrupt 放棄；打斷
*The doctor advised him to break off smoking．醫生勸他戒煙。
*Her intrusion broke off our conversation．她闖進來打斷了我們的談話。1．occur suddenly 爆發；（突然）發生
*The Second World War broke out in September，1939．第二次世界大戰於1939年9月爆發。
*A fire broke out in this hotel last night．昨晚這家旅館發生了火災。
*The economic crisis broke out first in the United States．經濟危機首先在美國爆發。
*Fighting has broken out on the border and is expected to continue until a settlement is reached．戰鬥在邊界打響了，預料會繼續下去直到問題得到解決。
2．escape 逃脫
*Three prisoners have broken out this week and are on the run．本周有3名囚犯越獄逃跑。
*He spent several months in a Nazi concentration camp before he broke out．他在納粹集中營裡關了幾個月後逃了出來。
3．show sudden violence in speech or behaviour（言語或行為）突然激烈
*The whole meeting broke out in cheers．整個會場爆發出陣陣歡呼聲。
*She broke out in tears．她突然哭了起來。
*He broke out：「That is not so！」他猛然吼道：「並不是這麼回事。」
*He is liable to break out into furious passions．他很容易暴跳如雷。1．break a way through；overcome 突破；衝破；克服
*The allied forces soon broke through the enemy's defence line．聯軍很快就突破了敵人的防線。
*The soldiers have managed to break through．戰士們已設法突圍。
*We broke through countless enemy encirclements and blockades until we finally reached northern Shanxi．我們突破了敵人無數次的包圍和封鎖，最後到達了陝北。
*All difficulties can be broken through．一切困難都能戰勝。
2．achieve sth．mew；make a discovery of a new and important kind 取得某種新成就；作出重大發現
*Nuclear physicists claimed to have broken through in several new aspects of the nature of the atom．核物理學家們宣稱，在有關原子本質的幾個新方面已有重大突破。
*Scientists hope to break through soon in their fight against heart disease．科學家們希望不久在治療心臟病方面有所突破。
*He failed many times but he finally broke through to find a successful polio vaccine．他失敗了許多次，但最終成功地發現了預防小兒麻痺症的疫苗。
3．make an appearance出現
*A little later the sun broke through the clouds．一會兒太陽就鑽出了雲層。1．smash to pieces；divide into small pieces 打破；弄碎；拆開
*She broke up the glass in her search for money．她在找錢時把玻璃打碎了。
*He can break up that stone with his hand．他用手能打碎那塊石頭。
2．end for a holiday（學校期終）放假
*The boys will break up for the Christmas vacation next week．孩子們下周放聖誕假。
*When does the school break up for the summer holidays？學校什麼時候放暑假？
*We break up on July 25th．我們7月25日放假。
3．end；stop 結束；停止
*The party broke up at midnight．晚會在午夜結束。
*What time is the meeting expected to break up？會議可望在幾點鐘結束？
*He broke up the fight between the two gangs．他制止了兩伙人打架。
*A fight started in that street last night，so the police were called in to break it up．昨晚在那條馬路上發生了一起鬥毆事件，人們把警察叫來制止。
4．become weak；upset completely （指人）身體衰弱；完全攪亂
*He may break up under all these troubles．遇到這麼多麻煩，他可能會垮下來。
*This trouble has really broken him up．這件麻煩事確實使他心煩意亂。
5．lose or destroy spirit or selfcontrol精神崩潰（常用於被動語態）
*She was all broken up after her daughter's death，and did not go out of the house for two months．她在女兒死後精神崩潰了，有兩個月沒有出家門。
6．stop being friends；separate絕交
*Mary and John were good friends，but then they had a quarrel and broke up．瑪麗和約翰原來是好朋友，但後來吵了一架便絕交了。1．cease one's association or friendship 同…斷絕關係
*He advised her to break with her boyfriend．他勸她和她的男友斷絕關係。
*He broke with his former friends when he became rich．當他成了有錢人時，就同以前的朋友斷絕了關係。
2．discontinue a practice or a habit 放棄（行為、習慣）
*It is not easy for the old to break with their old ideas．老年人放棄舊觀點是不容易的。break-bulk
