B~ him here with you. 
帶他一起來
Pilate brought Jesus out before the people. 
比拉多將耶穌帶到眾人前面來
2 a. 造成,引起,招致,帶來
The winter brought heavy snowfalls. 
那年冬天帶來了 [下了好幾場] 大雪
b. 給…招致 [帶來,造成] …; [給…]招致 [帶來,造成] …[to]
The benign weather brought North America a bumper crop. 
溫和的氣候給北美帶來大豐收
He ~s bad luck to anybody he comes in contact with. 
凡是跟他接觸的人都會倒楣
The bad smell brought tears to my eyes. 
這難聞的味道使得我眼淚直流
c. [給…]帶來 [造成] …[into, on, upon]
The brisk walk brought a little color into Grandmonther cheeks. 
快步行走使得她祖母的面頰微微泛紅
We must not ~ mass destruction on ourselves by waging an atomic world war. 
我們千萬不要發動世界核子戰爭而自招集體毀滅
3 a. <事物>引<某人>來 (某處) 
What ~s you here?. 
你來這裡有什麼事 [什麼風把你吹來] ?
An hour's walk brought us to our destination. 
走了一小時之後,我們到達了目的地
b. 使<人><做…>
The telephone call brought him hurrying to the office. 
電話使他急忙趕到辦公室 [他接到電話,趕緊到辦公室] 
4 a. 使… [至某種狀態] [to, into]
→ bring?to LIFE
~ a car to a stop 
把車子停下來
~ a war to an end 
結束戰爭
~ the police into the matter 
使警方介入此事
~ business and government into a harmonious relationship 
使官商關係和諧
→ bring?into BEING,bring?into LINE.
b. 影響<人><去做…>,誘… <致…> ,使…<做…>,說服
He wondered what brought her to see him. 
他想知道是什麼事使她想和他見面
c. [~ oneself]使自己<做…>
I could not ~ myself to believe it. 
我無法使自己相信這件事
5[對…]提起 <訴訟、控告等> ,興起,提出,舉出[against]
He brought a charge against me. 
他控告我
She brought a slander suit against him. 
她控告他誹謗
6 a. <物>能產生 <收入、利益> ; 能賣得,能換得 <多少錢> 
The products of her dairy were ~ing the highest prices in the market. 
她的制酪場的產品在市場能賣最高價格
b. 使<人>賺取 <收入> ,使…賺得…
His pictures ~ him 20, 000 a year. 
他的畫使他每年賺進兩萬英鎊的收入
bring about
(1) 引起,造成,招致,導致
Nuclear weapons may ~ about the annihilation of man. 
核子武器可能招致人類的滅亡
(2)『航海』使<船>轉向
bring around
(1) 使<人>復甦,使…清醒,使…恢復知覺 [精神健康 (等) ] 
The smelling salts brought her around. 
嗅鹽使她甦醒過來
A hot coffee will ~ you around. 
熱咖啡會使你恢復精神
(2) 說服<人>使其接受 […的意見] ,使…信服[…][to]
They tried to ~ me around to their point of view. 
他們試圖說服我接受他們的觀點
(3) 帶<人、物>來[…][to]
(4) = BRING about (2)
bring back
(1) 為…帶 [攜] 回…; 將…歸還[給…][to]
I'll ~ you back the book tomorrow. = I'll ~ the book back to you tomorrow. 
我明天會把書還給你
(2)[使人]記起 <往事> ,憶起,想起[to]
Your words ~ back many memories. 
你所說的話令人想起許多往事
The letter brought it all back to her. 
那封信使她想起了 (那事的) 全部情況
(3) 使<人>恢復 [健康狀態] [to]
The change of air brought him back to good health. 
易地療養使他恢復了健康
bring down
(1) 卸下<物>
(2) 擊落 <飛機等> ; 打下<鳥等>; 射倒 <獵物等> 
I brought down the lion at a shot. 
我一槍射倒那只雄獅
(3) 打倒 <政府、人等> ,使…垮台
~ down the government 
打倒政府
(4) 降低<物價等>; 向 <商人> 殺價[到…],使…降價[to]
~ down prices 
降低物價
~ unemployment down to 3% 
使失業率降到百分之三
~ a salesman down to a lower price 
向銷貨員殺價 [使推銷員同意減價] 
(5) 將 <歷史記錄> 延續 [到後代] [to]
The history has been brought down to modern times. 
其歷史延續到現代
(6) 招惹 <災禍等> [到…]; 使<怒氣等>落於[…][on, upon]
~ down a person's anger on one's head 
使某人的怒氣發洩到別人身上
(7)(俚)使<人>沮喪,貶低
bring forth
(文語)
(1) 生產,致生; 結 <果> ,萌 <芽> ,開<花>
April showers ~ forth May flowers. (
諺)四月的驟雨會帶來五月的花
(2) 提出,引起<問題等>
bring forward
(1) 提produce；cause to arise or happen 產生；導致；促成
*Many new changes will be brought about in China's industry．中國的工業將產生許多新的變化。
*I offered to act as mediator and try to bring about a reconciliation between the two parties．我自願擔任調解人，試圖使爭執雙方和解。
*The accident was brought about by John's carelessness．這場事故是由於約翰的粗心造成的。
*The heavy spring rains brought about the flood．特大的春雨造成了這場水災。carry 帶著
*Why don't you bring your gun along with you？We'll perhaps go hunting．你為什麼不把槍帶來？我們也許會去打獵的。1．persuade sb．to change his opinion勸告某人改變主意
*At first he stuct to his own opinion stubbornly but we brought him around to our way of thinking．開始他頑固地堅持自己的意見，但最後我們使他接受了我們的思路。
*We must bring them around to our point of view．我們必須勸告他們接受我們的觀點。
*In a strike situation，workers try to bring the management around to their view by refusing to work．罷工時，工人們企圖通過拒絕上班來迫使資方接受他們的要求。
2．bring sb．to an agreed place 帶某人到（約定的場所）
*He brought the visitors around to the exhibition hall．他把參觀者帶到了展覽廳。
3．cause to recover from fainting or illness 使甦醒；使復原
*Two girls fainted in the heat but we soon brought them around．有兩個女孩因中暑昏過去了，可是我們很快便使她們恢復了知覺。
*The doctor brought the man round shortly after the accident．醫生在事故發生後不久就使那人甦醒過來了。
4．direct（a conversation or discussion）to one's favourite subject把（話題或討論）引向自己愛好的題目
*By talking about the Women's Day he managed to bring the conversation around to the women's liberation movement．談到婦女節時，他就把話題轉到婦女解放運動上來了。1．return 送還；歸還；退還
*These books must be brought back within a week．這些書必須在一周內送還。
*If you don't like the dress you bought，you can always bring it back．如果你不喜歡你買的衣服，你隨時都可以退回來。
2．recall；bring to mind 回想起；記起
*The smell of the flower brings back her memories．花香喚起了她對往事的回憶。1．reduce；make low 減少（價格）；使跌落
*After much hard bargaining he brought the trader down to ＄100for the carpet．經過激烈的討價還價之後，他使賣主的地毯降到100美元。
*Some countries demand to bring down the price of petroleum．一些國家要求降低石油價格。
*Sellers at last agreed to bring down the prices by 5%．賣方最終同意降低5%的價格出售。
2．defeat；cause to come down 推翻；擊落
*The opposition party planned to bring the government down．反對黨謀劃推翻政府。
*This scandal could well bring him down．這件醜事很有可能使他垮台。
*He brought down 9 enemy aircraft during the Korean War．在朝鮮戰場上他擊落了9架敵機。
3．cause to be in low spirits；dePress；deflate 使情緒低落；使沮喪；使洩氣
*The temporary setback seemed to have brought them down completely．暫時的挫折似乎使他們完全失去了信心。
*Even the failure did not bring him down．甚至失敗也沒有使他沮喪。1．produce 生產；產生；提出
*His vegetable garden brings forth a great number of watermelons every year．他的菜園裡每年生產大量的西瓜。
*He brought forth a new plan，just as unworkable as the old one．他提出了一個新計劃，跟老計劃一樣行不通。
2．give rise to 引起
*Idleness and luxury bring forth poverty and want．懶惰和奢侈導致貧困和匱乏。
*Polluted water might bring forth a host of diseases．污染的水可能會引起許多疾病。
*His carelessness brought forth an accident．他的粗心大意惹出了意外事故。
3．reveal洩露
*Don't bring forth the secret．切勿洩露這個秘密。1．introduce；propose提出
*She brought forward a new proposal．她提出了一項新的建議。
*The matter will be brought forward at the next meeting．這個問題將在下次會上提出來。
*They have brought forward a plan to reform the curricula of our department．他們提出了一個改革我系課程設置的計劃。
2．advance in time提前
*They have brought the meetingforward to this Friday．他們已把會議提前到本週五召開。
*This warm weather will bring the crops forward．這種暖和的天氣會促使莊稼早熟。make realize；persuade sb．to believe使明白；使相信
*You must bring home to John where the difficulties lie．你必須使約翰認識到困難所在。
*Its importance has been brought home to me very strongly．我已非常深刻地認識到它的重要性。
*We should bring home to the public mind the practical importance of practising economy．我們應使公眾清楚地認識到勤儉節約的重要性。
*How can we bring home to him the seriousness of his conduct？我們怎樣才能使他清楚地認識到他的行為所導致的嚴重後果呢？1．gather（crop）收（莊稼）
*The farmers are busy bringing in the wheat．農民們正忙著收小麥。
2．introduce引入，引進（話題、風尚等）；提出（法案）
*The newcomers bring in new customs and new habits．新來者帶來新風俗、新習慣。
*They've brought in experts to advise on the scheme．他們請來了專家當該項目的顧問。
*The government has brought in a bill to deal with the matter．政府通過了一項法案來處理那個問題。
*You will have to bring in some outside help or you will never get the job finished in time．你必須借助一些外來的幫助，否則是不能按時完成這項工作的。
3．give a verdict判決
*The jury brought him in guilty．陪審團判他有罪。
4．yield（a profit）賺；贏
*In addition to his salary，he has investments which bring in about five hundred pounds a year．除了工資外，他的投資每年還有大約500英鎊的紅利。cause to be produced 使產生
*Reforms have brought great social and economic changes into being．改革帶來了社會和經濟的巨大變化。make very clear講清楚
*We touched on too many topics，so the group leader brought all of them into focus by summarizing our discussion．我們談及了許多話題，因此組長通過總結把所有討論的問題談清楚了。
*The new government of that country is too disorganized to bring its problems into focus and slove them．那個國家的新政府組織能力太差，根本不能把它的問題搞清楚並且解決好。cause sth．such as law to begin to operate使生效
*The new law will be brought into force from July．新的法律將從7月開始生效。make use of；bring…into action 發揮作用；調動（積極性）
*Now we have every opportunity to bring our talents into full play．現在我們有各種機會來發揮我們的才能。
*He brought all his strength into play to move the rock．他使出全身力氣來搬走那塊石頭。reveal；expose（a secret）揭露；揭示；公佈於眾
*The police investigation brought the crime into the open．警察的調查揭露了犯罪事實。
*The husband brought his feelings about their marriage into the open．丈夫公佈了他對於他們婚事的看法。1．carry away；rescue 運走；救出
*They brought off all the fishermen on board a sinking boat floating adrift in the sea．他們把飄浮在海上的一艘沉船上的漁民全部救了出來。
*The lifeboat brought off most of the crew．救生船搶救出了大部分船員。
2．succeed in；complete successfully 成功地完成
*He brought the deal off in a spectacular way．他驚人地完成了這項交易。
*You've brought it off at last．I am glad you have passed the test．你總算圓滿地把它結束了，我很高興你能通過這次考試。
*The plan will probably encounter a great deal of opposition，but with tactics and patience I think we'll be able to bring it off．這項計劃可能遭到許多反對，但是憑著機智和耐心，我想我們會成功的。1．cause to arise or occur；cause to develop or advance 引起；發生；使發展
*Living in damp surroundings may bring on rheumatism．生活在潮濕的環境裡會引發風濕病的。
*He has brought all the trouble on himself．麻煩都是他自找的。
*The rain helped to bring on the crops．這場雨有助於農作物的生長。
2．serve（food）up；introduce （usu．on a stage）端上（飯菜等）；介紹（通常在舞台上）
*She'll bring on our lunch right away．她馬上把午飯端上來。
*He brought on the guest speaker to the audience．他向聽眾介紹了請來的演講人。1．reveal clearly；present；bring to light；develop暴露；顯露；發展，發揮
*Difficulties can bring out a person's best qualities．艱難困苦方能顯示出一個人的優秀品質。
*The teacher helped to bring out the meaning of the poem．教師幫助闡釋這首詩的含義。
*This kind of work brings out the best in him．這種工作最能發揮他的才幹。
2．publish；produce or sell出版；發行
*They try to bring out one new book each month．他們爭取每月出版一本新書。
*An old college friend of mine has brought out a book on English poetry．我大學期間的一位老朋友出版了一本英文詩歌方面的書。
3．produce生產
*They are bringing out a new brand of soap powder next month．他們要在下月投放市場一種新牌洗衣粉。
*The factory is bringing out a new type of recorder．這家工廠正在生產一種新型錄音機。1．cause（sb．）to come with one 帶某人來
*She has just brought her family over from Shanghai．她剛把她一家從上海接來。
*It was brought over from China to Japan．它是從中國傳入日本的。
2．convert（sb．）to a different way of thinking，to a cause，etc．使某人改變想法
*With some difficulty，I brought my son over to my way of thinking．經過一番努力，我終於使我兒子同意我的看法。
*Most of his classmates were brought over to support him．他的大部分同班同學已被爭取過來支持他。
*They tried their best to bring the engineer over to their side．他們竭盡全力把工程師爭取到他們這邊來了。save（sb．）；conduct safely through 使（某人）脫險；使安全結束
*I am sure the doctor will bring him through．我相信醫生一定會使他脫離險境的。
*The peasants have brought all the newly transplanted seedlings through．農民已使所有這些剛插的秧苗成活了。
*It was courage and confidence that brought us through the crisis．是勇氣和信心使我們度過了困境。
*He brought his party through without accidents．他順利地結束了他的聚會，沒有發生任何意外事故。1．restore to consciousness 甦醒
*They threw some cold water over her head to bring her to．他們在她頭上撒了一些冷水使她甦醒過來。
*I once brought a fellow to that was drowned．我有一次曾經把一個溺水的人救活。
*He will soon be brought to．他會很快被救醒過來。
*The doctor has brought him to by artificial respiration．醫生用人工 呼吸使他恢復了知覺。
2．bring（a ship）to a stop使（船）停下
*The ship was finally brought to after a stormy voyage．船在暴風雨中航行了一段時間後終於停了下來。
*The sailors brought their ship to by dropping the anchor．水手們拋錨停船。end；conclude 使…結束
*The teacher brought the discussion to an end．老師中止了這場討論。
*I hope we'll bring our quarrel to an end as soon as possible．我希望我們盡快結束這場爭吵。disclose；reveal暴露出；揭發
*The trial brought to light many unknown details of the crime．這次審訊揭露了許多未被人發現的與這罪行有關的細節。
*After several months'investigation，the special committee brought to light some facts unknown to the outside world．經過數月的調查，特別委員會揭露了一些鮮為人知的事實。1．gain control of；defeat控制；壓制；鎮壓
*The firemen soon brought the fire under control．消防隊不久就把大火撲滅了。
*Those who opposed his wishes were brought under．所有違背他意願的人都遭到了鎮壓。
2．include in 包括在內
*Your suggestions can be brought under four headings．你的建議可包括在4個標題內。1．raise from childhood；educate 撫育；教育
*We must train and bring up millions of successors to out revolutionary cause．我們必須培養和造就千百萬革命事業的接班人。
*That child is very badly brought up．那孩子的教養很差。
*His father believed in bringing him up the hard way．他父親主張對他管教要嚴。
*The couple brought up many children of the martyrs．這對夫婦養育了許多烈士的後代。
2．mention or present for attention or consideration提出（讓人注意或考慮）
*Your suggestion will be brought up at the mext meeting．你的建議將在下次會議上提出來討論。
*In the course of study they brought up many questions．在學習過程中他們提出了很多問題。
*Please bring your plan up at the meeting．請將你的計劃在會上提出來。
3．cause to stop使…停下
*The captain was able to bring the ship up just before it hit a huge rock．在即將撞上巨石的關頭，船長把船停了下來。
4．vomit嘔吐
*Martin has been bringing up all morning．馬丁整個早上都在嘔吐。bring.ing-up
