[brʌʃ; brʌʃ]
<<名詞>>
1 (U)叢林,矮林,雜樹叢
2 (U)柴枝
3 [the ~](美)未開拓地 (backwoods)put away from；treat lightly；ignore；refuse to consider掃除（障礙）；漠視；輕視；不予理睬
*He brushed all obstacles aside on his way forward．他掃除了前進道路上的一切障礙。
*She brushed aside all difficulties and in the end succeeded．她藐視一切困難，最後終於成功了。
*Brushing aside all opposition，he put the matter to a vote．他不顧一切反對意見，把那件事付諸表決了。
*I don't like being brushed aside like this．我不喜歡讓人家這樣瞧不起。treat as neither important nor desirable 既不重視也不覺得稱心
*He brushed the whole business away．他對整個事情不予理會。
*You can't just brush away our opinions．你不能這樣置我們的意見而不顧。brush burn
擦傷brush cut
刷子頭
(一種男人髮型,似平頭)brush discharge
刷形放電brush fire
<<可數名詞>>
1 灌木叢的火災
2 (組織、部門、國家間等的) 持續的小問題; 突然爆發的 (軍事) 衝突1．remove with a brush；disappear or come off as a result of being brushed 刷去；刷落
*She brushed off the dust on her shoes．她刷去鞋子上的灰塵。
*Don't worry，the dirt will brush off easily．別著急，這髒東西很容易刷掉。
*He brushed the hairs off．她把身上的頭髮刷去了。
2．reject；dismiss curtly；not take seriously 拒絕；毫不客氣地把…打發走；對…不在乎
*He brushed off all our suggestions．他拒絕了我們所有的建議。
*I invited him to watch an opera with me yesterday，but he brushed me off．昨天我邀請他同我一起去看戲，但是他毫不客氣地拒絕了。
*I didn't expect her to brush us off like this．我沒有料到她會這樣拒絕我們。
*He cut his finger but he brushed it off and kept on working．他劃破了手指，但他若無其事地繼續工作。1．brush fully 全刷；刷遍
*I brushed the coat over．我把大衣全刷了一下。
2．treat lightly；almost ignore 輕率對待；幾乎忽視
*He brushed over the details of the policy．他忽視了政策的細節。1．encounter 碰到
*He has brushed up against trouble．他碰到了麻煩。
*She never loses heart when she brushes up against setbacks．她遭受挫折時從不灰心。
2．touch lightly 輕輕觸到
*I brushed up against her unintentionally．我無意間輕輕碰了她。1．review （a skill，knowledge）one has learned in the past 重新學習；複習
*I'll have to brush up my English before I go abroad．出國前我要溫習一下英語。
*He said he had to brush up on his history before the examination．他說他得在考試前複習歷史。
2．make clean or bright with a brush 刷淨；擦亮
*Your boots should be brushed up a bit．你的長統靴該搽搽亮。brush wheel
