burn
[bєn; bә:n]
<<可數名詞>>
(蘇格蘭.北英)小河,小溪,小川continue burning 不斷地燃燒
*The forest fire burned away for days．森林大火一連燒了好多天。1．burn completely 把…燒成平地；燒掉
*The building was burned down last week．這幢大樓是上周燒燬的。
2．lose heat or burn less brightly as the fuel is used up 漸漸燒完；燃料燃盡；火力減弱
*The fire has burned down；get some more coal please．火不旺了，再添點煤吧。1．destroy by burning 燒掉（家、店、財產等）
*The fire burned out his shop and left him deep in debt．火燒掉了他的商店，使他負債纍纍。
2．（electrical equipment）stop functioning；become useless 燒壞（電燈泡、電器）
*The electric light bulb is burnt out．電燈泡燒壞了。
*There are no lights in the house．Perhaps a fuse has burned out．屋裡沒燈，可能是保險絲燒壞了。
3．die；burn to an end（爐火等）燒盡；燃完
*The oil lamp has burned out．煤油燈的油燃盡了。
4．wear out or cause to wear out through overwork 因工作過度等而垮下；精疲力盡
*You'll burn yourself out if you go on working at this rate．如果你繼續這樣幹下去的話，你的身體會垮掉的。
5．（anger，etc．）disappear（怒氣等）消失
*Their anger seems to have burned out．他們的憤怒似乎已經平息。1．burst into flames again；burn brightly 燒起來；旺起來
*The fire burned up when she added some wood．她添了一些木柴，火就燒得旺起來了。
2．make angry 激怒；使…惱火
*His behaviour really burns me up．他的行為真使我惱火。
*He was burnt up about the matter．他為這件事大發雷霆。
3．burn completely；consume entirely 燒完
*The fire burned up a number of valuable manuscripts．那場火燒掉了一批珍貴的手稿。
*The house burned up before the firemen got there．消防隊員到達前，房子已燒光了。burn.a.ble
