5『軍』集中射擊; (機槍等的) 連放1．break in；smash in 闖入；破門而入
*The police burst in and told everyone to stand still．警察闖了進來，叫大家站著不動。
*They had to burst the door in because they had lost the key．他們丟了鑰匙，只好破門而入。
2．interrupt 打斷
*Father told his son not to burst in while adults are talking．父親叫他兒子不要打斷大人的談話。
3．appear suddenly 突然出現
*He'll be bursting in upon us at any moment．他會隨時突然出現在我們面前。
*We were talking about him when he burst in．我們正談到他時，他突然來了。1．enter suddenly；smash into 闖入；破門而入
*The police burst into the room．警察突然闖進了房間。
2．begin suddenly 突然開始；突然…起來
*The audience burst into applause．觀眾突然報以熱烈的掌聲。
*Mary burst into laughter．瑪麗突然大笑起來。
*The sad story made the girl burst into tears．悲慘的故事使那女孩突然哭起來。begin doing sth．suddenly 突然…起來
*Everyone was quiet when John suddenly burst out laughing．大家都很安靜，突然約翰大笑起來。
*Every time she thought about him she burst out crying．每當想起他，她就會突然哭起來。burst-up
