*The criminal tried to buy off the policemen．那個罪犯試圖賄賂警察。
*I don't like the way they are trying to buy me off－there must be something suspicious going on．我不喜歡他們這樣想方設法買通我，其中定有某種可疑之事。pay sb．in order to get his property；buy a business from sb．買下…產權
*The bigger company bought out all the shareholders of two smaller ones．這家大公司買下了兩家小公司的所有股份。
*He can sell his interest in that business any time because Mr．Smith will gladly buy him out．他隨時都可以把他在那個公司的股份賣掉，因為史密斯先生很樂意把他的股份買下。bribe；win over by paying money收買
*He was quite mistaken if he thought he could buy me over．如果他認為他可以收買我，那就大錯特錯了。
*He seems to think he can buy us over very cheaply．他們似乎認為可以輕易地收買我們。obtain by buying as widely as possible 全買；盡可以多地買進；囤積
*The speculators are trying to buy up the supplies of raw materials．投機商正在大肆囤積原材料。
*They have been buying up all available land．他們一直在買所有能買到的地皮。buy.a.ble
