1 在…近旁,在…之旁邊,在…身邊,靠近…
a house by the seaside 
海濱的房屋
I haven't got it ~ me. 
我身邊沒有這樣東西
【同義字】
beside 和 by 都有「旁邊」的意思,而 beside 比 by 更明確
2 
a. 由…的旁邊,經過…
go by me [the church] 
從我 [教堂] 旁邊走過
b. 通過<路>,沿著…,順著…
drive by the highway 
沿著公路駕車
pass by the river 
經過河邊
c. 經由…,取道… (via) 
travel by (way of) Italy 
取道義大利旅遊
3 
a. 用…,藉…,乘…,搭…
by letter [wire] 
用書信 [電報] 
send by post 
郵寄
go [travel] by bus [boat, bicycle, plane, rail(road), train, etc.] 
搭乘巴士 [船,自行車,飛機,火車 (等) ] 去[旅行]
go by water [air] 
由水路 [搭飛機] 去
by land [sea] 
由陸路 [水路] 
go by the 9:00 p.m. train 
搭下午九點的火車去
b. 用…,藉…,以…
by hand [machine] 
用手[機器] (制的) 
sell by auction 
以拍賣出售
learn by heart 
默記,背
c. 藉<做…>,以
Let's begin by reviewing the last lesson. 
我們開始 (上課) ,先溫習上一課
We learn by listening. 
我們以聽力訓練法學習
d. 因…
die by poison 
中毒而死
by reason of 
? 由於…,因為…
4 由…,被…
America was discovered by Columbus. 
美洲是由哥倫布發現的
Those locomotives are driven by electricity. 
那些火車頭是電動的
be made [written] by John Smith 
由約翰.史密斯製作 [執筆] 
a novel by Scott 
司各脫 (寫) 的小說
5 
a. 到…時已經,不晚於…,到…時為止 (not laterthan) 
by the end of this month ( 
最遲) 到這個月底
finish by the evening 
到傍晚完成
By the time we reached home, it was quite dark. 
我們回到家時,天已經很黑了
b. 在…時間內,在…期間 (during) 
I work by day and study by night. 
我在日間工作,夜間讀書
He went home by daylight. 
他在天還沒黑時回家了
6 a. 按…,依照…,依據…
It's five o'clock by my watch. 
依照我的表,時間是五點
judge a person by appearances 
以貌取人,根據外表判斷一個人
b. [by the?; 表示單位] 以…為單位,以…計,按…計算
board by the month 
按月包飯 [搭伙] 
sell by the yard [gallon] 
以碼 [加侖] 計價賣
pay a worker by the piece 
按件計酬
by the hundred =by (the) hundreds 
好幾百地,數以百計
He used to read by the hour. 
他從前常常一看書就是好幾個小時
7 a. 至於…程度; 至 (…之多) 
by degrees 
逐漸,漸次
miss by a minute 
遲一分鐘,只差一點而錯過
win by a boat's length 
以一船身之領先獲勝
He is taller than she (is) by five centimeters. 
他比她高五公分
little by little = bit by bit 
一點一點地,逐漸
day by day 
日復一日地
drop by drop 
一滴一滴地
one by one 
逐一
step by step 
一步一步地,逐步
room by room 
逐室,一個房間一個房?a
b. 以…
multiply 8 by 2 
以 2 乘 8
divide 8 by 2 
八除以二
a room (of) 12 ft. by 15 (ft.) 
十二?湛硎

by
[baI; bai]
<<名詞>>
= byeby chance；accidentally；unexpectedly 偶然地；意外地
*Columbus discovered America by accident．哥倫布偶然發現了新大陸。
*I met her by accident in the street．我在街上偶然碰到了她。1．of course；certainly；definitely當然；必定
*I said I would come straight to the point．「By all means，」he replied．我說，我想要直截了當地談。「當然可以，」他回答道。
2．trying every means possible；at all costs 竭力；務必；無論如何
*He will try to get the work done by all means．他會竭盡全力完成那件工作的。
*He felt that he should by all means warn his friend．他感到他無論如何要警告他的朋友。without question 無疑地
*By all odds we should win the game，because the other team is so weak．毫無疑問，我們應該贏這場比賽，因為對方太弱了。soon；before long 不久
*Things are bound to get better by and by．情況不久就會好起來的。
*The boy said he would do his homework by and by．這男孩說他一會兒就做作業。

by and by
不久以後; 不久; 不一會兒
he'll come back by and by 
他不久會回來on the whole；in general 總的說來；大體上說
*By and large，your suggestion is a good one．總的說來，你的建議是好的。
*By and large，you'll live longer if you try to be more easygoing about life．大體上可以說，如果你對待生活能寬容隨和的話，你就會活得長一些。in any way possible 無論用什麼辦法
*He said he would attend the seminar by any means．他說他無論如何也要參加這次學術討論會。by accident；unexpectedly 偶然地；意外地
*It happened by chance．這是偶然發生的。
*The apple fell by chance on Bobby's head．蘋果碰巧掉在鮑比的頭上。compared with 相比較
*This film is a greater success than that one by comparison．相比之下，這部電影比那部更為成功。
*This one is really cheaper by comparison．相比之下，這個確實便宜。during the day 白天
*He works in the factory by day and writes at home by night．他白天在工廠上班，晚上在家寫作。gradually；step by step 逐漸地；慢慢地
*The days are getting colder by degrees．天氣漸漸冷起來了。
*Their friendship grew by degryees into love．他們的友誼逐漸發展為愛情。
*We gained our experience by degrees．我們的經驗是逐漸獲得的。on purpose；as planned 故意地；有意地
*I don't know whether he did it by accident or design．She told me that he did it by design．我不知道他做這事是偶然的還是故意的，她說他是故意的。through；as a result of 通過；用…辦法
*The country boy succeeded by dint of persistent efforts．那個農村孩子經過堅韌不拔的努力而獲得成功。by rapid method of conveyance 快件郵寄
*She sent a letter by express．她用快件寄了一封信。1．evidently；clearly 明顯地
*He is by far the best student in this class．他顯然是這個班裡最優秀的學生。
2．by a large amount or degree；very much 甚為
*Books are by far the most lasting products of human effort．書籍是人類最持久的財富。
*The second half of his voyage was by far the more dangerous part，during which he sailed round the treacherous Cape Horn．這後半航程更為艱險，在此期間，他繞過了險情四伏的合恩角。irregularly；at intervals；without steady application 斷斷續續地；不持久地；無恆心地
*You will never get anywhere if you study just by fits and starts．如果你斷斷續續地學習，你將一事無成。
*He failed to get a fixed job，but went here and there working by fits and starts．他只是斷斷續續地一會兒在這兒干，一會又在那兒干，從沒有一份固定的工作。
*Nothing great can be done by fits and starts．沒有恆心，任何大事都不可能幹出來。compelling；by violent means 強迫；用暴力爭取
*The police took his property by force．警察搶走了他的財產。very 十分地
*He is clever by half．他十分聰明。imcompletely；imperfectly 不完全地；不完善地
*We do nothing by halves．我們做事從不半途而廢。
*He does everything by halves．他做事總是敷衍了事。
*The habit of doing things by halves would make you accomplish nothing all your life．半心半意地做事會使你終身一事無成。1．using one's own hand rather than some form of machinery 手工做的
*The peasants use tractors to pull the plough and milk their cows by hand．農民用拖拉機耕田，用手擠奶。
2．personally 親自
*The letter should be delivered by hand．此信必須由專人送去。by memory 記住；背會
*He can learn 100 new words by heart in one hour．他一小時能背100個單詞。by a land route 由陸路
*「Do you know whether she went to Shanghai by land or sea？」「By land，」he replied．你知道她是由陸路還是海路去上海的？「陸路，」他回答說。with long steps；very rapidly 躍進；突飛猛進
*In recent years our university's enrollments have been going up by leaps and bounds．近年來我們學校的招生一直在猛增。
*He made progress in English by leaps and bounds．他在英語學習上取得了飛快的進步。by a chance procedure 由抽籤決定
*The study groups were divided by lot．學習小組是以抽籤的方式劃分的。with the help of；by using sth．or some method 利用
*He recovered by means of seaair and seabathing．他通過呼吸海邊的空氣和洗海水浴恢復了健康。
*They succeeded by means of perseverance．他們依靠堅持而成功。
*The thief entered the house by means of a ladder．小偷用一個梯子進了房間。unintentionally；as a result of misjudgement or carelessness 錯誤地
*I took his book by mistake．我錯拿了他的書。using name or names 就名字；憑名字
*I still can't call every student in the class by name．我還叫不出這個班每個學生的名字。
*I only know him by name．我只是聽說過他的名字。arising from one's nature 天生地；天性
*He is by nature kind and generous．他是個天生仁慈和寬宏大量的人。
*She is narrowminded by nature．她天生小心眼。
*That man is proud by mature．那人天生驕傲。in no way；not at all；of course not決不
*Our government adheres to the principle that we will by no means be the first to use nuclear weapons．我國政府堅持在任何情況下決不首先使用核武器的原則。
*I am by no means interested in the work．我對這件工作一點也不感興趣。
*He will by no means lend you the money．他決不會把錢借給你的。without help；alone 獨自地；單獨地
*She felt very sad and lonely by herself．她獨自一人感到憂傷寂寞。
*He painted the door by himself．他自己把門漆好了。according to the number of days given to work 按日（計工等）
*They are paid not by the day but by the month．他們是按月而不是按天計酬的。
*The secretary works so hard that her working time can hardly be counted by the day．這位秘書工作十分努力，她的工作時間很難按天數來計算。incidentally；in passing 順便提一下
*By the way，what was she doing when you saw her this morning？順便問一下，你今天上午看見她時她在幹什麼？
*By the way，have you seen Harry recently？順便問一下，你最近見到哈利了嗎？one after another；in order 輪流；按順序
*The two brothers looked after their sick mother by turns．兄弟倆輪流照看生病的母親。
*She was laughing and crying by turns for nearly half an hour．她一會兒哭，一會兒笑，差不多有半個小時。because of；by reason of 因為；由於
*He rose high in society by virtue of his talent and learning．他因其才華和學識而飛黃騰達。
*He was promoted by virtue of his abilities．他憑他的能力而獲得了提升。
*They won the day，but only by virtue of hard fighting．他們完全是靠艱苦奮鬥才獲勝的。1．via 經由
*She went to Canada by way of Shanghai．她經過上海去加拿大。
2．as a kind of；in the way of 當作
*He said something by way of greeting．他說了幾句話表示歡迎。
*I offered her a pair of shoes by way of thanks．我送她一雙鞋以表謝意。
*By way of a present，he sent her a lovely cat and its small house．作為禮物，他送給她一隻可愛的小貓以及它住的小屋。by-
