<<可數名詞>>
1 (美) (裝設在街頭等的) 緊急用電話亭
(聯絡警察局、火災報警用)
2 (英)公共電話亭(tele) phone booth)call button
叫人鈴或警報鈴之按鈕call day
(英)每學期指定學生赴法庭見習之日1．scold；reprimand 斥責某人
*The director called Jim down for being late again．主任訓斥吉姆又來遲了。
*Mother called the child down for walking into the room with muddy shoes．媽媽訓斥這孩子穿著沾滿泥的鞋子走進房間。
2．summon，as from God；ask for祈求（天恩）；使降臨
*The old man called down curses on the head of those who killed his son．老人祈求上帝降禍於那些殺害他兒子的人。
*If you do that，you'll be calling the indignation of the masses down upon yourself．你那樣做，將激起群眾對你的憤慨。1．demand；ask for 要求
*The man sat down and called for some beer．那人坐下來，要了一些啤酒。
*This is a problem that calls for immediate solution．這是個要求立即解決的問題。
2．go to pick up；collect 去接（某人）；去取（某物）
*I'll call for you at eight o'clock．我8點鐘去接你。
*The grocer's boy calls every Monday for orders．雜貨店的服務員每週一來取定貨單。
3．require 需要
*The present situation calls for rapid action by the government．當前的局勢需要政府迅速採取措施。
*Success in school calls for much hard work．在學校的成功需要付出大量的辛勤工作。
*The work calls for endurance and patience．這工作需要忍耐和耐心。1．cause to be seen；be the cause of 喚起；引發
*Trouble can call forth a person's best qualities．逆境能顯示一個人的英雄本色。
*Oppression always calls forth the power of resistance．壓迫總是激起反抗。
2．produce and use；bring into play 產生並使用；發揮
*It was a situation that called forth all his initiative and courage．正是這一形勢使他的積極性和勇氣全部激發出來了。
*You will have to call forth all your energy．你必須全力以赴。call girl
<<可數名詞>>
(用電話聯絡召喚的) 妓女,應召女郎call house
<<可數名詞>>
(美) (介紹應召女郎的) 應召站; 妓女戶1．invite；send for 邀請
*They decided to call in a doctor because the child was not any better．他們決定請個醫生來，因為那孩子一點不見好轉。
2．pay a short visit；call at sb．'s house 拜訪某人的家
*I may call in some time this coming Sunday．Will you be home？我可能這個星期天的某時候來拜訪你，你會在家嗎？
3．ask to come indoors 要…進來
*Call the children in now；it's getting dark outside．外面天快黑了，叫孩子們進來吧。
4．require to be brought in；order the return of 要求歸還
*The library is calling in all outstanding books．圖書館要求歸還所有久借不還的圖書。
*The bank has begun to call its money in．銀行已開始要求償清貸款。call lamp
