(主要為銀行間資金的短期借款,借主可隨時要求支付)use ugly or unkind words when speaking to sb．罵人
*The child was punished by the teacher for calling names．那個小孩因罵人而受到老師的懲罰。call note
(鳥獸) 招呼其配偶或子女之鳴聲call number
<<可數名詞>>
(圖書館圖書的) 編目號碼1．abandon；cancel 取消
*He phoned her and called the appointment off．他打電話給她取消了約會。
*The press conference was called off．記者招待會不舉行了。
2．cause to keep away 叫開
*The dog threatened me until its master called it off．那條狗想咬我，後來主人把它喚開了。
3．divert（one's mind，etc．）；order to stop doing（sth．）把（思想）轉移開；命令…停止做（某事）
*The chief inspector called his men off．檢查官命令他的隨從停止搜查。
*He is engaged in his studies and nothing can call off his attention．他正在專心地學習，什麼事情也不能叫他分心。1．visit sb．formally either socially or on business 拜訪某人
*We'll call on you very shortly．我們不久就會去拜訪你。
*The deputies called upon the mayor to invite his cooperation in their work．代表們拜訪了市長，請他在工作上給予合作。
2．ask；invite；make a demand on；appeal to sb．to do sth．要求；請求；號召
*The government called on the people to practise economy．政府號召人們厲行節約。
*We have to call upon the parents to help us educate the teenagers．我們必須呼籲家長協助我們教育青少年。
*The Chairman called on Mr．Brown to speak at the meeting．主席請求布朗先生在會上發言。call out
插圖各部分之編號

1．shout loudly 大聲叫
*The little boy on the watch started calling out when he saw somebody approaching stealthily．放哨的小男孩看到有人偷偷地走過來，就大聲地叫喊起來。
*Jane called out her boyfriend's name when she saw him across the street．簡隔街看見男朋友時，就大聲喊他。
2．summon away from one's home or place of work 召集；召來；請來
*All the firemen in the city were called out to fight the big fire．城裡所有的消防隊員都被召集來撲滅那場大火。
*Doctors are often called out in the middle of the night．醫生們常常在午夜被請去出診。
3．summon to strike；order or bring into action 號召罷工；喚起或命令…行動
*The trade union officials have called their members out（on strike）．工會號召全員罷工。
*The fire brigade was called out twice yesterday．昨天消防隊出動兩次。call rate
