<<可數名詞>>
借書申請單call the names on a certain list 點名
*The dean usually calls the roll before the meeting begins．系主任通常在開會前點名。cause sb．to remember 使想起
*The film calls to mind what happened in my hometown ten years ago．這部電影使我想起了10年前我家鄉所發生的事情。call to quarters
『軍』 (熄燈號十五分鐘前吹的) 歸營號1．waken 喚醒
*Please call me up at four tomorrow morning．請在明天早晨4點鐘把我喊醒。
2．telephone 給…打電話
*Did anyone call me up while I was out？我不在時有人打電話給我嗎？
*I'll call you up when I need your help．需要你幫助時，我會給你打電話的。
3．order to join the armed forces徵召…入伍
*During the war，all the young people were called up to fight on the battlefield．戰爭期間，所有的年輕人都被徵召參戰。
*He got his callup papers yesterday．他昨天接到徵召入伍通知書。
4．bring to sb．'s mind 想起
*This picture called up memories of our class trip．這張照片使我們想起我們班的那次旅行。
5．summon before an authority；put forward for consideration 傳訊；提出…供考慮
*All the witnesses were called up when the trial began．審訊開始時，所有證人都被傳到庭。
*The design has been called up．這個設計方案已被提出議論過了。Call-A-Mart
