[`karI; ˋkari]
《源自拉丁文「用車運送」的意思》<<及物動詞>>
A
1 運送,搬運
a. (用手或背部) 運送,搬運 <人、東西等> 
Please ~ this trunk for me. 
請你替我搬這個大皮箱
I ran as fast as my legs could ~ me. 
我盡量快跑
This bus carries 90 passengers. 
這輛巴士載著九十名乘客
b. 把<人、物等> [裝載於…] 運送,搬運,帶去[on, in]
~ a box on one's back [shoulder] 
把箱子 [扛] 在背 [肩] 上
~ a stick in one's hand 
手裡拿著一根枴杖
~ a baby in one's arms 
懷裡抱著嬰兒
c. 載運<人>,搬運<物等> (到某處) 
~ a bag upstairs [downstairs] 
把皮箱搬到樓上 [樓下] 
A limousine carried us to the museum. 
一輛小型巴士載我們到博物館
C~ these dirty plates back to the kitchen. 
把這些髒盤子拿回廚房
2 a. 把 <消息、話等> 傳達[給…],傳遞,轉告[to]
Helen carried the news to the class. 
海倫把這消息傳達給班上同學
b. 傳送,傳播 <聲音、疾病等> 
The wind carries sounds. 
風傳送聲音
Some diseases are carried by flies. 
有些疾病是由蒼蠅傳播的
3 <動機、時間等> 使<人>去[…][to]
Business carried him to Milan. 
他因商務去米蘭
4 
a. 延長,使…擴張
The rail line was carried under the Tsugaru Strait (to Hokkaido). 
鐵路線從 (日本的) 津輕海峽下面延伸 (至北海道) 
b. 推進,驅策; 進行 (至某種程度) 
Hard work carried him to the top of his profession. 
勤勞使他躋身於同業中的領導地位
She carries her stinginses to excess. 
她吝嗇得過分
You carried the joke too far. 
你的玩笑開得太過分了
5 a. 貫徹 <主張> ; 使 [議會] 通過 <動議> [through]
~ one's point 
說服別人贊同自己的觀點; 達到目的
~ a bill through Parliament 
使議會通過法案
The motion to adjourn the meeting was carried by seven votes. 
休會的動議以七票贊成通過了
b. <選舉> 獲勝; 使 <候選人> 當選
c. 得到 <選區居民等> 的支持
6 a. 贏得; 攻陷 <要塞等> 
Our troops failed to ~ the enemy's fort. 
我軍未能攻陷敵人的要塞
→ carry the DAY.
b. […]吸引 [感動] <聽眾> [with]
His acting carried the house. 
他的演技博得滿堂的喝采
The lecturer carried his audience with him. 
那位演講者引起了聽眾的共鳴
71．take something away；remove帶走；沖走
*The flood has carried away the bridge．洪水把橋沖走了。
2．excite；cause to lose self control使…著迷，使…失去自製
*Take your time and think carefully－don't get carried away．別著急，仔細想想，不要鬼迷心竅。
*Don't be carried away by success．不要被勝利沖昏頭腦。
*The whole crowd were quite carried away by the young singer's performance．那位青年歌手的演唱深深地打動了所有的聽眾。
*The scenic beauty has carried her away．美景使她陶醉了。carry bag
<<名詞>>
(美)= SHOPPING bag1．be advanced 被推動；發揚
*We should carry forward the fine revolutionary tradition of plain living and hard struggle．我們應該發揚艱苦奮鬥的優良傳統。
2．pass forward to a new balance sheet 將帳目結轉次欄
*The money was carried forward to the next month．這筆錢被轉至下月帳上。1．take by force 搶走；拐走
*Thieves carried off the farmer's sheep during the night．小偷在夜裡劫走了那個農民的羊。
*The gerrillas broke into the armoury，and carried off 22 rifles．游擊隊衝進了武器庫，奪走了22支步槍。
2．perform；execute 進行；扮演
*The piano piece is difficult to carry off．這首鋼琴曲不容易演奏。
3．win；succeed in winning 贏；獲得
*He was a great success at school，and carried off all the prizes．他在學校成績突出，各種獎品都讓他拿到了。
*His horse carried off the first prize at the race．他的馬在比賽中獲得頭獎。
*I think he will manage to carry off the honours．我認為他能爭取到這種榮譽。
4．kill；cause the death of 殺害；造成…的死亡
*She was carried off by a heart attack．她因心臟病突發而死。
5．deal with successfull or easily成功地應付；巧妙地對付
*It was an embarrassing situation，but they carried it off well．這是一個尷尬的場面，但是他們成功地應付過去了。
*I think she carried it off well，considering her age．按她的年齡，我覺得她應付得很不錯了。1．continue；maintain 繼續；保持
*We must try to carry on our work in spite of difficulties．我們必須不顧困難，把工作繼續下去。
*I expect my son to carry on the family tradition．我希望我兒子能保持家庭傳統。
2．conduct（a business，a conversation，etc．）；follow 經營；進行（生意、談話等）
*The two cities have been carrying on trade for years．這兩個城市進行貿易已經多年了。
*It is difficult to carry on a conversation with all this noise around us．周圍很吵鬧，要在這裡談話很困難。
3．behave in an excited or anxious manner；behave wildly 吵吵鬧鬧；行動失常；惡作劇
*The children have been carrying on all morning．孩子們整個上午都在鬧著玩。fulfil；accomplish；perform 實行；履行
*He carried out the plan without difficulty．他毫無困難地實施了那項計劃。
*It is often easier to make plans than to carry them out．常常是訂計劃容易，執行計劃難。
*I expect her to carry out her obligations．我期待她履行她的義務。1．move to a later date 延期
*The concert will have to be carried over till next week because the singer is ill．因歌唱演員生病，音樂會不得不推延到下周舉行。
2．last；carry forward（continue in another place or time）延續；在另一地方或另一時間繼續下去
*The habit carries over from his childhood．這種習慣是從他童年時代延續下來的。
*The writing carries over on to the next page．這篇作品轉接下頁。
*Would you please carry the report over on to another page？請把報告續到另一頁紙上好嗎？
3．transport from one place to another；transfer… from one column，page，or book to another 從一地運到另一地；把…轉到（次欄、頁、冊上）
*Tobacco was carried over from the West to China．煙草是從西方傳入中國的。
*He carried the money over to the next month．他把錢過到下月份。
4．win to one's side 把…爭取到自己這邊來
*We did our best to carry him over and at last succeeded．我們盡力爭取他，終於成功了。1．complete in spite of difficulties（努力）完成
*He is determined to carry all his plans through．他決心完成所有的計劃。
2．help survive；continue to the end 使度過困難；支持到底
*Only his courage carried him through．是勇氣使他度過了難關。
*Perseverance will carry a man through．毅力能使人克服種種困難。car.ry-back
