*The prisoner is casting about for a way of escape．那個囚徒正急著找逃路。discard；throw away 置…而不顧；拋棄；去掉
*You can't just cast people aside like old clothes．你不能像拋棄舊衣服那樣扔下別人不管。
*Cast aside all illusions and go into the battle．丟掉幻想，投入戰鬥。1．throw away 丟掉
*They cast away the equipment they would not need．他們扔掉了他們不再需要的設備。
*He cast away an advantage．他失去了優勢。
2．wreck（a ship）（船）遇難；使（船）失事（常用被動語態）
*The new ship was cast away during the storm．這條新船在暴風雨中沉沒。
*A good many ships have been cast away in the Arctic Ocean．在北冰洋，曾有許多船隻失事。look back；direct to the past 回顧；回憶
*We cast back to our working together on the army farm in the Northeast．我們回憶起我們一道在東北軍墾農場勞動的情景。
*He cast back his mind to the earlier days．他回憶起先前的日子。
*They cast their thoughts back to happier times．他們回想起較為快樂的日子。1．demoralize；discourage；be lower in spirits 沮喪；洩氣；氣餒（常用於被動結構或作表語）
*The proud will be cast down．驕者必敗。
*In making scientific experiments，we should not be cast down by temporary setbacks．進行科學實驗時，我們不要因暫時挫折而垂頭喪氣。
*She was cast down at the news of her aunt's death．聽到她姑媽去世的消息，她情緒很低。
2．throw down；lower 放低；使放下
*She cast her eyes down shyly．她羞怯地垂下目光。cast iron
<<不可數名詞>>
鑄鐵cast net
<<可數名詞>>
撒網drive out；expel 趕出；逐出
*The members of the association did not like his behaviour，so they cast him out．協會會員們不喜歡他的行為，所以就把他開除了。
*He was cast out from our country．他被驅逐出我們國家。
*Having repeatedly broken the rules of the game，they were both cast out from the football club．他們兩人踢足球時經常犯規，已被開除出足球俱樂部。cast steel
<<不可數名詞>>
鑄鋼1．add up；calculate 加起來；計算
*The accounts have to be cast up at the end of each day．每天工作結束時，必須結賬。
*He tried to cast up the whole complicated thing．他盡力盤算這件複雜的事情。
2．refer to constantly in reproach一再埋怨地提起；以責備的口吻常常提起
*She's been casting that up at me all the time．她為了那件事老是埋怨我。
*He always casts up at her the fact that she crashed the car．他總是責備她弄壞了汽車。cast-off
