*Dry grass catches fire easily．乾草容易著火。catch meadow
利用山坡上泉水或小溪灌溉的草地1．become popular；be done or used by many people 流行；受歡迎；被很多人接受
*This novel caught on well．這本小說深受歡迎。
*It's a nice tune and will catch on quickly．這首曲子很好，不久就會流行開來。
*If only the idea could catch on，we should be able to make quite a lot of money out of it．但願這個主意被採納，那麼我們就能從中賺一大筆錢。
2．finally understand；grasp the point of 理解；明白；領會
*After two hours of trying to learn the new game，he caught on．這種遊戲，他學了兩小時才明白是怎麼回事。
*He didn't catch on to what you had implied．他沒有理解你話中隱含的意思。
*The lady repeated her question several times but I still couldn't catch on．那位女士把她的問題重複了好幾遍，但是我還是沒聽懂。
3．fasten accidentally on；catch；grab 掛住；抓住
*My coat caught on a mail and tore．我的上衣掛住了一根釘子，撕破
*The girl kept catching on to her mother's hand．這個小女孩一直抓住她媽媽的手。1．breathe in suddenly with fear or surprise；rest and get back normal breathing 因恐懼或興奮而屏住呼吸；喘氣以恢復正常呼吸
*The story is full of surprises which cause the reader to catch his breath．這個故事充滿了驚險情節，使讀者緊張得透不過氣來。
*After running to the bus stop we sat down to catch our breath．我們跑到車站後坐下來喘氣。
2．relax for a moment 放鬆一下
*After a day's work they sat down over tea to catch their breath．工作一天後，他們坐下來喝茶放鬆一下。catch phrase
亦作catchphrase
(廣告等的) 標語; 引為標語的短句;catch pit
集水溝attract sb．'s attention 引人注目
*The dress in the window caught her eye when she passed the store，櫥窗裡的服裝吸引了她。see for a moment；get a glimpse of看見；發現
*I caught sight of her getting on the bus when I came out of the bookstore．我從書店出來時看見她上了公共汽車。catch stitch
1 (在縫紡織品的邊時使用的) 十字針法
2 以大針斜縫1．succeed in pursuing；overtake；follow and finally reach 趕上；追上
*You'd better drive faster，beacuse the others are catching up quickly．你最好快點開，別人很快就會趕上來。
*You go on ahead；I'll catch you up in a few minutes．你前面走，我將在幾分鐘內趕上。
*There was a tenmile chase before the thieves were caught up by the police car．追了10英里，警察的車子才趕上盜竊犯。
2．seize hurriedly；take or pick up suddenly；be dragged into 突然拿起；匆忙抓住；被抱進
*He caught up the ball as it rolled along and threw it back．當球向前滾動時，他急忙抓了起來就向後投去。
*He caught up a stick and struck out at that man．他急忙抓起一根木棍向那人打去。
3．capture or trap … in a situation；concern or interest very much 俘獲；捲進；非常關心或極感興趣（常與in連用在被動結構中）
*His clothing was caught up in the machine．他的衣服被捲進了機器中。
*He regretted having been caught up in the affair．他後悔當初捲進了這件事。
*I was so caught up in the movie that I forgot the time．我對這部電影入了迷，以至於連時間都忘了。
4．adopt 採用；借用
*These phrases were caught up and immediately became popular．這些短語已被採用而且很快就流行了。
5．provide with the latest information 提供…最新消息
*They caught us up on what's happening at the front．他們把前線的最新消息告訴了我們。
6．follow and understand 聽懂； 理解
*They can't catch up what the foreign guest said．他們聽不懂外賓講的話。1．come level with；overtake 趕上
*We have a long way to go to catch up with the advanced countries．要趕上先進國家，我們還有漫長的路要走。
*He is working hard to catch up to the others after missing a month．缺席了一個月後，他在努力趕上別人。
2．have the expected ill effect or result on；arrest 對…產生預期的壞影響和結果；逮捕
*Excessive drinking and smoking will catch up on you．過度地抽煙喝酒，將會給你帶來惡果。
*The thieves had gone ten miles before the police caught up with them．竊賊跑了10里之後警察才抓住他。Catch-22
