*Please check off these lists again．請把這些清單再核對一下。
*She checked off the names she wanted to invite。她在要邀請的人員名字上做了記號。
*Please check off these parcels before they are despatched．在發送這些包裹前請打上查訖記號。
2．go off duty 下班
*We check off at six p．m．daily．我們每天下午6點下班。
3．deduct（union dues）from a worker's paycheck 從工資中扣除（工會費）
*My dues were checked off every month．我的工會費每月從工資中扣除。inspect；verify 核實；檢查
*We'd better check on this story before we print it．在印刷之前我們最好把這個情況核實一下。
*We'll check on the plane before it leaves．飛機起飛前我們要進行檢查。1．pay the bill and leave 結帳離開
*Guests must check out before noon，or they will be charged for the day．客人必須在中午前結帳離開，否則將付全日費用。
*We headed directly for the airport after we have checked out of the hotel．我們付了旅館費以後，就直接去飛機場了。
2．confirm by carefully checking檢驗無誤；核實
*Would you check out these names and numbers，please？請檢驗一下姓名和號碼好嗎？
*The accountant checked out the bills and found them OK．會計查對了帳單，發現正確無誤。
*Please check out each room to see if it is fit for a guest．請檢查每個房間看看是否適合客人住。
3．leave；resign；assist departure of 離開；離職；辭職；幫助…離開
*When he checked out，I was appointed his successor．他離職後，我被指定去接替他。
*They were checked out two hours ago．兩小時前，有人幫助他們離開了。
*The airline has checked their luggage out．航空公司已給他們辦了行李托運。
4．give or lend and make a record of it 發給或借出並登記
*I checked out this book from the library in the morning．我今天早上在圖書館借了這本書。
*The boss checked out the tools to the workmen as they came to work．工人們來上班時，老闆把工具發給他們並作了登記。
5．die 死
*I'm afraid he's just checked out．恐怕他剛剛去世。inspect carefully 仔細檢查
*He checked over the names on the list to ensure that everything was correct．他仔細檢查了名單上的姓名，以便確認一切準確無誤。
*Please check over the plane before it leaves．起飛前請檢查飛機。
*Check your test paper over again．再仔細檢查一下你的考卷。check to bearer
