chime in
(1) 配合,加入 (唱歌等) 
(2)<事物>調和,一致[with]
His views ~d in with mine. 
他的想法和我的一致
(3) 在談話中插嘴 [附和] [with]
(4) 同意 [某人、話等] [with]
(5) 隨聲附和
"Of course, "he ~d in. 
他隨聲附和說「當然」chime hoop
桶凸出處或口邊之箍1．join in singing 跟著唱起來
*The singer asked the audience to chime in．這位歌手請大家跟著一起唱。
*The whole group chimed in on the chorus．全組的人都參加合唱。
2．express agreement；break into a conversation同意；插話
*He was so interested in our discussion that he chimed in from time to time．他對我們的討論非常感興趣，不時地插話。
*I thought you'd chime in．我想你會同意的。harmonize with；agree；go well together與…符合一致；附和
*You should have your own viewpoint．Don't always chime in with others'opinion．你應該有你自己的觀點，不要附和別人的意見。
*I think your plans will chime in with mine．我想你的計劃會同我的一致。
*When father suggested going to the beach for the vacation，the whole family chimed in with the idea．當父親提議去海濱度假時，全家欣然同意。harmonize with；chime in with與…協調一致
*The holiday music should chime with our feelings．假日音樂應該和我們的心情和諧一致。
*Those blue curtains will chime with the carpet．這些藍色的窗簾會同地毯的顏色協調。chi.me.ra
