1 健康證明書
2 『俗』某團體或個人經調查後,被確認無不道德行為而適於擔任公職1．tidy or clean thoroughly；get rid of使潔淨；清除
*She asked the children to clean out their drawers．她要孩子們把抽屜清理乾淨。
2．render bankrupt；leave sb．without money 使破產；使…失去錢財
*He hasn't got a penny．He is quite cleaned out．他一文不名，完全破產了。
*We played cards and he cleaned me out．我們玩了紙牌，他把我的錢全贏去了。clean room
(經過徹底消毒以進行實驗工作之) 絕對清潔室1．clean thoroughly 打掃乾淨；整理
*She had to clean up the room after the children's party．孩子們的晚會結束後，她要把房間收拾一下。
*They are cleaning up the mess．他們在打掃這堆亂七八糟的東西。
2．wash and make oneself presentable梳洗；打扮
*She often spends a lot of timecleaning herself up every morning．她每天早上往往要花大量時間梳洗打扮。
3．make a lot of money賺大錢
*His friend has cleaned up in the stock market．他的朋友在股市上賺了一大筆錢。
*The company cleaned up in real estate．這家公司做房地產生意賺了很多錢。
4．eliminate（enemy forces，etc．）；root out（a social evil，etc．）消滅（敵軍等）；根除（社會弊端等）
*Leave a few men behind to clean up the last of the enemy positions．留下一些士兵來摧毀敵人的最後陣地。
*So long as capitalism exists，corruption can never be cleaned up．只要資本主義存在，貪污現象就不可能消除乾淨。
*The mayor has decided to clean up the city．市長已下決心整頓市容。clean-cut
