他 (向我) 透露他是如何做那事的
2 (信任地) 將 <某物、人> 委託[給…],托付[to]
The children were ~d to the care of a neighbor. 
那些小孩委託給一位鄰居照顧1．trust；believe in相信
*You can confide in me，my dear．Your affair will be kept private．你可以信任我，親愛的，你的事情我會保密的。
*Why should I not confide in those that have been so kind to me？為什麼我不該信賴那些一直待我這樣好的人呢？
*I confided in your good judgement．我堅信你有良好的判斷力。
*Do you confide in my ability to finish the work on time？你相信我有按時完成工作的能力嗎？
2．share secrets and intimate matters with 向…吐露秘密；講心裡話
*Her heart was breaking，and she had no one to confide in．她傷心欲絕，而且又沒有人可以傾訴。
*Modern girls seldom confide in their mother．現代女孩子很少向母親吐露心事。1．give to the care of托…照管；委託
*He confided his child to the care of his neighbour．他把他孩子托鄰居照看。
*You'd better confide your jewels to the bank．你最好把珠寶托銀行代管。
2．tell as a secret；tell secrets to吐露（秘密）
*She confided her secret to her best friend．她把秘密告訴了最親密的朋友。con.fi.dence
