5(C)『棒球』 (打擊者的) 好壞球的報數be worth；be of importance 有價值；有重要性
*He seems to count for quite a lot in the firm．他在公司內似乎舉足輕重。
*In our factory，quality counts for as much as quantity．在我們廠裡，質量和數量同等重要。
*The dam project counted for much in promoting agricultural production in our county．這個水壩工程對發展我縣農業生產起很大作用。include 包括
*If you are going out for a picnic，please count me in．如果你們出去野餐的話，請把我也算進去。
*Have you counted in those who are absent？你把缺席的人也算進去了嗎？count noun
<<名詞>>
= countable1．count aloud from one end of a line of men to the other 報數
*The soldiers counted off from right to left．戰士們從右向左報數。
*Count off！（口令）報數！
2．select 挑選
*He counted off three men to help with the job．他選出了3個人來幫助做這件事。depend on；trust 依靠；信賴
*You can count on Mr．Li．He will never fail you．你可以依靠李先生，他決不會讓你失望的。
*The team was counting on me to win the race．運動隊指望我贏這場賽跑。
*Don't count on going abroad this summer；we may not have enough money．別指望今年夏天能出國，我們可能錢不夠。1．count one by one 一個一個地數出（數目）
*The boss is counting out his money．老闆正在數錢。
*The old lady counted out fifteen penceand passed it to the salesgirl．那老太太慢吞吞地數了15便士給女店員。
2．exclude 排除
*You can count me out of your plan．你們的計劃可以不把我包括進去。count palatine
