within cry (of?) 
在聽得見 (…) 叫聲的地方1．silence sb．by shouting 大聲喊以使…靜下來
*Before he was halfway through his speech，the crowd cried him down．他才講到一半，公眾就把他哄下了台。
2．depreciate 貶低
*The critic cried down the book．那位評論家貶低那本書。
*He cried down everyone except the rich and the powerful．除了有錢有勢的人，他什麼人都瞧不起。1．express a desire for by weeping or shouting 哭著要；嚷著
*The child is crying for some more sweets．那孩子哭著要再吃一些糖果。
*The strikers cried for a raise of pay．罷工者叫喊著要求增加工資。
2．need very much；be in pressing need of 急需；要求
*The crops are crying for rain．莊稼急需雨水。
*The housing problem in this citycried for immediate solution．該城市的住房問題急待解決。call off；withdraw from（an agreement or undertaking）取消；撤回（協議或任務）
*I had intended to go but I cried off at the last minute．我本來要去的，但是最後一分鐘打消了這個念頭。
*He cried off this research project and left his friends in great difficulty．他撒手不管這個研究項目，使他的朋友們陷入困境。
*John was going to help us，but he cried off．約翰本來要幫助我們的，但是他沒有履行諾言。1．shout loudly 大聲喊叫
*When the boys and girls saw so many yellow handkerchiefs，they cried out with delight．當男孩女孩看見這麼多黃手帕時，他們高興地喊了起來。
*The wounded soldier cried out in pain．傷兵痛苦地喊叫著。
2．be in great need 急需（後接動詞不定式）
*The car is crying out to be repaired．這部車子急待維修。
*The business is just crying out for some capital．這筆生意正急需本錢。complain loudly；protest strongly大聲抱怨；強烈抗議
*The workers are crying out against their being maltreated by the factory owner．工人們強烈抗議工廠的老闆對他們的虐待。
*Many people are crying out against the new rule．許多人正在強烈抗議這項新的規則。
*The people are crying out against this injustice．人民正在大聲疾呼反對這不公正的行為。weep because of；grieve about 因…而哭泣；因…感到悲痛
*The man was crying over his misfortune．那人為自己的不幸而哭泣。
*Don't cry over spilt milk．不要作無益的後悔。cry.baby
