12 『紙牌戲』
a. 將 <一組牌> 分成兩部分 (以上)give a good impression of；make oneself conspicuous in the hope of being admired 出風頭；炫耀
*Shouting and waving，he cut a figure at the head of the procession．他走在隊伍前頭，又是喊叫，又是招手，出盡了風頭。1．go a short way；take a short cut across 走捷徑；抄近路穿過
*They didn't want to walk to the corner and turn，so they cut across the lane to the bus stop．他們不想走到街道的拐角處拐彎而是穿過小巷到了汽車站。
*We can gain time if we cut across this field．如果我們抄近路從這田野橫穿過去，就可以贏得時間。
2．interrupt 打斷
*Her loud voice cut across their conversation．她的高嗓門打斷了我們的談話。
3．contradict；be opposite to 跟…相牴觸；與…背道而馳
*The chairman's decision cuts across the opinion of the whole committee．主席的決定與委員會全體成員的意見背道而馳。
*I don't wish to press my suggestion if it woulh cut across anything you have in mind．如果我的建議違背你的想法的話，我不打算強迫你接受。1．return quickly 迅速返回
*He cut back through the woods to where he had been standing before．他急速穿過樹林回到原先一直站立的地方。
*The wounded soldier recovered and cut back to his unit．這位傷兵養好了傷，很快就歸隊了。
2．make shorter by cutting 剪短
*The tailor cut the cloth back．裁縫把布剪短了。
*We have cut the roses back in order to improve their growth．為了使玫瑰長得更好，我們已經修剪了枝幹。
3．reduce in quantity or amount 削減；壓縮
*The only way to do that is to cut back expenses．做到這一點的唯一辦法就是減少開支。
*After the big job was finished，the builder cut back the number of men working for him．那項大工程完工之後，建築商便裁減了工人的人數。1．make sth．fall by cutting 砍倒
*Many big trees along the road have been cut down for building houses．路旁的許多大樹都被砍掉建房了。
2．reduce；lessen 削減；降低
*This factory's production has been cut down．這家工廠的生產減少了。
*Strenuous efforts have been made to cut down government expenses to a desirable level．政府已盡力把開支削減到了一個理想的水平。
*In the end，I cut the dealer down by another＄ 5.00．最後我使商販把價格又減少了5美元。
*The workers are doing all they can to cut down the accident rate．工人們正在盡一切努力降低事故率。
3．deprive of life or health（by disease，etc．）因疾病等奪去生命
*The man was cut down in his primeof manhood by a pneumonia．那人因患肺炎而英年早逝。
4．destroy（an argument）駁倒
*His arguments are very easy to cut down．他的論點很容易被駁倒。
*He was so eloquent that he cut down the finest orator．他非常能言善辯，駁倒了最好的演說家。
5．reduce the size of（clothes，etc．）改小或縮短（衣服等）
*The tailor is cutting down my dress．裁縫正在把我的衣服改小。cut back on；reduce 減少；削減
*The doctor asked him to cut down on smoking．醫生叫他少抽煙。
*You must cut down on the amount of carbohydrates you eat if you want to get slim．如果你想變得苗條，必須減少你的吃糖量。cut glass
<<不可數名詞>>
雕花玻璃 (器具)1．interrupt；intervene；interpose插嘴（後不帶賓語）；干涉；插入
*She always cuts in when other people are talking．別人談話時她總要插嘴。
*The telephone operator cut in and said that I had already spoken 3minutes．總機插話說我已經通了3分鐘的話了。
*I think I ought to cut in on what they are doing．我想我應該干預他們的事。
*He was stopped when he tried to cut in on the queue．他想插隊時被人阻止了。
2．enter sharply into the path of another 超車；搶先
*We were driving peacefully along the road when a police car cut in，forcing us to slow down．我們的車子在平穩地向前行駛，突然一輛警車超了上來，迫使我們減慢了速度。
*Accidents are often caused by drivers who try to cut in．司機超車搶先常常造成意外事故。
*The police car cut in ahead of the escaping robber．警車攔截了那個逃跑的強盜。
3．include；absorb 包括；吸收
*I would like to be cut in on this project．我想加入這個項目。
*「If you contribute ＄ 1，000，we'll cut you in，」the chairman of the charity committee said to Mrs．Robinson．「如果你捐助1000美元，我們就吸收你入會。」慈善委員會主席對魯濱遜太太說。1．interrupt sth．（such as conversation）打斷；插嘴
*She didn't cut into the conversation but waited till they had finished speaking．她並沒有打斷他們的談話而是一直等到他們談完為止。
*It is impolite of you to cut into the discussion in this way．你這樣打斷別人的討論是不禮貌的。
2．reduce；use part of（sth．such as money，time）unwillingly from減少；很不樂意地從…用去一部分（如錢、時間）
*「But that would cut into cut into our profit，」he said．他說：「那樣會減少我們的利潤。」
*No doubt the extra work to be assigned you will cut into your sparetime．毫無疑問，安排給你的額外工作將會減少你的業餘時間。
*This plan of yours cuts into our schedule rather badly．你們的這個計劃在我們的日程表裡佔去很多時間。
*I shall have to cut into my savings to pay for the holiday．我將不得不從我的儲蓄裡拿出一部分錢來作為假期裡的開支。cut man
1 (美)拳賽助手
(拳賽各回合之間替拳擊手治傷之人)
2 負責廣告及版面設計之新聞從業員1．disconnect（the supply of water or electricity）；interrupt；turn off切斷（水、電）；中斷；關掉
*Their water supply was cut off．他們的水源被切斷了。
*All communications are cut off．一切交通都被切斷了。
*The telephone operator cut us off before we had finished our conversation．我們還沒有談完，電話就被總機接線員切斷了。
*The chairman will cut a speaker off if he talks too long．如果發言人講得太長，主席會打斷他的發言。
*The motor was cut off as soon as something seemed to be wrong with it．一旦發現發動機似乎有點毛病，就立即把它關掉。
2．remove by cutting the ends 切下來；剪下來
*They cut off the heads of their captives．他們把俘虜的頭砍了下來。
*The rope is two feet longer than we needed，so we cut off the extra length．繩子比我們需要的長兩英尺，因此我們把多餘的給剪下來了。
3．isolate；make lonely 孤立
*The enemy soldiers were cut off from their headquarters．敵軍同總部的聯繫被切斷，成了孤軍。
*The flood cut the villagers from the rest of the world．洪水切斷了村民們與外界的聯繫。
4．disinherit 剝奪繼承權
*He has cut his son off without a penny．他取消了兒子的繼承權，一便士也不給。1．remove by cutting 剪下；剪裁
*She cut out the photograph from the paper．她從報紙上把照片剪了下來。
*The affected tissue was cut out from his leg．他腿部有病的組織被切除了。
2．miss out；omit 刪除
*You'd better cut out that sentence．你最好把那個句子刪掉。
*Let's cut out the unimportant details．我們把不重要的細節刪掉吧。
3．refrain from；stop doing sth．戒掉；停止
*He has decided to cut out smoking and drinking．他已經決定戒掉煙酒。
4．outrival；replace 勝過；取代；把…排擠掉
*The new supermarket will cut all the small shops out．這家新超級市場將會把這些小店全都擠垮。
*He has managed to cut out his rival and marry the girl．他終於擠掉了競爭者而娶了那個姑娘。
5．stop operating suddenly and unexpectedly 出乎預料地突然停止運轉
*As our engine suddenly cut out in the way we had to walk．因為發動機在半路上突然出了毛病，我們只好下車步行。
6．shape sth．by cutting 裁剪
*The tailor cut out my coat very well．裁縫把我的上衣裁得很好。be naturally wellsuited for；have talent for；fit for 天生地適合做；有…的天才
*I doubt whether John is cut out for a doctor．我懷疑約翰是否適合當醫生。
*I think she's cut out to be a nurse．我認為她適合當護士。
*I'm sure he'd make a good journalist；he seems to be cut out for the job．我相信他會成為一個出色的新聞記者，他似乎有這方面的天才。1．stop or interrupt suddenly 突然停止
*Their conversation was cut short by the telephone ringing．他們的談話被電話鈴聲打斷了。
*He was about to go on talking when his mother cut him short．他正要繼續講下去，他媽媽打斷了他。
2．make shorter 停止；縮短
*We'll have to cut our visit short，as we want to get back before dark．我們必須縮短訪問時間，因為天黑前還得趕回去。
*His life was cut short by cancer．癌症過早地結束了他的生命。
*If you anything more to say，please cut it short as your time is nearly up．如果你還有什麼要說的話，請簡短一些，因為你的時間已經快到了。
*I'll cut a long story short．我就長話短說吧。cut time
『音』= alla breve1．cut into small pieces 切碎
*Please cut the apple up into equal pieces．請把蘋果切成大小相同的塊。
*The cook was cutting up the meat for making jiaozi．廚師正在切肉包餃子。
*The tailor cut up a large piece of cloth to make one shirt for me and two for my son．裁縫把一大塊布裁開給我做一件襯衣，給我兒子做兩件。
2．wound 受傷
*Her face was badly cut up in the car crash．她的面部在車禍中嚴重受傷。
3．cause suffering to hurt the feeling of；upset 使痛心；使難過
*She was very cut up about her father's death．她父親的去世使她悲痛萬分。
*The boy was badly cut up when his girlfriend gave him back his ring．當女朋友還給他戒指時，這男孩非常傷心。
*There is no need to be so cut up at not succeeding this time．不必因這次沒成功就這樣難過。
*This news has cut him up．這消息使他心煩意亂。
4．attack；criticize 攻擊；批評
*His book was severely cut up by the critics．他的書遭到評論家的嚴厲批評。
5．behave in a comic，boisterous or unruly manner 行為滑稽；吵吵鬧鬧；不守規矩
*The boys cut up when the old folks were away．大人一走開，孩子們就開始胡鬧起來。
*At the party they cut up and broke the chairs．他們在晚會上胡鬧並把椅子弄壞了。
6．destroy or severely damage 嚴重破壞；毀壞；受傷
*The machine guns cut up the enemy like knives．機關鎗象刀子一樣切入敵軍心臟摧毀了敵軍。cut-and.dried
