《源自拉丁文「下降」的意思》<<不及物動詞>>
1 
a. (由高處) 下來,下降
( 
←→ ascend) 
He ~ed from the top of the mountain. 
他從山頂下來
The sunlight ~ed from the sky. 
陽光從天空射下
The stream ~ed to the sea. 
這條溪水流注入1．go or come down from 從…下來；傳下來；遺傳
*He descended from the tower．他從塔上下來。
*The ring has descended from her grandmother．這枚戒指是她祖母傳下來的。
*The sword descends from the Tang dynasty．這把劍是從唐朝傳下來的。
2．have one's family origin in；originate from 是…的後裔
*He claimed to have descended from the royal family．他自稱是王族之後。
*According to the Bible，we have all descended from Adam．按照《聖經》上的說法，我們都是亞當的後裔。attack suddenly；visit unexpectedly 突然拜訪；突然襲擊
*Thieves descended on the travellers and took their money．盜賊出其不意地襲擊旅行者，搶走了他們的錢。
*The enemy descended upon the village at midnight．敵人在午夜突然襲擊了這個小村莊。
*My two old friends descended on me at Christmas．我的兩個老朋友在聖誕節突然來看望我。de.scen.dant
