<<名詞>>
1 (C)(口語)
a. 戳,刺,撞
give a person a ~ in the ribs 
戲戳一下某人的肋骨 [側腹] 
b. 挖苦,諷刺
have [take] a ~ at a person 
挖苦某人
That's a ~ at me. 
那是在挖苦我
2 (C)
a. 挖,掘
b. (考古學上的) 挖掘 (工作) ; 挖掘 (中的) 現場; 發掘物
3 [~s; 常當單數用] (英口語)學生宿舍,寄宿舍1．work hard；begin to work 勤勉工作；努力幹；開始幹起來
*My son dug in and finished his homework very quickly．我兒子很認真，很快就把家庭作業做完了。
*If you expect to finish all this work in two hours，you'd better dig in．如果你想在兩小時之內完成這項工作，就得馬上幹起來。
2． begin eating with appetite津津有味地開始吃起來
*The boys dug in ravenously．男孩們開始狼吞虎嚥地吃起來。
*Dinner's ready．Dig in， everybody！晚餐已準備好了，大家吃吧！
3．protect oneself by digging a trench，etc．； cover by digging挖壕溝等以藏身；把…埋在土裡
*The company commander ordered his soldiers to dig themselves in．連長命令戰士們挖戰壕，以便掩蔽。
*The soldiers have dug in along the river．士兵們沿河邊挖了戰壕。
*Dig this chemical in and crops will grow faster．把這化肥埋進土壤裡，莊稼就會長得更快。
4．establish oneself firmly in a position，etc．鞏固自己的地位等
*He has been working in this department for ten years and he's pretty well dug himself in．他在這個系工作已經10年了，已經站穩了腳跟。
5．stick to one's own idea堅持自己的意見
*When facts have shown that you are mistaken，you mustn't dig in．當事實已經證明你錯了，你就不應該再堅持自己的意見。1．eat heartily； eat with appetite 痛快地吃；大吃
*They were so hungry that as soon as supper was served，they dug into it hungrily．他們餓極了，晚飯一端上桌，他們就狼吞虎嚥地大吃起來。
2．delve into；investigate thoroughly努力鑽研；徹底調查研究
*When he digs into a problem he does not give up until he gets to the bottom．他要是鑽研一個問題，就非弄個水落石出不可。
*The detectives are digging into this whole business．偵探們正在徹底地調查整個事件。
*He is digging into Chinese history．他正研究中國歷史。
3．apply oneself to集中精力做；全力以赴地干
*They dug into their work with a will．他們全力以赴地工作。
4．make inroads on（savings，etc．）侵佔；動用（積蓄等）
*They were forced to dig into savings to pay their current debts．他們被迫動用存款償付債務。1．remove by digging；discover by digging挖走；發掘出
*The gardener dug out the weeds．園林工人剷除了雜草。
*They are digging out a large ancient tomb．他們正在發掘一座古墓。
2．make bg digging挖；掘成
*They are digging out a tunnel．他們正在挖一條地道。
3．release； rescue by digging通過挖掘救出
*He was buried under the avalanche and had to be dug out．他被埋在雪堆中，必須把他救出來。
*The rescuers managed to dig out the trapped miners．救護人員設法挖出了困在礦下的工人。
*Some people are still being dug out of the ruins of the building．人們仍在挖掘壓在建築物廢墟裡的一些人。
4．find out；obtain發現；取得
*Through investigation they have dug out all the facts．通過調查，他們已弄清了所有事實。
*Where on earth did yod dig out these old clothes？你究意是從哪兒翻到這些舊衣服的？1．bring to light by digging what has been buried or hidden因挖掘而發現
*An old Greek statue was dug up here last month．上個月這裡挖出了一座古希臘雕像。
*The archaeologists have dug up a remarkable collection of historical relics．考古工作者發掘出一大批歷史文物。
*These relics were dug up last year．這些文物是去年出土的。
2．make a money contribution出錢
*We all dug up to keep the poor on relief last month．上個月我們大家都出錢救濟窮人。
3．find or get sth． with some effort發現；找到
*The girl dug up some useful material for her English composition．這女孩為寫她的英文作文找到了一些有用的資料。
*The newspaper loves to dig up scandals．報紙喜歡揭露醜聞。
*He always manages to dig up a fresh excuse for being late．他總能為他的遲到找到這樣那樣的新借口。
4．break up（land）by digging；remove from the ground by digging 翻土；自地上挖掉
*They are digging up land for a new garden．他們正在翻土建一個新花園。
*They want to dig these trees up to make the street wider．他們想把這些樹挖掉拓寬街道。di.gal.lic acid
