a. 照料<客人>
I'll do you now, sir. [. 
在理髮廳等] 我現在要 照料您 [為您理發] 了,先生
b. 為<某人>服務 (周到) ,招待<某人> (很好) 
(cf. DO by) 
They do you very well at that hotel. 
那家旅館服務很周到
c. [~ oneself; 與 well 等連用] 奢侈
He does himself fairly well. 
他相當奢侈
7 
a. 演…的角色
He did Hamlet well. 
他把哈姆雷特的角色演得很好
She always does the hostess admirably [very well]. 
她是個令人讚賞的女主人,待客和藹可親
b. 裝得 <像…> ,假裝; 模仿 <…的樣子> 
do a1．abolish；get rid of；put an end to廢除；去掉
*The teachers want to do away with cheating in the school．老師們想在學校裡消滅作弊現象。
*They have done away with the old laws．他們廢除了舊法律。
*Can you do away with your bad habit？你能改掉壞習慣嗎？
*We must do away with all manifestations of disunity．我們一定要消除一切不團結的現象。
2．murder謀殺
*It is said that they will do away with him by poisoning him．據說他們會用毒藥把他幹掉。
*He did away with his enemies．他殺死了他的敵人。1．be suitable for適合
*The coat will do for Alice．這種上衣艾麗絲穿合適。
*You won't do for a teacher．你不適合當教師。
*These shoes won't do for mountainclimbing．這種鞋子爬山不行。
2．serve the purpose of用作；充任
*The box will have to do for a desk until the furniture arrives．傢俱來到之前，這個箱子就得當作書桌用了。
*This place will do for a gymnasium．這個地方可以做體育館用。
3．care for；attend to照料；幫…做事；替…管家
*Mrs．Black has been doing for the manager for ten years．布萊剋夫人為經理料理家務已經10年了。
*Mrs． Wang did for me during my illness．我生病時王太太照應我。
4．kill；murder；destroy殺死；殺害
*He said that he would do for the policeman when he got out of prison．他說他出獄後要幹掉那個警察。
*Henry received a blow on the head that I thought had done for him．亨利頭上挨了一下子，我想這下子已經送了他的命。
5．ruin； finish off；destroy破壞；毀掉
*The severe storm did for most of the farm buildings．猛烈的風暴摧毀了大部分農舍。
*Our team is done for．我們的隊完蛋了。
*My camera is almost done for．我的照相機差不多壞了。
6．wear out entirely極其疲乏
*At the end of a long day's hard work I'm just about done for．苦幹一整天下來，我幾乎累垮了。
7．manage to solve or obtain設法解決或得到
*How did you do for food during your camping trip？你們野營時是怎樣設法弄到食物的？
*What will you do for water while you're crossing the desert？你們穿越沙漠時將如何解決水的問題呢？1．murder； kill； cheat謀殺；殺死；欺騙
*Her neighbour tried to do himself in by taking poison．她的鄰居企圖服毒自殺。
*The criminals have done in the old man．罪犯們已把那個老人殺害了。
*He tried to do her in，but luckily she escaped．他企圖害死她，但她很幸運地脫險了。
2．exhausted；destroyed精疲力竭；搞壞；毀壞
*The horse was done in after the race．那匹馬在競賽後已精疲力竭了。
*I felt done in after a long day's hard work．苦幹了一整天我感到疲憊不堪。
*This hard work did them in．幹這麼重的活，他們累壞了。
*His business was done in by a big fire．他的商行給一場大火燒燬了。1．treat in a fair way；show the true value of公平對待；公正地評判
*We should do justice to everyone．我們應該公正地對待每個人。
*To do him justice， he has done something valuable for the Chinese revolution．公平地說，他為中國革命做過一些有價值的工作。
2．be very much alike酷似
*The photograph does justice to her．這幅照片極像她。
3．eat to one's full飽餐
*The children did justice to the good dishes．菜不錯，孩子們飽餐了一頓。try very hard盡力
*I don't understand this new plan very well myself but I'll do my best to explain to you．我自己還不很明白這個新計劃，但是我將盡力向你解釋。sweep or clean out；put in order掃除；整理
*This room needs doing out．這房間需要清掃。
*She did the rooms out completely．她把房間收拾得乾乾淨淨。
*While you do out the diningroom，I'll tidy up the study．你打掃餐廳時，我將整理書房。1．do again；repeat重做；重複
*The secretary did the work poorly，so her boss told her to do it over．秘書把這工作做得太差，因此老闆要她重做。
*Please do over yesterday's assignment．請把昨天的作業重做一遍。
*Do your homework over；it is full of mistakes．把家庭作業重做一遍，錯誤太多了。
2．renovate；redecorate裝修；重新裝飾
*If you don't like the colour of the wall，you'd better do the room over．如果你不喜歡牆壁的顏色，你最好把房間再刷一次。
*The redecorating company did my whole house over．裝修公司把我的家重新裝修了一遍。
*After being done over，the room really looks much nicer．房間重新裝飾後，確實變得好看多了。be helpful to sb．；perform a good deed to sb．對（某人）有幫助；對（某人）做一件好事
*They did him a good turn by lending him the money during the crisis．他們在危機中把錢借給他，幫了他大忙。
*do（sb．）good／do good to（sb．）be beneficial to sb．對（某人）有益處
*Outdoor sports will do you good．室外運動對你健康有益。
*I don't know what good that would do？我不明白那樣有什麼好處？
*The medicine does good to your headache．這種藥對治療你的頭痛很有用。
*What good would it do to blame others？埋怨別人有什麼好處？
*do（sb．）harm／do harm to（sb．）cause injury對（某人）有害
*A few drinks will do you no harm．稍微喝幾杯對你不會有害。
*Leave it alone for a time，talking about it may do harm．把這事擱一段時間，現在談論這事沒有好處。1. deceive sb．in order to gain；cheat sb．從某人處騙取某物
*The clever salesman did the child out of all her money．那個狡詐的商人騙走了孩子所有的錢。
*She did him out of ＄1，000．她騙走了他1000美元。
2．deprive剝奪
*He thinks that they did him out of that job．他認為是他們剝奪了他的那份工作。
*The boss did me out of the job．老闆把我解雇了。1．fasten扎牢；扣住；扣鈕扣
*She did up the dress．她扣好衣服。
*Please help me do up the knot．請幫我把這個結打好。
2．wrap up；pack up包裝
*The books have been done up in brown paper．這些書已經用牛皮紙包好了。
*Do up these papers and lock them in the safe．把這些文件包裝起來，鎖進保險櫃。
*Please do these things up for me．請幫我把這些東西包一包。
3．repair；improve；renovate；put in better condition維修；裝修；收拾
*We'll have to do up the old house next summer．我們明年夏天得維修那座舊房子。
*The house needs doing up．這房子需要修繕一下。
*Let's do up this room first！我們先收拾這個房間吧！
4．make oneself more beautiful打扮
*She has done herself up for the party．她把自己打扮了一番，準備參加聚會。
5．wash and press洗熨
*Would you please do up my clothes？你給我熨一下衣服好嗎？
6．exhaust；make tired疲憊不堪（多用於被動結構）
*He had been chairman of the meeting for five hours．He was very done up．他主持了5個小時的會議，非常累。
*They were all done up after a whole day's work．一天工作下來，他們都感到疲憊不堪。
*He was completely done up after walking so many miles．走了這麼遠的路，他簡直累壞了。1．treat；deal with對付；處理
*The teacher didn't know what to do with the naughty pupil．教師不知道該怎樣對待那個頑皮的學生。
*What will you do with these imported goods？你們準備如何處理這些進口貨？
*The play was terrible；half the actors didn't know what to do with their hands．這個戲糟透了，一半的演員不知道手往哪裡放。
2．make do；be content with；manage with對付用；對…滿意；將就著；湊合用
*I will just have to do with what I've got．我只能將就著用我現有的東西。
*Can you do with 500 yuan this school term？500元錢這學期你夠用嗎？
*We don't have tea．Can you do with a glass of water？我們沒有茶，你能湊合著喝杯水嗎？
*We couldn't afford fish， so we had to do with meat．我們買不起魚，只好將就吃點肉。
3．tolerate；endure；put up with 容忍，忍受（跟can或could的否定式連用）
*I just can't do with those boastful people．我受不了那些愛吹牛的人。
*He couldn't do with waiting any longer，so he left．他不能忍受再等下去，因此走了。
*We can't do with such carelessness．我們不能容忍這樣的粗枝大葉。
4．find useful or helpful；need；want；be glad to have需要；樂於接受（跟can或could搭配）
*After a day's hard work，he could do with a bath and a good meal．辛苦工作了一天後，他需要洗個澡並美餐一頓。
*Oh，I could do with a cup of tea．哦，我想喝杯茶。
*Your coat could do with a clean．你的大衣需要洗一洗了。
5．work with；be acquainted with 跟…打交道；相處（跟have搭配）
*You shouldn't have anything to do with those people．你不要跟那些人相處。
*He has to do with computers．他得跟計算機打交道。
*I have got nothing to do with the matter．我跟這件事一點關係也沒有。
6．finish做完；幹完；與…絕交（通常與have或be連用）
*Have／Are you done with the book I lent you？我借給你的書看完了沒有？
*I wanted to be done with it as soon as possible．我想盡快了結這件事。
*He told me that he had done with those people．他告訴我他已不和那些人來往了。
*Hitler，having done with his last meal，fetched Eva Braun for another and final farewell to his most intimate collaborators．希特勒吃罷最後一餐，帶著愛娃?勃勞恩，與他最密切的合作者再一次作最後告別。
*I have done with cigarettes．我已經戒煙了。manage without沒有…也行；不用…也可以
*If you don't like it，you can just do without．你不喜歡它可以不用。
*If there's no suger for our coffee，we'll do without．如果咖啡裡沒有糖，我們也行。
*I can do without your advice，thank you．謝謝你，我不需要你的勸告。
*No one can do without sleep for very long．沒有人能長時間不睡覺。do-all
