*His illness is dragging him down．他的病正在把他拖垮。
*The gambler not only destroyed himself but also dragged his family down．賭博不僅毀了他自己而且也把他的家庭給拖垮了。
*The high fever has been dragging him down．高燒使他感到虛弱。
*If you marry that man，he'll drag you down．如果你嫁給那個人，他會把你給毀了。
2．pull down把…拉下
*The thief was dragged down from the platform by the students．學生們把小偷從台上拉了下來。introduce sth．unconnected with the main subject；introduce with an effort插入討論；硬把…拉扯進來
*Don't drag in things that are irrelevent to the topic under discussion．不要把與討論無關的內容硬扯進來。
*Whenever anyone mentions travel，she dragged in the trip to Canada she took two years ago．不論什麼時候誰談到旅遊她都要把她兩年前去加拿大的旅行硬扯進來。
*Why must you always drag this subject in when we are talking？在我們談話時你為什麼總是把這個問題硬牽扯進來？drag link
