我會畫一張草圖給你
c. (用言語) 描述
The characters in this novel are well drawn. 
這部小說裡的人物刻劃得很好
2 作 […之間的] <比較、區別> ,指出 <類似之處> [between]
~ a distinction (between 
?) 指出 (…之間的) 差異處
~ a parallel (between 
?) 指出 (1．move off；pull away離開；拉開；引走
*The car drew away as we approached．當我們走近時，車開走了。
*The arrival of the teacher drew away the children from their play．老師來了，孩子們不做遊戲了。
2．move ahead；move away from one's opponent in a race，etc．跑到前頭；在賽跑中跑到對手前面並與之拉開距離
*The old man ran faster and faster and at last he started to draw away from others．這位老人跑得越來越快，終於超過別人並且拉開了距離。
*The car was faster and soon drew away．小車速度比較快，一會兒就跑到前面去了。
3．isolate oneself孤立自己
*She has drawn away lately and we can't find out why．她近來不跟人們來往，我們也搞不清是什麼原因。1．move backwards；withdraw後退
*The crowd drew back to let the firemen through．人群向後退去，給消防隊員讓出一條路。
*The children drew back from the dog when it barked at them．孩子們當狗衝著他們叫的時候退了回來。
2．be unwilling to fulfill不願履行
*The firm has drawn back from its promise．這家公司收回了承諾。draw curtain
<<可數名詞>>
『戲劇』 (向左右兩邊拉開的) 拉幕
(cf. drop curtain)1． pull down拉下
*The sunlight is too strong；you'd better draw down the blinds．陽光太強了，你最好拉下百葉窗。
2．be the cause of招致；惹起
*His behaviour drew down a storm of protest from the workers．他的行為招致了工人們的強烈抗議。
3．expend消耗
*The purchasing of arms considerably drew down the country's gold reserves．購買軍備花了那個國家的大量黃金儲備。call forth喚起；博得
*An urgent need may draw forth one's latent abilities．在緊急情況下一個人的潛在的才能會充分地發揮出來。
*Their performance drew forth applause from the audience．他們的表演博得了觀眾的掌聲。
*Her bitter cxperience drew forth people's great sympathy for her．她的悲傷經歷引起了人們的同情。1．arrive；come into the station到達；進站
*As we reached the station，the train was just drawing in．我們到達車站時，列車剛好進站。
2．bring in；attract to participate in or join；induce to enter吸引；吸引參加；引誘
*This play is drawing in large crowds every night．這戲每天晚上都吸引著大量觀眾。
*We must draw in the broad masses to take part in the work．我們必須吸引廣大群眾來參加這項工作。
*The prisoner pleaded that he was drawn in to the commission of the crime．囚犯辯解說他是受人引誘而犯罪的。
3．pull in；breathe in收進；吸入
*The fisherman drew in the net．漁民把網收進來了。
*He drew in some fresh air．他吸進一些新鮮空氣。
4．（the days）become shorter；be more economical（白天）變短；緊縮開支
*The days are drawing in as winter approaches．冬季來臨了，白晝漸漸變短了。
*We must draw in a bit， although essential expenditure should not be cut．雖然必要的開支不能削減，但是我們還是要稍為節約點。
*I'm getting short of money．I'll draw in my expenditure．我的錢快用完了，我得要緊縮開支。1．come near in time；gradually approach接近；臨近
*Winter is drawing on．冬天來臨了。
*The fateful date drew on．決定命運的日子臨近了。
2．put on穿上
*Help her draw on these boots．It's raining outside．幫她穿上靴子，外面在下雨。
*Hastily John drew on his trousers and rushed out into the street．約翰匆匆忙忙穿上褲子，向街上衝去。
3．make use of（money，etc．）；take or use as a source利用；動用（錢等）
*The company can draw on their vast reserves to pay for the project．公司可以動用其雄厚的儲備金來支付該工程的費用。
*We mustn't draw on our savings．我們不可挪用我們的積蓄。
*A writer has to draw on his imagination and experience．作家必須要利用自己的想像力和經歷進行創作。
*She kept drawing on her bank account to such an extent that the bank soon notified her that she was overdrawn．她不斷從銀行取款，不久銀行就通知她透支了。
*Fat reserves are like bank accounts to be drawn on in the winter when food supplies are limited．脂肪儲備如同銀行裡的存款，供冬天食物來源有限時支取使用。
4．encourage；induce or make sb．continue on his course鼓勵；誘使某人繼續…
*Professor Chen encouraged his students to draw on their speeches freely．陳教授鼓勵他的學生們繼續自由地演講下去。
*She drew him on to tell her about what had happened．她鼓勵他說出所發生的事情。
*The feeling that he was near his destination drew him on．他感到目的地在望，這鼓勵他繼續前進。
*He drew the monkey on till he brought it into a trap．他引誘猴子直到使它掉進了陷阱。1．take out；pull out取出；拉出；掏出
*She drew out her wallet．她掏出了錢包。
*He drew out a revolver from his pocket and aimed it at the policeman．他從口袋裡掏出一把手槍，向警察瞄準。
2．prolong or stretch拖長；拉長
*The director drew out his speech to almost two hours．主任洋洋灑灑講了將近2小時。
*This meeting has been drawn out long enough．這次會議拖得夠長的。
*The singer draws her notes out too much．唱歌者把調子拖得太長了。
*He heated the mental and drew it out into a long wire．他將那金屬燒熱，並把它拉成一根長的金屬絲。
3．（of days）become longer（指白天）變長
*With the approach of spring the days begin to draw out quite noticeably．隨著春天來臨，白天開始很明顯地變長了。
4．work out；formulate擬定
*The committee has drawn out a plan for the building of the city．委員會已經擬定了一個城市建設規劃。
*I am drawing out a teaching plan．我正在起草一份教學計劃。
*The general drew out his plan of action．將軍擬定了他的作戰計劃。
5．encourage or cause to speak鼓勵或使某人說出
*The girl was very shy，but we managed to draw her out and make her tell us her fiance's name．這女孩很害羞，但我們還是設法使她說出了未婚夫的名字。
6．（a train）move away from the platform（火車）出站
*We missed the train by about a minute；it was drawing out just as we arrived on the platform．我們大約晚了一分鐘而誤了火車，我們趕到月台時，火車剛剛出站。
7．take money from a place of deposit提取存款
*She drew some money out from the bank to buy a bicycle for his son．她從銀行取出一些錢，給兒子買自行車。
*They drew their savings out before they went on holiday．他們在度假前取出了存款。
8．develop；make known or seen 闡述
*The teacher drew out the meaning of the poem to his students．教師給學生們闡述這首詩的意義。direct sb．'s attention to 引起…注意
*The teacher was not wrong to draw the child's attention to the errors in spelling，but he should have centred on the child's ideas in composition．這位老師要孩子注意拼寫錯誤並不錯，但是他應該把注意力集中在孩子在作文裡所表達的思想上。
*He drew my attention to a point I had overlooked．他提醒我注意我所忽略的一點。come to an end結束；終了
*The summer term is coming to a close．夏季的這一學期就要結束了。
*The day drew to a close．這一天就要過去了。1．attract towards吸引
*He has something in his character that draws people to him．他身上有一種吸引人的東西。
2．approach；come near臨近
*The day was drawing towards evening．天色漸近黃昏。1．prepare；compose；draft（a legal paper，contract，treaty，agreement，etc．）草擬；制定（合同、協議等）
*The lawyer has drawn up the agreement．律師制訂了協議書。
*The two countries drew up a peace treaty after the war ended．戰爭結束後兩國簽訂了和平條約。
*They have drawn up a contract．他們已經草擬了一份合同。
*The plan drawn up by the Party committee has been adopted at the meeting．黨委制定的計劃已經在會上通過了。
2．（a vehicle）come to a stop（車子）停下來
*The police drew up outside the house．警察在房子外面停了車。
