dream up
(俚)想到 <意外的事等> ,構思,憑空想出,杜撰pass one's time idly虛度光陰
*She dreams the time away．她虛度時光。
*If you go on like this， when you get old you'll regret for dreaming your life away．如果你繼續這樣，當你年老時，你會因虛度年華而悔恨。1．think of or imagine想到
*The boy dreams of becoming a pilot．那男孩一心想當飛行員。
*I never dreamed of meeting you here．我真想不到能在這兒見到你。
*We have achieved what our forefathers never even dreamed of．我們已經取得了我們的祖先連想都沒有想過的成就。
2．have a dream about夢見
*I dreamed of my hometown last night．我昨天夢見了我的老家。
*Do you ever dream of me？你夢見過我嗎？
3．have hopes for sth．；wish for sth．希望；渴望
*For centuries man dreamed of achieving vertical flight．幾個世紀以來，人類一直渴望達到垂直飛行。
*Scientists now have wonderful drugs of which no one could have drcamed years ago．科學家現在已經掌握了幾年前沒有人能夢想到的靈丹妙藥。make up；think up；think of in imagination構思；想出；虛構
*Where did you dream up that idea？你從哪兒想出那個主意來的？
*He is good at dreaming up a plan which is almost impossible to be carried out．他善於空想一個幾乎總是不可能實現的計劃。
*She can always dream up some new reasons for not doing anything unpleasant．她總能編出不做令人不愉快的事情的新理由。dream world
