『軍』軍禮服1．dress formally；put on smart clothes盛裝；穿上漂亮的衣服
*The girls all dressed up to take part in the evening party．姑娘們全都打扮起來去參加晚會。
*Are you going to dress up for the party？你準備盛裝赴會嗎？
2．make sth．or sb．seem different；disguise化裝；喬裝；偽裝
*She was dressed up to represent a flowerseller．她把自己化裝成一個賣花姑娘。
*The prisoners escaped by dressing up as guards．囚犯們偽裝成哨兵逃跑了。
3．improve；make sth．seem better or more important改進；使某物看上去更好或更重要
*This scheme should be dressed up to look more attractive．這個計劃應該改進一下，使其更有吸引力。
*A fresh coat of paint will dress up the old house．刷層新油漆會使這房子舊貌換新顏。
*Your proposal is fine．Dress it up a bit and then send it to the committee．你的建議不錯，修改一下再交給委員會。dress-guard
