→ drop ANCHOR,drop the CURTAIN
~ a line 
放下釣線,垂釣1．pay a causal visit；come across to visit串門；隨便拜訪
*Mrs Barton lives on the other side of the road．She often drops across to have coffee with us．巴頓太太住在馬路那邊。她經常來串門和我們一起喝咖啡。
*On my way back from school I'll drop across at my friend's home．放學回來的路上，我要順便去我朋友家看看。
2．bring帶來
*I'll drop the book across to you this evening．今晚我把那本書給你帶來。get away；become less走掉；減少
*It was a tedious lecture．The listeners dropped away one by one．演講冗長乏味，聽眾一個個都走掉了。
*The attendance has dropped away in recent months．最近幾個月的出勤率下降了。1．fall back in position落後；地位倒退
*I've dropped back in work．我的工作落後了。
*He has dropped back to fifth in his class．他在班上的名次已經退到第5名。
2．lessen減少；減輕
*The unemployment figures dropped back last month．上月的失業人數下降了。
*As the medicine took effect，the symptoms dropped back．隨著藥物的作用，症狀減輕了。
3．move or step backwards； retreat退後；撤退
*The enemy dropped back before our army's attack．我軍還沒有發動進攻，敵軍就撤退了。drop curtain
<<可數名詞>>
『戲劇』 (舞台前的) 垂幕,吊幕1．descend or fall quickly下降
*The temperature has dropped down．氣溫已經下降了。
*She dropped down into an armchair，exhausted．他精疲力盡，一下倒在扶手椅裡。
2．lower oneself quickly俯身
*The peasants dropped down on their knees in front of the temple．那些農民在寺廟前跪了下來。drop hammer
<<可數名詞>>
『機械』落錘,吊錘,打樁錘visit unexpectedly；pay a visit to sb．without telling him beforehand 順便拜訪
*Some friends dropped in to tea．幾位朋友順便來喝茶。
*We were just sitting down to dinner when my friend dropped in．我們剛坐下吃晚飯，突然我朋友來了。call on or visit sb．unexpectedly順便拜訪
*If you are ever in our neighbourhood，be sure to drop in on us．如果你到我們這個地區來，一定要來我們這兒玩玩。
*Why don't we drop in on her and find out how she is doing？我們何不進去坐坐，順便看看她幹得怎麼樣？drop initial
『印刷』章首字
(書籍雜誌等各章節開頭較本文字體大兩三倍的第一個字母,亦稱inset initial)drop leaf
桌子活動翻板drop letter
(美)本局直遞郵件1．fall off掉下
*My top button has dropped off and I can't find it．我最上面的鈕扣掉了，找不到了。
2．become fewer or less；decline 減少；下降
*The number of students has been dropping off recently．近來學生人數減少。
*Sales have been dropping off badly．銷售額下降得厲害。
*Attendance at football matches has dropped off since the coming of television．自有電視以來，到現場觀看足球比賽的人就減少了。
3．fall asleep睡著
*I was just dropping off when the telephone rang．我剛要睡著，突然電話鈴響了。
4．let sb．get down from a vehicle；set down讓某人下車；放下
*Where do you want me to drop you off？你要我在哪兒讓你下車？
*Tom dropped me off at the postoffice and I've walked the rest of the way．湯姆讓我在郵局下了車，剩下的路我就步行了。
*He said he would drop the parcel off at the post office．他說他要在郵局寄一個包裹。
*I can drop the laundry off on my way to work．我可以在上班的路上把要洗的東西送掉。leave；cease to attend離去；不出席
*A few had even dropped out，but nearly half of these had returned to graduate．少數人甚至已輟學，但近一半的人又返校以求畢業。
*She has dropped out of society．她已經退出社交界。
