c. 慢慢地把<東西>移動成…
He ~d the door open. 
他慢慢地推開門
<<不及物動詞>>
1 <痛苦、氣勢、緊張等> 緩和,減輕
2 緩慢地移動
He ~d into the car [a seat]. 
他緩慢地坐進車子 [椅子] 
The car ~d out of the garage. 
汽車緩慢地駛出車庫
ease up[off]
(1) <痛苦、緊張等> 緩和,減輕
(2) 減輕工作,輕鬆地做
(3) 緩和 [對人的] 嚴厲態度[on]
E~ up on her. 
對她的態度緩和一些吧
(4) 放鬆,減少[on]
He ~d off on the accelerator. 
他放鬆變速器1．be accustomed gradually 逐漸適應
*Don ' tworry！You'll be eased in to the new job．不要擔心！你會漸漸適應新工作的。
*He is gradually eased in to the weather here．他慢慢地適應了這裡的氣候。
2．move or place sth．carefully into a position 小心地把某物移入或放入某一位置
*He eased the bolt in carefully．他小心地插上插銷。relieve of緩解；減輕
*This medicine will ease you of your pain．這種藥會緩解你的疼痛。1．remove gently 小心翼翼地取下
*The nurse eased the bandoge off．護士輕輕地揭掉繃帶。
*He eased the stamp off．他小心翼翼地取下那張郵票。
2．become less tense or troublesome緩和
*The rain should ease off before midday．這雨到中午會變小。
*According to the weather forecast，the storm will ease off．根據天氣預報，風暴會漸漸平息下來。
*After the injection his pain began to ease off．打針後，他的疼痛開始減輕。
*The tension eased off slowly when the two sides began negotiations．談判開始時，雙方的緊張局勢就慢慢緩和下來了。1．be relieved from pain 解除痛苦
*A doctor's duty is to ease up patients．醫生的職責是解除病人的痛苦。
*The pain began to ease up after she was grven a sedative．給她用了止痛劑後，疼痛輕多了。
2．become less tense；relax 緩和；輕鬆；放鬆
*The situation should ease up now that the two sides are prepared to talk．既然雙方在準備談判，局勢應該緩和了。
*I'll be glad when the pressure of work has eased up a little. I'm far too busy at the moment．如果工作壓力減輕一點，我會很高興的，現在我太忙了。
*She refused to ease up the least bit，even if she was already tired．雖然她已累極了，但她絲毫不肯放鬆自己的工作。
3．slow down;decelerate 放慢；減、速
*Ease up，we're going too fast！慢點，我們走得太快了！
*The machine eased up．這機器的速度減慢了。
4．move along（usu．to make space for sb．else）移動（常指為別人讓出座位）
*They eased up a bit to make room for those without seats．他們移動了一下，騰出地方給沒有座位的人。
*I wonder if you could ease up a little as there are severla people without seats．有好幾個人沒有座位，不知你們是否可以挪一挪讓出點座位來。ease.ful
