*What ate at her was not what you had said but something else．使她煩惱的事不是你所說的，而是其它事情。1．destroy gradually（逐漸）腐蝕；消耗
*The acid has been eating away the sides ofthe container．酸侵蝕了容器的壁。
*Cancer ate away the healthy flesh．癌症侵蝕了健康的肌體。
*Our money was eaten away by inflation．我們錢都被通貨膨脹吞蝕了。
2．eat continuously 連續不斷地吃
*They have been eating away for more than three hours.他們一直吃了3個多小時。eat at home在家吃飯
*Are we eating in tonight？今晚我們在家吃飯嗎？admit one has been wrong in sth．one has said收回自己說過的話
*Dick insisted the United States was larger than China but he had to eat his words when Beth showed him his map．狄克堅持說美國比中國大，但當貝思給他看地圖時，他不得不收回他的話。
*Don't boast too much．You will be forced to eat your words one day．不要吹得太厲害，總有一天你不得不收回你說的話。1．eat in a restaurant instead of at home在餐館吃飯Once in a while we eat out．我們時而在外面飯店用餐。
*We need a babysitter tonight，because we are eating out．今晚我們需要一個看孩子的，因為我們要在外面吃飯。
2．rust；rot or be destroyed使生銹；使腐爛
*Rust has eaten out the sword．劍已經生銹了。1．finish eating； eat all of 吃光
*Make sure the children eat their vegetables up！一定要讓孩子們把蔬菜吃光。
*After working all afternoon，we quickly ate up all of the dinner.我們整整幹了一個下午以後，一會兒就把飯吃光了。
2．use all of；consume用完；消耗
*Extravagance ate up his inheritance．奢侈的生活耗盡了他繼承的遺產。
*The central heating eats up a lot of electricity．暖氣耗費大量的電力。
*Idle talk had eaten up the hour before they knew it．閒談不知不覺地把他們的時間都耗掉了。
3．destroy as if by eating；distress 毀壞；使苦惱 The mountain flood ate up many buildings．山洪沖毀了許多建築物。
*What's been eating him up lately？近來他為什麼一直在苦惱？
*The heavy and monotonous job ate him up．繁重而單調的工作使他苦惱煩悶。eat.a.ble
