edge in
(1) 插嘴
He didn't let me ~ in a word. 
他不讓我插進一句話
(2) 漸漸逼近[某人][on]
He ~d in on his opponent. 
他漸漸逼近對手
edge out
(1) 漸漸把<人> (從地位等) 擠落,排擠
He ~d me out. 
他漸漸把我排擠出去
(2) 小勝<對手>urge on慫恿
*The boy committed the crime partly because he was edged on by others．這男孩犯罪部分是因為受他人慫恿。
*The girl edged her boy friend on to buy a colour TV camera．這女孩慫恿她的男友買彩色電視攝像機。1．displace 取代
*Colour TV sets are gradually edging out black and white ones．彩電正在逐漸取代黑白電視機。
*Imported cars from Japan are edging out American cars.從日本進口的汽車正在取代美國的汽車。
2．supplant; defeat or surpass by a small margin排擠掉；險勝
*That forceful young woman edged out the forner chairman and is now chairman herself．那位年輕的女強人逐漸擠掉了前任主席，現在她自己當上了主席。
*In the last election they succeeded in edging their opponents out by a small margin．在最近的一次選舉中，他們以微弱的多數票擠掉了對手。edge tool
