That didn't ~ into their calculations. 
那件事他們沒有想到 [考慮到] 
(3) 介入 <感情、想法等> ,起共鳴; 領略,體會 <氣氛、氣候> ,充分瞭解
I tried to ~ into the spirit of the occasion. 
我試著去領會該儀式的精神
enter on[upon]?
開始,著手做,
(1) 開始考慮 <新工作、問題等> 
~ upon a task 
著手做一件工作
(2) 進入,踏入
~ on the last phase 
進入最後的階段
(3) 獲得…的所有權,繼承
~ on one's inheritance 
繼承 (某人的) 遺產put one's name down for（a contest，an exam，etc．）報名參加（競賽、考試等）
*How many students entered for the competiion？多少學生報名參加比賽？
*All the students in Band 4 have entered for College English Test Band 4．所有 4級的學生都報名參加了大學英語4級考試。
*I want to enter for high iump． 我想報名參加跳高比賽。1．come or go in；begin（correspondence，conversations，negotiations，etc．）進入；開始（書信、談話、談判等）
*Shortly after graduation from college，he entered into business．大學畢業後不久他就進入了商界。
*The two old men entered into a long discussion．這兩位老人開始了長時間的討論。
*They entered into negotiations with their business rivals．他們開始跟業務上的對手進行談判。
*At that time he entered into correspondence with an American for im provement in the English language．那時候他開始同一位美國人通信以提高英語水平。
2.relate in detail；begin to consider；examine 詳述；開始考慮；研究
*Without entering into all the advantages and disadvantages，we can see that the plan is feasible．儘管沒有詳述優缺點，我們也看得出這個計劃是可行的。
*We can't enter into details at present．我們目前還不能討論細節。
*Let's enter into an elaborate investigation．讓我們開始詳細調查吧。
3．take part in 參加
*A catalyst changes the speed of chemical reaction without entering into it．催化劑能改變化學反應的速度而不參加反應。
4．form a part；be part of 成為…一部分
*Oxygen enters into many compound bodies．氧是許多化合物的組成部分。
5．sympathize with；understand；comprehend同情；理解；深知
*I can enter into your feeling at the loss of your father．我能理解你失去父親後的心情。
*She did not enter into my mood．她不體諒我的心情。
*All of us have come from developing countries，so we can enter into one another's feelings and views．我們都來自發展中國家，因此能理解彼此的感情和觀點。
6．come into a state of 進入…狀態
*The actress acted very well because she has entered into the feelings of her part．這位女演員表演得很好，因為她已經進入了角色。
*The country has entered into a state of war．這國家已經進入戰爭狀態。1．begin（an age，a career，a term of office，etc．）開始（一個時代、生涯、新職務等）
*Our country has entered，on a new period．我們國家已進入一個新時期。
*After the splendid wedding party，the new couple entered on a new stage of their life．在隆重而壯觀的婚禮以後，這對新婚夫婦開始進入了生活的新階段。
*He felt proud when he entered on the duties of his new appointment．當他開始擔任新職務時，他感到很自豪。
2．begin to consider；begin to deal with 開始考慮；開始研討
*Let's enter upon the question．我們開始討論這個問題吧。
*Once we enter on a question，we should not easily give it up．一旦我們研究某個問題，就不要輕易放過它。
3. take possession of 得到；佔有
*She entered upon a large property．她獲得了一大筆財產。En.ter Ri.os
