[`ivєn; ˋi:vn]
<<不可數名詞>>
(古.詩)傍晚,黃昏 (evening)although 即使…也
*I won't mind even if he doesn't come．即使他不來，我也不介意。
*I won't lose heart even if I don't succeed．即使是失敗，我也不灰心。1．make（a surface，etc．） even or smooth使（表面等）平坦或光滑
*The workers are busy evening out the surface of the road．工人們正忙著平整路面。
*When the building of the bridge was finished，the workers began evening out the ground of the construction site．當橋樑建造完工時，工人們開始平整建築工地的路面。
2.stabilize 穩定
*It is expected that prices will even out next year．預料明年的物價會穩定。
3．equalize；make regular or equitable使平均；使均衡
*I'll pay this time and yod pay next time；it'll even out in the long run．這次我付，下次你付，最後還是平攤了。even permutation
『數』偶排列; 偶置換equalize；make（accounts，etc．）balanced；make equal 平均；使（帳目等）平衡；使…成為平局
*According to the contract，the two parties should even up accounts with each other．根據合同，雙方的收支賬目應該相等。
*If you give him an apple you must give his brother one to even things up．你要是給他一個蘋果，就也得給他弟弟一個，這樣才公平。
*The two teams evened up their score．這兩隊打成平局。e.ven-mind.ed
