『音樂』 (固定唱法) C 大調的第四音
(cf. sol-fa)1.diminish；decline 減少； 衰落；減弱
*The wind fell away and all was calm．風變小了，周圍一片寂靜。
*The number of people coming to the club has fallen away a lot．來俱樂部的人數大大減少了。
*Attendances are falling away steadily．出勤率在逐漸下降。
2．go away；vanish離開；消失All his old friends fell away from him．老朋友們都疏遠了他。
*The old customs have fallen away into disuse．這些舊風俗已經廢棄了。
3．fall out and down；drop away 脫落；落掉
*Flowers are falling away．花在凋謝。
*The stones have fallen away from the side of the house．房子側面的石頭脫落了。
4．decay；betray 變質；背叛
*Atrue revolutionary should never fall away in time of danger．一個真正的革命者在危急時刻絕不應該背叛。
*Meat is kept from falling away in cold storage．肉放進冷藏庫以防變質。
5．move back;retreat返回；撤回
*He fell back in surprise．他被嚇得往後退縮。
*Badly beaten，the enemy had to fall back in disorder．敵軍被打得一敗塗地，亂成一團向後撤退。
*As the enemy advanced，we fell back．敵人進攻時我們就後退。
*The audience fell back into silence．觀眾又靜了下來。
*fall back on／upon  1．rely on；turn to sb．for help依賴；求助於
*Doctors sometimes fall back on old cures when modern medicine does not work．當現代藥物不管用時，醫生有時依靠古老的醫療方法。
*It's good to have a friend to fall back on.有個可依靠的朋友是很好的。
*When the big bills for his wife's hospital care came，he was glad he had money in the bank to fall back on．當他收到妻子的一大筆住院費的帳單時，他因為銀行裡有一筆錢而感到欣慰。
*We can always fall back upon Bill when we are in difficulties if we can't get anyone else．遇到困難時，如果找不到別人，我們隨時都可以求助於比爾。
2.go back to回過來再談；重提
*You must fall back on what you said at the meeting．你必須回過來把會上講的再說一遍。fa.al.ite
