感恩節適逢十一月的第四個星期四
c. (偶然) 到來
ilaugh hysterically 狂笑
*They were falling about．他們在狂笑。
*We fell about when we saw his funny gestures．我們看到他那滑稽的動作不禁捧腹大笑。1.break in pieces without force being used 破裂
*This cup just fell apart in my hands．這杯子在我手中破裂了。
2.end in failure崩潰；倒台
*With all these increasing costs， the business could fall apart.由於成本增加，這家商行可能倒閉。
3．separate in a relationship關係破裂
*We used to be good friends， but fell apart about a year ago．我們過去是好友，可是大約一年前，關係破裂了。fail to keep up落後；跟不上John fell behind in his studies and finally had to leave school．約翰學習跟不上，最後只好退學。
*To be promoted or to fall behind is not a matter of salary but even more a matter of selfrespect．升職或者落後不僅僅是薪金的問題，更重要的是自尊。
*I don't want to fall behind in my studies．在學習上我不想落伍。
*Diligence helps one to go forward，where as laziness makes one fall behind．勤奮使人上進，懶惰使人落後。1．accept as true；be cheated by信以為真；受騙
*You didn't fall for his sad story about his sick wife and children，did you？ He told that to everyone just to get sympathy！你沒被他那套關於病妻弱子的鬼話所騙吧？他編造給大家聽的目的只是為了得到同情。
*Don't fall for his tricks！不要輕信他的伎倆！
2．become keen on； fall in love with熱心於；迷戀；愛上
*She fell for him in a big way．她非常喜歡他。
*He fell for her at first sight．他對她一見鍾情。
*My wife always falls for the most expensive dresses in the shop！我妻子總是迷戀商店裡最昂貴的衣服。fall grain
