一種青魚
(學名 Pomolobus mediocris,產於北美鱈角以南之大西洋沿岸)1．fall into sth．accidentally； drop into 掉入；跌入
*The child was near the river and I was afraid he would fall in．孩子在河邊，我怕他會掉進河裡。
*He plunged into the lake to rescue the child who'd fallen in．他跳進湖去救那個落水的孩子。
*The water's deep here． Mind you don't fall in．這裡水深，當心別跌進去。
2．sink inwards凹進
*Because of long illness his eyes fell in．由於長期生病，他的眼睛向裡凹陷。
3．agree同意
*Once the chairman had stated his decision，the rest of the committee fell in．主席一宣佈決定，委員會的其餘成員都表示同意。
*He made a very good suggestion at the meeting and we fell in immediately.他在會上提出了一個非常好的建議，我們立即同意了。
4．（of a debt）become payable；expire（債務）到期；滿期
*The city's debts fall in at the end of this year and the council are worried about paying them．市府的公債年底到期，市政會正為如何償還這筆債務發愁呢。
*The lease of the land has fallen in．土地的租期滿了。
5．get into line；form ranks站隊；集合
*He ordered the men to fall in．他命令士兵集合。
*At eight o'clock the students fell in．8點鐘學生們集合。come in for；get 受到；得到
*He didn't think he would fall in for the major share of the blame.他認為他不會是受到主要指責的對象。
*The coach fell in for most of the blame when his team lost the game．比賽失敗後，該隊教練受到的指責最多。
*The girl fell in for some sympathy when she was attacked by that gangster．這女孩受到歹徒襲擊時，得到了人們的同情。begin to love 愛上
*They fell in love when they were students in high school．他們在中學時就互相愛上了。
*I've fallen in love with your beautiful house．我已經愛上了你那漂亮的房子。1. come upon unexpectedly意外遇到
*I fell in upon of my old classmates on my way home.在我回家的路上我遇到了一位老同學。
2. visit by chance順便訪問
*You are welcome to fall in upon us at any time you like．你什麼時候來玩，我們都歡迎。1．meet sb．by chance 偶遇
*On our trip we fell in with some interesting people.在這次旅行中我們遇見了一些有趣的人。
*We fell in with some French tourists from the same hotel．我們結識了住在同一旅館的幾位法國旅遊者。
2．join；associate oneself with 同…合夥；聯合
*He has fallen in with some strange people．他跟一些奇怪的人勾搭上了。
3.rejoin重返
*As soon as he recovered，the soldier fell in with his company．這戰士一恢復健康，就回連隊去了。
4. accept；agree with接受；同意
*I have decided to fall in with your plan．我已決定接受你的計劃。
*He will fall in with any suggestion that involves eating and drinking．他對任何關於吃喝方面的建議都會接受的。
*She fell in with my views at once．她立即同意了我的觀點。
5. coincide with；match 與…協調；相稱
*The colour of your coat doesn't seem to fall in with your complexion．你的上衣的顏色與你的膚色不協調。
*The idea you put to us fell in exactly with what we our ourselves had in mind.你提出的主意正好與我們頭腦裡想的一樣。1．come down from a higher place落入
*The child fell into the lake and had to be pulled out．小孩落入湖中，必須把他拉上來。
2．flow into流入
*The river falls into the sea．這條河流入大海。
3．form；acquire 養成
*Don't let children fall into bad habits．不要讓孩子養成壞習慣。
4．begin開始
*He fell into a quarrel with his classmate．他與同學吵了起來。
5．be divisible into分成
*His book falls into four chapters．他的書分成4章。
6．belong to 屬於
*Things of a kind come together，people of a mind fall into the same group．物以類聚，人以群分。
7．pass into（a certain state，etc．）進入（某種狀態）；陷入
*She was so tired that she fell into a doze in the armchair．她十分疲勞，以致於在扶手椅裡睡著了。
*The company has fallen into extreme difficulties due to the economic depression.這家公司由於經濟蕭條，陷入了困境。fall line
1『地質』瀑布線
2 阿帕拉契陡坡
(在皮得蒙高原與大西洋海岸平原之間)
3『滑雪』直接下滑線1．fall from 跌落
*When you are learning to ride a bicycle，you often fall off．學騎自行車時，經常會摔下來。
2．decline in number； lessen in intensity 數量下降；削減
*Attendance at church has fallen off this summer．今夏去教堂的人已減少。
*Our sales have fallen off seriously during the past six months．我們的銷售額在過去的6個月中猛減了。
*The number of passengers fell off slightly in January．一月份乘客數量略有減少。
3.decrease；decline in quality降低；衰退；質量下降
*Their enthusiasm seems to be falling off a bit．他們的熱情似乎小了一點。
*His support has greatly fallen off．他的支持明顯減少。
*The service in this restaurant has been falling off for a long time．這個飯店的服務質量長時間來一直在下降。
*Your cooking is falling off．你的烹飪技術越來越不行了。
*The quality of the products of this factory has fallen off．這個工廠的產品質量已經下降。1．descend on；drop on； befall落在；落到…身上
*Snow has fallen on the mountains all night．山上徹夜降了雪。
*Tears fell on the letter she was reading．眼淚滴在她正念的那封信上。
*All the expenses fell on me．所有開銷均由我付。
*The responsibility of defending the country falls on all the people．保衛祖國，人人有責。
2．attack；go and fight with進攻；襲擊
*They fell on the enemy vigorously．他們向敵人發起了猛烈的進攻。
*The gangsters fell on her from behind the building．歹徒從大樓的後面向她襲擊。
3．come to pass on or occur on（a certain day）適逢
*National Day falls on a Sunday this year．今年國慶節適逢一個星期日。
4．chance upon偶然碰到；偶然發現
*I'm lucky to have fallen upon you.碰到你，真幸運。
*His gaze fell upon a small party of men moving up the hillside．他突然看到一小群人向山坡上走去。
5．meet with（misfortune，disaster，etc．）；encounter遭遇
*He has fallen on hard times．他遭到了不幸。
*She didn't lose heart even though she fell on a bad setback．雖然她遭到嚴重的挫折，但她仍不灰心。fall out
1 『軍』離隊
2 失和; 爭吵
3 發生; 產生

1．fall accidentally 脫落
*As she picked up the envelope,a key fell out．她拾起信封又掉了鑰匙。
2．be carried away as waste排除（廢物）
*The dirty water falls out through a pipe into the sea．污水經管道排入大海。
3．quarrel吵架；鬧糾紛
*Most married people fallout over money．多數已結婚的人為金錢而鬧糾紛。
*She's always falling out with her nerghbour．她老是和鄰居吵架。
*Don't get angry！ I don't want to fall out with you.別發火！我不想跟你吵架。
4．come to pass； happen結果是
*ThingS fell out well．事情的結果很好。
*Don't worry！Things will fall out all right in the end．別著急！事情到頭來會好轉的。
*It fell out as we expected．結果正如我們所料。
*Everything has fallen out splendidly．一切進展很好。
5．leave the ranks or a parade；dismiss from the ranks 離隊；原地解散
*He was told to fall out．他被叫出隊列。
*Fall out！就地解散！
*Although all of them were exhausted，not a single man fell out．雖然他們大家都很疲勞，但是沒有一個人掉隊。
6．withdraw（from a group of people who are engaged together on some activity）撤出；退出（一夥人所從事的某種活動）
*Nine people were working on the project，but two had to fall out because of illness.原來有9個人接這個項目，但是有兩人因病不得不退出來。
*Two of the team have fallen out，and I don't know who can replace them．已經有兩名隊員退出，我不知道誰能接替他們。Fall River
