(一個工業都市,前為紡織品中心,在美國麻省之東南部)1．be insufficient 不足
*The supply is falling short．供給不足。
*The rope fell short.繩子不夠長。
2．fail to measure up to達不到（目標）
*The performance they offered fell short of my hopes．他們的表演有負我的希望。
*The novel fell short of my expectation．這本小說達不到我的願望。1．descend accidentally through掉進
*The boy fell through the ice and was drowned.這個男孩掉入冰水中淹死了。
2．fail to be completed，fail to occur失敗；不執行；落空
*If your new agreement falls through，the workers in your company will go on strike．如果你們的新協議不落實，貴公司的工人就要罷工了。
*I hope the plan doesn't fall through a second time owing to lack of funds．我不希望這項計劃因缺少資金再次落空。
*We are going on a picnic tomorrow，unless it falls through because of the weather．我們明天要去野餐，除非天氣不好去不成。fall-front
