fasten down
(1) 釘住 <箱蓋等> 
(2) 確定 <意義等> 
We haven't yet ~ed down the meaning of his statement. 
我們還沒有確實弄清楚他的聲明的意思
(3) 使<人>[對…]下決心[to]
He is finally ~ed down to his work. 
他終於決心做他的工作1．fix firmly in place扎牢
*You will have to fasten the lid down with nails．你必須用釘子把蓋子釘牢。
*The windows have been fastened down．窗戶都已扣牢了。
*He fastened down the collar of his coat．他扣緊了大衣領子。
2. make sb．give a decision使（某人）下決心
*Can you fasten him down to a date？你能使他確定一個日期嗎？finish fastening打結；結牢
*Fasten the thread off with a knot．把線打個結紮牢。1．attach oneself to a person（usu．to the annoyance of the person concerned）纏住某人（通常引人討厭）
*I object to being fastened on in that way．我反對那樣被糾纏。
*Our unpleasant neighbour fastened herself on me throughout the party．那位令人討厭的鄰居整個晚會一直纏著我。
*No sooner had I got in the door than my son came and fastened himself upon me．我剛一進門，我兒子就來纏住我。
2．attach responsibility（blame， a fault，a crime，etc.）to a person 將責任（過失、錯誤、罪行等）加在某人頭上
*Someone must have broken the plate，but why fasten on me？一定是有人把盤子打碎了，但是為什麼把責任推到我身上？
*Why do you fasten such a nickname on me？你為什麼把這個外號強加在我身上？
*They tried to fasten the responsibility for the accident on me，but luckily I could produce witnesses to prove that I was not at fault．他們企圖把事故的責任加到我的頭上，幸而我能舉出證據來證明我是沒有過錯的。
*It looks as if the blame has been fastened on an innocent person.好像錯誤已經加到一個無辜者頭上了。
3．hold on to ； adopt quickly堅持；抓住不放；迅速採納
*Don't fasten upon his idea so uncritically．別那樣不加批判地接受他的意見。
*She fastened upon the idea of going to London．她採納了去倫敦的意見。
*She fastened upon his suggestion as an excuse for her actions．她抓住他的建議當做她行動的借口。
*Once he's fastened on an idea， you can't get him to change his mind．他一旦堅持某種看法，你就休想叫他改變主張。
4．concentrate on;focus one's attention on集中注意力於；集中於Fasten upon what I am saying．注意聽我說。
*Everyone's eyes fastened on the little girl in the middle of the stage．大家的目光集中在舞台中央的那位小姑娘身上。fas.ten.er
