3 同情[人]; [feel comfortable感到很舒暢
*We had a good time by the sea during the holidays．Everybody felt quite at home there．我們假期裡在海濱玩得很痛快，每個人都感到舒暢。
*Do you feel at home if you are on board a ship？如果在船上，你感到舒服嗎？1．pity；sympathize with同情
*I feel for that poor widow．我同情那可憐的寡婦。
*It's easy to feel for people in need；it's harder to bring youself to do something practical about it．對有困難的人表示同情是容易的，但要自己為些做點實際的事情就不那麼容易了。
*We all felt for the parents on the loss of their only child．我們對那死去獨子的父母深表同情。
*He felt for her in her sorrow．他同情她的痛苦。
2．search for sth．with the hands用手摸索
*I felt for the book in the dark room， but could not find it．我在沒有燈光的房間裡摸著找書，但未能找到。
*In the fog he felt for the kerb with his walkingstick．他在霧中用手杖試探路邊的鑲邊石。
*She felt along the wall for the door．她沿著牆在摸門。
*The old woman felt in her pocket for the piece of paper on which her son had written down the address．那位老婦人在口袋裡摸一張紙條，上面有她兒子寫下的地址。1．seem like to the touch摸起來如同
*This new manmade material feels like real leather．這種新的人造材料摸起來如同真皮革。
*I'm holding something that feels like a potato．我拿著一個摸上去像土豆的東西。
2． feel as if one is感覺像是
*I felt like a fool at that moment．我那一會兒好像是個呆子。
*I felt like an idiot when I answered wrong．當我答錯時，我自覺像是個白癡。
3．be inclined to；have the desire to想要
*Do you feel like a swim？你想游泳嗎？
*I feel like taking a walk．Would you like to go with me？我想去散散步，你願和我一起去嗎？
*I felt like laughing at the joke．聽了這個笑話，我想笑。be in the best of health and spirits精神旺盛
*He had a headache yesterday but feels like a million dollars today．他昨天還頭痛，但今天卻感到精神很好。talk or act carefully with sb．and find what he thinks試探；摸清楚
*Let's feel out the situation first before we take any definite steps．我們先把情況摸清，再採取具體措施。
*The best thing to do is to feel out where he stands before we broach the subject with him．在和他商量這個問題以前，我們最好先摸清楚他的意見究竟如何。
*At first the boxers felt each other out．拳擊賽一開始，拳擊手各自小心試探對方的實力。
*John felt out his father about letting him have the car yesterday evening．昨天晚上約翰試探他父親，看他是否能把車借給他。feel able to；feel capable of（undertaking）覺得能夠擔任；感到有能力做
*I'm so tired that I don't feel up to going shopping today．我很疲勞，今天不能去買東西了。
*Do you feel up to going to the theater after your recent illness？你最近剛好，有精神去看戲嗎？
*He didn't feel equal to the task．他感到自己擔當不了這項工作。
*He is a person who never feels up to a challenging position，so we can not count on him．他是一個永遠也不能擔負起具有挑戰性工作的人，因此我們不能依靠他。
*We can go on now if you feel up to it．如果你覺得能幹，我們就繼續下去。sympathize with同情
*The whole nation feels with the families of those who were drowned in the great floods．全國都對遭受洪水災害的家庭表示同情。
*We feel with her when her parents died．她父母雙亡時，我們都同情她。sense or suspect that sth．is the case預感；猜想；覺得會；確信
*I feel it in my bones that they will never get along well together．我預感到他們永遠不會相處得好。
*I know in my bones that God will protect us．我相信上帝一定會保佑我們的。feel.er
