fend for oneself
自己謀生,自食其力feed oneself without outside assistance獨立謀生；照顧自己
*The old couple have no one to do the washing and heavy cleaning；they have to fend for themselves．這對老夫婦無人幫他們清洗打掃，他們只能自己照顧自己。
*An orphan in the old society，he was left to fend for himself．他在舊社會是個孤兒，全靠自己謀生。
*Having depended on his aunt formany years，he finally decided to leave her home and fend for himself．多年來他一直依靠姑母生活，後來他終於決定離開她家獨自謀生。ward off；keep off躲開；擋回；避開；迴避
*He fended off the blow with his arm．他用胳膊擋回了打擊。
*The speaker fended off the diffi cult questions．演講者迴避了難題。
*He is not the kind of person to fend off difficulties．他決不是那種見了困難就躲開的人。fend.er
