fight shy ofengage in war against；contend with； oppose對…作戰；與…鬥爭；反對
*Great Britain fought with France against Germany．英國與法國並肩抵抗德國。
*She has many temptations to fight against．她必須抵抗許多誘惑。struggle to control；suppress；hold in check努力抑制；壓服；克服
*She fought back her tears as she said goodbye．她告別時抑制住了淚水。
*She fought down her excitement and went on with her work．她極力克制自己的激動，繼續幹工作。
*The firemen fought down the flames at last．消防隊員終於控制了火勢。
*He fought down his anxiety．他忍住急躁。
*She tried to fight down her terror．她盡力控制自己的恐懼感。fight to the end；resolve or settle by fighting決一雌雄；辯個明白
*They fought it out with knives．他們刀刃相見，決一雌雄。
*It's not a good way to fight a dispute out．決一雌雄來解決紛爭，這不是一個好辦法。
*There was no other course open to us but to fight it out．我們除了打到底，別無出路。
*We had better fight this thing out．我們最好把這個問題辯個明白。
*We are determined to fight it out come what may．不管怎麼樣，我們決心幹到底，決一勝負。1．defeat in a fight；repel擊退
*He fought off three men who attacked him．他打退了3個襲擊他的人。
*Our troops have fought the invaders off．我們的部隊已擊退了侵略者。
*The boat's crew fought off the attack of the octopus．船上水手們擊退了大章魚的襲擊。
2． drive away with effort趕走；努力擺脫；驅除
*Although the girl tried to fight him off，in the end she was caught by him．雖然這女孩努力擺脫他，但最後還是讓他抓住了。
*She fought off her drowsiness and went on with her reading．她盡力驅趕睡意，繼續讀書。
*We can fight off a cold by taking aspirin．我們可以服用阿斯匹林來治療感冒。struggle to leave打開一條生路；殺出一條活路
*Having been surrounded by the enemy，we must fight our way out．我們已被敵人包圍，必須殺出一條活路。fight-off
