充分休息1．fill completely填滿
*The workman dug a hole，mended the pipe， and then filled the hole in again．這位工人挖了一個洞，修好了管道，又將洞填了起來。
*The ruts must be filled in so that traffic can pass．這些車轍必須填平，以便車輛能夠通過。
2．write what is necessary on sth．such as a paper填寫
*You got the date wrong when you were filling in the check．你填寫支票時，把日期弄錯了。
*When you get the application form，fill it in．當你拿到申請表時，要填好。
*Fill in your name and address here．在這裡寫上你的姓名和地址。
3．pass time消磨時光
*How am I going to fill in this afternoon now that he's not coming？既然他不來，今天下午我該怎麼度過呢？
4．act as a replacement for；substitute暫時代替
*I can't go to the meeting．Will you fill in for me？我無法參加那個會，你能代替我去嗎？
*While our teacher was ill， Mr．Wang filled in for him．當我們的老師生病時，王先生來代替了他。
*I'll fill in if absolutely necessary．如果絕對有必要，我來補缺。
5． provide in full詳盡提供
*Can you fill in the details for us？你能向我們提供詳細情況嗎？substitute satisfactorily for；take the place of sb． and do as well成功地代替
*When Jack got hurt，the coach had nobody to fill his shoes．傑克受傷時，教練找不到能代替他的好球員。
*It will be difficult to find someone to fill the old professor's shoes．要找個能勝任的人來替代這位老教授的工作是很困難的。1．complete sth．such as blanks，forms，etc．填寫（空格、表格等）
*Please fill out the answers to the following questions．請填寫下述問題的答案。
*When she applied for her passport，Grace had to fill out a half dozen different forms．格蕾絲申請護照時得填寫許多表格。
2．（cause to） grow fatter（使）長胖
*John stopped growing taller last year，and now he's filling out．約翰去年不再長高了，而現在正在長胖。
*The baby has filled out a lot under the care of the nursery．這嬰兒在托兒所的照料下長胖了許多。
*You have filled out a lot since I last saw you．自我上一次看到你以後，你胖多了。
*The girl was pale and thin after her sickness，but in a few months she filled out．這女孩病後面黃肌瘦，但幾個月後又長胖了。
3．make fuller， more substantial by adding material充實；增補
*The chief editor said they'll publish your paper if you can just fill it out a little．主編說，只要你把論文內容稍加充實，他們就刊登。be just what is needed； be good enough for sth．正合需要；合乎條件
*With regard to putting him up for the summer， our cottage will just fiff the bill．關於給他安排暑假的住處問題，我們的小別墅正適合他的需要。
*The boss was worried about hiring a deaf boy， but after he tried Tom out  for a few weeks，he said that Tom filled the bill．老闆擔心僱用一個耳聾的孩子，但試用湯姆幾個星期以後，他說湯姆正符合他的條件。1．（cause to） become completely full（使）裝滿；客滿
*The lake is filling up after the heavy rain．大雨之後湖水漲滿。
*Please fill up the tank．請把油箱裝滿。
*She filled his glass up a second time．她第2次給他斟滿了杯。
*All the theatres were quickly filling up．所有的劇院很快客滿了。
*The vacancy in the office must be filled up．辦公室的空缺必須補充。
2．complete sth．such as blanks，forms，etc．填寫（空格、表格等）
*I want you to fill up this form according to my instructions．我想讓你按我的指示填寫這張表格。fill-dike
