fit
<<名詞>>
『古』詩歌的一節in very good health十分健康；精力旺盛
*The old man is more than 80 years old but fit as a fiddle．這位老人已經80多歲了，但仍身體健康，精神很好。
*Professor Li rested at home for a few weeks after his operation；now he is fit as a fiddle．李教授手術後在家休息了幾周，現在他精神很好。suited for對…合適的；有資格勝任
*Such a boat is fit only for a calm sea．這種船隻適於在風平浪靜的海上航行。
*This meal is not fit for me．這種飯不適合我吃。
*He is in poor health；he is not fit for heavy work．他身體不好，不適合做重活。
*What kind of work are you fit for？你適合做哪種工作？1． find space for sth．安排（地方）；放進；為某物騰出空間
*There was so much furniture in the room that it became impossible to fit any more in．這個房間放了那麼多家俱，不能再放進什麼東西了。
*Somehow she managed to fit everything in the suitcase．她設法把全部東西都裝入箱子。
*Can you manage to fit this small table in somewhere？你能設法找個地方放這張小桌子嗎？
2．find time for sb．為某人騰出時間
*Although I'm very busy， I'll try to fit in a game of tennis at the weekend．儘管我很忙，本週末我打算安排打一場網球。
*I hope the hairdresser can fit me in today．我希望理髮師今天能給我安排個時間（理發）。
*There are still two patients to be fitted in this afternoon．今天下午還有兩位病人需要安排治療。
*Our director can't fit in any more visits this week．本周我們主任已再沒時間接待來訪者了。
3． adjust well to one's surroundings；live in harmony適應環境；相處融洽
*She doesn't fit in here， I'm afraid．我擔心她在這兒不適應。
*Brought up in a big city， he found it quite difficult to fit in in the countryside．由於在城市長大，他發現他很難適應農村的環境。
*He fitted in well with his room mates．他和同房間的人處得很融洽。1．accord；harmonize；coincide符合；一致；協調；適應
*This information does not fit in with what I was told yesterday．這消息和我昨天聽到的不一致。
*The expectations may not fit in with the results．估計與結果可能不相符。
*We must fit our plan in with yours．我們的計劃得和你們的一致。
*Your ideas fit in with mine．你的想法和我的是一致的。
*Our literature and art must fit in with our socialist economic base．我們的文學藝術必須和我國的社會主義經濟基礎相適應。
*Our office fits in beautifully with its surroundings．我們的辦公室跟周圍的環境很協調，顯得很漂亮。
2．cooperate；get on with合作；和…相處得好
*She tried to fit in with the others，but it was difficult．她力求與別人配合，但很難。
*For years，he has fitted in well with his neighbours．多年來，他一直和鄰居相處得很好。
*How are you fitting in with your new colleagues in your new job？你在新的工作崗位上與新的同事合得來嗎？equip裝備
*The ship has been fitted out with a new engine．那船已安裝了一個新的發動機。
*We must fit the expedition out with the best equipment．我們必須給考察隊最好的裝備。
*It is quite expensive nowadays to fit a child out with all he needs when he is going away to school．如今，當孩子離家上學時，為他準備所需的各種物品，花費是相當可觀的。
*The hotel was fitted out in the latest style of comfort．這家旅館有舒適的最新設備。1． fit together and place in position；install固定；安裝
*It took us about half an hour to fit up the apparatus．我們花了半小時左右安裝了這個設備。
*The new machine has been fitted up for a trial．這部新機器裝配好了，準備試機。
*The carpenter fitted up the wall cupboards．木匠裝好了壁櫥。
2．equip to serve a specific purpose為一定目的而佈置；裝置；配備
*We fitted up one of the bedrooms as a study．我們將其中一間臥室佈置成書房。
*A shed at the back of the house was fitted up as a workshop．屋子後面的一間工棚被改成了一個車間。
*They are to fit up that school with every modern convenience．他們用一切現代化設備來裝備那個學校。
3．supply sb．'s needs；supply with necessaries供給；供給…必需物
*His parents helped to fit him up for a long journey．他父母幫他準備長途旅行用的東西。
*Could you fit me up with a new bike？你能給我配備一部新自行車嗎？
*John needs fitting up with a new hearingaid．約翰需要買一隻新助聽器。fitch
