燃燒點; 著火點1． suddenly begin to burn more brightly or fiercely突然燒起來
*The fire flared up again and then died．火又突然燃燒起來，而後又熄滅了。
*When they put a burning match to the oil，it flared up．他們把點燃的火柴放在油裡，油一下就燒了起來。
*The bonfire flared up as I poured petrol on to it．我倒上汽油，那篝火便熊熊燃燒起來。
*The enemy bomber flared up when it was hit by antiaircraft artillery．敵人那架轟炸機被高射炮擊中，頓時燃燒了起來。
2．burst into a sudden rage突然發怒
*His temper flared up when he heard how much money had been spent．當他聽到花錢的數目時，他突然發脾氣。
*The mayor flared up at the reporter's remark．市長對記者的報道勃然大怒。
*The minute he mentioned her name，she flared up again．他一提到她的名字，她又突然發怒了。
*There's no need for you to flare up at such a slight thing．為了這點小事你大可不必發怒。
*I meant no harm by my remark，but she flared up at me as though I had insulted her．我的話並沒有惡意，可是她卻對我大發其火，彷彿我侮辱了她似的。
3． begin again suddenly， esp．for a short time after a quiet time；reach a more violent state突然發作；突然復發；突然加劇
*His arthritis flared up sometimes．他的關節炎有時會突然發作。
*Late at night，my stomach trouble flared up again．深夜，我的胃病又突然復發了。
*Feeling had risen so high that it seemed that a quarrel might flare up at any minute．情緒已經非常激動，看來隨時都有可能爆發一場爭吵。flare-lamp
