(pl. flashmen)
(俚)盜賊; 惡徒; (尤指) 假裝上流人士者1．speak in a sudden outburst of passion情緒突然激動地說話
*She flashed out at Martin：「Do you really believe that no one has any idea what's going to happen？」她突然激動地對馬丁說：「你真相信沒有人想到要發生什麼事情嗎？」
*She couldn't help flashing out at such a rude remark．聽了這種粗魯無禮的話，她不禁勃然大怒。
2． appear like a sudden bright light突然發出閃光；閃亮
*The lightning flashed out from the black clouds．烏雲中電光閃閃。
*The lights flashed out and night became day．燈光閃爍，黑夜變得亮如白晝。
3．appear or flash very quickly很快地出現或閃現
*With a pocket calculator，the exact answer flashes out as soon as one presses four buttons．有了袖珍計算器，按下4個按鈕，準確的答案就立即出現了。flash picture
