flesh out
(1) 使…長肉
(2) 增加 [充實] …的內容
(3) 長胖,發胖1．a close relative；close relatives骨肉；親人
*To my surprise，she gave me such an answer；she is my own flesh and blood．令我大吃一驚，她竟這樣回答我，她還是我的親人呢！
*The girl was the old man's own flesh and blood．這女孩是老人的親骨肉。
*The people in Taiwan are our own flesh and blood．台灣人民是我們的骨肉同胞。
2． the appearance of being real or alive真實感；活生生
*The author doesn't give his characters any flesh and blood．這位作家筆下的人物沒有真實感。
*It was a flesh and blood performance．這是一次真實的演出。
3．the human body血肉之軀；普通人
*Before child labor laws， small children often had to work 50to 60hours a week in factories．It was more than flesh and blood could bear．在兒童勞工法出現之前，童工在工廠裡一個星期常常要工作50到60小時，這不是血肉之驅所能忍受的。
*It is known that there are certain things which flesh and blood cannot bear．人人都曉得，有一些事情是血肉之軀所不能忍受的。
*He is flesh and blood， and has weaknesses like everyone else．他同任何人一樣，也是個有血有肉的普通人，也有他的不足之處。flesh crown
