have[take]a fling at?
嘗試,試圖…1．leave abruptly；depart hastily突然離開；急匆匆地離開
*She flung off in a fury．她怒氣沖沖地跑掉了。
*He flung off without saying a single word．他一聲不吭氣呼呼地走了。
*The boy slammed the door and flung off to school．這孩子砰地一聲把門關上，就往學校跑去。
2． produce casually； give utterance or expression to（a compliment， a tune，etc．）casually偶然發出；漫不經心地發出（讚美的話、曲調等）
*He just flung off a remark about getting a new job．他偶然談起要找一份新的工作。
*She flung off a merry tune．她隨意地哼出愉快的調子。
3．discard；rid oneself of丟棄；擺脫；甩開（某人）
*How did you manage to fling off your pursuer？你是怎樣設法甩掉追你的人的？
*She has decided to fling off all restraints．她已決定擺脫所有的限制。
*I wish I could fling off all these petty considerations．我要是能擺脫這些雜念該多好。1．give up； resign from放棄；辭去
*He talked to me of flinging up the design of building a new house．他跟我談到要放棄蓋新房子的計劃。
*I feel like flinging it all up．我想全部都放棄。
*He says he'll fling up the whole thing if they don't give him more money．他說如果他們不多給錢，他就把整個事情都辭掉。Flint
