fob
[fɑb; fәb]
<<及物動詞>>
(fobbed; fob.bing)
僅用於下列成語
fob off
(1) [用劣貨、贗品等] 混騙,搪塞<某人>[with]; 用 <劣貨、贗品> (冒充上等貨、真品) 推銷,賣給[某人][on, upon]
~ a person off with an imitation gem 
用仿造寶石混騙某人(◆用劣貨或其他任何東西搪塞,想趕走某人之意)
~ off an imitation gem on a person 
用仿造寶石 (冒充真寶石) 推銷給某人
(以銷售劣貨為目的)
(2) 搪塞<某人>[with]
~ a person off with empty promises 
用空洞的諾言搪塞某人
(3) 避開,忽視 <要求、人等>fob chain
懸於表袋外之表煉1．get sth．false or inferior accepted as good or real； trick or deceive sb． into buying or accepting以假貨或次貨騙人；欺騙某人購買或接受
*Actually the foreign stamps displayed in the window were of very little value， but he had found that they could be fobbed off upon children．說實在的，櫥窗裡展出的外國郵票並沒有什麼價值，但他發現那些郵票卻可以拿來哄騙小孩。
*The peddler fobbed off pieces of glass as diamonds．這小販魚目混珠，以玻璃充當鑽石騙人。
2．put aside ； not really answer but get rid of丟在一邊；置之不理
*Her little brother asked where she was going， but she fobbed him off with an excuse．她弟弟問她去哪裡，但她卻藉故不答。
3．put sb．off by deception or trickery用欺騙、詭計打發某人；搪塞某人
*He tried to fob us off with the excuse that he had been ill， and so had overlooked the matter．他企圖以病為借口欺騙我們，說因為生病才忽略了這件事。
*When the creditors demanded their money， they were fobbed off with a promise to pay them when he received his rents at the end of the month．當債主們來索錢時，他以月底拿到租錢就付款的謊言搪塞他們。fob watch
