<<及物動詞>>
把<羊>圍起,把…關入欄內1．end in failure ；go bankrupt ；close up以失敗而告終；破產；倒閉；停止營業
*The business folded up．買賣失敗了。
*In an economic crisis， smaller enterprises are usually among the first to fold up．小的企業在經濟危機中往往最先倒閉。
*Most of his amibitious schemes folded up on him．他的野心勃勃的計劃大部分都玻產了。
*The new restaurant folded up in less than a year．這家新開的飯館不到一年就關門了。
2． suffer moral or spiritual collapse 垮掉；精神崩潰
*She didn't fold up when her only son died． She kept on working even harder．當她的獨生子死去時，她並沒有精神崩潰，相反更加努力地繼續工作。
*He folded up when the prosecutor discredited his story．當檢察官不相信他的陳述時，他精神崩潰了。
3．collapse with mirth or pain（因高興或疼痛）坍下來（笑得要命，痛得要命等）
*From the moment the clown appeared on stage，the audience folded up in their seats．這個小丑一上場，觀眾們就坐在椅子上笑得前俯後仰。
*The pain in her stomach was so sharp that she folded up．她的胃疼得她連腰都直不起來了。
*He folded up with laughter．他笑彎了腰。
3．make smaller by folding疊小
*She folded up the papers．她疊起了報紙。
*Fold up your clothes tidily，please．請把你的衣服疊整齊。
*Would you fold up the garden chairs and put them in the storeroom？你能把花房裡的折疊椅疊起來放入儲藏室去嗎？
4．collapse ；break down坍塌；倒塌
*He sat down on the chair， but it suddenly folded up under him．他往椅子上一坐，但是突然那椅倒塌下來了。
*The table folded up under the heavy weight．這張桌子因上面放的東西太重而倒塌了。fold.a.ble
