*The United States of America is called USA for short， or USA is the short for the United States of America．美利堅合眾國的簡稱是USA，或者說USA是美利堅合眾國的縮寫。for the advantage of為了…利益
*The teacher repeated part ofhis previous lecture for the benefit of those who had been absent．教師為了缺課的學生把上次講的內容的一部分又重講了一遍。
*He was travelling for the benefit of his health．為了身體健康，他出去旅行了。
*He told the story for the benefit of the children．他講那個故事是為了孩子們好。good or best； not bad as thought；lucky； happily最好；不差；幸運；快樂地
*Maybe it's for the best that your team lost； now you know why it's undesirable to get conceited．也許你們輸一次是好的，現在你們該知道為什麼不能驕傲了。
*John's parents thought it would be for the best if he stayed out of school for the rest of the year．約翰的父母認為休學一年比較好。
*You feel unhappy now because you got sick and couldn't go with your friends，but it will all turn out for the best．雖然因為生病你不能和你的朋友一起去玩而悶悶不樂，但這對你是會有好處的。with a better result； for sth．that is better較佳；好轉
*The doctor felt that having a few days' rest would be for the better．醫生認為休息幾天較好。
*The world situation is changing for the better．世界形勢日趨好轉。
*His state of health has changed for the better recently．近來他的健康狀況好轉了。in general； mostly； in most cases 大部分；通常
*His in formation is ，for the most part，reliable．他的信息多半是可靠的。
*For the most part his statement is correct．他說的大部分是正確的。
*The earth is for the most part covered with water and mountains．地球的表面大部分是山和水。
*They are for the most part workers．他們大部分是工人。temporarily；just now暫時；目前
*They are wearied and have to suspend the work for the present．他們累了，得暫時停止工作。
*I'm rather busy for the present．我眼下相當忙。
*For the present we had better wait and see．目前我們最好還是等等再說。with the object of； with the intention of為…目的
*For the purpose of building our country into a great socialist state，all of us must work hard．為了把我國建成一個偉大的社會主義國家，我們一定要努力工作。
*He came here for the purpose of collecting material for his research．他到這裡來，目的是為了他的研究搜集資料。
*He has gone abroad for the purpose of studying chemistry．他已經到國外去學化學了。
*The yound man jumped into the river for the purpose of saving the drowning child．那個年輕人跳入河中為的是救落水的孩子。for the purpose of； because of為了；因為
*We must be patient for the sake of peace．為了和平，我們必須有耐心。
*For the sake of settling the matter they agreed to compromise．為了解決這個問題，他們同意妥協。for the present ；temporarily目前；暫時
*We really need a new car but for the time being we'll have to continue using the old one ．我們的確需要一部新車，但目前我們還得繼續用這部舊車。
*Ihave no time to spare for the time being．暫時我抽不出時間來。
*He is getting better for the time being．眼下他身體好些了。with a worse result；for sth．that is worse or not as good惡化；變壞；不如原來好
*The sick man's condition changed for the worse．這位病人的病情在惡化。on any account無論如何；不管怎樣（用於否定句）
*I wouldn't hurt her feelings for the world．我決不會傷害她的感情。
*I wouldn't，for the world miss that show ．我無論如何也不會錯過那部電影。for-
