*They haven't a cent in the bank，as they have lived from hand to mouth all their lives．他們在銀行裡一分錢存款也沒有，因為他們一輩子都是現掙現花，僅夠餬口。
*from head to foot/from top to toe all over the body從頭到腳；全身
*He trembled from head to foot．他渾身發抖。
*He was dressed in blue from head to foot．他穿一身藍衣服。
*He eyed her from top to toe．他從頭到腳地看她。
*I was wet with sweat from top to toe．我從頭到腳都汗濕了。in future； from this time onward 今後
*From now on you are free．今後你獲得自由啦。
*I'll be more careful from now on ．我今後會更加小心。
*I hope you will ，from now on，do more and talk less．我希望你今後多幹活，少說話。from that time onward從那時起
*From then on he was a teacher．從那時起他就是一位老師。
*Mr．Li became rich from then on．李先生從那時起就發財了。at times；（every） now and then ；occasionally；once in a while有時；時時；偶爾；間或
*I see him at the library from time to time．我有時在圖書館見到他。
*He called at our home from time to time．他有時到我們家玩。
*From time to time we invite experts to give lectures in our department ．我們經常請專家來我們系講課。From.bork
