*The soldiers fought hard and began to gain ground．戰士們奮力作戰，開始佔領了陣地。
*The rumour is so silly， I don't see how it can gain much ground． 這謠言大荒唐，我相信它不會有市場。
2．become stronger； make progress； improve變強壯；取得進展；好轉
*The sick man gained ground after being near death．這位病人差點死去，現在病情又好轉了。
*Under Lincoln， the Republican party gained ground．在林肯的領導下，共和黨大有進展。1． draw closer to（sb． or sth． pursued）； catch up with逼近；接近；趕上
*The horsemen were rapidly gaining on their enemy．騎士們很快就追上了敵人。
*The runner was catching up with his rival， gaining on him with every step．那位賽跑運動員正在追趕他的對手，一步步向他逼近。
*The company is gaining upon its rivals in the volume of sales．這家公司在銷售額上快要趕上它的競爭者了。
2．move further ahead of跑得比…快；超過
*The leading group of three continued to gain on the rest of the runners and were soon half a mile clear of them．領先的3個人繼續拉大同其他選手的距離，不久就把他們拋在半英里之後了。
*The days are gaining on the nights．白晝正越來越長，黑夜正越來越短。
3．consume part of；erode蠶食；侵蝕
*Year by year the ocean gained upon the shore，and finally took a toll on the houses that had once been pride of the town．年復一年海水侵蝕著海岸，終於把這個城市曾一度引以為榮的那些房子衝垮了。
*Solid embankments have been constructed to prevent the river from gaining on the land．人們修築堅固的堤岸，以防止河水對土地的侵蝕。gain.a.ble
