*A small crowd gathered round the speaker to hear what he had to say．一小群人圍在演講者周圍聽他講什麼。1．collect all one's power fof a strong effort鼓起勇氣；打起精神
*After he had been hit， he got up，gathered himself up and ran off．他被擊倒後又爬了起來，振作一下就跑掉了。
*You'd better gather yourself up to try again．你最好鼓起勇氣再試一下。
*He gathered up his strength for a hard job．他集中精力去幹一項艱苦的工作。
2．pick up and place together；accumulate集攏；收集；概括
*Gathering up his scattered papers，he pushed them into his case．他將散落的文件收攏起來，放入箱子裡。
*Gathering up the thread of his story，he set about writing．他收集整理了故事的線索，開始寫作。
*The title best gathers up the subject．這個標題把問題很好地概括起來了。
*We gathered up a great amount of firsthand data．我們收集了大量的第一手資料。gath.er.ing
