gear
[gIr; giә]
<<名詞>>
(英俚)高品質; 格調; 等級gear case
1 齒輪箱
2 保護殼
(腳踏車輪及鏈條外的)gear cutter
1 切齒工具
(用以銑齒,滾齒,刨齒及刨齒的機械)
2 銑刀
(特製以切輪齒的)1．change into a lower gear in order to lose speed使汽車換慢檔；使車輛減速
*Going down a steep grade，the driver geared down the car．下陡坡時，司機放慢了速度。
*The driver geared down as he came into the corner．司機拐彎時換了慢檔。
2．reduce in force or intensity減弱；降低
*The courses have been geared downto the lower ability of students in the special classes．對水平較低的特殊班級的學生，已經降低了一些課程的要求。
*The dosage was geared down to a level which would work on the infected cells but not upset their normal metabolism．藥量減到了一定程度，既能對受感染的細胞起作用，又不影響正常的新陳代謝。
3. able for安排（調節）以適應
*Education should be geared to the children's needs and abilities，教育應與孩子們的需要和能力相適應。gear shaper
插齒機; 刨齒機gear train
齒輪聯 (三個以上的) ; 齒輪列
(連結之)1．change（a car，etc．）into a higher gear車輛換快速檔
*We'd better gear up our car，or we'll be late．我們最好加快車速，否則要遲到了。
2．speed up；increase使加快速度；增加
*They have been gearing up production in order to fulfil their task ahead of time．為了提前完成任務，他們一直在加速生產。
3．make ready作好準備
*I hope you are all geared up for the new sales campaign．我希望你們都為新的銷售活動作好準備。
*He geared himself up for the interview．他為面試作好了準備。
*Our department is gearing up for an increased intake of students．我們系正準備招收更多的學生。gear-driv.en
