代我把這本書交給你哥哥
b. 把 <飲食品> <以…狀態>端給<某人>
She gave us our coffee black. 
她端給我們 (不加糖、牛奶的) 黑咖啡
c. 交 [托,借] 給<某人>…,委託管理…,把…交 [托,借] 給[某人],把…的管理委託給[某人][to]
I gave the porter my bags to carry. 
我把袋子交給腳夫搬運
G~ me your newspaper to read. 
把你的報紙借給我看
d. 把…委託給 […管理] [into]
~ a thing into the hands of 
? 把某物委託給…
3 a. 給<某人><東西>,出讓,出售; 把<東西>給[某人],出讓,出售[to][for]
I gave him my camera for a tape recorder. 
我把我的相機給他以交換錄音機
How much [What (price)] will you ~ me for the car?. 
你想出多少錢買我這輛車子?
I gave. 
￡6 for his help.我對他的幫助酬以六英鎊
I gave it to him for $5. 
我以五美元代價把它賣給他
b. <為了…而> 交給<某人>…; <為了…而> 把…交給[某人][to]
I would ~ (you) a lot [anything, the world] to know where he went. 
為了知道他去那裡,我什麼都可以給你
4 
a. 給<人等> <時間、機會、許可、休息等> ,認可,准許
G~ him a week to do it. 
給他一周的時間去做那件事
I gave myself an hour for the journey. 
我給自己一小時跑那一段路程
b. 向<對方>承認…是事實
He's a good worker, I ~ you that, but. 
?.我承認他是一位好工人,但是…
That I'll ~ you. 
這一點我承認
5 a. 派給… <場地、角色等> ,出 <課題等> ; 把 <場地、角色等> 派給[…],把 <課題等> 出給[…][to]
~ an actress a good role=
~ a good role to an actress 
派給女演員一個好角色
~ homework to a class 
給班上出家庭作業
b. 給<某人>指定 <時日> 
G~ the starting time for the race. 
給賽跑指定開始的時間
6 a. [對…]加以 <注意、考慮等> [to]
She gave it special attention. 
她特別注意那件事
~ thought to a problem 
考慮一個問題
b. 花費<時間>[在…上],[對…]付出 <努力> ,貢獻[to]; [為…]犧牲 <生命等> [for]
He gave all his free time to golf. 
他把閒暇時間全花在打高爾夫球上
He gave his life to the research [for his country]. 
他獻身於這項研究工作 [他為國而犧牲生命] 
c. [~ oneself]埋頭[於…],熱中[to]
He gave himself to the horse racing. 
他熱中於賽馬
7 a. <人、事情> (結果) 給… <利益、損害> ,帶來; 使…產生 <感情、狀態等> ; 給與 <印象、想法等> 
~ a person a lot of trouble ( 
帶) 給某人許多麻煩
Does your foot ~ you pain?. 
你的腳會痛嗎?
It ~s me great pleasure to meet you again. 
我很高興再見到你
This ~s him a right to complain. 
這使他有抱怨的權利
b. 傳給<某人><疾病>; 把<疾病等>傳給[某人][to]
Somebody has given me a cold. 
有人把感冒傳染給我
c. 使…具有 <性質、情況> ,添加; 給…帶來 <性質、情況> [to]
~ order tochaos 
整治混亂 (的局面) ,治亂
The furniture gave the room a modern look. 
那些傢俱給房間增添現代化的感覺
8 
a. <動植物、事情> 生產,供給… <產物等> 
Cows ~ (us) milk. 
母牛供給 (我們) 牛奶
This lamp ~s little light. 
這盞燈暗
b. <女子 [男子] > <與…之間> 生有<孩子>
She gave him two sonsdo well；act in a way that brings credit表現良好
*He gave a good account of himself in that research．他在那項科研工作中表現很好。give help to 幫助
*He is always ready to give a hand to others．他總是樂於助人。1．compromise；mutual concession妥協；互相謙讓；寬容
*There must be give and take if the negotiations between the two parties are to succeed．如果雙方的協商要想成功的話，他們必須有互相謙讓的精神。
*Relations between her and her husband would be much more harmonious if only there were a little more give and take．她和她丈夫之間只要稍微互相謙讓一些，關係就會融洽多了。
2．friendly talking or arguing back and forth；friendly sharing of ideas which may not agree；an exchange of teasing remarks 友善地交換意見；雖然意見不同但友善地保持一致；互相取笑
*Tom and Jerry were always arguing，but it was all in the friendly spirit of giveandtake．湯姆和傑裡常常爭論，但總是在友好的氣氛中進行爭論。1．give as a present 贈給
*He gave away all his books before death．他臨死前獻出了他的全部書籍。
*He gave all his possessions away and became a monk．他把所有的財產都送給了別人，自己出家當了修士。
*The millionaire gave all his money away．這位百萬富翁把他所有的錢都捐出來了。
2．reveal 洩露
*Don't give away our secret．不要洩露我們的秘密。
*They suspected that the secret had been given away by one of their friends．他們懷疑秘密已被他們的一個朋友所洩露。
*She's not giving away anything he told her．他告訴她的事，她一點兒也沒有洩露。
3．betray 出賣
*He was given away by a traitor．他被一個叛徒出賣了。
*Nobody knows I've done this，so please don't give me away．沒有人知道我幹了這件事，所以請你不要出賣我。
4．distribute 分發
*The guest gave away the prizes．客人分發了禮品。
*The headmaster gave away the prizes at the sports meeting．市長在運動會上頒發獎品。
5．（in a marriage ceremony）lead the bride to the groom's side and give her to him（在婚禮上）把新娘帶到新郎身邊並交給他
*The bride was given away by her father．新娘由其父親領著交給了新郎。1．return；reflect 返回；反射
*This chamber gives back a marvellous echo．這個房間能反射一種奇妙的聲音。
*The two opposite mirrors gave back many parallel images．兩面對照的鏡子反映出許多相同的形象。
2．allow to enjoy again（health，freedom，liberty，etc．）恢復（健康、自由等）
*There was nothing the doctors could do to give me back the use of my legs．醫生已沒有辦法使我的腿恢復功能。
*They gave those people back their freedom．他們恢復了那些人的自由。
*Living in the country has given me back my health．居住在鄉村使我恢復了健康。
3．withdraw from a position or a place；retreat 向後站；後撤；後退
*The crowd gave back to let the policemen through．人群向後退讓警察走過去。bring forth children 生（孩子）
*Jane's mother has just given birth to twins．簡的媽媽剛剛生了一對雙胞胎。1．believe that sb．possesses；credit with 相信；信以為真
*Few of us gave credit to his story．我們中間沒什麼人相信他講的話。
*Do you give credit to his story of what happened？你對他講的所發生的事情相信嗎？
2．give recognition，praise，approval（對某事）給予承認、稱讚或讚許
*The credit for the success of the English Speech Contest should be given to the teacher who organized it．成功地組織這次英語演講的老師應該受到稱讚。
*One must give credit where it is due．該稱讚的就應該稱讚。
*I gave you credit for being more sensible；but you are less sensible than I thought．我過去讚揚你很懂事，但是我未料到你不像我想像的那樣懂事。listen to carefully 傾聽
*You must give ear to what the teacher tells you．你必須傾聽老師對你講的話。1．produce and send out（a sound，smell，etc．）產生；發生（聲音等）
*The bell，when struck，gives forth a sound．鍾被敲打時就發出聲響。
*Jasmin gives forth a pleasant fragrance．茉莉花散發出一種誘人的芳香。
2．publish；report發表；公佈；傳說
*He has given forth three books in a year．他在一年之內已發表了3本書。
*Soon after，it was given forth，and believed by many that Hitler was dead．不久有消息傳來，說希特勒已經死去，很多人都相信這個傳聞。release esp．a liquid，gas or smell散發（液體、氣體等）
*Boiling water gives off steam．開水產生蒸汽。
*If you don't shower more often，your body will give off an unpleasant odor．如果你不經常淋浴，你的身體就會散發出一股難聞的味道。act proud；act vain 盛氣凌人；裝腔作勢；擺架子；神氣活現
*John gave himself airs when he won first prize in the English Speech Contest．約翰在英語演講賽中獲得第1名，便神氣活現。
*He always gives himself airs．他總是擺架子。show guilt；show one has done wrong 洩露罪行；露馬腳；現原形
*The thief gave himself away by spending a lot of money．小偷大量揮霍鈔票而露了馬腳。
*His accent gave himself away．他的口音暴露了他是哪兒人。apply oneself habitually to專心致力於；迷戀於
*Give yourself to didigent study and you will certainly succeed．刻苦鑽研，你準能成功。
*He has given himself to his work，body and soul．他一心撲在工作上。
*She has given herself to vicious habits．她已陷入惡習不能自拔。stop hiding or running away；surrender 自首；投案；投降
*News came that the murderer had given himself up．有消息說，殺人犯已經投案自首了。
*The thief gave himself up to the police．小偷向警方自首了。
*Mr．Thompson hit another car，and his wife told him to give himself up．湯普森撞到了另一輛車，其妻叫他去投案。not to hold oneself back from；let oneself enjoy；apply oneself wholly to 縱容；沉溺於；致力於；獻身於
*He gave himself up to a life of wandering．他任其一生過著流浪的生活。
*He has given himself wholly up to the study of the subject．他全身心地致力於這門學科的研究。1．send out（sound or light，etc．）產生（聲音、光等）；散發
*The sun gives out light and heat to the earth．太陽給大地以光和熱。
*Roses give out a sweet smell．玫瑰花發出芬芳的氣息。
2．distribute 分給；散發
*The government gives out payments to people out of work．政府給失業的人發放救濟金。
*Give out the papers ten minutes before the examination．考前10分鐘發試卷。
*The children gave out flowers to the soldiers．兒童向戰士們獻了鮮花。
*We saw a man giving out leaflets in the street．我們看到一個人在街上散發傳單。
3．announce；declare；make known 宣佈；公佈；發表
*He has refused to give out any further information on the matter．他拒絕就這一問題發表任何更多的消息。
*He gave out that the mayor had been elected．他宣佈新市長已經選出。
*The news of the event was given out over the radio．關於這個事件的消息已通過電台發佈了。
*It was given out that the strikers had decided to return to work，and place their dispute in the hands of their union．據宣佈，罷工者已決定復工，並決定將其爭端交給工會解決。
*The result of the examination will be given out this week．考試成績將在本周公佈。
4．be used up；become exhausted用完；耗盡；力竭
*When their ammunition gave out the enemy troops had to surrender．當彈藥用完時，敵軍只好投降。
*His strength gave out after he ran that long distance．跑完這麼一段長距離，他已精疲力竭。
*We had just reached home when the petrol gave out．我們剛好到家，汽油用光了。
*His patience gave out long ago．他的耐心早已消磨殆盡。
5．stop functioning 停止運轉；出故障；拋錨
*We were ten miles from Shanghai when the engine gave out．我們在離上海還有10英里時，發動機壞了。1．stop doing sth．停止
*Please give over crying．請不要哭了。
*The rain lessened gradually and gave over at last．雨漸漸小下來，終於停了。
2．hand over；transfer 移交；委託
*The keys were given over to our neighbours during our absence．外出時，我們把鑰匙交給了鄰居。
*He gave charge of the office over to his successor．他將職務移交給他的接班人。
3．set apart for a particular purpose 騰出；留出
*The fifth floor is given over to the administrative offices．5樓留作行政辦公室。
*The area is now given over to a huge hotel．這塊地現在騰出造一個大飯店。
4．abandon 放棄；不再抱有希望
*The patient was given over by the doctor．醫生認為這病人已無法治療。
*It's about time you gave over that kind of conduct ．該是你改掉這種行為的時候了。
5．yield（oneself）；devote one's time to 放任；沉溺於
*Don't give yourself over to drink all day long．不要整天沉溺於飲酒。cause 引起
*Such conduct might give rise to misunderstandings．這種行為可能引起誤會。
*A branch floating in the water gave rise to Columbus'hopes that land was near．一根漂在水上的樹枝使哥倫布產生了大陸就在附近的希望。make sb．disgusted or annoyed 使人討厭或煩惱
*Bruce's laziness gives his mother a pain．布魯斯的懶惰使他母親煩惱。
*His bad manners give his teacher a pain．他的粗魯使他的老師頭痛。be fair to sb．；give sb．credit that he deserves 公平合理；有功必賞
*You should give a good worker his due．你對好的工人應有功必賞。think of 想到
*The plan is good，and I've given no thought to change．計劃很好，我並沒有想到要改變它。1．stop trying；cease doing sth．停止做某事；放棄做某事
*I did want a holiday abroad，but I've given up the ided．我確實想出國度假，但現在已放棄了這個想法。
*If everyone gave up smoking and drinking，it would bring about the breakdown of tobacco and liquor indurstries．如果人人戒掉煙酒，就會使煙酒業破產。
*He seems so ungrateful for anything we did that we have given up trying to help him．他對於我們為他做的任何一件事是如此忘恩負義，以致我們不打算幫助他了。
*She realized she was wrong and gave up the argument．她意識到她錯了，便停止了爭論。
2．stop hoping for；give up as a bad job；abandon hope；lose hope對…不抱希望；對…絕望
*Her brother was given up by the doctors after the accident，but he lived just the same．她弟弟在那場事故以後已被醫生宣佈活不長了，但他卻活得很正常。
*She seems to have given up all hope．她似乎已放棄了一切希望。
*The climbers were given up for lost．尋找失蹤的登山者是沒有希望了。
*Just as it had been given up for lost，the necklace was found．項鏈丟失了，正對它不抱希望時，卻又找到了。
*We shall never get that fellow to see the error of his ways；we may as well give him up as a bad job．我們絕不會使那個傢伙認識到自己的錯誤，我們還是不去管他算了。
*Much time and money was spent on attempting to repair the machine，but it had to be given up as a bad job．花了很多時間和錢想把這台機器修好，但是沒有希望，只好放棄。
3．hand over；deliver up 交出；讓出；移交
*He refused to give up the documents，alleging that they had been entrusted to him by their owner．他拒絕交出文件，聲稱那是文件的主人委託他保管的。
*He gave the books up to his brother．他把書交給了他弟弟。
*The passengers gave up their tickets as they left the railway station．旅客們離開火車站時交出了車票。
*The young man gave up his seat on the bus to the old man．這位年輕人在公共汽車上把座位讓給了那位老人。
*When she realized that she would have to give up her children，she dropped the idea of getting a divorce．當她意識到她要失去孩子時，就放棄了離婚的念頭。
4．devote；set apart or devote to a particular purpose or use 從事；全部用於（常用於被動態）
*The rest of the evening was given up to letter writing．那晚其餘的時間用來寫信了。
*The whole winter was given up to physical training．整個冬季都用來體育訓練。
*His weekends were given up to golfing and motoring．他的週末都用於打高爾夫球和駕駛汽車。
*Her Sundays were given up to the preparation of a lecture．她的星期日都用來備課。
*The new building will be given up to the library．新大樓將作圖書館。
5．break the courtship off with；stop keeping company with與…斷絕戀愛關係；不再同…交朋友
*The young lady threatened that if her sweetheart did not stop gambling she would give him up．這位年輕的小姐威脅她戀人說，如果他不停止賭博，她就同他斷絕關係。
6．reveal；disclose 洩露；透露
*She didn't give up the secret of the Party．她沒有洩露黨的秘密。
7．surrender 投降
*The murderer has given himself up．殺人兇手已投案自首。1．retreat；make room；get out of the way 退卻；讓路
*Private cars should give way to an ambulance．私人汽車應給救護車讓路。
*The enemy army is giving way before the cannon fire．敵軍在炮火前撤退。
*John gave way to the old lady and let her pass．約翰讓路給老太太過去。
*The crowd slowly gave way before the policeman．警察迫近時，那群人便慢慢退後。
2．collapse 倒坍
*The walls gave way in the earthquake．牆在地震時倒坍了。
*The wooden bridge gave way under the heavy load．那座木橋因吃不住重壓而倒塌了。
*The river was so high that the dam gave way．河水水位太高，堤壩崩潰了。
3．yield 屈服
*Her fear gave way to joy when she learned that the accident had not been serious．她得知事故並不嚴重時喜形於色，不再恐懼。
*A deadlock was reached in the discussions，as neither side would give way to the other．討論已陷入僵局，因為雙方互不讓步。
*Mary refused at first to marry him，but she gave way at last．瑪麗最初拒絕嫁給他，但是她最後讓步了。
*We finally had to give way to his persuasion．最後，我們聽從了他的勸告。
*You must not give way to his unreasonable demands or he will only make further demands．你切不可對他的無理要求讓步，否則，他就會得寸進尺。
4．lose control of oneself；lose one's courage or hope忍不住；失去控制；失去勇氣
*She didn't give way during the flood，though she was very frightened．她在洪水來臨時雖然很害怕，但是沒有失去自控。
*She forced herself not to give way to her emotions．她極力克制自己的感情。
*He was so frightened that his legs gave way under him．他嚇得兩腿發軟，站都站不起來。
5．allow oneself to be overcome by；allow to decide被…征服；聽憑決定
*Don't give way to despair．不要被絕望所壓倒。
*She gave way to her husband in buying a new car．她任她丈夫決定買部新車。
6．be replaced or succeeded by；give place to 讓位；轉變為
*The grey clouds gradually broke up and gave way to a blue sky．烏雲漸漸消失，天晴了。
*As winter gave way to spring，the day began to lengthen．冬天轉變為春天時，白天開始長了起來。
*Jealousy gave way to admiration of thir prowess．人們已由嫉妒轉變到欽佩他們的傑出才幹。
*Sorrow gave way to joy．傷心轉為喜悅。
*Black and white television has given way to colour television in popularity．黑白電視已普遍為彩色電視所取代。
*When she saw the clowns，her tears gave way to laughter．當她看到小丑演出時，破涕為笑。
*Her grief gave way to happiness as soon as she heard that her husband was still alive．當她聽到她丈夫還活著時，她一下子轉悲為喜。give-and-take
