go
[go; ^ou]
(went[wnt; went]; gone[gn; n]; go.ing)
<<不及物動詞>>
(
→going,gonna,gone) 
A 1 去
a. 往 (某場所、他人) 處 (方向) 去,去
go abroad [upstairs] 
出國 [上樓] 
We sometimes ~ to the sea. 
我們有時去海邊
Go back to your seat. 
回到你的座位去
He has gone to France. 
他已經去法國
→be going to do.
b. (為從事活動等而) 去,上[某處][to]
go to bed 
就寢,睡覺
go to school [church, market] 
上學 [教堂,市場] 
go to the vocational school [a private school] 
上職業學校 [私立學校] 
→go to SEA,go on the stage (→stage A 2) 
I went to his lecture. 
我去聽他的講課
c. (為某目的) 去[做…] [for,on] 
go for a drive [walk, swim] 
去兜風 [散步,游泳] 
go on a journey [hike, walk, demo, visit] 
去旅行 [遠足,散步,示威,訪問] 
d. 去<做…>
go skiing [hiking, walking, sightseeing] 
去滑雪 [遠足,散步,觀光] 
My father often goes fishing in the river. 
我父親常去那一條河釣魚
e. 去<做…>
go (to) visit 
去訪問
"Where are you going now ?" "I'm going to do some shopping.". 
「你現在要去哪裡?」「我要去採購一些東西」
2 <火車、公車等> 運行,通行
The train is ~ing along the valley. 
火車沿著山谷行駛
This train goes between Glasgow and Edinburgh. 
這列火車來往於格拉斯哥與愛丁堡之間
3 a. 移動,前進
go 10 miles along [down] the road 
沿路前進十哩
We can talk as we go. 
我們可以邊走邊談
The car's going too fast. 
那部車子太快
There he goes!. 
他在那裡走!
b. 搭[…]去 [by,on] 
go byrail [ship, air, land, sea] 
搭火車 [搭船,搭飛機,由陸路,由水路] 去
go on horseback [on a horse] 
騎馬去
go by bicycle [on a bicycle] 
騎腳踏車去
4 a. (離) 去,出去,出發,動身
It is time to go. 
該走[離去]的時候了
Well, I must go [be going] now. 
嗯,我現在得走了
He came at two and went at five. 
他兩點來,五點離去
She went off without saying good-bye. 
她沒說再見 [告別] 即離去
Where do we go from here?. 
我們從這裡要去哪兒?; (口語)我們接下去做什麼?
b. 開始行動
Here goes !. 
好,干了!
One, two, three, go!. 
一,二,三,跑[開始]!
c. <時間、期間> 過去,經過 <by,on> 
Sundays go quickly. 
星期日很快過去
Two hours went by without his noticing. 
在他不知不覺間已過了兩小時
in days gone by 
在過去的時候
5 被運去
a. <東西>被送往 (…) ; <問題等> (為檢討等) 被轉到 (…) ,被提出
The ball went through the window. 
那球穿過窗子飛去
The message went by wire. 
該信息以電報發出
b. <東西>落入 […的手中] ,給與,歸於; <財產、地位等> 讓[給…][to]
The prize went to his rival. 
獎品落入他的對手
Victory does not necessarily go to the strong. 
勝利不一定歸於強者
c. 賣得 [若干金額] ,出售 [for,at] 
How much did it go for ?. 
它賣了多少錢?
The eggs went for [at] 30 pence [a high price]. 
那些蛋以三十便士 [高價] 售出
The house went very cheaply [cheap] at auction. 
那棟房子在拍賣時以很低價賣出
Going, going, gone (for ten thousand dollars) !. 
要賣了,要賣了, (一萬元) 賣了!(拍賣時用語)
d. <金錢、時間等> 用 [花] [在…] [in,on,for,to,toward] 
This money goes to charity. 
這筆錢要用於慈善事業
Her money goes on [for] clothes. 
她的錢花在衣服上
Most of his time goes in watching TV. 
他的大部分時間都用在看電視
e. 被使用<做…>
This money will go to build a new church. 
這筆錢將用於蓋新教堂
6<東西>被納入 [放置於,裝入] (該放之處等) 
Where do the knives go ?. 
這些刀子要放在哪裡?
This atlas goes here [on this shelf]. 
這本地圖集可放在 [這裡] 這架子上
This letter won't go into the envelope. 
這封信裝不進這個信封
The coat won't go round him. 
這件外衣 (太小) 他穿不下
7 
a. <數字>包含 [於其他數字中] ,可除[into, in]
Six goes into twelve twice.= Six into twelve goes twice [two]. 
六除十二得二
b. <數量> 相當[於…][to, into]
How many pence go to the pound?. 
多少便士是 [相當於] 一英鎊?
8 變沒有
a. 被放棄,被廢止,被除去
That paragraph will have to go. 
那一段不得不除去
b. 消失
The pain has gone (away) now. 
疼痛現已消失
All my money has [is] gone. 
我的錢全沒有了
Where has my watch gone (to)?. 
我的表到哪裡去了?
c. 死,逝世,失去意識
Poor Tom has [is] gone. 
可憐的湯姆死了
d. 衰退,衰弱,變壞
His sight is going. 
他的視力在衰退
e. < 
東西> 倒塌,壞掉,折斷; 磨斷
The roof went. 
那個屋頂倒塌1．move freely（四處）自由走動
*People are going about more now that the weather's better．天氣轉好，人們四處走動的更多了。
*Teenage boys tend to go about in groups．十幾歲的男孩喜歡成群結伙地四處閒逛。
*It is dangerous to go about on the construction site without a safety helmet．不戴安全帽在工地上走來走去是危險的。
2．circulate；go around；spread流傳；四處傳播（謠言、消息等）
*The story may not be true，but it is going about all the same．故事可能不真實，但照樣四處流傳。
*There is another rumour going about that the President will resign soon．還有一條傳聞說，總統不久就要辭職。
*There are whispers going about the city that the Bank is to raise its interest．城裡流傳說銀行要提高利率。
3．be busy with；be occupied with；keep working on 忙於
*The children are going about their homework very seriously tonitht．孩子們今晚忙著認真地做作業。
*Go about your businss．去忙你自己的事吧。
*The best cure for grief is to go about your usual work．消除悲傷的最好辦法是做你通常做的事。
4．tackle；make a start at交涉；對付；著手處理
*Can you help me with this problem？I don't quite know how to go about it．你能幫我解決這個問題嗎？我不太清楚如何處理。
*I'm afraid you're not going about it the right way．你這樣做恐怕方法不對。
*He will go about it with his whole heart．他將全心全意地從事這項工作。
*We must go about our work or we'll fall behind the schedule．我們必須著手這項工作，否則就完不成預定的計劃了。
5．keep company for friendship or for courting 來往密切；戀愛
*How long have Eric and Hilda been going about with each other？埃裡克和希爾妲戀愛多久了？
*He goes about with a group of nice boys．他常和一群好孩子在一起玩。
*That pretty girl is about with a man who is old enough to be her father．那位漂亮的姑娘正同一個年紀大得足以做她父親的人來往很密切。
6．（ship）change direction（船）改變航向；掉轉方向
*As soon as the captain heard the cry 「Man overboard」，he ordered the ship to go about and search for the missing man．船長一聽到「有人落水」的喊聲，就命令掉轉船頭尋找失蹤的人。mind one's own business；occupy oneself with one's own affairs；stop interfering with the affairs of other people專心於自己的事；不要管別人的閒事
*You'd better go about you own business．你還是管管自己的事吧。
*I've no time to play chess with you；I've got to go about my business．我沒有時間跟你下棋，我要干我的事情了。1．move across 過（馬路）；渡（海）
*We go across to the island every summer；it's so peaceful there．我們每年夏天都渡海到那個島上，那兒非常寧靜。
*They went across to the other side of the street．他們從這一邊橫穿到街的另一邊去了。
2．become understood or accepted 被理解；被接受
*Did your speech go across to the crowd all right？你的講話那群人都理解了嗎？1．chase；try to catch 跟蹤；追
*Half the guards went after the escaped prisoners，but they got away free．半數的哨兵都去追趕逃犯，但他們還是跑掉了。
2．aim for以…為目標
*They went there after petroleum．他們去那裡是為了那裡的石油。
*Jim's gone after another job．吉姆一直在尋找另一份工作。
3．try to win；pursue 贏得；追求
*Jim intends to go after the big prize．吉姆想得大獎。
*He is going after the championship．他在爭取冠軍。
*They both went after the same girl．他們倆追求同一個姑娘。
*We shouldn't go after fame and wealth．我們不應追求名利。1．oppose 反對
*It's no use going against the customs of a country that you are visiting．反對你所訪問國家的風俗習慣是沒有用處的。
*I don't know why everything seems to go against me．我弄不懂為什麼事事都好像在跟我作對。
2．be not in favour of 不利於
*I am afraid the case will go against you．我擔心這案件對你不利。
*The war goes against them．這場戰爭對他們不利。
*The umpire's decision went against our team．裁判員的判決對我們隊不利。
3．be opposite to；be contrary to違背
*It goes against my nature to get up early in the morning．我生性不習慣早起。
*What you have done goes against your parents'wishes．你所做的事與你父母的願望相反。
*His likes of purposely going against the opininons of most people put him in a disadvantageous position．他喜歡故意違背大多數人的意見，這使他處於很不利的地位。
*Lilly went against her mother's withes when she married Tony．莉莉違背母意與托尼結婚。
*We mustn't do anything that goes against the interest of the people．我們決不能做違反人民利益的事。be contrary to sb．'s nature or inclination 不合自己的性格或本意
*Staying in bed may go against the grain but that's what you must do if you want to get better．臥床休息雖說你並不喜歡，但是如果你想恢復健康就必須這麼做。1．begin to do sth．；not wait著手做某事；儘管去做；不要等（常用於祈使句）
*「May I ask you a question？」「Yes，go ahead．」「我可以問你一個問題嗎？」「可以，問吧！」
*「May I start？」「Yes，go ahead．」「我可以開始了嗎？」「行，開始吧。」
*The teacher told the students not to write on the paper yet，but John went ahead and wrote his name．老師還沒叫學生在紙上寫，約翰就已開始寫了他的名字。
2．continue 繼續
*The council at last gave us permission to go ahead with our building plans．委員會最後准許我們執行建築計劃。
*Don't be disturbed；just go ahead with your work．不要受干擾，你們只管幹你們的活。
3．make progress；proceed；go forward 進展
*With the strike settled，word on the new bridge went ahead like wildfire．罷工的問題解決之後，新橋樑的建設速度突飛猛進。
*They are going ahead rapidly in their capital construction in the city．他們城市的基本建設進展很快。
4．go first；go in front；move forward領先；先走一步；走在前面
*The athlete quickly went ahead in the race．那位運動員很快在比賽中取得領先地位。
*You go ahead and tell them that we will be there shortly．你先走一步，告訴他們我們隨後就到。
*He is going ahead of me in English study；it's difficult for me to catch up with him．他英語學習超過了我，我很難趕上他。
*When the first trains ran，a law was passed stating that a man had to go ahead with a red flag to warn people that the train was coming．當第一批火車開始運行時，通過了一項法律：必須有一個手持紅旗的人在前面警告人們列車來了。make one's utmost effort 盡某人最大努力；鼓足幹勁
*The police are going all out to put a stop to the violence．警察們正全力以赴制止這場暴力。
*We shall have to go all out if we are to win the race．如果我們想贏得這場比賽，就得全力以赴。
*They are going all out to make the fair a success．他們正在全力以赴使這次交易會獲得成功。
*The government is going all out to clear the cities of air pollution．政府正在盡一切努力消滅城市污染。agree completely；and in every respect；be in complete agreement完全同意；完全一致
*I go all the way with what George says about Bill．我完全同意喬治對比爾的看法。
*Much of what you say I agree with，but I cannot go all the way with you．你說的話很多我都同意，但我不能完全同意你的看法。
*I would go all the way with you in what you have just said．我完全同意你剛才所說的話。go on 繼續
*Work like this becomes less interesting as you go along．這樣的工作越往下干就越覺得沒有興趣。
*You may have some difficulty with this book at first，but you will find it easier as you go along．開始時你會覺得這本書有點困難，但你繼續讀下去時，便會覺得較為容易了。1．accept；agree with同意；贊成
*We cannot go along with you on this point．在這一點上我們不能同意你的意見。
*I can't go along with your plan．我不能同意你的計劃。
*He could go along with it most of the way，but not entirely．他大部分同意，但不完全同意。
*I don't go along with doing things like that．我不能同意那樣做。
2．go together with；accompany與…一道前進；伴隨
*Increasing unemployment has gone along with rising prices all over the world in recent years．近年來，全球的失業人數增加是與物價上漲齊頭並進的。
*You go along with Henry；I'll come shortly．你隨亨利去，我一會就來。
*I go along with you as far as the post office．我陪你走到郵局為止。1．move about到處走動
*The young man is going around looking for work．這位年輕人到處找工作。
2．spread流行；傳播
*There are a lot of colds going around．感冒正在流行。
3．be shared；be enough to give to everyone夠分；分配；分享
*If there aren't enough chairs to go around，I can bring some from the other room．如果椅子不夠坐，我可以從隔壁房間搬一些過來。
*Only a few guests came，so there were more than enough apples to go around．客人來得不多，所以蘋果夠分了。
4．go together；keep company同行；相伴
*Bill goes around with boys older than he is because he is big for his age．比爾和年齡比他大的男孩在一起玩，因為他比同齡人長得大。1．attack攻擊
*The newspapers are really going at the government，aren't they？報界確實是在攻擊政府，對嗎？
2．go towards and overcome撲向
*The thier went at the wall and cleared it．那竊賊撲向那堵牆，並且翻了過去。
*The crazed man went at the policeman with a knife．那個瘋子拿著刀向警察撲過去。
3．undertake energetically努力從事
*I have taken physical exercise；now I must go at my lesson．我已經體育鍛煉過了，現在得溫習功課。
*How are you going to go at the job？你打算如何著手幹這工作？
*You've been going at it all day．Shouldn't you take a rest now？這事你已幹了一整天，還不該休息一會兒嗎？1．leave 離去
