他的小孩1．become more interesting or liked by更加使人感到有趣；使人更加喜歡
*At first glance this doesn't seem in teresting but it grows on me．乍一看這並不有趣，但是它漸漸吸引了我。
*I didn't like the song at first，but it grows on me the more I hear it．我起初並不喜歡這首歌，可是我越聽越覺得好聽。
*The more Jack saw Mary，the more she grew on him．傑克看瑪麗，越看越喜歡。
2．become stronger in；increase as a habit of對…越來越有影響
*The sense of uneasiness grew on the little girl as she came before the silent stranger．在那個沉默的陌生人面前，這個小女孩越來越感到緊張。
*The habit of early rising has grown on me．我已經養成了早起的習慣。1．develop from發展自
*Most international firms have grown out of small family businesses．多數國際性公司是從小的家庭企業發展起來的。
2．arise or result from起因於
*His illness grew out of his tendency to overwork．他的病是工作過度所致。
*The accident grew out of his carelessness．這場事故是由於他粗心而造成的。
3．become too big or too old for太大或太老而不再適合於…
*My son has grown out of his shoes；
*I have to buy him new ones．我兒子已長大，穿不下這些鞋子了，我得給他買新的。
*There is no sense in buying expensive clothes for children，as they soon grow out of them．給小孩買貴重的衣服划不來，因為他們很快就會長大穿不下了。
*My daughter has grown out of these toys．我女兒已經長大，不再玩這些玩具了。
*He has grown out of the bad habits of his boyhood days．他長大了，已經改掉了童年時代的一些壞習慣。pass from children to the stage of being adult；reach maturity長大
*Susan wants to be a doctor when she grows up．蘇珊長大想當個醫生。grow.a.ble
