*You'd better have that tooth pulled out．你最好把那顆牙拔掉。
*You had better not go by air．你最好不要坐飛機去。
*You had better finish today's assignment，for tomorrow we'll have other things to do．你最好把今天的任務完成，因為明天還有明天的事。but for；without如果沒有
*Had it not been for your help，I could not have finished the work．假如沒有你的幫助，我是無法完成這項工作的。choose to（do one thing instead of another）；like better to；would prefer to寧可；寧願
*He invited me to the movies，but I had rather go on a picnic with the girls．他邀請我去看電影，但我倒是喜歡跟女孩們去野餐。
*I had sooner live in the city than in the countryside．我寧願住在城裡而不願住在鄉村。would regard as preferable；had better寧願…不願
*He had rather die than surrender．他寧死不屈。ha.dal
