(不達到目的不罷休)
(5) 將 <招牌、旗幟等> 懸掛在外面
(6) 將 <洗好的衣服1．wait without purpose or activity慢慢騰騰
*Don't hang about；we have a train to catch．別慢慢騰騰的，我們要趕火車。
2．pass time or stay idly徘徊不定；閒蕩
*Two suspiciouslooking fellows were seen hanging about the village last night．昨夜有人看見兩個形跡可疑的人在村裡走動。
*The boy has nothing to do，just hanging about the street corners．這孩子無事可做，只在街頭遊蕩。
*Bill is hanging about that attractive girl．比爾在那迷人的小姐附近徘徊著。1．hesitate猶豫
*They hung back from committing themselves to the scheme until they knew more about it．在他們未瞭解更多的情況之前，對是否答應負責這個項目一直猶豫不決。
*She hung back from asking the questions．她猶豫著沒提出那些問題。
*We wanted Fred to join the club，but he hung off．我們想讓弗雷德參加俱樂部，可他猶豫不決。
2．stay some distance behind or away；be unwilling to move forward退縮；躊躇不前
*The old lady offered the little girl candy，but she was shy and hung back．這位老婦人給那個女孩糖吃，但她卻害羞而躊躇不前。
*Most of us dashed quickly across the street，but two hung back．我們中大多數人很快地衝過大街，但有兩個人卻畏縮不前。
3．hold back抑制
*The pupil is so reserved that he hangs back from many activities．那個學生太內向，許多活動都不參加。
4．restore to a hanging position掛回；掛著擱放
*If you don't need the clothes，hang them back in the wardrobe．如果你不需要這些衣服，就掛回衣櫃裡去。stay in a place after others have left；lag behind別人離開後仍留在原處；落後
*One or two of the audience hung behind after the lecture to have a word with the speaker．演講結束以後，一兩個聽眾仍遲遲不走，想和演講者聊聊。
*She was hanging behind，too shy to speak．她拖在後面，不好意思發言。depend on a very small thing；be in doubt千鈞一髮；處於緊急關頭；安危未定
*He has lost so much blood that his life hangs by a thread．他失血過多，生命垂危。
*For three days he was so sick that his life hung by a thread．他病危，3天，真是命若游絲。
*His life hung by a hair，but the doctors managed to revive him．他生命垂危，但醫生們設法把他救了過來。1．fail or be slow in shooting or firing發射不出；發射遲緩
*He pulled the trigger，but the gun hung fire and the enemy escaped．他扣動扳機，但槍打不響，敵人跑了。
2．be slow in beginning；be delayed延遲；耽擱；進展緩慢
*Our plan for organizing a picnic hung fire because of the bad weather．因為天氣不好，我們組織去野餐的計劃擱下來了。
*The scheme for developing the area has hung fire for two years for lack of fund．發展這個地區的計劃因資金短缺已拖延了兩年。hang glider
<<可數名詞>>
1 滑翔翼
2 從事滑翔翼運動之人hang gliding
<<不可數名詞>>
滑翔翼運動pass slowly or uninterestingly；be boring with little to do悶得發慌；過得太慢而無聊
*The vacation time hung heavy on Bell's hands because all his classmates were away．假期對比爾來說過得太慢了，因為他的同班同學都走了。show pluck；persist表現出勇氣；堅持到底
*Our teacher often encourages us to hang in no matter what kind of difficulties we come across．我們老師常常鼓勵我們不管遇到什麼困難都要無所畏懼，堅持到底。
*Hang in，boys！堅持下去，孩子們！have reached a critical point；have two equally possible results到了關鍵時刻；安危（勝負、成敗）未定She is very sick and her life hangs in the balance．她病得很厲害，生死難卜。
*The future of the nation was in the balance．國家的存亡處於緊急關頭。
*The outcome of the game hung in the balance．比賽的結果勝負難分。1．let go放開
*Don't hang off the rope，or you will fall down．不要放開繩子，否則你就要摔倒。
2．=hang back 1．2．3．1．continue listening on a telephone繼續聽電話；不要掛斷
*Please hang on a second；I'll look for the manager and tell him you are on the phone for him．請稍等片刻，不要掛掉，我去找經理並告訴他你在電話裡等他。
2．lean or support oneself upon倚；靠
*Her head hanging on her mother's arm，the girl fell asleep．這女孩倚在她媽媽懷裡，睡著了。
3．persevere；continue doing sth．堅持；堅忍；繼續做
*It is a hard task，but if you hang on，you will succeed in the end．任務雖然艱巨，但如果你堅持下去，你最終是會成功的。
4．cling to；hold on to sth．tightly抓住；握緊
*The climber almost fell off the cliff，but managed to hang on until help came．登山者差點掉下懸崖，但他設法抓住崖邊直到有人救他。
5．depend on；wait on 取決於；依賴於；有待於
*Everything hangs on his decision．一切取決於他的決定。
*It all hangs on whether he is willing to cooperate with us．一切都取決於他是否願意和我們合作。
6．listen with fascination聽得著迷；注意聽
*The students hung on his every word．學生們全神貫注地聽著他的每一句話。
*Everyone was hanging on his answer，but he kept silent．大家都在注意聽他怎麼回答，但他卻一直不吭聲。
7．continue to sound；continue to cause suffering繼續響著；繼續存在（疾病）
*The concert had come to an end，but the strains of music seemed to hang on in our ears．音樂會已經結束，但樂曲聲似乎仍在我們耳邊迴盪。
*My cold has hung on for weeks，I just can't shake it off．我感冒已經好幾個星期，就是好不了。1．hold tightly 牢牢抓住
*It was so windy that I had to hang on to my hat all the way along the street．風太大，在街上我得一直牢牢抓住我的帽子。
*Hang on to my hand，while we cross the street．過街時要緊緊抓住我的手。
2．rely on依靠
*The only thing I can hang on to is none other than my own brain and hands．我唯一能依靠的只有我自己的頭腦和手。
*Her son's death depressed her so much that she thought nothing was left for her to hang on to．她兒子的死使她十分地傷心，以致於她認為沒有什麼是她可以依靠的了。
3．retain possession of留住；保留
*You'd better hang on to those shares；they'll be going up again soon．你最好留下那些股票，它們很快又會看漲的。1．lean out伸出身體
*The dog lay in the shade with his tongue hanging out；it was so hot．那條狗趴在陰涼處伸著舌頭，因為天氣太熱。
2．fasten，spread，or show sth．out of a building掛出門（窗）外
*People hang flags out on the national holiday．國慶日，人們把旗子掛在門外。
3．endure；not give in；be unyielding忍受；堅持；不屈服
*The besieged soldiers had to hang out for four days without supplies．被圍困的戰士們不得不在斷絕給養的情況下堅持了4天。
*The striking workers hung out for more money before resuming work．罷工的工人堅持要提高工資才復工。
4．last（of supplies，resources，etc．）維持；延續（供應、資源等）
*Our food will hang out for two days．我們的食品能維持兩天。
5．live；reside居住；生活
*Where are you hanging out these days？這日子你住在哪兒？
6．spend one's time idly鬼混；閒蕩
*The teacher criticized Bill for hanging out in a bar．老師批評比爾在酒吧鬼混。
*If you continue to hang out with that group of bad boys，you'll fail in your exams．如果你繼續和那群壞孩子鬼混，你考試會不及格的。1．be going to happen；threaten籠罩；威脅
*Trouble hangs over the little town because its only factory has closed down．這個小鎮陷入困境之中，因為它唯一的工廠已經關閉。
*Danger hung over his head as he spoke．他說話時，危難正降臨到他頭上。
2．continue繼續
*I expect the situation to hang over till next week．我希望這種局面會繼續到下周。
3．remain to be finished or settled擱下來有待解決
*We'll take up the business that hung over from last meeting．我們將討論上次會上遺留下來的問題。
*The court decided to let the suit hang over till its next session．法庭決定把這個訟訴案留到下次開庭時解決。1．take hold of抓牢
*The bus is turning the corner．Please hang to the straphanger．公共汽車要轉彎了，請抓住吊帶站穩。
2．keep persistent contact with與…保持接觸
*The hound hung to the trail of the fox．獵犬緊緊追蹤那隻狐狸。1．stay united；help and defend one another團結一致；互相幫助
*If we all hang together we are sure to succeed in our plan．如果我們都團結一致，我們的計劃一定能成功。
*We always hang together when one of us is in trouble．我們當中無論誰有困難，大家都團結一致，互相幫助。
2．form a satisfactory whole；be consistent編得前後一致；沒有破綻；合乎邏輯
*His story of why he was absent from seems to hang together．他沒來上課的理由似乎還合乎邏輯。
*His argument was a good one and hung together．他的論據很好，邏輯性強。
*These two assertions do not seem to hang together．這兩種說法似乎互相矛盾。hang up
1 放在鉤、栓等上面; 掛; 吊
2 把電話聽筒放回原處; 掛斷電話
3 擱置; 拖延; 中止
The new plan has been hung up. 
該新計畫已被擱置

1．put a telephone receiver down掛上電話
*Don't hang up（on me）；I haven't finished talking to you．別掛電話，我還有話對你說。
2．delay；cause a delay；put aside；cause to wait擱置；推遲；拖延；使等候
*The project was hung up for lack of fund．工程因資金短缺而被擱置下來。
*The heavy rain hung up the work on the building site for three weeks．大雨使工地上的工作耽擱了3周。
*I'm sorry I'm late．I got hung up by a friend on the way here．對不起我來晚了。路上遇到一個朋友，所以耽擱了。
*Rehearsals for the school play were hung up by the illness of some of the actors．校戲劇節目的綵排因幾位演員生病而推遲了。
3．stick or cause to be stuck or held so as to be immovable受困；擱淺
*For nearly twenty minutes the train was hung up in a tunnel with the signal against it．沒有發通行信號，火車停在隧道裡將近20分鐘。
*The bus was hung up in snow and the driver could not get it out．公共汽車受困於雪地裡，司機無法將它開出來。
*A big ssenger ship hung up on a sandbar for several hours．一條大客輪擱淺在沙州已有幾個小時了。
4．set a record破紀錄
*He hung up a school record for longdistance swimming．他破了遠程游泳的校紀錄。
5．place on a hook or hanger掛起
*When the children come to school，they hang up their coats in the cloakroom．孩子們到校後把外衣掛在衣帽間。hang-up
