你一定是在開玩笑enjoy oneself very much玩得痛快
*After the teacher left，the children had a ball．老師走後，孩子們玩得很痛快。
*Mary and Tom had a ball exploring the town．瑪麗和湯姆快活地逛城市。be related to；affect；influence對…有影響；與…有關
*The points you are raising have some bearing on the case now being tried．你提出的幾點對正在審理的案子有一些關係。
*Whether you love him has no bearing on whether he's good or bad．你是否愛他與他這個人是好是壞沒有什麼關係。
*have a finger in the pie have sth．to do with what happens；share interest or responsibility．參與；有關；干涉
*It's none of your business；there's no need for you to have a finger in the pie．這件事與你無關，用不著你插手。
*When the girls got up a Christmas party，I felt sure Alice had a finger in the pie．當姑娘們籌備聖誕舞會時，我確信愛麗絲一定會參與的。1．have a sudden illness with stiffness or jerking of the body．突然發作而痙攣
*He suffers from epilepsy；that's why he had a fit yesterday．他患有癲癇病，所以昨天他痙攣不止。
2．become angry or upset發怒
*When Bell decided to drop out of college，his parents had fits．當比爾決定退學時，他父母很生氣。
*He had a fit when he learned about his son's misbehaviour at school．當聽到他兒子在校表現不好時，他大發脾氣。1．be strongly inclined to很想
*He has a good mind to study abroad．他很想出國去讀書。
2．have nearly made up one's mind to 幾乎已下定決心
*She has a good mind to tell him the truth．她幾乎想把實情告訴他。enjoy oneself玩得痛快
*We had a good time on the farm yesterday．昨天，我們在農場玩得很痛快。have a part in or influence over；be partly responsible for參與或影響
*All of us respect Professor Zhang and he has a hand in every important decision made by our department．我們很尊重張教授，他參與我們系所做出的每一項重要決定。
*It is a very important project．Do you have a hand in the planning？
*這是一個很重要的項目，你參與規劃了嗎？
*He had no hand in that matter．他與那件事毫無關係。experience trouble or misfortune歷盡艱辛
*He seems to have had a hard time of it．他看上去歷盡了艱辛。stop being mean；be kind and generous or sympathetic發發慈悲；做做好事
*Have a heart，Bob，and help me with the work；otherwise I can't finish it on time．鮑勃，做做好事，幫我做這事情吧，否則我不能按時完成。respect尊敬
*He has a great regard for his teachers．他很尊敬他的老師。（have invested money，effort，etc．in sth．and therefore）stand to lose or gain（對某事進行了投資或花了精力，因此）與某事有利害關係
*The manager is worried over the decline in the business at the company．As a big shareholder he has quite a stake in it．經理對公司的生意蕭條甚為憂慮。作為一個大股東，他跟公司有著密切的利害關係。1．have trouble；have a hard time有麻煩；有一段艱苦的時間
*Suzan had a time trying to get the children to go to bed．蘇珊很難使孩子們入睡。
*He had a time passing his maths exam．為了要通過數學考試，他忙了好一陣子。
2．have a good time度過歡樂的時光；快活（與反身代詞連用）
*Mary had herself a time dancing at the party．瑪麗在舞會上跳得真高興。
*He had himself a time playing football．他踢足球踢得很開心。be able to lead，persuade，or influence很有辦法（領導、說服、影響）
*The boss has such a way with his employees that they do everything he tells them to do．這位老闆很有辦法，能讓他的僱員們做他所吩咐的每一件事。
*Ted will be a good teacher，because he has a way with children．泰德將是一位優秀的教師，因為他知道如何管理孩子。
*have a word with sb．speak to sb．與某人談話
*May I have a word with you after the meeting？會後我可以跟你談話嗎？be in a better position than佔優勢
*This football team has an advantage over its opponents in manoeuvring．這個足球隊在機動靈活方面優越於對手。be able to judge correctly；be able to detect，or appreciate sth．（because one's senses are alert or well trained）有眼光；很能鑒賞；對…感興趣
*She has an ear for music．她對音樂很有欣賞能力。
*A good reporter has a nose for news．好的記者對新聞很敏感。
*She has an eye for color and style in clothes．她對服裝的顏色和式樣很有鑒賞力。
*have an/the edge on sb．be in a position of advantage（compared with sb．else）（與某人相比）佔優勢；勝過某人
*In typing，he has an edge on everyone else in our class．論打字，他比我們班任何人都強。
*We can't beat them at tennis，but we have an edge on them in pingpong．打網球我們贏不了他們，可是論乒乓球，我們比他們強。stop；finish結束；完成
*When the teacher had done，she asked for questions from the class．老師講完課後就問學生有無問題。
*If you have done，I'll explain the matter．如你已講完了，我將解釋這件事。1．stop doing or using sih．停止做某事；停止使用某物
*l wish you would have done with your criticisms．我希望你能停止批評。
*When you have done with my book，please return it to me．你看完我那本書以後，請還給我。
*I have done with painting．我已經不搞繪畫了。
*Have done with all these nonsense．別瞎胡鬧了。
2．stop being friendly with sb．不再與某人打交道；不再與某人有關係
*I have found him dishonest，so I have done with him．我發覺他不老實，所以不和他來往了。
*He told me that he had done with those people．他告訴我他已不和那些人來往了。have sb．stay at one's house as a guest請某人來家作客
*They are planning to have some good friends down for the holiday．他們打算請幾個好朋友來家一起過假日。
*Shall we have our grandchildren down for the weekend？我們是不是把孫兒孫女們一起請來過週末？have experienced or suffered all one can；have come to the end of one's patience of life受夠了；吃盡了苦頭；無法忍受；生命沒救了
*「I've had it．I'm resigning from the job right now．」「我已經受夠了，我要立刻辭去這份工作。」
*When the doctor examined the man who had been shot，he said，「He's had it．」醫生檢查過被槍殺的人以後說：「他已經沒救了。」
*I don't know how to thank you．If it had not been for your help，I'd have had it．我不知道該如何感謝你，要是沒有你的幫助，我就吃盡苦頭了。
*「The boat is taking in water．」the sailor cried：「We've had it．」那個水手大聲喊道：「船漏水了，這下我們可完了。」entertain sb．at home；have sb．working in one's house在家裡招待某人；請某人來家裡幹活
*They had Professor Wang in for supper yesterday evening．昨晚他們把王教授請來家裡吃晚飯。
*We'll have the electrician in today to fix the light．今天我們將請電工來裝電燈。
*You'd better have the doctor in to see the child．你最好請醫生來給孩子看看。1．have or possess佔有
*I have no money in hand．我手頭無錢。
2．control控制
*We have the situation well in hand．我們完全控制了局勢。enjoy two advantages；maintain two positions which are incompatible with each other兩全其美；保持兩種不能並存的立場
*You must choose between a low rate of interest but security for your capital，and a higher rate of interest with the attendent risks；you cannot have it both ways．你要麼選擇低息而資金有保障的措施，要麼選擇高利率而冒險的措施，二者不能兼得。wish or mean to harm；hold a grudge against；have a bitter feeling against伺機報復；懷恨在心
*He has it in for a neighbour who complained about him to the police．他對向警察局告發他的鄰居懷恨在心。
*George has it in for Bob because Bob told the teacher that George cheated in the examination．因為鮑勃向老師報告喬治考試作弊，所以喬治懷恨在心伺機報復。
*The manager has had it in for John ever since that mistake in the accounts was discovered．自從帳目上的錯誤被發現後，經理對約翰一直懷恨在心。discuss angrily with生氣地把事情談清楚；爭論明白
*I must have the whole matter out with her next time I see her．下次見到她，我一定要把整個事情跟她爭個明白。
*For a long time my resentment of him grew until finally I had to have it out with him．長期以來，我對他的怨恨越來越大，直到最後不得不氣憤地和他攤牌。have no right to do sth．無權做某事
*You have no business to come so late；you should have come earlier．你不該來得這麼遲，應該早點來。
*You had no business taking my car without my permission．你無權未經我允許就開我的車。have no connection with與…毫無關係
*The teacher asked some questions which had nothing to do with his lessons．老師問了一些與上課內容毫無關係的問題。1．wear穿
*They had their best suits on for the celebration．他們穿著節日盛裝去參加慶祝活動。
*He went to bed drunk，and when he woke up he found that he still had his shoes on．他喝醉後就上床睡覺了，一覺醒來後發現自己還穿著鞋子。
2．have arranged or planned；be engaged in doing；have an engagement有…安排或計劃；忙於做；有約會
*What do you have on for tomorrow night？明晚你有什麼安排？
*I am engaged for the whole of today，but I've nothing on on Saturday．我今天整天都有事，但星期六有空。
*He has a lot on at the moment．他這會兒有許多事要做。
*I'm sorry I can't attend your dinner party，but I have a meeting on for tonight．很抱歉我不能參加你的宴會，今晚我要參加一個會議。
3．deceive；tease；mislead欺騙；戲弄；引入歧途
*I'm afraid he must have been having you on．我擔心他一定是在騙你。
*He tried to have me on too many times before，so it's not for me to take him seriously this time．以前有好多次他老是捉弄我，所以這次我再也不把他的話當真了。
*Stop having us on，please！請不要耍弄我們。
*I've been had on too often to take his stories seriously．我受騙次數太多了，不再認真聽他的話了。
4．have sth．in progress在進行中
*He has a lot on at the moment．他這會兒有許多事要做。
*I found they had very important discussions on in the office at the moment．我發現他們那會兒正在辦公室討論很重要的事情。1．have to do with；be occupied with or engaged in有事要做；從事於；手中有事
*I have some hard work on hand．我手中正有一件艱難的工作要做。
*He'll be absent for the next few days because he has a sick mother on hand．他這幾天不能來了，因為他母親生病要他照料。
2．have for disposal or for sale有物要處理掉；有物待出售
*I have many extra copies of the magazine on hand；do you want some？這種雜誌我手頭有好多本，你想要一些嗎？
*He has many articles on hand．他有許多貨要出售。see or want nothing else but；give all one's attention to；be interested only in看中；獨鍾情於
*Of all the bicycles in the store，Jack had eyes only for the white one．商店中所有的自行車中，傑克只看上了那部白色的。
*The girl had her eyes on a yellow scarf and decided to buy it．這女孩看中一條黃顏色的頭巾，便決定把它買下來。
*Many girls liked Fred，but he had eyes only for Helen．許多女孩都喜歡弗雷德，但他只對海倫感興趣。have as much work as one can do；be very busy手頭工作很忙；無法分身
*The worker said that he had his hands full and could not take another job．這位工人說他手頭工作很忙，不能再做另外的工作。
*We shall have our hands full when the freshmen arrive．新生一到，我們就要大忙了。
*have one's/a hand in have a share in；participate in干涉；參與
*It is impossible that she could have had a hand in this notorious crime．她不可能參與這種罪惡勾當。want sth．very much；desire greatly十分想要
*Tim doesn't know what to do．His wife has her heart set on a fur coat for Christmas but he can't afford to buy it for her this year．蒂姆不知如何是好，他的妻子一心想買一件皮外衣過聖誕節，但是他今年買不起。get one's own way；do or obtain what one wishes（esp．against opposition or contrary advice）隨心所欲；按自己的意思辦事
*My wife always wants to have her own way，but this time，for a change，she is going to do what I say．我妻子總是按她自己的意願辦事，但是這次變了，她要按照我說的去辦。
*Let him have his own way．隨他去吧。
*have one's own way to make have to advance in life by one's own efforts自食其力；自立
*At the age of twelve，he was left penniless by the death of his father，so he had his own way to make．在12歲時，他父親就死了，分文沒有留給他，所以他只好自食其力。obtain what is desired如願以償；達到目的
*It is not good for a child to have his will in everything．讓孩子樣樣都得到滿足，並非好事。
*You have always had your will．你總是自行其是。1．have removed or extracted除去；拔掉
*My tooth was aching so much that I had to have it out．我有顆牙齒疼得很厲害，只好拔掉它。
2．invite sb．out請某人出去（參加活動、吃飯等）
*I'd like to have you out for dinner this evening．今晚我想請你去吃飯。
3．discuss or argue towards a conclusion討論或爭論出結果
*They had it all out last night and cleared the air a little．他們昨天晚上爭論有了結果，問題有所澄清。
*It's no use keeping your anger to yourself；let's have the whole matter out now．你生悶氣也沒有用，我們還是把整個事情說說清楚為好。
*I must have the whole matter out with them next time I see them．下次見到他們，我得把整個事情跟他們弄清楚。
*If you've got a complaint，the best thing is to see the person concerned and have it out with him．你如果有什麼意見，最好去找有關人員說個明白。
4．continue until complete繼續做完某事
*Let him have his sleep out；he's very tired．讓他睡個夠吧，他太累了。be concerned with與…有關
*He has to do with that matter．他同那件事有牽連。monopolize獨佔；霸佔
*You can't have all these apples to yourself．你不能一個人獨佔這麼多蘋果。
*You haven't paid the rent yet；you can't have the room to yourself．你還沒有付房租，不能獨佔這房間。overestimate；regard too highly過高地評價；過分尊重
*The teacher has too high an opinion of his own students．這位老師對他的學生估計過高。
*That engineer has too high an opinion of his own talents．那位工程師對自己的才能估計過高。have an alternative or choice有兩手準備
*You've made sure in both directions．It's always good to have two strings to one's bow．你已經在兩個方面都落實了。有兩手準備總是好的。1．bring；order or invite（sb．）up from a lower place（從較低的地方或把較低職位的人）請來；叫來
*The manager had the clerk up and reprimanded him for his constant carelessness．經理把職員召喚進來，指責他經常粗心大意。
*Shall we have the Greens up this weekend？這個週末咱們把格林夫婦請來好嗎？
*I had him up to see me，to explain what he was doing．我叫他上來見我，說明一下他在幹什麼。
2．bring up for investigation；cause to appear in court傳訊；把某人傳到法庭
*If you go on saying things like that about me，I'll have you up for slander．如果你繼續那樣說我，我就上法庭告你誹謗罪。
*He was had up by the police for dangerous driving．他因違章駕駛被警察傳去。
3．be aroused in使被激起
*He had his temper up and swore loudly．他發起脾氣來大聲咒罵。have effect on對…有影響；對…產生效力
*His opinions have great weight with us．他的意見對我們影響很大。dispute；quarrel爭執；爭論
*Every time they two get together they have words．他們倆一到一起就吵嘴。
*He had words with his wife last night．昨晚他和妻子發生口角。have-not
<<可數名詞>>look at for a moment看一看
*Take your hat off and let me have a look at it．把你的帽子摘下來讓我瞧瞧。have responsibility for負責
*He has charge of the project．他負責這個工程項目。Ha.vel
