(1) (因噪音等而提高聲音) 使別人聽得見自己的聲音
(2) 把自己的意見[主張]說給別人聽
won't [wouldn't] hear of [(美)to] ?
不聽從 [不願考慮,不允許,不贊同] …
My father won't ~ of it. 
我父親不會允許此事
I won't ~ of you [your] coming to meet me at the station. 
我怎麼也不讓你到車站來接我learn about聽說
*I've just heard about his illness．我剛聽說他病了。1．receive a letter from sb．收到信
*He hears from his son every month．他每個月都收到兒子來信。
2．receive a reprimand from受到…申斥
*You'll hear from your father when he gets home．你父親回家後要責罵你的。
*If the maid didn't have dinner ready，she would hear from him．如果女僕沒有把晚飯準備好，她會受到他的訓斥的。1．know about；be told of；hear mention of聽到；聽說
*How did you hear of our product？你怎麼聽說我們的產品的？
2．entertain the idea of；consent to；permit or listen to（usn．used in negative form）聽從；同意；准許；採納（常用否定結構）
*Mother just won't hear of such an idea．母親就是不同意這樣的主意。
*I would not hear of his complaint．我不想聽他的抱怨。
*I will not hear of you making a trip wirh him．我不會准許你和他一起去旅行。
*The soldiers were demanded to start off，but none of them would hear of parting with the villagers．戰士們接到命令出發，但是他們當中沒有人願意離開老鄉們。listen to the end聽完；聽到底
*Let's hear him out；don't interrupt him before he finishes telling the whole story．讓他把話講完，事情沒說完之前不要打斷他。
*Don't judge the man guilty without at least hearing his story out．你連這個人的話都沒有聽完，就不能判斷他有罪。
*We decided to hear him out before making any judgements on what he haddone．我們決定先聽他講完，再判斷他幹了什麼事。heard
