*The acrobatic show was so wonder ful that it hit us right between the  eyes．雜技表演非常精彩，給我們 留下了深刻的印象。
*It was a wonderfully lifelike pic ture and it hit Sol right between the  eyes．這是一幅非常美妙而逼真的 照片，給索爾印象極深。
*To learn that his parents had en dured poverty for his sake hit John  between the eyes．當得知他父母為 他吃了很多苦時，他大為驚訝。enjoy one another's company；be  happy and comfortable in each other's presence相處甚歡；氣味相投
*John and Mary hit it off from the very beginning．約翰和瑪麗一開始就相處得很好。
*I don't think those two will hit it off very well；both of them are  too quick tempered and too prone to  take offence．我想那兩個人不會 相處得很好，他倆都太性急，都太 容易生氣。hit man
<<可數名詞>>
(美俚)職業殺手1. imitate 模仿
*I am too stupid to hit off．我很 笨，不善模仿。
*He imitates voices，and can hit off some famous people beautifully．他模仿別人的講話聲音，而且能 把某些知名人物的講話聲音模仿 得極像。 
*He imitates animal calls and can hit off cows and sheep perfectly．他 會學動物叫，能逼真地模仿牛羊 的叫聲。
2．represent or describe cleverly巧 妙地描繪出
*In his new book he hits off the  American temperament with amazing insight．在他的新書裡他對美 國人性格的描繪表現了驚人的觀 察力。
*I never saw a character in a novel so thoroughly hit off．我從未見過 小說裡的人物被描寫得如此淋漓 盡致。
*She can hit off a poem，though she  is not educated．她雖然沒有受過 學校教育，但能即席作詩。
3．suit；be in harmony適合；符合
*Your proposal hits off with our plan．你的提議符合我們的計劃。
*The plan hits off with the present conditions．這個計劃與目前的條 件相符合。1．discover or think of sth． by lucky chance偶爾發現；偶然想到
*At last someone hit upon another road through the mountains．有人 終於發現了另一條穿山路。
*The scientist experimented for a long time before hitting upon the solution to his problem.這位科學家經過長期實驗才偶然發現這個問題的解決方法。
*I hit on a good idea．我想出了一個好主意。
2. choose by chance碰巧選擇
*He hit on a business that was just  starting to grow rapidly．他剛好 選擇了一個正在開始迅速發展的 行業。1. strike with the fists 用拳猛擊； 猛打
*He was hitting out right and left at his assailants．他左右開弓地回擊攻擊他的人。
2. attack violently in words抨擊
*The government wants us to hit out against corruption．政府要我們抨擊腐敗現象。
*The manager sat calmly and let his critics have their say，then he rose to his feet and in a spirited speech hit out at them.經理冷靜地坐著 聽批評者的發言，接著他站起來， 猛烈地回擊了他們。
*Several news commentators hit out at the president on his foreign policy．有幾位時事評論員猛烈抨擊總統的對外政策。
*He made a speech hitting out at  racial discrimination.他做了一次 演講，猛烈地抨擊種族歧視。hit parade
<<可數名詞>>
流行歌 [暢銷曲等] 的排行榜,暢銷曲目錄attain one's object； succeed達到目的；成功
*My brother hit the mark when he  purchased a quantity of cotton cloth just before the rise in the market. 我弟弟剛好趕在市場漲價之前購 進一批棉布，賺了大錢。
*Your answer just hit the mark．你 的答案正好擊中要害。get sth．exactly right；speak or act  in the most fitting or effective way  語言中肯；一針見血；恰到好處
*The teacher hit the nail on the head  when he said Bell's chief fault was  vanity．老師說比爾的主要毛病是 好虛榮，這實在是一針見血。
*Your criticism really hits the nail on  the head．你的批評恰到好處。
*The Mayor's talk on race relations  hit the nail on the head.市長談論種族關係時語言中肯。hit-and-miss
