我不贊成那個提案
hold 
?against a person 以…理由怨恨某人
She still ~s it against him that heblame；put the blame on責備；因…認為某人不好
*I can hold his failure against him because he never tried for a passing grade．他的失敗怪他自己，因為 他從來連及格的分數都不努力爭 取。 
*Do you hold it against Mary that she divorced you？瑪麗和你離婚， 你認為是瑪麗不好嗎？1．keep sth./sb.in place；prevent from 阻止
*Police horses were used to hold back the crowd．警方的馬隊被用來阻 止群眾。
*If I had not held him back， he would have beaten you soundly．要 不是我阻止了他，他一定把你痛 打一頓。
2． restrain oneself；control（sth．such as a feeling）克制；抑制（表 情）
*Jim held back his anger and avoided a fight．吉姆忍住了怒氣，避免了一場鬥毆。
*He was so impatient that I could not hold him back．他非常急躁，我制止不了他。
*I held myself back from saying a word．我克制自己不說一個字。
*Though very angry，I held back from telling him exactly what I thought.雖然非常生氣，但我能克制，未把我的真實想法告訴他。
3．delay 拖延Heavy rain on the road held us back．路遇大雨我們耽擱了。
*We can't hold the meal back for more than half an hour to wait for you．我們不能因為等你而把開飯時間推遲半小時以上。
4． retain possession of； keep back 保有；扣留
*He held the money back from his client.他把錢扣下不給當事人。
5．keep from（advancing to the next grade， stage， level， etc．）阻止（前進）；使留在（原級、原階段、原水平等）
*No one can hold back the wheel of history.誰也不能阻止歷史車輪前進。
*You show promise as a musician but your lack of practice is holding you back．你有希望成為音樂家，但你懶於練習，使你毫無進展。
6．stay back or away； show unwillingness；remain behind 走開；退縮；畏縮不前；猶豫不定
*When danger appeared，every one of them held back．當出現危險時，他們中每一個人都退縮了。
*We must never hold back before difficulties．我們在困難面前決不 退縮。
*She is very shy；she always holds back when we invite her to a party. 她很害差，我們請她去聚會時，她 總是猶豫不決。
7．conceal； keep（a secret， etc．）to oneself隱瞞；保守（秘密等）
*He told me most of the facts of the  affair，but I'm sure he's still holding back some important in formation．他對我講了那件事的大部分 情況，但我相信他仍保留了一些 重要的東西沒有告訴我。
*You shouldn't hold anything back  from us；we want to know the whole story．你不應有所隱瞞，我 們要知道全部事實。
*I could tell from his nervousness that he was holding back．看他局 促不安的樣子，我就知道他心裡 隱瞞了什麼事。1．adhere to；accept堅持；接受
*We'll hold by our decision.我們將 堅持我們的決定。
*He always holds by his own opinion．他總是堅持他自己的意見。
*I don't hold by such foolish ideas． 我不接受這類愚蠢的想法。
2．support；approve of 支持；扶 助；贊成；允許
*Although he did not hold by us， he honoured us.雖然他沒有支持我 們，但是他尊重我們。1． control or limit the freedom of；keep in obedience壓制；使服從
*Kings used to know very well how to hold down the people．國王很了 解如何使人民服從他們。
2． keep on the ground or in place 固定在地上或原地
*The police held the man down to prevent him escaping．警察把這人按倒在地上以防他逃跑。
*We must hold the tents down because of the strong wind．風很大，我們必須把帳篷固定住。
3． work satisfactorily at；keep（a job）順利地工作；保住（工作）
*Mr．Wang has held down the tough job for a long time．王先生幹這份艱苦的工作已經很長時間了。
*He seems to be unable to hold any job down．似乎他什麼工作都保不住。
*My father holds down quite a good job in the university．我爸爸在這所大學有份相當好的工作。
4.restrain；check ；control；keep at a low level壓制；壓低；控制；縮減
*Hold down the noise！將聲音放低一點。
*These measures helped to hold down traffic accidents．這些措施有助於減少交通事故。
*When Bob gets mad， you can't hold him down．鮑勃發火的時候，你無法控制他。
*We should hold down our expenditure．我們應該壓縮開支。
*Last year we had to hold down the enrolment because of the cuts in the grants．由於補助金減少，我們去年不得不壓縮招生人數。
5.take care of照應；照料
*Her neighbour held down her family duties while she was out on an errand．她出差期間，她的鄰居料理她的家務。1.offer； propose提出（供）
*The manager held forth a promise  of advancement to the more success ful salesmen．經理提出了要提拔 成績突出的推銷員的諾言。
*I have no idea to hold forth．我沒 有什麼意見可提。
*The director held forth a way to  do the job．主任提供了一種方法 去做這工作。
2.speak at length高談闊論
*The speaker held forth on the same  theme for at least two hours．演講 者就同一話題至少講了有兩個鍾 頭。
*He was holding forth on free trade．他在高談闊論自由貿易問 題。
*When we entered the auditorium，the speaker was holding forth on  the shortcomings of the young students．當我們進入大禮堂時，演講 者正在談論青年學生的缺點。
3．take place舉行；發生
*In winter， the three northeastern  provinces of our country are a region where a great variety of winter sports hold forth．在冬季，我 國東北3省是舉行各種各樣冬季 體育活動的好地方。
*hold good/true for  remain valid； effective有效；適用
*The firm's promise holds good for  all its products．該公司的承諾對 其各種產品均有效。
*These rules should hold good in many cases.這些規章制度應當在 許多情況下都適用。
*The contract holds good for five  years．這合同有效期為5年。
*Your remarks do not hold good in this case．你的話在這種場合不適 合。1．control or restrain控制；抑制
*Your horse is going too fast；you  must hold it in．你的馬跑得太快 了，你得勒住些。
*My mother is good at holding in her emotions．我母親很善於克制 自己的感情。
2．contain oneself； exercise restraint忍耐；克制自己
*He was raging inside，but held himself in for fear of saying something he would regret．他內心 很生氣，不過他忍著，生怕說出他 會後悔的話。
*He wanted to speak up but thought better of it and held in．他真想開 口說話，但仔細想想還是忍住了。1．（cause to） remain at a distance；be aloof（使）拉開距離；（使）不接 近；疏遠；冷漠
*His cold manner holds people off． 他的冷漠態度使人不敢接近。
*Finally he came to realize it was his haughtiness that held people off． 他終於意識到是他的傲慢態度使人不敢同他接近。
*Mr．Flynn holds off from everybody． I think he is shy．弗林先生遠離大家。我想他是害羞。
*The ship held off from the shore because of dangerous crosswinds.由於危險的側風，船沒有靠岸。
2．delay； postpone拖延；延期
*As so many different ideas were put forward，they had to hold off making the decision there and then．因為各種各樣的意見提了一大堆，所以他們當場只好不作決定。
*Jack held off paying for the television set until the dealer fixed it．傑克拖延到商家把電視機裝好才付錢。
3． resist 抵抗
*Our task is to hold off the enemy's attack for a few hours.我們的任務是將敵軍的進攻抵擋住幾小時。
*The police had difficulty in holding the fans off when the popstar was getting in the car．當那位流行歌星上汽車時，警察費了很大勁兒才把歌迷們阻擋住。
4． fail to appear（天氣）未出現；拖延
*The rain held off for the whole morning，although we had all expected a storm．雖然我們都預料到要有一場暴雨，但整個上午都沒有下下來。
*The weather forecast predicts that the rain will hold off till this evening．天氣預報說這場雨要到今天晚上才會下。1．grasp；hold tightly to sth．抓住
*Hold on to my hand while we cross the street．過馬路時，抓住我的手。
*It's pretty windy．You'd better hold on to your hat．風很大，你最好抓住你的帽子。
2．continue；go on繼續
*We held on our way．我們繼續趕路。
*Rain held on steadily all afternoon.雨下了整整一個下午。
3．wait and not hang up a telephone（電話）別掛掉
*When he left the telephone to find a pencil， he asked me to hold on．離開電話找鉛筆的時候，他讓我別掛掉。
*Could you hold on a minute？你能等一會兒，不要掛掉電話好嗎？
4． keep on with a business or job in spite of difficulties； endure不顧困難繼續經營；繼續堅持；忍受
*It was hard to keep the store going during the depression， but he held on and at last met with success．經濟不景氣時生意很難維持，但是他繼續經營，最後終於成功。
*If he can just hold on a little longer， we can get help to him．如果他能再堅持一會兒，我們就可以幫助他了。
*The soldiers held on in that isolated position for more than two hours.戰士們孤軍奮戰，堅持了兩個多小時。
5．wait a minute；stop（usu．used as a command）等一下；停止（常用於命令式）
*Hold on！I can't hear what you are saying．等一等！我聽不清楚你在說什麼。
*Just hold on a second while I get  my breath back．等一下，讓我喘口 氣。1． hold tightly抓住
*Hold on to my arm on this icy surface．過有冰的路面時抓牢我的 胳膊。
2.stick to堅持 
*If we believe something is true and  good we should hold on to it.如果 我們認為某事既真又好就應該堅 持下去。
3. stay in control of控制；抑制I was so frightened that I had to hold on to myself not to scream．我 非常害怕以致於不得不控制自己 不尖叫出聲。
*He was very angry but he had to hold on to his temper．他非常氣憤但又不得不控制自己不發脾氣。1． cease breathing for a short time  屏息 We held our breath when listening  to her song，我們屏息聽她唱歌。
*The race was so close that everyone  was holding his breath at the fin ish．賽跑競爭激烈，快到終點時每 個人都屏息著。
2． endure great anxiety， nervousness or excitement忍受著憂慮、緊 張或感到興奮
*He held his breath for days before  he got word that he was accepted by that college．在那所大學錄取 他之前，他緊張憂慮了好些天。maintain one's position；refuse to  retreat or surrender堅持自己的地 位或立場；不讓步
*Throughout the debate he firmly  held his ground and won out in the end．在整個辯論中，他堅持一步 不讓，終於得勝了。
*Our troops held the ground bravely．我們的部隊勇敢地堅守陣地。maintain one's position and be equal to it， usn． under stress守住 陣地；堅持立場；沒有失敗（失利、 惡化）
*He is a skilled debater， and can  hold his own against any opponent. 他是個熟練的辯論家，能在任何對手面前堅持自己的立場，從不 失敗。
*Mary had a hard time after the operation， but soon she was holding her own．瑪莉手術後身體很弱， 但很快她就康復了。
*John's parents have never worried  about him；even as a small boy he  proved that he could hold his own in any situation.約翰的父母親從 不為他擔心，甚至在他還是一個 小男孩時，就顯示他在任何情況 下都能挺得住。be silent and not speak against sth．； keep quiet沉默不發表意見
*I did not agree with the manager，but held my peace as he was rather angry．我不同意經理的意見，但 是由於他很生氣，我只好保持沉 默。remain silent； say nothing of what one knows保持沉默；守口如瓶； 住嘴
*You had better hold your tongue． 你最好不要開口。
*If people would hold their tongues  from unkind speech，fewer people would be hurt.人們如果都能保持 不饒舌，很多人就不會受到傷害。
*「Hold your tongue！」he said．「住 嘴！」他說。1．stretch forward；extend延伸； 伸出
*They were ready to hold out a friendly hand．他們準備伸出友 誼之手。Hold your arms out．將兩臂伸出。
2.offer（usu．promise，hope，likelihood，etc．）提供（允諾、希望、可能性等）
*These were the promises they held out．這些是他們許下的諾言。
*I can hold out no hope of the invalid recovering．我認為這位病人 康復無望。
*Some hope was held out by the chairman that the financial position of the company would improve．董 事長認為，該公司的財政情況有 好轉的希望。
3. prove to be sufficient夠用；能維持（下去）
*How long will our supplies hold out？我們的給養能維持多久？
*I will stay in Maxico as long as my  money holds out．只要我的錢夠 用，我將一直呆在墨西哥。
4．continue to operate繼續運轉
*I think the engine will hold out till  we get home，then I can have it  seen to．我想這發動機可繼續工作 到我們回到家，然後我可檢查一 下。
5． resist； continue in spite of diffi culties抵抗；（不畏困難地）繼續
*The town was surrounded， but the  citizens held out until help at last  came．城市被圍困，但居民們能頑 強堅持到最後得救。
*The sailor held out against the  strong wind and big waves for two  days and nights．這水手在大風大 浪中挺了兩天兩夜。
*The regiment held out against the  enemy until reinforcements ar rived．這個團堅持頂住敵人直到 增援部隊的到來。
6．survive；last生存；堅持 We must hurry，because the  trapped miner cannot hold out  much longer．我們得快點，受困的 礦工不能再堅持多久了。
7． refuse to agree or settle（until  one's wishes have been agreed to） 拒絕同意或妥協（直到某人的要 求被接受）
*The strikers held out for a raise of five cents an hour．罷工者堅持要 求每小時提高工資5美分決不妥 協。1．postpone延期；推遲
*The meeting was held over until next week．會議延期到下一周。
*Let's hold the matter over until the next meeting， because it's too late to begin a discussion on it now．咱們把這個問題推遲到下次會上再討論吧，現在太晚了，不能對這個問題展開討論了。
*The directors held over their decision until they could get more in formation.董事會決定延期，等到有更多的信息時再作決定。
2． continue or keep until a later time期滿後繼續延長
*They are going to hold that movie over for another week．他們打算延長一周繼續放映那部電影。
*The old treasurer held over for six months when the new treasurer died suddenly．新任會計突然死亡，老會計繼續留任6個月。
*Miss Wang will hold over till a successor is appointed.王小姐將留任到繼任者上任為止。
*The actors cannot be held over without additional pay．不付額外工資演員們是不可能超期再演出的。
3.keep保存
*Please hold over the rest of the goods．請保存其餘貨物。
4．threaten；use…as a threat以某事威脅
*He is holding my past record over me．他用我過去的檔案記載來威脅我。
*He knows I have been to prison and is holding it over me．他知道我坐過牢，就以此要挾我。
*hold still remain quiet； not move靜止
*How can I take your picture if you don't hold still？如果你不安靜下來，我怎麼能給你照相呢？1．abide by or adhere to堅持；固守
*Whatever your argument，I'll hold to my decision．不管你有什麼理由，我將堅持我的決定。
*He held to everything he said at the meeting despite the fact that several persons contradicted him．他不顧好幾個人反對，堅持他在會上的發言。
*The boy held to his explanation； he would not admit it was wrong.那*  男孩堅持他的解釋，不承認那是錯的。
2．insist that one keep（a promise or a bargain， etc．）堅持要某人執行（允諾、契約等）
*He has made a bargain，and I shall hold him to it．他已講好了條件，我要堅持讓他履行。
*You've made such a promise，and should be held to it．你們既然作了這樣的允諾，就必須履行。
*「You can have the car when I go abroad．」「I'll hold you to that．」「我出國時，你可以使用我的汽車。」「希望你說話算數。」
3. seize抓住
*The storm was so severe that even the sailors had to hold to the ropes．風暴特大，就是水手也得抓住繩索。1.support；raise舉起；抬；拿
*My husband has lost so much weight that he has to wear a belt to hold his thousers up.我丈夫體重減了好多，他只好用根帶子把褲子提起來。
2．prove true；prove effective or accurate證明屬實；證明準確、正確
*The police were doubtful at first，but that worker's story held up．警察起初懷疑，但那位工人的敘述證明情況屬實。
*The weather forecasts don't always hold up．天氣預報並不總是那麼準確。
*The contract will hold up for ten years．這合同有效期10年。
3．remain good；not get worse保持不衰；不壞
*Sales held up well．銷售情況不衰。
4. support；keep from falling承受住；不倒
*Don't worry．The house will hold up.別擔心，房子不會倒下。
*The chair was too weak to hold you up．這椅子不牢，經受不住你的體重。
*How does he hold up under such a responsibility？他怎麼能承受住這麼大的責任？
5. keep up跟得上；不掉隊
*Though it was a long walk，the youngsters held up until the last minute．雖然這是長途跋涉，但是孩子們一直跟到最後，沒有掉隊。
6． keep one's courage or spirit up；remain calm；keep control of oneself振作精神；穩定情緒；自己控制自己
*The grieving mother held up for her children's sake．這位傷心的母親為了孩子們在控制自己的情緒。
7．stop for a short time；delay暫時停止；停頓；延續
*The policeman held up the traffic to allow pedestrians to cross the road．警察擋住車輛讓行人過街。
*Work on the building site has been held up by bad weather．由於天氣惡劣，建築工地上的作業被延誤了。
*We were held up for nearly an hour on our way by the traffic accident．我們在路上被交通事故耽擱近一個小時。
*The steel strike may hold up production for several months，鋼鐵工人的罷工會使生產停頓數月之久。
8. rob搶劫
*The criminals held up the plane and took all the passengers'money．這些歹徒劫持了飛機，並將乘客的錢財洗劫一空。
*That bank has been held up threetimes．那家銀行被搶了3次。
9. show…as an example提出（作為榜樣）
*He was held up to the students as a model of emulation.他被提出來作為學生的楷模。
*Our English teacher held up excellent models of composition for her class to imitate．我們的英語老師在班上展出了優秀作文讓同學們模仿。
10．last；maintain in a state持續；維持；堅持；挺住
*I think the car will just about hold up till we reach London.我認為這輛車能差不多正好讓我們開到倫敦。
*Mr．Black holds up very well， in spite of all the trouble and illness he's had．布萊克先生儘管遇到了 許多麻煩而且又生病，但是他挺 住了，過得不錯。
*Smith's bank could hardly hold up in the depression史密斯的銀行在 經濟蕭條期間很難堅持下去。prove true；stand testing； bear examination證明是正確的；經得起 考驗；站得住腳
*None of his arguments seemed to me to hold water．我覺得他的論點一條也站不住腳。
*It sounds a good idea but onlywhen we try it out can we see if it holds water.這個主意聽上去不 錯，不過，只有通過實踐才能知道 它是否是正確的。
*His argument can hold water all right．他的論點很有道理。1． be in agreement with； approve of同意；贊成
*I don't hold with his pessimistic views．我不同意他的悲觀看法。
*I hold with you that young people  should dare to think，dare to speak and dare to act．我同意你的看法， 年輕人應該敢想、敢說、敢幹。
*We do not hold with heavy drinking and wild parties．我們不贊成 酗酒和放蕩的聚會。
2． tolerate； forgive容忍；原諒
*I won't hold with such lawless acts． 我不能原諒這種目無法紀的行 為。
*He is so insupportable that even his wife can't hold with him．他實在 不能讓人容忍，連他的妻子都不 能原諒他。make oneself quiet and peaceful；not become angry平靜；不生氣； 不激動
*The meeting would have gone  smoothly if the director had kept his temper．要是主任不激動的話， 那個會議本來是會開得順利的。hold.all
