in the circumsall together；as a group全體
*They moved forward in a body． 他們全體向前進。
*They resigned in a body．他們集 體辭職。
*The delegates came into the assembly hall in a body．代表們一起步 入會議大廳。without any progress無進展；無結 果
*He seemed to be working hard，but  was．just running around in a cir cle．他似乎工作很努力，但還是干 不出什麼結果來。
*The committee debated for two  hours，just talking in circles.委員 會辯論了兩個小時，但仍然毫無 結果。likely to；with every likelihood of  很有可能；有相當把握
*The young man is in a fair way to  succeed．那年輕人很有成功的希 望。
*He had come back to England in a  fair way of making money．他回 到英國來有相當把握會賺到錢。
*The doctor thinks that his patient is in a fair way to recover．醫生認為 他的病人有恢復健康的希望。1． as if belonging to the family；informally如同家人；不客氣；不 拘禮節地
*We'll ask him and his wife to come  over in a family way and dine with  some other friends．我們將邀請他 和他妻子一起來不拘禮節地和其 他朋友一起吃飯。
2． going to have a baby懷孕；快 要生孩子了
*Susan is in a family way. 蘇珊快 要生孩子了。suddenly；immediately突然地；剎 那間
*The boy got over the fence in a flash and started running down the road．剎那間，那個男孩越過籬 笆，沿路飛奔而去。mentally confused糊里糊塗
*I wonder why he always seems to be in a fog．我不知道為什麼他似 乎總是糊里糊塗。having brightness of color容光煥發；紅光滿面
*The children came in from play in a glow．孩子們玩得滿面通紅地 跑了進來。anxious to act or move quickly慌 張地
*He was in a hurry to leave．他匆 匆忙忙地離開了。
*The composition was written in a hurry；I have to go over it again.那篇作文是匆匆忙忙寫出來的，我得再看一遍。
*Nothing is ever done in a hurry．匆匆忙忙是辦不成事的。to a certain degree；somewhat在某種程度上；在某種意義上
*The work is in a manner done already．這工作大體上可以算是完 成了。very soon；in an instant即刻；馬上；立即
*I'll finish the work in a moment．我馬上就做完這件事。
*He'll be over in a moment．他馬上就來。in the briefest time立刻；不一會兒
*If you shout in the valley， and in a second the echo will come from the hillside with great distinctness．如 果你在山谷中大叫一聲，不一會兒就能聽到從山邊傳來非常清楚的回音。in a way；in one respect在某種意義上
*What you say is true in a sense．你 所說的在某種意義上是對的。
*In a sense，arithmetic is a language．從某種意義上說，算術是 一種語言。1．to a certain extent；a little；somewhat在某種程度上；有幾分
*Your composition is well done in a way．你的作文在某種程度上寫得很成功。
*I like Jane in a way，but she doesn't like me．我在某種程度上喜歡簡，但是她不喜歡我。
2.in one thing就一方面而論；從一方面看
*In a way，it is an important book．從某一方面來說，這是本重要的 書。
3．agitated；much concerned 激動；憂慮
*Mr． Smith is in a way about his son's misbehavior.史密斯先生對於他兒子的不良行為頗為焦慮。in summary；in short總而言之；簡言之
*In a word，if we want to do our work well， we must make preparations carefully.總之，如果我們想把工作做好，就要好好準備。
*In a word， matters are going from bad to worse.總之，情況越來越壞。
*In a word， while the prospects are bright，the road has twists and turns．總之，前途是光明的，道路是曲折的。

to sum up briefly 簡言之；總之
*In a word，I have no objection．總之，我不反對。in ab.sen.ti.a
