(=forever; to eternity)altogether共計
*There were in all a hundred persons present.共計有10O人參加。
*The tickets we had bought num bered twelve in all．我們總共買了 12張票。
*There are twenty in all．總計20 個。very likely很有可能
*In all likelihood I'll be away for  Shanghai for two weeks．很可能 我要去上海兩周。in every case or respect在各方面
*They resembled one another in all  respects．他們在許多方面都彼此 相似。in an effort to為了
*Her father sent her to the warm  south in an attempt to restore her health．她父親把她送往溫暖的南 方，希望她恢復健康。immediately； very soon立即；立刻
*The operator touched the key，and in an instant the message was at its destination．話務員一按鍵，信息立即就到達目的地了。
*The mother told her child to stay in the room， saying that she would be back in an instant.母親叫孩子留 在房間裡，說她馬上就會回來的。
*He heard the news and started off  in an instant．他聽到消息立刻動 身。in and out
1 進進出出地
2 徹底地; 完全地
investigate something ~ 
