1． coming in and going out often  進進出出；來來去去
*There is no hope for Jim．He's  been in and out of prison for ten  years running．吉姆沒希望了，他 進出監獄已連續 10年之久了。
*He was very busy Saturday and  was in and out all day．星期六他 非常忙碌，終日進進出出忙個不 停。
*He's always in and out of hospital． 他時常生病住院。
2．thoroughly；completely徹底地 We know each other in and out．我 們彼此非常瞭解。
*He understands his business in and out．他對自己的業務非常熟悉。in reply to應…而；響應；回答
*He only shrugged his shoulders in answer to the question．他對問題的 回答只是聳了聳肩而已。
*The doctor came at once in answer to my telephone．醫生接了我的電 話立即就來了。
*In answer to her shouts people ran out to help．人們一聽到她的叫喊 聲都跑出來幫忙了。expected；awaited；prepared for  預期；期待；預備
*I have a journey to the White Mountains in anticipation.我預計 將到白山旅遊。in expectation of； in view of期望； 預期；鑒於
*All troops have been mobilized in  anticipation of the coming war.全 軍動員以應付即將來臨的戰爭。at all events；whatever happens無 論如何
*In any event I'll call you before I  make a final decision．不管怎樣， 我在作出最後決定前會打電話給 你的。
*In any case， you must get here no later than five o'clock，無論如何， 你務必5點鐘前到達這裡。in between
在兩者之間; 在兩端之間in print or writing；written on paper印刷；書寫；白紙黑字
*They insisted on having the agree ment written down in black and  white．他們堅持要把協議用白紙 黑字寫下來。
*You must have your statement in black and white．你得把你的聲明 寫下來。in short；briefly簡（而）言之
*It's a long letter， but in brief， he says「No．」 這是封長信，但簡單地 說，他就是「不同意。」
*He gave in brief the story of the storm.他扼要地談了風暴的情 況。in cam.er.a
[In`kamˏrә; inˋkamŋrʌ]
1 私下 (會議) ; 秘密的
2 『法律』不公開審訊的; 秘密庭的if 如果；若
*In case he arrives be fore I get back，please ask him to wait．如果 我回來前他就到了，請叫他等我。
*In case it rains，do not expect me． 如果天下雨，就不要指望我來了。
*in case of in the event of； as for要是；在… 時（候）In case of fire，the alarm bell．如遇火災，即按警鈴。
*In case of any difficulty，call me at once．如有任何困難，立即找 我。
*In case of illness， you must consult a doctor．假使有病，你必須請醫 生診治。having the care or management負 責
*Who is in charge here？誰是這兒的 負責人？
*He'll take this affair in charge．他將主管這件事。
*Professor Chen is in charge of scientific research in our department． 陳教授負責我們系的科研工作。
*He is a teacher in charge of our class．他是負責我們班的老師。held back；controlled在控制中； 被阻止
*I advise you to hold your temper in check．奉勸你不要發脾氣。
*Mary couldn't hold her feelings in  check any longer and began to cry． 瑪麗再也控制不了她的感情而哭 了起來。1．at the head；in or having the  highest place or authority 居首；有 最高之權位
*He was a commander in chief．他 過去是總司令。
2. most of all； especially主要；尤 其
*He has many good points but in  chief his modesty．他有很多優點， 其中最主要的是他很謙虛。
*He did it for many reasons，and  this one is in chief．他所以這樣 做，原因很多，這個原因是最主要 的。cruelly；ruthlessly殘酷地；殘忍地
*The dictator，in cold blood，or dered the execution of all his ene mies．那位獨裁者殘酷地下令將 他所有的敵人處死。
*The robbers shot in cold blood ev erybody who was in their way．搶 劫者殘忍地槍殺了所有阻擋他們 的人。1．shared equally相同；相似
*We have very little in common in our taste．我們的嗜好相同處很 少。
2． for or by all共有的；公用的
*We have everything in common.我 們什麼都是共用的。
*We have a kitchen in common.我們 的廚房是共用的。in the same way as；like相同；相 似
*He believed，in common with the majority，that it was true．他同多 數人一樣，認為那是真的。
*They have nothing in common with each other．他們之間毫無共同之 處。when compared with同…比較
*Yangzhou is much smaller in comparison with Beijing．揚州同北京比起來小多了。
*The tallest buildings in London are small in comparison with the skyscrapers in New York．同紐約的摩天大樓比較，倫敦的最高建築物還是算矮的。complying with聽從；依從；按照
*She gave up the idea compliance  with her parents'desire．她依從父 母的願望放棄了自己的想法。
*They will set up another middle school in this area in compliance with the wishes of the people. 他們將根據人們的願望在這一地區再另建一所中學。lastly最後；在結束時
*In conclusion，I world like to thank you for your coming to the meeting.最後，我對各位出席這次會議表示感謝。
*In conclusion，I'd like to say how much I've enjoyed staying in your beautiful country.最後，我想說說我呆在你們這個美麗的國家裡是多麼愉快。in good health；physically fit健康狀況良好；身體條件適合
*People who take part in sports must keep in condition.參加體育鍛煉的人健康狀況一定是好的。
*You must train regularly to be in condition.你應該經常鍛煉以保持良好的體魄。secretly；privately秘密地；私下地
*I'm telling you this in confidence；please don't tell anyone else.這件事我只告訴你一個人，請別告訴別人。in agreement，accordance or harmony with；according to；in obedience to；in compliance with同意；遵照；依據；聽從
*His action was in conformity with the law．他的行為是合法的。
*All these are entirely in con formity with the interests and aspirations of the people of our two countries．這一切完全符合我們兩國人民的利益和願望。
*We should build our country in conformity with the principle of achieving greater，faster，better and more economical results．我們應按照多、快、好、省的原則建設我們的國家。together with與…共同；連用
*He runs a store in conjunction with his relative．他同親戚共同經營一家商店。regarding；relating to關於；同…有關
*He asked many questions in connection with life in Britain．他問了許多有關英國生活的問題。
*The meeting is in connection with a proposal to construct a new swimmingpool．這個會議是討論一項建造新游泳池的建議。
*We are working on the project in connection with another firm．我們正與另一家公司共同建設這項工程。
*in consequence as a result； therefore結果
*His conduct was bad， in consequen ce， he was dismissed．他行為不軌，因而被開除了。
*You studied hard， and in consequence you passed the test．你學習很努力，所以考試通過了。as a result of由於…原因
*In consequence of the deep snow，school will not open today．由於雪很深，學校今天停課。
*In consequence of your bad behaviour I'm forced to dismiss you．由於你行為不軌，我只好解雇你。1．after thinking about and weighing；in view of； because of考慮到；由於
*In consideration of the boy's young age，the judge did not put him in jail for carrying a gun．考慮到這小孩尚年輕，法官不因他攜槍而判他入獄。
*They didn't give him heavy work in consideration of his youth．鑒於他年幼，他們不給他繁重的工作。
2． in return for報酬
*We paid him well in consideration of his labour．我們給他優厚的工資，作為他的勞動報酬。
*In consideration of the extra work he had done，his boss gave him extra pay．考慮到他做了額外的工作，他的老闆付給他額外的酬金。
*I presented him with a Chinese painting in consideration of his assistance．我送給他一幅中國畫以酬謝他的幫助。owing欠…的債
*He is in debt to all his friends．他欠所有朋友的債。
*He is heavily in debt．他債台高築。minutely詳細地；詳盡地
*There isn't time to explain in detail．沒有時間詳細闡述。
*The teacher explained the text in detail．老師詳細解釋了課文。at the exact time及時
*He arrived in due time．他及時趕到了。
*Spring and summer will arrive in due time．春季夏季會適時來臨的。serious（ly）認真的／地
*Her parents thought the girl was joking when she said she wanted to be a scientist，but she was in earnest．這女孩說她想當一名科學家，她父母認為她是在開玩笑，但她卻是認真的。
*Surely you are not in earnest in saying that，are you？你說那話不是當真的，是嗎？
*Did you say it in earnest？你那樣講是當真的嗎？1．in fact實際上
*The two methods are in effect identical．這兩種方法實際上是一樣的。
2．（of law）become active（法律）生效
*These regulations are still effect．這些規定仍然有效。
*The law remains in effect．這條法律仍然有效。mistaken；wrong弄錯
*He has sent the book to you in error．他把書錯寄給你了。
*You were in error in assuming that he would wait for us．你誤以為他會等我們。in es.se
[In`ZsI; inˋәsi]
