<<形容詞>>
實際存在地[的]
(cf. in posse)in its nature；as a matter of fact在本質上；實質上
*In essence，both proposals are much the same．這兩個建議實質上是差不多的。
*Officially he is in charge，but in fact his secretary does all the work．從職位上講是他負責，但實際上，他的秘書做所有的工作。easily seen明顯；顯而易見
*She's the sort of woman who likes to be very much in evidence．她是個特愛出風頭的女人。
*Smith was nowhere in evidence．史密斯無論在何處都不惹人注意。
*The tulips are blooming；spring was in evidence．鬱金香盛開，春天顯然到了。exchanging for（以…）交換
*I gave him my used textbooks and received a dictionary in exchange．我把舊課本給了他，換得了一本字典。existing現有（的）；存在的
*This is the largest ship in existence．這是現有的最大的船。
*Many species of animals which once lived on the earth are no longer in existence．有許多動物曾一度在地球上生存過，但今天已不復存在了。in ex.ten.so
