臨死之時; 在危急狀態中in f.
in the end; finally; in short; to sum upactually；really；indeed實際上
*I think so；in fact，I'm quite sure．我想是這樣，事實上我十分相信是這樣。1． in support of贊成；支持
*Are you in favour of the proposal？你贊成這個建議嗎？
*The students were in favour of reform．學生們都贊成改革。
*Everyone in the class voted in favour of the dancing party．班裡的每個人都投票贊成開舞會。
2．to the advantage of；helping有利於
*The evidence is in favour of the defendant．證據對被告有利。
*Price control would gradually dis appear in favour of a free market．價格控制將逐漸消失而代之以自由市場。
*The law is in favour of the poor people．這條法律有利於窮苦人。
*Prices are in buyers' favor．價格對買主有利。
3．be paid to支付；以…為收款人
*Cheques should be drawn in favour of the treasurer．開支票應以會計為收款人。
*Please make out your checks in favour of the corporation．開支票時，請寫明本公司為收款人。in flagrante delicto
『拉』當場
(=in blazing crime,現行犯)1．have power；become law生效
*The system of conscription has been in force for many years．徵兵制度已經實行好多年了。
*The treaty shall remain in force for a period of ten years．這條約的有效期為10年。
*New timetable is in force．新的時間表現在生效。
2．a great number of；in a large group大批；大量
*The enemy is in force behind the hill．敵人在山後集結了大量兵力。in for.ma pau.pe.ris
