『拉』將來; 此後
(=in the future)1．as a rule；usually 通常；照例
*In general，your suggestion is good．你的建議總的來說是好的。
*I am speaking of students in general．我說的是一般學生。
*The weather in Florida is warm in general．佛羅里達的天氣通常是溫暖的。
*In general， the bus is here by 9 a．m．通常公共汽車是9點前到達這裡。
2．for the most part；in most cases 大多數
*Boys in general like outdoor sports more than girls do．大多數男孩比女孩愛好戶外運動。systematically arranged（放置）整齊地
*She kept everything in the room in good order．她把房間收拾得井然有序。1． on time準時
*We arrived in good time．我們準時到達。
*The students finished their school work in good time．學生們按時完成了作業。
2．immediately趕快；立即
*Get the letter off in good time．趕快把這封信寄出去。in two； into halves 分成兩半
*The party is likely to split in half．這個黨有可能分裂成兩派。
*The cake was cut in half．餅子被切成了兩半。in a joyous mood高興
*All of us were in high spirits when we heard the good news．聽到那則好消息，我們大家都很高興。as an honour to； for showing respect or thanks to尊敬；向…表示敬意
*We celebrate Mother's Day in honour of our mothers．我們慶祝母親節是對母親表示敬意。
*The city dedicated a monument in honour of the general．該市為對這位將軍表示敬意建造了一個紀念碑。
*A great banquet was held in honour of our distinguished guests．我們為貴賓舉行了一次盛大的宴會。according to； consistent with按照；協調（一致）
*A good man's actions are in keeping with his promises．正直人的言行一致。in a large amount大量地
*He buys cotton in large quantities．他買進大量棉花。in li.mi.ne
