《源自拉丁文 'in memory (of) ' 的意思》<<介係詞>>
為紀念…; 為追悼…
(英國桂冠詩人但尼生 (Tennyson) 為追悼親友 Hallam 之死而寫的詩)keeping alive the memory（為）紀念
*They are going to erect a monument in memory of the men who laid down their lives in defense of their country．他們將樹碑紀念為保衛祖國而獻身的人們。
*A monument has been erected in memory of their beloved teacher．為了紀念他們敬愛的老師，他們已經樹起了一塊紀念碑。in appearance or by title名義上
*She is the president of the association only in name．她只不過是這個協會的名義上的主席。
*The old man is a doctor in name only． He does not have patients now．這位老人僅僅是掛空名的醫生。目前他沒有任何病人。in poverty；in difficulty 在貧困中；在困難中
*A friend in need is a friend indeed．患難朋友才是真朋友。
*He is in great need．他非常貧窮。not inclined沒有心情
*I am in no mood to make up a story about Santa Claus．我沒有心情編造一個關於聖誕老人的故事。
*She seems worried about something and is in no mood for joking today．她今天像是惦記著什麼事情似的，沒有心思說笑。not at all並不；毫不
*The older boy is in no sense wiser than the younger one．那個歲數大的男孩一點也不比那個歲數小的聰明。very quickly；very soon很快地；不久
*With a pair of scissors， she can turn out a beautiful design in no time．用一把剪刀，她可以立即剪出一個美麗的花樣來。
*Take this medicine，and it will cure you in no time．吃了這種藥，你的病馬上就會好的。
*They finished the work in no time at all．他們立刻完成了這項工作。under no circumstances； never決不；並不
*Your plan is in no way different from ours．你們的計劃與我們的計劃並沒有什麼不同。
*He is in no way superior to me in knowledge．他在知識方面並不比我強。
*She is in no way to blame．她完全不應該受責備。by no means；in no manner毫不；絕不
*He has in no wise changed his opinion．他絲毫沒有改變他的看法。
*He'll in no wise lose his reward．他決不會失去他應得的報酬。in nu.bi.bus
[In`njubIbєs, -`nu-; inˋnju:bibәs, -nˋnu:-]
『拉』未定的; 未實現的in sum total；altogether總計；共計
*One's bosom friends are always few in number．知己的朋友總是很少的。
*We were ten in number．我們一共10人。obeying服從
*You should act in obedience to the decisions of the Party organization．你必須服從黨組織的決定。
*Soldiers act in obedience，to the orders of their officers．士兵們總是服從軍官命令的。in one's own manner； freely按自己的方式；自由地
*They can act in their own way．他們可以按自己的辦法行事。opposite to反對；同…相反（的）
*What he has done is in opposition to his wishes．他事與願違。having sth．neatly arranged整理好；井然有序；保持整潔
*The books are kept in alphabetical order．這些書是以字母順序放好的。
*He put his papers in order before he left the office．離開辦公室前，他把文件整理好。for the purpose of為了
*Come early in order that you may see him．要想見到他，你就得早來。
*He ran in order to catch the train．他跑著趕這趟火車。（of lines） continuing at the same distance from one another（線條）彼此平行
*The trees stand in parallel with the road．樹長得與路平行。partly；to an extent部分地；（在）某種程度（上）
*His success is in part owing to luck．他的成功在某種程度上是由於走運。
*It is in part your own fault that you have failed．你的失敗有一部分是你自己的過錯造成的。especially特別地；尤其是
*I remember one of them in particular．我特別記住了他們之中的一位。
*I am interested in stories in general，and in detective stories in particular．我總的來說對小說感興趣，尤其是對偵探小說感興趣。
*Are you doing anything in particular tonight？你今晚有什麼特別的事要做嗎？
*There are so many books here．Why do you like that one in particular？這裡有這麼多書，你為什麼特別喜歡那一本？personally親自
*Will you apply for the position by letter or in person？你申請那個工作是親自去還是寫信去？
*I can't attend the meeting in person， but I'll send someone to speak for me．我不能親自出席會議，但是我將派人替我發言。
*You had better go and speak to him in person．你最好親自去跟他談。in per.so.nam
