『拉』秘密地 (指教皇未在教廷參議院提名而逕行任命樞機主教) ; 私下地1．in correct order or position（在）適當的（位置）；各得其所
*She likes to have everything in place．她喜歡把什麼事都安排得井井有條。
*Please take a look and see if everything is in place．請看看是否一切都安排妥當了。
*Please put all the books in place on the shelf after you finish reading them．看完書後請放回書架原處。
2．suitable適當的
*We don't think your suggestion is quite in place．我們認為你的建議不很恰當。as much as or more than is needed；a large number of富裕；充足；大量
*There are good books in plenty．有大量的優秀書籍。indeed；truly；really事實上
*She told you she'd seen it，but in point of fact，she wasn't really there．她告訴你說她親眼看到此事，實際上她根本不在場。in pos.se
[In`pәsI; inˋpˏsi]
《源自拉丁文》<<副詞>>
<<形容詞>>
可能地[的]
(=in possibility or capacity)
(cf. in esse)having or controlling；occupying 佔有；具有
*The old professor is in possession of many books．這位老教授擁有大量的書籍。
*Our library is in possession of several sets of encyclopaedias．我們圖書館存有好幾部百科全書。
*Peter is in possession of the house which belonged to his father．彼得現在佔用原來屬於他父親的房子。1． practising；in fact實踐中；實際上
*They have rich experience in practice．他們有豐富的實踐經驗。
*Your idea sounds good but will it work in practice？你的主意很好，但它能實現嗎？
2．in proper condition to do sth．well through practice在不斷練習中
*The iceskater keeps in practice by skating every day．這位溜冰者每天練習溜冰。
*A pianist gets his fingers in practice by playing scales．鋼琴家練習音節，磨練手指的靈活。in prae.sen.ti
[Inpri`zZntaI; inpri:ˋzˏntai]
『拉』現在; 目前
(=at the present time)praising讚揚；表揚
*Much has been said in praise of our monitor．人們說了許多讚揚我們班長的話。
*Everyone of us spoke in praise of her heroism．我們大家都讚揚她的英雄行為。as a general rule；as a matter of principle 大體上；原則上
*I agree with you in principle．我原則上同意你的意見。
*This，in principle，is a good project，but we need to go further into the details．這個計劃大體上是好的，但在細節方面我們還得作進一步的推敲。privately；secretly私人地；秘密地
*I wish to talk to you in private．我想同你私下談談。in relation to the degree與…成比例
*Each man's pay will be in proportion to his work．每個人的報酬將與其工作成比例。
*His expenditure is not in proportion to his income．他的支出與收入不平衡。
*The house is tall in proportion to its width．按照寬度來說這房子是很高的。in pro.pri.a per.so.na
[In`propriєpә`sonә; inˋproupri:әpә:ˋsounә]
『拉』親自; 自身
(=in one's own person)near to 接近；靠近；臨近
*His house is in close proximity to a park．他的住宅毗鄰公園。openly；publicly公開地
*Don't quarrel with each other in public，will you？不要在大庭廣眾之下吵架，好不好？
*He is nervous in public．他在公開場合很緊張。
*He doesn't like to speak in public．他不願當眾講話。act of pursuing 追求；追趕；追捕
*They immediately set out in pursuit of the enemy．他們立即出動，追擊敵人。
*The police car raced through the streets in pursuit of another car．警車在街上急馳，追趕另一輛汽車。
*He does it in pursuit of health．他為了健康而做這事。under consideration or discussion 正被談論或考慮的
*Where is the man in question？ 剛剛談到的這個人在哪兒？
*Here are the two students in question．這就是我們所談到的兩個學生。
*The book in question was published in 1990．該書是1990年出版的。in re
[In`ri; inˋri:]
『拉、法律』關於
(=in the matter of ; in regard to ; concerning)actually；in fact實際上；其實
*She looks about thirty，but in reality she's nearly forty．她看上去大約30歲，但實際上她快40歲了。
*This may seem a bad thing， but in reality it is a good thing．這看起來是壞事，其實是好事。1．reasonable正當的；合情合理
*We will give serious consideration to anything in reason that he suggests．對他提的建議，只要合情合理我們都願意慎重考慮。
*I will do anything in reason．只要是合情合理的事我都願意去做。
2．within sensible limits道理上
*They cannot，in reason， doubt what he says．在道理上，他們不能懷疑他所說的話。in rem
[In`rZm; inˋrәm]
『拉、法律』對某事物
(如財產、地位或權利等)in answer to答覆
*What did you say in reply to his suggestion？你怎麼答覆他的建議的？put aside for future use保存起來；儲備
*They keep grain in reserve for emergencies．他們存糧以備急用。
*He spent some of his money and kept the rest in reserve．他花了一部分錢，餘款存了起來。in reply to應…的；為回答…
*He contributed one hundred dollars in response to my request．他應我的請求而捐了100美元。
*Many young people have volunteered to reclaim the remote regions of their motherland in response to the call of the Party．許多青年人響應黨的號召自願去開墾祖國的邊遠地區。as repayment；as a reward回報；作為報酬
*I hope I can be of some servise to you in return．但願我能為你做點事作為報答。
*What can we do for them in return for all the help they have given us？我們將怎樣來報答他們所給我們的種種幫助呢？ I gave him some books in return for his assistance．我給了他一些書，作為對他所提供的幫助的回報。broken to pieces變成廢墟
*Berlin was in ruins after World War Ⅱ．二次大戰後，柏林一片廢墟。in a way that is good for sb．；to sb．'s advantage對某人有益
*Bob made good grades in high school，and that was in his favour when he looked for a job．鮑勃在中學時成績優秀，這在他找工作時，對他有利。
*People always make in ferences in her favour．人們常作出有利於她的推斷。such as one likes； be accustomed to；be capable of內行；在行；適合；擅長
*Storekeeping is not in my lines．開店與我性情不合。
*You may make a speech or write a poem，but such things are not in my line．你可以演說或寫詩，但這些不是我的特長。possible or practicable for sb．在某人的能力或權限內
*I will do all in my power to help you．我一定盡力幫助你。
*It is not in my power to grant you the loan of five thousand dollars．我無權給你5000美元的貸款。in sb．'s situation處於某人之地位
*I wouldn't be in your shoes for all the wealth in the world．給我世界上所有的財富，我也不願處於你那個地位。
*If I were in your shoes I'd ask for more money．如果我處於你的地位，我會要更多的錢。
*He's always in debt；I wouldn't be in his shoes for anything．他總是向別人借錢，我無論如何不願過他那種日子。
*Supposing you put yourself in his shoes， would you have behaved differently in the circumstances？假如你處在他的位子上，在那種情況下你會做得和他不一樣嗎？according to sb．'s opinion 在…看來；依…之見
*In my view，there is much oil here．依我看，這兒石油很多。1．within reach；likely to be met；before sb．可及；可得到；在眼前
*The chance to work for a printer was put in my way．一個在印刷廠工作的機會擺在我面前。
2． in sb．'s path as a hindrance；placed so as to block the way 妨礙；阻礙；擋路
*A big tree had fallen across the street and was in our way as we drove．一棵大樹倒在大街上，擋住了我們的路，車開不過去。
*My son is always getting in my way．我兒子總是妨礙我。seeking or looking for；in pursuit of尋找；追尋
*We are in search of a typist．我們在招聘一名打字員。
*The prospecting team traversed far and wide in search of mineral deposits．地質勘探隊為尋找礦藏走遍四面八方。
*They went out to Australia in search of gold．他們去澳大利亞淘金。1．at the time of a year when sth．is plentiful盛產季節；旺季；正當時令
*Fruit is cheapest in season．水果旺季時，價格最便宜。
*Native watermelons will be in season soon．地產西瓜就要上市了。
2． at the right time恰好的時候
*I arrived in season for the examination．我及時趕上考試。
*He spoke a word in season to me．他及時地勸導了我。in brief簡言之；總之
*In short，he is a promising young man and has a bright future．總之，他是一個有希望、有前途的青年。
*In short，we must be prepared．總之，我們要有所準備。
*In short，finishing the job is not so easy as you may think．總之，完成這工作不是你想像的那麼容易。visible；able to be seen；within sight看得見；出現
*There was not a ship in sight．看不到一隻船。
*A ship came in sight from the horizon．天際出現了一條船。
*Peace is now in sight．現在和平有望。
*With success in sight they all felt jubilant．成功在望，他們都歡天喜地。where one can see or be seen by在看得見的地方
*We were in sight of land．我們已看見陸地了。
*You'll soon be in sight of Tian An Men．你就要看見天安門了。speechlessly；soundlessly默不作聲地；靜悄悄地
*They looked at each other in silence．他們默不作聲地相互對視。
*As night fell，everything was in silence．夜幕降臨，一切靜悄悄。in si.tu
[In`saItu, -tju; inˋsitju:]
《源自拉丁文'in (the) site'的意思》<<副詞>>
在原處,在原位置to the extent that；to the point that就…而言；視…而定；在…範圍內
*In so far as the report is concerned，I have already had it copied．至於那份報告，我已經將它複印了。
*In so far as the definitions of some obscure expressions are concerned，there may still be a few inaccuracies in this dictionary．就某些疑難詞組的釋義來說，這本詞典可能還有一些不夠準確的地方。in a frank manner明確地；直截了當地
*He refused my invitation in so many words．他明確地拒絕了我的邀請。inwardly；in one's thoughts or imagination在精神上或思想上
*I in spirit flew into the sky．我在想像中飛入了天空。
*I am beside you in spirit．我在想像中在你身旁。
*My friend couldn't come to my birthday party， but she said she would be there in spirit．我朋友不能來參加我的生日宴會，但她說她在想像中將和我們在一起。in a good humor；laughing and joking和顏悅色；興高采烈
*He is always in spirits．他總是興高采烈的。
*She was in low spirits because he failed in the exam．她情緒不好，因為她考試不及格。despite；not withstanding；regardless of不管；不顧
*In spite of the bad storm John delivered his papers on time．雖然天下暴雨，約翰仍按時投遞報紙。
*In spite of the rainy weather，the streets were full of people on May Day．五一節那天，儘管下雨，街上還是擠滿了人。
*He succeeded in the end in spite of the immense difficulties．儘管困難重重，他最終還是成功了。not withstanding one's own efforts 儘管有所努力；情不自禁；不由自主地
*At the sight of his little sister dressed up for the play in the role of an old woman he laughed aloud in spite of himself．看到自己的小妹妹扮演劇中老太大的角色，他情不自禁地哈哈大笑起來。
*On hearing the news，the poor old man cried in spite of himself．聽到這消息，這位可憐的老人不由自主地哭起來了。
*On hearing the joke， they all laughed in spite of themselves．聽了這個笑話，他們全都情不自禁地笑了起來。in sta.tu quo
[In`stʃtjuˋkwo, -`statәu-; inʃstatju:ˋkwou]
《源自拉丁文 'in the existing [same] condition' 的意思》<<副詞>>
在現況下,在同樣情況下,按原樣available有現貨
*The store had no more red shoes in stock，so Mary chose brown ones instead．店裡紅色的鞋子無貨，所以瑪麗選了雙棕色的。
*We do not have a shirt of your size in stock now，but we can order it for you．你這種尺碼的襯衣我們現在無貨，但我們可以為你定購一件。1．about to happen；waiting 必將來到或發生；等候
*What does the future hold in store for the boy who ran away？等待那外逃男孩的前途是什麼？
*We don't know what is in store for us．我們不知自己將來的遭遇如何。
*When he was arrested by the enemy，he knew perfectly well what was in store for him， but he remained calm．遭到敵人逮捕時，他清楚地知道等待著他的是什麼，但他還是非常沉著。
*I hope a bright future is in store for you．我希望光明的前途在等著你。
2．saved for future use備用；貯藏著
*There are many other energy sources in store．有待開發的能源還有好多種。
*If the electricity goes off， we have candles in store．如果停電，我們備有蠟燭。
*We'd better keep some of these in store for next year．我們最好把這些東西貯藏一些待明年使用。fashionable時髦
*A welltailored suit it always in style．做工好的衣服總是時髦的。1．in important fact；in the main or basic parts主要地；大體上；基本上
*The two cars are the same in substance， except one is red and the other is red and white．這兩部車除了一部是紅的，另一部是紅白色的，其它大體相同。
*I agree in substance with what you say，but differ on some small points．我大體上同意你所說的，但在一些細節問題上與你的意見還有不同之處。
2．actually；really 實在地；真正地
*This composition is in substance better than the previous one．這篇作文實際上比上一篇作文要好一些。one after another in order，sequence，or in the course of events 接連地；相繼
*She's won the national championship in tabletennis for two years in succession．她連續兩年榮獲乒乓球全國冠軍。1． in the matter of；on the subject of；especially about 關於；特別是
*In terms of output per capita that country's agriculture is very efficient．那個國家的農業，按人口計算的產量來說是很有效率的。
*It is a small country both in terms of size and population．就面積和人口而論，它都是個小國。
*In terms of money they're quite rich，but not in terms of happiness．就錢而論，他們很富有，但是沒有幸福。
2．in the language of用…措辭
*He talked about his students in terms of praise．他對他的學生大加讚揚。
3．expressed by用…表示
*It is not to be considered in terms of money．這件事不能從金錢方面考慮。in ter.ro.rem clause
[Intә`rˏrєm; intєˋrˏ:rәm]
『法律』警戒條款
(遺囑中聲明繼承人如對遺囑提出異議即失去繼承權之條款)for the reason that；because因為
*I like the city， but I like the country better in that I have more friends there．我喜歡這個城市，可是我更喜歡農村，因為在那裡我有更多的朋友。1． being away不在
*In the absence of their parents，the children played in the house．家長不在時，孩子們便在家裡玩耍。
2．lacking缺乏
*In the absence of evidence，the suspect was released．因缺乏證據，那個嫌疑犯被釋放了。1．unsettled；uncertain未確定的
*Our plans are in the air．我們的計劃還懸而未決。
2． going about流傳
*There are rumors in the air．謠言傳開了。1．with no light黑暗
*Don't leave the child alone in the dark；he'll be afraid．不要把孩子單獨留在黑暗中，他會害怕的。
*I hit my head against the door in the dark．黑暗中我的頭撞在了門上。
2．in ignorance不知道；隱瞞
*John was in the dark about the job he was being sent to．約翰對於指派他做的工作一無所知。
*Tax payers don't like being kept in the dark about the government's intentions．納稅人不希望對政府的打算一無所知。
*I am still kept in the dark about the matter．對這事我仍然一無所知。
*It is not necessary to keep it in the dark．這件事沒有必要保密。far away；at a distance 遠處
*A small house can be seen in the distance．遠處可以看到一幢小房子。finally； eventually； at last最後
*They reached the top of the mountain in the end．他們最後爬到了山頂。
*He succeeded in the end．最後他成功了。
*in the event of in case of；if there is假如；萬一
*The wall was built along the river in the event of floods．沿河築牆，以防洪水。
*In the event of his not coming，what shall we do？如果他不來， 我們怎麼辦？in the special line of 在…（學術）方 面
*He made several important inventions in the field of telegraphy．他在電報方面有過幾項重要發明。1．in the beginning；before now 早先；起初；早就
*You already ate breakfast！ Why didn't you tell me that in the first place？你已經吃過啦！你為什麼一開始不告訴我呢？
*We would have finished the job long ago if we had listened to him in the first place．要是我們一開始就聽他的話，這工作早就完成了。
*Carl patched his old ball but it soon leaked again． He should have bought a new one in the first place．卡爾把舊球補好，可很快又漏氣了。他早就該買個新球了。
2． firstly首先
*You cannot go swimming．In the first place，the water is too cold；and in the second place，there is no enough time before dinner．你不能去游泳。第一，水太冷；第二，晚飯前沒有足夠的時間。
*In the first place，students should study hard．首先，學生應該努力讀書。habitually習慣地
*He is in the habit of scratching his head when thinking．他思考時習慣抓頭。
*She is in the habit of smoking．她有吸煙的習慣。
*You're in the habit of reading the newspaper at breakfast．你有邊吃早飯邊看報紙的習慣。
*Are you in the habit of rising early？你有早起的習慣嗎？possessed by為…所有
*The town is still in the hands of the enemy．這個城鎮仍在敵人控制之下。for the sake of為了…的利益
*They are exploring the space in the interest of humanity．他們在為人類的利益開發空間。even a little；in the smallest degree；to the least degree or extent （常用於否定句中）一點（不）；絲毫（不）
*Mike was not upset in the least by the storm．暴風雨一點也沒有使邁克感到焦慮不安。finally； in the end最終；從長遠觀點來看
*Real ability will win in the long run．真正的才能最終會使人獲得成功的。
*It pays in the long run to buy goods of high quality．買優質產品終歸是合算的。
*You may make good grades by studying only before examinations，but you will succeed in the long run by studying hard every day．你考試前才看書也許會取得好成績，不過你若每天努力學習最終定會成功。in most cases 大體上；多數情況下；基本上；主要
*What he has said conforms in the main to facts．他所講的基本上符合事實。
*The letters were in the main from my old classmates．這些信件主要是我老同學寫來的。
*In the main，the students did well on the test．總的說來，學生們考得不錯。
*The results are in the main satis factory．結果總的來說是滿意的。as regards在…上；就…而言
*He is strict in the matter of discipline．他在紀律方面是嚴格的。
*He has not a good reputation in the matter of honesty．要說誠實，他的名聲不好。
*You have everything you need in the matter of books．就書而言，你需要的都有。at the same time；meanwhile同時
*In the meantime，they took part in various contests and games．與此同時，他們參加了各種比賽和遊戲。between two sides of an argument，two choices，etc．在…之間；夾在爭論雙方的中間或兩種選擇之間
*Mary found herself in the middle of the quarrel between Joyce and Ethel．喬埃斯和埃塞爾發生爭執，瑪麗不知該傾向哪一方。
*John promised Larry to go fishing but his father wanted him to help at home．John was in the middle．約翰答應萊裡去釣魚，可是他父親卻要他幫助做家務。約翰為難了。1．using the authority of憑…的權威；以…的名義
*I arrest you in the name of the law．我根據法律逮捕你。
*I am speaking in the name of all the students of our class．我是代表我們班全體同學講話的。
2．for the sake of為了…的緣故
*He did it in the name of his brother．他為了他弟弟的緣故而這樣做。1．not within a building露天
*They slept in the open last night．昨夜他們露宿。
2．without secrecy公開的；非秘密的
*The problem caused discussion in the open．這個問題引起了公開的討論。owned or controlled by被…佔有
*The famous portrait is now in the possession of the National Gallery，那張有名的照片被保存在國家美術館裡。before在…面前
*He was calm in the presence of danger．他臨危不亂。
*The girl was shy in the presence of stangers．這個女孩在陌生人面前顯得靦腆。
*He didn't get discouraged in the presence of failure．他在失敗面前沒有氣餒。in the same trouble；sharing the same misfortune 境遇相同；共患難
*Dick was disappointed because Fern refused to marry him，but he knew others were in the same boat．狄克很失望，因為費恩不肯嫁給他，不過他知道，其他人也沒能娶上費恩。
*They were in the same boat during the war．他們在戰時共患難過。
*We are all in the same boat．我們的處境都是相同的。1．at the same time同時
*He admitted and denied his mistake in the same breath．他剛承認了錯誤又立即推翻了。
2．in the same class；in as high a group（usu．used in the negative）在同一等級；同一程度；相提並論
*Mary is a good swimmer，but she should not be mentioned in the same breath with you．瑪麗是一位很好的游泳者，但她還不能和你相提並論。1．doing the same things that other people are doing做別人正在做的事；隨大流
*Jim found some college friends at the lake that summer and soon was in the swim of things．那年夏天吉姆發現他的一些大學同學在湖邊度假，於是他很快加入到他們的活動中去。
2．following fashion趕時髦
*Mary went to the city and found girls were dressed in green，and soon she was quite in the swim．瑪麗去那座城市，發現姑娘們都穿綠色的衣服，於是很快也趕上了潮流。in a moment；very quickly 頃刻間；一剎那
*The children finished eating all the candies in the twinkling of an eye．孩子們剎那間就把糖果全吃光了。as a result of；right after；following由於；緊隨
*There were many troubles in the wake of the war．戰後許多麻煩接踵而來。
*There were heavy losses of property in the wake of the flood．由於洪水使得財產受到重大損失。
*Traders came in the wake of the conquering armies．商人隨著征服的軍隊而來。
*The students followed in the wake of the teacher．學生們跟在老師的後面。placed so as to block the way；causing inconvenience 擋路；妨礙人的；礙手礙腳
*Fred tried to get to the door， but the table was in the way．弗雷德試圖走近大門，可是桌子擋住了去路。
*I will visit you on Sunday，if there is nothing in the way．如果沒有什麼妨礙的話，我將在星期日去拜訪你。
*They are very busy now， so let's take our leave quickly，otherwise we'll be in the way．他們眼下正忙著，我們還是快走吧，要不就礙事了。
*Mary tried to clean the house， but her baby got in the way．瑪麗想打掃房子，可是她的孩子總是礙手礙腳的。1．in a favorable position for doing or getting在有利的地位；便利於
*She put me in the way of a good job．他幫我找到了一份好工作。
2．in the matter or business of；as regards關於；有關
*We have done a lot in the way of improving living conditions for the workers．我們已經在改善工人的居住條件方面做了大量的工作。
*They have a small stock in the way of short skirts．他們有一小批短裙的存貨。
*We have not yet done much in the way of invention．我們在發明創造方面做的還不多。
3．in the habit of習慣於
*I'm not much in the way of working on Sundays．我沒有星期天工作的習慣。
4． in the process of在…過程中
*Failure，success，failure again，success again－that's quite normal in the way of scientific experiments．失敗，成功，再失敗，再成功，這在科學實驗的過程中是很正常的。1．seeming probable看上去有可能的
*Changes in the top management of the company had been in the wind for weeks．公司最高主管的變動已醞釀了好幾個星期了。
2．soon to happen； about to occur 快要發生的
*Tom's close friends knew that his marriage was in the wind．湯姆的好朋友都知道他很快要結婚。
*They are having an urgent session；there must be something in the wind．他們在召開緊急會議，肯定發生了什麼事情。at all；ever；of all possible things 究竟
*Who in the world is that fellow？那人究竟是誰？
*Where in the world did you find that necklace？你究竟是在哪兒發現這根項鏈的？
*He didn't understand what on earth the teacher meant．他不能理解老師究竟說了些什麼。to blame；in error不正當；錯誤
*He is in the right and you are in the wrong．他是對的，你錯了。
*In attacking a smaller boy，Jack was plainly in the wrong．傑克欺侮一個比他小的孩子，很明顯是他不對。
*He knew he was in the wrong， but refused to concede to the point．他知道他錯了，但不肯認錯。
*You are both in the wrong．你們兩位都錯了。theoretically 理論上
*The plan should work in theory，but will it work in practive？ 這項計劃在理論上一定有效，但在實踐中能行得通嗎？1．within or before a fixed time及時
*We got to the station just in time to catch the train．我們及時趕到火車站乘上火車。
*A stitch in time saves nine．及時處理，事半功倍。
*You can rest assured that we'll finish the work in time．你放心吧，我們一定按時完成任務。
*The doctor came in time to save his life．醫生及時前來挽救他的生命。
2．eventually；in the end； after a while；in the future不久；最好；將來
*Fred and Jim did not like each other at first，but in time they became friends．弗雷德和吉姆開始互不喜歡，可是最終他們成了好朋友。
*You'll get used to the weather in Nanjing in time．你遲早會適應南京的氣候的。
*If you keep on trying，you will succed in time．只要你繼續努力，你遲早會成功。
3．in step合拍子
*The marchers kept in time with the band．遊行者和著樂隊的節奏往前走。when one is in當處於…之時
*Confidence is a great weapon，especially in time of fear，uncertainty and danger．信心是一種重要的武器，尤其是在恐懼、疑慮和危險的時候。under no circumstances 決不
*I will in no case reveal your secret．我決不會把你的秘密洩露出去。
*In no case have I noticed that matter．我決沒有注意到那件事。in to.to
[In`toto; inˋtoutou]
《源自拉丁文 'in the whole' 的意思》<<副詞>>
整個地,全部,完全 (as a whole)1．in contact with；communicating with與…接觸；同…保持聯繫
*Please get in touch with me while you are away．你走後請與我聯繫。
*A newspaper keeps one in touch with the world．報紙使人們同世界保持聯繫。
2． having a delicate appreciation and intimate knowledge of；in sympathy with深知；熟悉；同情
*He is not quite in touch with anyone in this neighbourhood．他和這一地區內的任何人都不熟悉。
*She is in touch with the latest developments in the case．她對這一案件的最新發展情況是知道的。
*He reads the daily press regularly to keep in touch with the developments both at home and abroad．他經常讀報以瞭解國內外形勢的發展。in trans.
in transit1．in a difficult situation；suffering 在困擾中
*He always offers his help when I am in trouble．每當我陷入困境，他總伸出援助之手。
*She is a kind friend to everyone in trouble．她對處於困境的人都很友善。
2．going to be punished將受懲罰；被責難
*He is in trouble again，because he has broken a window．他又受到了責罰，因為他打碎了窗戶。in fact；in reality；actually實際上；實事上
*In truth， he cannot teach you anything on French．事實上，他不能教你法語。
*This is in truth an ideal site for a power plant．這裡的確是建設發電廠的理想場所。
*This is in truth very poorly made．說實在的，這個東西做得太差勁了。one by one依次
*Each man in turn got up and spoke．每個人依次站起來發言。
*I'll see you all in turn．我將一個一個地去看望你們大家。in half分成兩半
*There was only one piece of cake，so we cut it in two．只有一塊蛋糕，所以我們把它分成兩半。in u.te.ro
[In`jutˏro; inˋju:tәrou]
『拉』在子宮內的in va.cu.o
[In`vakjJˏo; inˋvakjuou]
『拉』在真空中; 脫離現實
(=in a vacuum)without success；without effect徒勞地；無效地
*He passed his life in vain．他虛度了一生。
*The drowning man called in vain for help．溺水者求救無門。
*All the doctor's efforts were in vain and the man soon died．醫生所有的努力都無效，那個人很快就死了。1．in sight 看見；在望
*We reached the hill top and there was the sea in view．我們爬上山頂，看見了大海。
2．as a purpose 意在
*He has some pleasure in view．他意在找些快樂。considering；on account of由…看來；考慮到；由於
*Schools were closed that day in view of the heavy snowstorm．由於暴風雪，學校那天沒有上課。
*You must do your best in view of ．由 於暴風雪，學校那天沒有上課。
*You must do your best in view of those facts．鑒於那些事實，你應當盡力而為。
*He was pardoned in view of the circumstances．由於考慮到當時的情況，他被寬恕了。by virtue of；because of，on the grounds of；by means of由於；因為
*Plastic bags are useful for holding many kinds of food，in virtue of their clearness，toughness and low cost．塑料袋因透明、牢固、價廉而被用來包裝多種食物。in vi.tro
[In`vaItro, -`vI-; inˋvaitrou, -ˋvi-]
『拉』在玻璃容器內; 在試管內
(in a test tube)in vi.vo
[In`vaIvo; inˋvaivou]
『拉』在活的有機體內; 
(=in a living organism)in need of；wanting需要
*The baby is in want of special care．這個嬰兒需要特別護理。
