b. 把 <裝飾等> 弄得花裡花俏<up>jazz buff
爵士樂迷1．brighten up；make more exciting 使活躍起來；使更振奮
*The party was very dull until Peter jazzed it up with his drum．聚會枯燥無味，直到彼得敲鼓才改變了氣氛。
*The newsman jazzed up the story to sell himself to the editors of the weekly．這個記者把報道寫得繪聲繪色，以求博得那家週刊編輯們的青睞。
*Go out and get some more to drink；this party meeds jazzing up a bit．你出去多買些飲料，這次聚會需要搞得熱鬧點。
2．improve；give an appearance of improvement 改進；使帶有改進的外觀
*The room decorations appeared to have been jazzed up．房間的裝飾好像已經改觀了。
*I've tried to jazz up the old car with a spot of paint and some accessories．我設法用少量油漆和一些配件修整這輛舊汽車。
*Our exhibition stand was dull and boring last year．－Can't we jazz it up a bit this year？我們的展覽架去年很枯燥無味。－今年我們可不可使它吸引人一點？jazz.man
