<<可數名詞>>
連接處 [點,線,面] ,接縫處unite；join hands 聯合；通力合作
*The American soldiers joined forces with the British in the war against Germany．戰爭中美國士兵與英國士兵會師共同抗擊德國。
*The tourist offices in the regions have agreed to join forces with the office in the capital to try and attract more interest and also to reduce costs．這些地區的旅行社已經同意跟首都的旅行社聯手經營以吸引更多的人並降低費用。take part in 參加
*We invited him to join in our discussion．我們邀請他加入我們的討論。
*Five of us joined in the research project．我們中間有5個人參加了這個研究項目。1．attach oneself to 附隨；依附於
*The people were hurrying to see the parade，and we joined on at the rear．人們趕去看遊行，我們也跟在後面。
2．attach；fix 裝上；接上
*They joined the wires on and made the necessary new connection．他們把電線接了起來，接通了所需的新線路。1．offer oneself as a recruit；join the army 參軍；入伍
*He joined up at the age of twenty．他20歲參了軍。
*On leaving collage，my brother joined up．我的兄弟大學畢業後參軍了。
2．connect；link together 連接
*The electrician joined the wires up．電工把電線接好了。
3．form or enter into an alliance or league；link up 組成或參加聯盟；會合
*The two companies were ordered to join up with each other at Bridge No．3 before dawn．那兩個連奉命於黎明前在3號橋會師。join.der
