<<可數名詞>>
『軍』指定敵後傘兵著陸區take or accept quickly and gladly 欣然接受
*Johnny jumped at the invitation to go swimming with his brother．喬尼欣然接受邀請，同個哥哥一塊去游泳。
*Alice would jump at the chance of going to Egypt．艾麗絲會非常高興地接受這次去埃及的機會。
*The children jumped at the chance of visiting the television studios．孩子們立即同意去電視製作中心看看。jump ball
『籃球』跳球jump belt
袖珍火箭帶
(綁在身上使人跳過障礙物或作短距離飛行)jump bid
『橋牌』跳級叫牌reply sharply and angrily to sth．sb．has said尖銳或粗暴地回答
*He jumped down my throat at the mere mention of the subject．一提到這事，他就粗暴地回答我。
*Even if I'm wrong，you needn't jump down my throat like that．即使我錯了，你也用不著這樣粗暴地對待我。jump head
跳頁標題
(報章雜誌之文章太而轉入另一頁時所用的標題,由原標題精簡而成)criticize sharply or suddenly 嚴厲批評；突然斥責
*He jumped on her for that misbehaviour．他對她的錯誤行為進行了嚴厲的批評。
*He'll jump on anyone who contradicts him．誰不同意他，他就罵誰。be badly frightened；be very much surprised 驚嚇；大吃一驚；嚇了一跳
*The door slammed with such a bang that I nearly jumped out of my skin．門砰地一聲關上了，嚇了我一跳。pass over；disregard or omit sth．intervening 忽略；遺漏；略去
*Let's jump over all those tiems．讓我們把那些項目全部略去吧。
*As time was limited，the professor had to jump over the details．因為時間有限，教授只好把一些細節省掉了。
*Aware that the listeners were absentminded，the reader jumped over some paragraphs without anyone noticing．意識到聽眾心不在焉，宣讀者略去了一些段落，誰也沒有發覺。jump pass
