先被嘲笑者> 這次輪到自己嘲笑別人; 這次佔優勢1．laugh to scorn；mock嘲笑
*It is unkind to laugh at a person in trouble．對人幸災樂禍有欠忠厚。
*Don't laugh at her．不要嘲笑她。
2．get amused about；make fun of 因…發笑
*What are you laughing at？你們在笑什麼？
*It's nothing to laugh at．那沒啥可笑的。
3．show apathy or indifference to；reject一笑置之；付之一笑；輕視
*He laughed at the idea．他對這個意見不以為然。
*We advised him not to laugh at the official warnings．我忠告他不要對官方的警告不以為然。
*The daring climbers laugh at danger．勇敢的登山者對危險付之一笑。1．continue laughing笑而不止
*The crowd were still laughing away as they left the theatre．人們離開劇場時仍笑聲不止。
*I don't know why he was laughing away to himself all the time．我不知道為什麼他自己一直在笑個不停。
2．dismiss or get rid of with a laugh； scorn付之一笑；輕視
*He just laughed away the enemy's threats．對敵人的威脅，他一笑置之。
*Those who can laugh away all regrets are sure to live longer．能用笑聲來解愁者必長壽。
*There is no point in trying to laugh away this problem．It has to be dealt with realistically．對這個問題想一笑了之是不行的，必須切實加以處理。
3．while away（time） with laughter以笑來消磨時光
*He talks and laughs away his vacant hours．他談笑風生，消磨無聊的空餘時間。
*We laughed away the time when we were together．我們說說笑笑消磨了我們在一起的時間。defeat， dismiss or silence by laughing用笑聲壓倒、拒絕或打斷
*The audience laughed the speaker down．聽眾的笑聲打斷了演講者的談話。
*I don't know why they laughed down my proposal．我不懂他們為什麼用笑聲來拒絕我的建議。laugh line
笑紋1．dismiss with a laugh as not important or not serious； not take seriously一笑置之；不予重視
*This is a mistake that can't easily be laughed off．這不是一個可以等閒視之的錯誤。
*He had a bad fall while iceskating but he laughed it off．他在溜冰時重重地跌了一跤，但他一笑了之，沒把它當回事。
2．escape from or get rid of by laughing以笑來排除；笑著逃過
*We could but laugh off his suspicions．我們只好以笑聲來排除他的疑心。
*Beset with embarrassing questions at the press conference， the diplomat tried to laugh off his predicament．在記者招待會上，這位外交官給一些難題弄得很尷尬，只好以笑聲加以掩飾。laugh while talking about笑著談論
*We laughed over the tale we had just heard．我們笑著談論那則剛剛聽到的故事。
*The old couple laughed over the letter they had received from their little grandson．老倆口收到小孫子的來信，一邊談一邊笑。laugh.a.ble
