lay
[lә; lєi]
(laid[led; leid])
<<及物動詞>>
1 橫置,置放 
a. 橫置
He laid his bag on the table. 
他把提袋放在桌上
She laid her baby (down) in the crib. 
她把嬰兒放到小床裡 (睡覺) 
She laid her hand on her son's shoulder. 
她把手放在兒子的肩膀上
b. [~ oneself]躺,臥
He laid himself down on the ground. 
他躺倒在地上
c. 埋葬<人>
~ one's bones in Westminster Abbey 
把某人埋葬於西敏寺
~ a person to rest [sleep] 
下葬某人
2 a. 把 <磚等> 鋪整齊,砌,鋪設,建造
~ bricks 
砌磚
~ a pavement 
鋪設人行道
~ a railroad track 
鋪設鐵路軌道
b. 奠定 <基礎等> 
~ the foundation(s) of 
? 奠定…的基礎
He tried to ~ a future course for himself. 
他努力為自己的attack襲擊
*The three men laid about him with their hands and boots．3個傢伙對他拳打腳踢。
*He rushed upon those who were causing the trouble， and laid about them．他衝向那些肇事者，把他們痛打了一陣。lay analyst
<<可數名詞>>
業餘精神分析家1．put to one side；cease temporarily some work or activity in which one is engaged暫停某一工作或活動
*At eight o'clock every evening she laid aside whatever she was doing to tell the children a story before they went to bed．每晚一到8點，她就丟掉手頭在做的一切，給孩子們講故事，以讓他們睡覺。
*The students laid aside their books to listen to the news broadcast．學生們收起書本去聽新聞廣播。
*Lay aside your book and go to bed．放下你的書去睡覺吧。
2．save； put by for some special purpose節省；為特定目的而積蓄
*He is laying aside money for his old age．他在積蓄錢以備晚年。
*Half the prize money he spent，and the rest was laid aside for a rainy day．他花了一半獎金，其餘的錢存起來以備不時之需。
*She laid aside one hour a day for reading．她每天抽一個小時來看書。
*Every family has spare money to lay aside and surplus grain in store．家家有存款，戶戶有餘糧。
3．abandon；reject拋棄；拒絕；除去
*He has laid aside the habit of smoking．他已戒煙。
*It's time to lay aside our differences and work together for a shared purpose．是我們放棄不同意見，為共同目標而通力合作的時候了。
*I want you to lay aside these useless prejudices．我希望你丟開這些無益的偏見。1．save儲蓄；把商品留存起來（待以後交貨）
*She laid a little of her pay away each week．她每週儲蓄一點薪金。
*The store would be glad to lay away this dress for you till Christmas．本店願意把這服裝為你保留到聖誕節。
2．bury埋葬
*He was laid away in his favorite spot on the hill．他被安葬在山上他最喜歡的地點。lay baptism
非教士主持的洗禮lay brogher
『天主教』俗人修士
(修道院裡做雜役)save，esp．a little at a time儲蓄；儲存
*He laid a little money by every week till he had enough for a trip to Florida．他每週儲蓄點錢直到足以去佛羅里達旅行一趟為止。
*The farmer laid by some of his best corn to plant the next year．這位農場主留存了一些最好的玉米，以備來年下種之用。lay communion
『天主教』神職人員還俗lay day
『商』裝卸貨物日 (租船契約所允許) ,停泊日1． resign辭職
*The old man has laid down his office to make way for a younger man．這位老人為了給年輕人讓位，辭去了他的職務。
2．store away for future use貯藏
*They laid down provisions for the voyage．他們貯備糧食以備航行之用。
*He has laid down some excellent vintoges．他貯藏了非常好的葡萄酒。
3．cease using放下
*Please lay down the watch gently．請把手錶輕輕放下。
*Tell your men to lay down their armsthe war is over．告訴你們的人投降吧，戰爭已經結束了。
4．sacrifice犧牲
*He laid down his life for the country．他為國犧牲。
*Thousands of young men laid down their lives for the cause of peace．成千上萬的年輕人為了和平事業獻出了自己的生命。
5．state clearly and definitely明確規定
*It is laid down that no changes can be made after a committee decision．按規定，委員會決定後不能再做任何修改。
*The school authorities have laid down some new rules．學校當局制訂了一些新的規章制度。
*The Act lays it down that no pension can be paid to anyone under the age of sixty unless he is disabled．法令規定，除殘廢者外，60歲以下者，不得領取養老金。
6．bet下賭注
*How much is Martin ready to lay down on the horse？馬丁打算在這匹馬上下多少賭注？
7．construct；build建造
*They are laying down a nuclear submarine．他們正在建造一艘核潛艇。
*Several of the newtype tankers are being laid down．有幾艘新型油船正在建造之中。
*The track was laid down in the 19th century and is in need of repair．這條鐵路是19世紀鋪設的，急需整修。
*Many new railways have been laid down in the past few years．幾年來建造了許多新鐵路。
8．plant or sow（a field） with a certain crop； convert（land） into pasture在（耕地上）種上；把（耕地）改成牧場
*This year we must lay the big field down to grass．今年我們必須把這塊大田改種牧草。1．give strict orders下命令；嚴令
*He could usually be found in the centre of a small group of people to whom he was laying down the law．我們常看到他在一小群人當中發號施令。
2．speak severely or seriously about a wrong doing；scold嚴厲斥責；呵斥
*The principal called in the students and laid down the law to them about skipping classes．校長集合學生嚴責他們逃課。
*Father is laying down the law to the children again； I wonder what they've done now．父親又嚴厲地訓斥孩子們了，不知道他們現在又幹了什麼事。let sb． know your position and interest openly； act without trickery or secrets公開表明態度或意願；行為光明正大
*In talking about buying the property Peterson laid his cards on the table about his plans．彼得遜在購買那份產業時，明白說清了他置產的計劃。lay figure
