*We have laid in a good supply of food for the winter．我們已經貯存了足夠的糧食過冬。
*Every time they came to land， they laid in a good plenty of fresh water．他們每次靠岸都要備足淡水。lay intermediary
『法律』訴訟中間人1．attack physically； go at vigorously毆打；痛擊；猛擊
*The two fighters laid into each other as soon as the bell rang．鈴聲一響，兩位拳手互相猛擊起來。
*I saw Jones lay into a man twice his size．我看見瓊斯狠揍一個比他個子大一倍的男人。
2．attack with words用語言攻擊；抨擊
*I let him have his say，and then I laid into him．我讓他把話說完，然後把他痛罵了一頓。
*The senator laid into the opponents of his bill．那位參議員猛烈抨擊了反對他的提案的人。
*At the meeting they laid into each other fiercely．在會上他們激烈地相互指責。1．dismiss temporarily，generally because of lack of work臨時解雇
*If business continues to be slow， we may have to lay off ten people．如果生意繼續蕭條，我們可能得暫時辭退10個人。
*Bill hasn't lost his job． His firm laid him off for two weeks．比爾沒有失業，他的公司臨時解雇他兩個星期。
*Was John fired or laid off？約翰是被解雇了，還是被臨時辭退一段時間？
*The work there was seasonal， and there was a great deal of hardship among the employees when they were laid off each winter．那裡的工作帶有季節性，所以每年冬天雇工們被解雇時，日子是很難過的。
2．discontinue work or activity；take a rest停止工作或活動；休息
*The doctor told him to lay off for a rest．醫生囑咐他把工作停下來休息一段時間。
*You'd better lay off smoking for a while．你最好這會兒不要抽煙。
3．stop doing sth．which irritates or annoys；stop bothering；leave alone不要惹人生氣；不要打擾別人
*I didn't like some of the things he was saying about her so I told him to lay off．他在說她的一些事，我不願聽，所以我告訴他不要再說了。
4．stop using or taking戒除；勿再
*His doctor told him to lay off smoking．他的醫生要他戒煙。
5．mark out the boundaries or limits標出界線
*The boundaries are clearly laid off on the map．地圖上清楚地標出了界線。
6．take off；put（a garment，etc．）aside脫掉；把（衣服等）擱在一邊
*It's time we were able to lay off these heavy winter clothes．現在是我們可以把這些厚重的冬裝換下擱在一邊的時候了。1．supply（gas， water， electricity）to a building； provide供應（煤氣、水電等）；提供
*The house has water and electricity laid on．這座房子有水電供應。
*It was years before gas was laid on to the village．好多年以後這村子才裝起了管道煤氣。
*They lay on all essential services．他們提供一切必要的服務。
*The bus company intends to lay on two more buses for this route．公交公司打算再給這條線路提供兩部車。
2．beat；strike；attack violently猛打
*As he laid on blows to the boy's back，a man came up and took the whip out of his hand．他鞭打男孩背部時，一個男人走過來奪了他手中的鞭子。
*Little John seized a club and began to lay on for dear life．小約翰拿起一根棍子拚命亂打。
3．cover with；apply塗
*He told us that we should lay on a second coat of paint for better protection against the weather．他告訴我們，為了防止氣候侵害應再塗一層油漆。
4．organize or arrange for（entertainment，concert，etc．）組織安排（文娛活動、音樂會等）
*During the whole tour we hadn't to trouble about anything ourselves；everything was laid on for us．整個旅遊過程中，我們什麼都不用自己去操心，一切都為我們安排好了。
*Stage shows were laid on to entertain the foreign guests．安排了幾場演出招待那些外賓。
*Has all the food and drink been laid on？所有飲食都已安排好了嗎？
5．impose（taxes，commands，penalties）征（稅）；下（命令） ；施加（懲罰）
*The government has laid on a new tax．政府已徵收新稅。
*The firm is laying on higher prices．這個公司正在強行加價。
6．provide as a gift，bonus or treat 作為贈品贈送；奉送；招待
*The owner of the factory laid on a Christmas dinner for the employees．工廠的老闆設聖誕宴會招待其員工。try very hard努力；盡力去做
*They promised that they would lay themselves out to help us．他們答應將盡全力幫助我們。
*Larry wanted to win a medal for his school， so he really laid himself out in the race．拉裡想為學校贏得獎牌，因此他確實在比賽中下了很大功夫。
*He may want the job，but I haven't seen him lay himself out trying to get it．他可能想得到這個職位，但是我沒有看到他竭力去爭取。1．spend；pay花費；付錢
*He is always hard up because he doesn't lay out his money wisely．他總是沒錢，因為他用錢不會精打細算。
*The committee decided to lay out all their budget on redecorating the college．委員會決定把他們所有的預算都花在重新修繕這所大學上。
*His money is well laid out．他花錢很得當。
*She laid out a lot of money on this house．她為這幢房子花了許多錢。
2．spread out ready for use or so as to be seen easily； display展現；呈現；陳列
*The scene that was laid out before the climbers was magnificent．呈現在登山者面前的風景是非常壯麗的。
*The shopassistants were busy laying out their windows for the coming National Day．售貨員為了迎接國慶節的到來，正忙著佈置櫥窗。
3．plan； plot；organize計劃；安排
*Come here， Fred， I have a job laid out for you．過來，弗雷德，我替你安排了一個工作。
*He laid out the day's work for his students．他給學生們安排了當天的工作。
*The work for tomorrow is all laid out．明天的工作都安排好了。
4．prepare；prepare（a corpse） for burial準備；為（屍體）作殯葬準備
*The servants laid out his meals carefully．傭人們為他精心準備了飯菜。
*The family passed one by one through the small parlour where the father's body was laid out．一家人一個接一個地走過放著父親遺體的小客廳。
*The undertaker laid out the corpse prior to burial．殯儀員做好屍體的殯葬準備。
5．knock down or make unconscious打倒；擊昏
*He hit the secret agent on the jaw and completely laid him out．他朝那特務的下巴一拳打去，把他打昏在地。
*The thieves laid out two of the guards during the armed robbery．在武裝搶劫時，盜賊們殺死了兩個衛兵。
*With one blow he laid his attacker out．他一拳就打昏了襲擊他的人。
6．plan the building or arrangement of；design設計
*The architect laid out the interior of the building．建築師設計了大廈的內部。
*The pictures in．the magazine are well laid out．那本雜誌裡的圖片編排得很好。
*The garden is tastefully laid out．花園設計得很優雅。1．put off until later；delay；postpone推遲；耽延
*We voted to lay the question over to our next meeting for discussion．我們一致贊成將這個問題推遲到下次會議討論。
*For various reasons， the meeting was laid over till the next day．由於種種原因，會議延至次日舉行。
*The concert had to be laid over for several days because one of the singers had hurt her throat．因為一個女歌手的嗓子受了傷，所以音樂會只能延期幾天舉行。
2．arrive in one place and wait some time before continuing the journey（旅途中）稍作停留
