你必須把私人的所有物留在那櫃子裡
She left her textbooks on the desk. 
她把教科書留在桌上
Don't ~ your work till tomorrow. 
不要把工作留到明天才做
I was thinking about what was left of him in the room. 
我在想房間裡他留下的東西
b. <郵差> 遞送<郵件>
The postman has left this letter for you. 
郵差給你送來這封信
2 a. 剩下,剩餘
Two from four ~s two. 
四減二剩下二
There was little coal left. 
煤已所剩不多
b. 留<東西>給[…][for]
L~ a bone for the dog. 
留一塊骨頭給狗
Nothing was left for us to eat. 
沒有剩下任何食物給我們
c. 留…給<人>,留<東西>給[人][for]
He left her nothing.= He left nothing for her. 
他什麼也沒有留給她
I was left no choice.= No choice was left for me. 
我已經沒有選擇的餘地
d. 使<人>維持…狀態
She was left standing there. 
她被留下來在那兒站著
e. 留給<人>[東西][with]
The payment left me with only one dollar. 
付款之後我只剩下一美元
They were left with nothing to eat. 
沒有留下任何食物給他們
f. 作為缺點留下
It ~s something [nothing] to be desired. 
這還有不足之處 [完美無缺] 
3 a. 死後遺下 <妻子、財產、名聲、紀錄等> ,遺留 <behind> 
She died, leaving three children behind. 
她死後遺下三個孩子
b. 遺留給<人><財產>; 遺留<財產>[給人][to]
He left his wife 3 million pounds.= He left 3 million pounds to his wife. 
他 (死後) 遺留給妻子三百萬鎊
She was left a big fortune by her husband. 
她繼承了她 (已故) 丈夫遺留的鉅額財產
c. 死後使 <妻子等> 成為…狀態
She was left a widow. 
丈夫去世後她成了寡婦
The man left his children poor. 
那個人死後,使其子女陷於貧困之境
4 a. 留下 <傷痕、感情等> 
The wound left a scar. 
那傷口留下了一個疤
There was a stain of ink left on the desk. 
桌上留有墨水的污點
b. 留給<人>[感情等][with]
I was left with some misgivings [a feeling of sadness]. 
我 (心中) 留下了些許不安 [悲傷的感覺] 
5 a. 把<人、物>置於…的狀態
You have left the door open. 
你把門敞開著沒有關
Her beauty left me momentarily speechless. 
她的美使我一時啞然失聲
→ let[leave]?alone
He left the remark unnoticed. 
他沒有注意到那句話
He ~s nothing undone. 
他什麼都不能放著不做
She left the sentence unfinished. 
她把句子留下沒有說完
Better ~ it unsaid. 
不說為妙,說出來反而不好
L~ things as they are. 
讓一切保持現狀吧
b. 讓<人、物等>維持…狀態
(cf. B 2 d) 
Somebody has left the water running. 
有人 (沒有關水龍頭而) 讓水一直流著
I left him reading a book. 
我任他繼續看書
c. 留給 [任由,委託,交由] <人等>…
Let's ~ her to solve the problem. 
我們把這個問題任由她去解決吧
d. 使<人等>熱中 [著迷] [於…][to]
L~ him to his foolish dreams. 
任由他去做愚蠢的夢好了
6 a. 把 <物、判斷等> 委託 [付託,托] [人][to]
I [I'll] ~ the choice of his occupation to him. 
我聽憑他自己選擇職業
I [I'll] ~it to you to decide.= I'll ~ the decision to you. 
這事我交給你決定
b. 把 <物、事> 托[人][with]
L~ a message with my secretary if I'm out. 
如果我不在,請把口信留交我的秘書
I left my trunks with a porter. 
我把皮箱委託給搬運行李的侍者看管
c. 委託 [付託] <人>[…]
I'll ~ him to choose his occupation. 
我要讓他自己選職業(cf. B 6 a) 
You'd better ~ them to do as they like. 
你最好讓他們隨心去做
d. (美口語)使<人>… (let) 
L~ us go. 
請讓我們去
L~ hi

leave
[liv; li:є]
《leaf 的動詞》<<不及物動詞>>
<植物>長葉子,生葉 (leaf)1．not bother or interfere with；not touch 不要打擾；不要碰
*Go way and leave me alone．走開，不要管我。
*You leave my sister alone or I'll be telling my father．別惹我妹妹，不然我要告訴我爸爸了。
*Leave that machine alone．別碰那台機器。
2．cause sb．to remain alone 撇下…一個人；讓…一個單獨呆著
*I don't want to be left alone．我不願一個人呆著。go away without 遺留；留下
*Can you tell me the time？I've left my watch behind．你能告訴我時間嗎？我沒帶表。
*I realized I'd left my umbrella behind on the train．我意識到把雨傘忘在火車上了。go to；start for 離此而去…；往…出發…
*We are leaving for Canada next week．下星期我們要去加拿大。leave of absence
休假
Peter obtained a ~ from the university. 
彼得從大學得到休假1．stop 停止
*Please leave off biting your nails．請不要咬指甲。
*He told the boys to leave off teasing his little brother．他要那些孩子們停止戲弄他的小弟弟。
*I think we should leave off now and have a cup of tea．我想我們該停下來喝杯茶了。
*We leave off work at 12．我們12點鐘下班。
2．no longer wear；stop wearing or using不再穿；不再使用
*They left their woollen underwear when the weather got warm．天氣轉暖時，他們不穿羊毛衫了。
*She left her coat off when she went out．她沒穿外衣就出去了。
*I have left off my overcoat．我已經不穿大衣了。
*He has left off all ather medicines．他已停服其它所有的藥。1．continue wearing繼續穿
*I feel a bit cold so I'll leave my coat on．我覺得有點冷，所以外套就不脫了。
*It's rude for a man to leave his hat on indoors．一個男子在室內仍戴著帽子是不禮貌的。
2．allow to stay in place or position 使…留在原處
*Leave the cloth on．I want to lay the table for supper．檯布不要取下，我要擺桌子開晚飯了。
3．not switch off 不關
*The electric fire had been left on overnight．電爐整夜沒有關。
*Don't leave the light on when you go out？出去時，請關燈。
*I want to leave the soup on all morning to thicken it．我想把這個湯煮一個上午，讓湯煮稠點。1．omit 省略；刪去
*We can leave out the third sentence．我們可以刪去第3句。
*You can leave out the details；just give us the main facts．你可以省去細節，就告訴我們主要的事實就行了。
2．neglect to put in 遺漏
*In copying this paper，be careful not to leave out any word．抄這個文件時，不要漏掉任何一個字。
*She left out an important detail in her account．她的賬目漏掉了一個重要的項目。
3．exclude；ignore 排除；忽略；冷落（某人）
*Please leave me out of your plans．你的計劃中請不要把我考慮在內。
*Don't leave our teachers out from the invitations．請不要忘記邀請我們的老師們。
*It's Mary's own fault if she feels left out at the party；she makes no effort to be friendly to peple．要是瑪麗感到在晚會上遭冷落，那是她自己的過錯，她一點也不想親近人們。
*You left out the possibility that the train might be late．你忽略了火車晚點的可能性。
4．leave available 留下備用
*If you aren't home when I go to bed，I'll leave some food out for you．如果我睡覺時你還沒回來，我就給你留飯。leave sb．to look after himself；not control sb．聽任某人自行其是；自己照看自己；不去管
*I decided to leave Jim to himself after he had refused to accept any of my suggestions．吉姆拒絕我的任何建議之後，我決定一切由他去。
*The children were left very much to themselves during the holidays．孩子們在假期中可以自由活動。leave-taking
