[lZt; lәt]
<<及物動詞>>
(let.ted,let; let.ting)
(古)妨礙…
<<可數名詞>>
『運動』球觸網
(網球、桌球、排球等發球時,雖然球沒有出界,仍不予計算而須重新發球)
without let or hindrance 
『法律』毫無阻礙地1．allow sb．to do sth．unaided；not interfere with 別管；別干涉
*When joe gets mad，just let him alone．喬發怒時不要去管他。
*Please let my things alone．請不要干涉我的事情。
2．not to mention；to say nothing of 更不用說
*I can't afford a bicycle，let alone a car．我連一部自行車也買不起，更不用說買小轎車了。
*He doesn't have enough money for food，let alone amusements．他連吃飯都不夠，更不用說娛樂了。
*I wouldn't speak to him，let alone trust him and lend him some money．我理都不願理他，更談不上信任他，把錢借給他了。let the past be forgotten 既往不咎
*After a long angry quarrel，the two boys agreed to let bygones be bygones and made friends again．兩個孩子進行了長時間的激烈爭吵，後來同意言歸於好，既往不咎。1．descend；lower 放下
*Please let down the blinds．請把百葉窗放下。
2．disappoint；betray 使…失望
*The team felt that they had let the coach down．隊員們覺得他們讓教練失望了。
*We've been let down so many times by the importers，who always seem to be late delivering the goods．進口商們已多次令我們失望，他們似乎總是要推遲交貨。
*He won't let you down；he's very reliable．他不會讓你失望的，他很靠得住。
3．slow up；slacken 慢下來；鬆懈
*The horse let down near the end of the race and lost．那匹馬在近終點時慢了下來，所以輸了。
*Don't let down even if the going is good．即使在順利的情況下也不要松勁。
*We must not let down our vigilance against the enemy．我們決不可放鬆對敵人的警惕性。
4．lengthen；make（clothes）longer延長；把（衣服）放長
*She let the dress down，several centimetres．她把這件衣服放長了幾厘米。
5．loosen and let fall 披散
*She let her hair down．她披散著頭髮。
6．deflate 放氣
*A naughty boy has let down the back tyre of my bike．一個頑皮的男孩把我自行車後胎的氣給放了。1．release；stop holding 釋放；放手
*The boy grabbed，Jack's coat and would not let go．小男孩抓住傑克的衣服不放。
*The balloon flew up into the air as soon as the child let if go．那孩子一鬆手，氣球就升上了天。
*Let him go．放他走。
2．neglect；pay no attention to 忽視；不注意
*Robert let his teeth go when he was young and now he has to go to the deatist often．羅勃特年輕時對自己的牙齒不注意，現在他不得不常去看牙科醫生。
*After she was married，Jane let herselt go and was not pretty any more．簡結婚以後忽視了打扮自己，就不再漂亮了。
3．weaken and break under pressure 破裂
*The old water pipe suddenly let go and water poured out of it． 舊水管突然破裂，水流了出來。
4．allow sth．to pass；do nothing about 聽其自然；放任；不予計較
*The children teased Frank，but he smiled and let it go．孩子們逗弗蘭克，他笑笑就算了。
*When John was late，the teacher scolded him and let it go at that．當約翰遲到時，老師訓斥了他一頓以後就算了。
5．discharge from a job；fire 撤職；革職
*Mr．Wilson got into a quarrel with his boss and was let go．威爾遜先生與他的老闆吵了一架，被解雇了。
6．make sth．go out quickly；shoot；fire 發射；射出
*The soldiers let go a number of shots．戰士們連發了數槍。
*Paul was so angry that he let go a blow at the boy．保羅生氣揮拳揍那男孩。
*The truck driver saw the flat tire and let go a loud curse．卡車司機看見輪胎漏氣癟了，大罵起來。
7．be free in one's actions or talk；relax 行動或說話無拘束；輕鬆
*Mr．Brown let go at the reunion of his old class and had a good time．布朗先生與老同學重聚時玩得輕鬆愉快。
*The workers worked hard all week，but on Saturday night they went to town and let themselves go．工人們辛苦工作了一周，但在週六晚上則進城去放鬆放鬆。1．（of water）enter by leakage （水）漏入
*These rubber shoes are letting in water．They need repairing．這雙膠鞋漏水，得補一下了。
2．admit；allow to enter or penetrate容許進入
*You'd better open the window and let in the light and fresh air．你最好打開窗戶讓光線和新鮮空氣進入室內。bring sth．upon sb．；cause sb．to incur（a debt，an obligation，a task，etc．）使某人招致某事；使某人捲入（債務、責任、任務等）
*I'm not feeling very pleased with those children；through their carelessness I've been let in for something like thirty dollars．跟那些孩子們在一起感到不太愉快；由於他們不小心，使我花費了大約30美元。
*He's letting himself in for a lot of trouble．他給自己惹來許多麻煩。
*He was let in for a good hundred pounds by his son's bankruptcy．他兒子的破產使他也受到了足足100鎊的損失。share a secret with；allow sb．to know about sth．； permit to participate in 透露秘密；讓某人介入某事；准許加入
*We mustn't let him in on our plans．我們不應讓他瞭解我們的計劃。
*Do let me in on your secret！一定得讓我知道你們的秘密。
*We re fused to let him in on any information concerning the research project．我們拒絕告訴他有關那個研究項目的任何消息。1．allow to enter 讓…進入
*Who let you into the building？ 誰讓你進入大樓的？
2．put into the surface of 嵌入；插入
*She let a piece of lace into her dress．她在衣服上鑲了一條花邊。
3．allow to share （a secret） 告之；使知
*We have let her into the secret．我們已經把秘密告訴了她。
4．assail either physically by blows or with words 責罵某人；拳打某人
*I was so infuriated by what he said that without a word I let into him．他說的話使我大怒，以致於我一句話沒說就揍了他一頓。
*Mr．Brown rose to his feet and let into the last speaker．布朗先生站起來，責罵前一個發言的人。1．allow to go free； set free；loosen； release from restraint 放開；釋放；鬆開；放出
*The farmer opened the gate and let the bull loose in the pasture．農夫打開門，把牛放到草地上。
*Jim caught Ruth' s arm and would not let loose．吉姆抓住露絲的手臂不放。
2．give freedom to sb．to do sth．；allow sb．to speak or act freely 隨心所欲；自由言論；不加限制
*Mother let Jim loose on the apple pie．母親任吉姆吃蘋果餅。
*Who let this teacher loose on that class？ 誰讓這個老師隨心所欲地管那個班的？
*The teacher told Henry that some 368day she was going to let loose and tell him what she thought of him．老師告訴亨利總有一天她要痛快地說出她對他的看法。1．explode；fire；release放（槍、炮、煙火等）；排放
*The boys were letting off fireworks．孩子們在放煙火。
*The engine let off steam in sudden blasts．機車突然放出一股蒸汽來。
*In honour of the distinguished guest．they let off a salute of 21guns．為向貴賓表示敬意，他們鳴禮炮21響
2．excuse from a penalty 免罰
*Two boys were caught smoking in the school but the principal let them off with a warning．兩個男孩在學校抽煙，不過校長對他們提出警告後放了他們。
*With your record， you can hardly expect to be let off lightly．你有前科， 很難指望會從輕發落。She's been let off the dryingup again．她再次忘記台詞又沒有受到批評。
*The magistrate told the youths he would let them off this time, but that they would be severely punished if they appeared before him again．地方法官告訴這些年輕人；他這次放過他們，但如果他們再次在他面前出現，他們將受到嚴懲。
3．discharge；allow to get off 卸下；讓…離開
*The train stops to let off passengers on signal．這列火車按信號停車讓旅客下車。
*I asked the captain to let me off at the next port of call．我請求船長在下個停靠岸讓我下船。
4．excuse from a task or an obligation免除任務或責任等
*Mary's mother said that she would let Mary off from washing the supper dishes．瑪麗的母親准許瑪麗晚餐的碗碟不洗了。
*The factory closed for a month in the summer and let the workers off．工廠夏天停工一個月，放了工人的假。
5．lease in portions；allow to rent a building in portions 分開出租
*The five floors of this large building were let off as separate flats．這座大樓的5層全都分為套間出租。1．allow to be known；reveal one's knowledge of（usu．used in the negative）洩露（常用於否定式）
*Don't let on that I told you．不要說出我告訴了你。
*She was terrified at the information，but didn't let on．她聽到消息十分害怕，但沒有洩露。
*Don't let on about what they did．不要講他們幹的事。
2．pretend；make believe 假裝；裝做
*He let on that he did not see me．他裝做沒有看見我。
*She is not as rich as she lets on．她並不像她裝得那樣有錢。
*They let on that they didn't care about not being invited，but I could tell they were hurt．他們未被邀請，作出滿不在意的樣子，但是我知道他們的自尊心受到了傷害。
*He got the job by letting on that he had a lot of experience．他裝著很有經驗的樣子得到了這份工作。reveal；inform；tell 告訴；通知
*Don't let onto Helen that we are planning to go to the movies tonight．不要告訴海倫我們今晚要看電影。1．rent out 租出去
*He used to let out cars．他過去出租汽車。
*In the park boats are let out for 3yuan per hour．在公園裡，可以以每小時3元的價格出租小遊艇。
2．allow to go out or escape 放出The guard let the prisoners out of jail to work in the garden．看守放犯人出牢房，在園子裡幹活。
*Let me out！I'm locked in！讓我出來！我被鎖在裡面了！
*The doctor is letting her out of hospital next week．醫生打算下周讓她出院。
3．tell；reveal 洩漏
*I'll never tell you another secret if you let this one out．假如你把這個機密洩漏出去，有秘密的事我再也不告訴你了。
*Who let out the exam results？They were supposed to be confidential until tomorrow．誰洩露了考試結果？在明天以前這些結果都屬於機密。
*Someone has let the news out．有人把這個消息洩露出去了。
4．make larger 放大
*Mary's mother had to let out Mary's dress because she was growing so tall．瑪麗的母親不得不把瑪麗的衣服放大些，因為瑪麗長得那麼高。
*If she gets much fatter she will have to let out all her dresses．如果她繼續發胖，她所有的衣服都得放寬。
5．dismiss 解雇；革職；開除
*The shop closed down and all the men were let out．店關了門，所有的員工都被辭退了。
6．terminate；be finished；end（學校）放學；（戲院）散場；（訓練）結束
*When does the university let out for the summer？大學何時放暑假？
*The coach let us out from practice at 3 o'clock．訓練到 3點鐘，教練把我們解散了。
*They were waiting for school to let out．他們在等學校放學。
7．make（a sound）come out of the mouth；utter 自口中發出（聲音）
*A bee stung Charles．He let out a yell and ran home．一隻蜜蜂咬了查理，他大叫一聲跑回家了。
*He let out a cry of pain as the nail went into his foot．釘子扎進他的腳時，他痛苦地大喊了一聲。
8．release from further responsibility；release from an obligation 免除進一步的責任；免除義務
*I was glad to be let out of that nasty affair，and have someone more experienced handle the trouble．我高興的是我從那件討厭的事情中解脫了，已讓另外一個更有經驗的人去處理。
*My flu let me out of attending the meeting．由於患了流感；我參加不了那個會了。
*The regular teacher is back，that let me out．正式的老師回來了，我可以解脫了。
9．release from restraint；allow to gather speed 使放開速度；讓…加速前進
*He turned into an express way and let the car out．他把車子轉入高速公路，然後加速前進。
*The rider let out his horse to try to beat the one ahead of him．騎士放馬快跑想追上領先的那匹馬。1．lessen in intensity；diminish；slacken off 減少；放鬆
*It's raining hard as ever．It's not letting up at all．雨下得還是那麼大，根本沒有小下來。
*Harry never lets up for a minute．哈利一刻也沒有松勁。
2．stop working 停止；停止做
*Let up for a few minutes．You can't work hard all day．歇一會吧，你不能整天苦幹。
*The doctor has been working for fifty hours without letting up．醫生已馬不停蹄地連續工作了50小時。
3．become easier，kinder or less strict 寬容（常與on連用）
*Let up on Jane．She is sick．對簡寬容點，她病了。
*Let up on him．He didn't mean any harm．饒了他吧，他並沒有什麼惡意。

