<<可數名詞>>
(英) (鐵路和馬路等的) 平面交差,平交道( (美)grade crossing)1．make level by lowering the height of 剷平；弄平
*That path is too high；level it down from here．那條路太高，從這裡把它剷平。
2．lower；reduce 降低；減低
*We must make sure the expansion of higher education does not level down university standards．我們一定要做到既發展高等教育又不降低大學水平。1．make flat or level 整平；弄平
*The bulldozers quickly levelled off the site．推土機很快就把工地平整了。
2．even off；become steady 穩定；達到平衡
*After going up for half a year，the cost of living levelled off in September．物價上漲了半年之後，在9月份穩定了。
*Production has levelled off now and we don't expect to increase it．現在生產已經穩定，我們並不期望增加生產。
3．return to a horizontal position in flight（飛機）恢復水平飛行
*The plane climbed to 10，000 metres and then levelled off．飛機升到1萬米高度後就水平飛行了。1．move horizontally（after climbing）； remain steady（上升後）水平飛行；達到平衡
*We climbed steeply after takeoff，and levelled out at 25，000 feet．我們起飛後就急劇上升，到達2萬5千英尺時才水平飛行。
2．remove by means of a lever 用槓桿移動
*He levelled the stone out．他用槓桿挪動那塊石頭。
*They have tried to level him out of his powerful position．他們試圖把他從有權力的職務上拉下來。
3．lift out 抬起
*He levelled himself out of the chair．他從椅子上站起來。bring what is lower to an equality with what is higher 提升；提至高水平
*The old clerks with small salaries applied to have them levelled up to the salaries of the newcomers．薪水低的老職員請求把他們的薪水提高到和新來的人一樣高。level-headed
