輕油discover by chance；find or come upon unexpectedly 偶然發現；無意中發現；偶爾得到
*If you look hard enough in this field，you may light on some valuable ancient coins．你若在這塊地上用心找，或許能找到一些有價值的古錢幣。
*The explorers suddenly lit upon an entrance to secrer chamber．搜索人員突然發現了密室的一條通道。
*When I was in a secondhand bookshop I lighted on a book I had been looking for for ages．我在一家舊書店無意中得到了我已找了好久的書。light opera.
<<名詞>>
= operetta1．run as fast as one can 盡快跑；拚命跑
*John lit out for home with the bully chasing him．因為有流氓在追他，約翰拚命地往家跑。
2．go away in a hurry；leave suddenly 匆匆離去
*The gang packed their bags and lit out of town．那幫傢伙收拾行李匆匆逃出了城。
*The robbers lit out for Mexico．盜匪們匆匆向墨西哥逃去。light pen
