(某星球與較弱星球等中任何星球亮度之比)light stand
燈台light trap
遮光通路; 殺蟲燈1．fill with light；illuminate brightly or extensively 照亮
*The searchlight lit up the whole area．探照燈把整個地區都照亮了。
*The house was all lit up as though a big celebration was going on．滿屋燈火通明，宛如在進行一場大慶典。
*The streets were well lighted up．街上燈火輝煌。
2．switch on the headlights of a motor vehicle at dusk；switch on the street lighting（黃昏時）打開車燈；開亮街燈
*It's seven o'clock，and still one or two cars haven't lit up．已經 7點鐘了，仍有個別車輛沒有開燈。
*At this time of the year，the official hour to light up is sixthirty．在這個季節，規定開街燈的時間是6點半鐘。
3．light a pipe，cigarette or cigar 點上煙斗、香煙或雪茄
*I had difficulty lighting up my cigarrette in the strong wind．刮這麼大的風，我很難點著煙。
*The two men lit up their pipes and then sat down for a chat．兩個人點上煙斗，坐下來談心。
*As soon as the meal was over all the smokers lit up．一吃完飯，所有抽煙的人都點上了煙。
4．suddenly look pleased and happy；become cheerful 突然高興；面露喜色
*Her face lit up with joy when she heard the good news．當她聽到這則好消息時，面露喜色。
*Tom will surely light up when he sees his new bike．湯姆看到他的新自行車時，必定很高興。
*Her face lit up with happiness．他臉上喜氣洋洋。light valve
光閥light wave
