(春分及秋分時期常發生的風暴或暴風雨)1．form into a line；form a queue 排列一行；排長隊
*The people lined up at the ticket office．人們在售票處排隊購票。
*I hate lining up in the cold to go to a cinema．我討厭為了看一場電影而在大冷天排長隊。2．take places in a line or formation；stand side by side；form a line or pattern 排隊；整隊；排列起來*The monitor lined up his class in the playground．班長讓全班學生在大操場排好隊。*Shoes of various sizes were lined up on the shelves．貨架上排列著各種尺碼的鞋子。
3．arrange 安排
*Who lined you up to speak at the meeting？誰安排你在大會上發言的？
*What songs are lined up for tonight's broadcast？今晚的廣播安排了哪些歌曲？
4．make ready for action；take up a position，for election，etc．；complete a plan or agreement for；arrange完成佈置；安排妥當；為選舉擺開陣勢等
*His friends lined up so many votes for him that he won the election．他的朋友們幫他拉了很多票，所以他競選成功了。
*The political parties have lined up behind their candidates．各政黨都已擺開陣勢來支持他們的候選人。
*He lined up a summer job before school was out．學期結束之前他已經為自己安排好了一個暑假工作。
5．obtain；contrive 獲得；設法做到
*They have lined up a lot of support for their candidate．他們已經為他們的候選人爭得了許多票。
6．become ready for action；come together in preparation or agreement 聯合起來；一起行動
*Larry wanted to go to the seashore for the family vacation，but the rest of the family lined up against him．萊裡想要全家去海邊度假，但是家中其他人一致反對。line-fir.ing
