[laIv; laiv]
活櫟樹,維吉尼亞櫟
(學名Quercus virginiana,產於美國東南部,其木材極為堅硬,從前多用於造船)1．survive on 靠…活下去
*He lived off fruit and nuts in the forest．他在森林裡靠水果和堅果維持生命。
*These animals with long necks live off leaves of tall trees．這些長頸動物吃高樹的樹葉。
2．live at the cost of；depend on for support and shelter 靠…供應
*He's been living off his brother for nearly a year．近一年來他一直靠他兄弟接濟。
3．find enough food or income尋求足夠的食物或收入
*She will not be able to live off her writing．靠寫作她是難以謀生的。1．have…as food or diet；rely on as food 以…為食
*They live chiefly on rice．他們以米為主食。
*He lives on plain food．他靠粗茶淡飯度日。
2．depend upon for support，etc．靠…過活
*How can he manage to live on that pension？依靠那點養老金他怎樣生活呢？
*He lost his job and lived on credit．他失去了工作，靠借貸過日子。
*I can't live on air！我總不能靠喝西北風過日子！
*Don't live on rumourmongering and lying．不要靠造謠說謊過日子。
3．continue to live；continue 繼續活著；繼續存在
*He will die，but his fame will live on after him．他是要死的，但是他的聲譽將永存。
*These traditions will live on for centuries．這些傳統將世代相傳。
*live on one's name／reputation keep one's position or continue to earn money because one has been successful in the past 靠過去的名聲維持生活（或掙錢）；吃老本
*Tom has only written one bestselling book；he can't live on his reputation for ever．湯姆只寫了一本暢銷書，他不能只靠這本書的名聲過一輩子。1．stay alive through；survive；last through；endure to the end of 活過（一段時期）；保持壽命；忍受到最後
*He lived out the earthquake，but his house was completely destroyed．他雖然經歷地震而活過來了，但他的房子徹底完了。
*The patient lived out another month．病人又活了一個月。
*I doubt if she'll live out the winter．我懷疑她是否能熬過這個冬天。
2．live outside a place of work or institution在所在單位外寄宿My servant lives out．我家的傭人不住在我家。
3．finish（a period of time）； spend 完成（一段時間）；消磨時間
*After retiring，John and his wife lived out their lives in Florida．退休後，約翰和他太太在佛羅里達度過餘生。live parking
<<不可數名詞>>
駕駛人不離開的停車live steam
[laIv; laiv]
活汽,新汽
(直接從鍋爐出來的高壓蒸氣)experience and survive 經歷…而未死；活過
*The old worker who spoke to us yesterday had lived through the three revolutionary civil wars．昨天跟我們講話的那位老人經歷過3次國內革命戰爭。
*I don't think the old man will manage to live through another bad winter．我想這位老人熬不過明年的嚴冬了。
*All those who lived through the earthquake still have fear in their hearts．所有經歷過那次地震的人至今仍然心有餘悸。1．reach or maintain a certain high standard達到；不辜負（期望）；無愧於
*This car wil certainly live up to all your expectations if you buy it，sir．如果你買這輛車的話，先生，它將肯定會使你一切如願的。
*It was clear that he would never live up to his father's expectations．很顯然他永遠也達不到他父親對他的期望。
*We'll live up to what our Party expects of us．我們決不辜負黨對我們的期望。
2．act according to；agree with；follow 遵守（原則）；履行（諾言）等
*Students should live up to certain standards of behaviour．學生應該遵守一定的行為準則。
*It is difficult to live up to the principles of the Christian religion．實行基督教的信條是不容易的。
*You must live up to your promises．你必須履行你的諾言。live weight
