look for?
(1) 尋找…; 尋求…; 採集
~ for a job 
找工作
She ~ed in her bag for her house key. 
她打開手提包找房子的鑰匙
They are ~ing for exciteme1．be on the watch；be on the lookout提防；留心；注視；戒備
*When you ride in the street you must look about lest you bump into someone．在街上騎自行車時，你必須留神四周，免得撞著別人。
*Look about before you cross the street．過馬路前，要四下看看。
2．turn one's eyes to；go about observing in（a country，town，etc．）觀察；察看；遊覽
*They spent two months in New York looking about the city．他們在紐約花了兩個月的功夫遊覽該城。
*The boy looked about with great interest．這男孩懷著極大的興趣四周看看。
3．inspect or survey（moving about while doing so）視察；調查
*You must look about before making the decision．你得考慮好了再作決定。
4．search around 四處尋找
*I'm looking about for a house．我正在找房子。
*For a whole month Bill went here and there，looking about for a job．整整一個月，比爾到處奔波找工作。1．take care of；attend to照顧
*John's mother told him to look after his younger brother．約翰的母親告訴他好好照顧弟弟。
*She has looked after her elderly parents for many years．多年來她一直照顧她年邁的父母。
*When he went to Europe，Mr．Jenkins left his son to look after the business．詹金斯先生去歐洲時，把生意交給兒子照管。
2．follow（a departing person or thing） with the eye 目送
*My mother stood at the gate and looked after us as we walked toward the railway station．我媽媽站在大門口，目送著我們向火車站走去。
3．pay attention to；concern oneself with 對…關注；為…操心He knows how to look after his own interests．他知道如何照顧到他自己的利益。
*Don't look after your own interests to the exclusion of those of others．不要只顧自己的利益而不顧別人的利益。think of and prepare for future needs考慮到將來；展望未來；預料
*We must look ahead before we go further in the matter．在進一步進行這件事情之前，我們必須考慮得遠一些。
*We are looking ahead to a prosperous future．我們預料將會有一個繁榮昌盛的未來。1．watch 看
*Father always looks at me with love in his eyes．父親總帶著慈祥的眼光看著我。Everybody looked at the hero with great admiration．大家都以欽佩的目光注視這位英雄。
2． have a way of thinking or feeling toward； think about sth．in a certain way； consider對…持某種看法或感覺；考慮
*Is he a hero or a villain？ That depends on how you look at it．他是英雄還是惡魔？那要取決於你如何看待他了。
*We should look at problems from different aspects，not from just one．看問題要從各個方面去看，不能只從單方面看。
*What he looks at is its economy．他是從經濟的角度看問題的。
3． judge by the outward appearance從表面看來；從外觀來看
*To look at her， you'd never guess that she is a university professor．從外表看，你決不會猜到她是一位大學教授。
*The building is not much to look at．這幢房子的式樣不怎麼好看。
4．examine；inspect檢查；察看；調查
*You'd better have your ankle looked at by the doctor．你最好讓醫生檢查一下你的踝骨。
*Have you asked the plumber to come and look at the leaking pipe？你叫管道工來檢查過漏水的管子了嗎？
*We must look at all the facts．我們必須調查所有事實。
5．consider or accept（a proposal，suggestion， offer， etc．）（usu．used in negative form）考慮或接受（建議、提供等）（通常用否定式）
*I wouldn't look at a job like that．我不願接受那樣的工作。
*After the way he treated her， she wouldn't look at another man．她領略了他對待她的方式以後，就不願再和任何男人打交道了。1．review the past ； think of what has happened回顧過去；回想
*If we look back， we will realize the tremendous changes reform has made．回顧過去，我們就會發現改革帶來的巨大變化。
*He looked back with remorse on the serious mistakes he had made．他回顧自己所犯的嚴重錯誤，深感悔恨。
*As John looked back，his life seemed good to him．約翰回顧過去的生活時，他覺得過得不錯。
2． show signs of retrogression or interrupted progress後退；停止不前；畏縮
*Don't look back； you will succeed．不要畏縮，你一定會成功的。1．look angry面現怒容
*He looked black at his enemy．他怒視敵人。
2．appear threatening；indicate misfortune（形勢等）看上去嚴峻；呈現危機
*The future looked black when father got hurt and could not work．父親受了傷不能去上班，前景很嚴峻。
*As prices dropped lower and lower，things looked black for Henry's company．價格一再下跌，亨利的公司面臨了危機。appear astonished，confused or perplexed吃驚；茫然不知所措
*He looked blank when he was informed of his dismissal．聽說他被解雇時，他茫然不知所措。1．look unhappy；look disheartened or dejected愁眉不展；沮喪
*She looks blue all day．她整日愁眉不展。
*The banker looked blue when he read of the decline in stocks．那位銀行家讀到股票下跌的新聞時，神情十分沮喪。
*You are looking blue， what's the matter？你愁眉苦臉，出了什麼事啦？
2． have no hope無希望
*Things look blue．事情沒有希望了。feel scorn at； think of as worthless 鄙視；瞧不起
*He looks down his nose at his classmates'interest in Jazz．他鄙視班上的同學醉心於爵士樂。
*Jerry was the athlete who looked down his nose at the weak students．傑裡是位運動員，他看不起身體不強壯的學生。
*Why do you always look down your nose at people who aren't dreesed as smartly as you？你為什麼總要看不起那些穿著不如你瀟灑的人呢？despise； scorn； consider inferior蔑視；輕視
*Jack looked down upoo Alf for his poor manners．傑克因阿爾夫舉止粗魯而瞧不起他。
*Everyone looks down upon you，just because you've not got a job．大家都瞧不起你，就是因為你沒有工作。
*They are snobs． That is why they look down upon us．他們是勢利眼，這就是他們看不起我們的原因。1．try to find； seek；search for尋找；尋求
*He is looking for a job．他在找工作。
*We are looking for an ambitious young assistant．我們正在找一名有雄心壯志的青年助手。
2．expect期待
*Bob wouldn't go for a ride with other boys because he was looking for a phone call from Julie．鮑勃不肯與其他男孩一起去兜風，因為他在等朱麗的電話。
*It's clear that the result of the experiment was better than we had been looking for．很明顯，試驗的結果要比我們預料的好。
*We didn't look for such a success．這樣的成功是我們沒想到的。
*Don't look for any help from him．別期待他會幫助你。
3．do things that cause（one's own trouble）自找（麻煩）
*Joe often gets into fights because he is always looking for trouble．喬常跟人家打架，因為他總是惹麻煩。
*If you say the opposite of everything that others say， you are looking for a quarrel．假若你跟人家唱反調，你就是在自找麻煩。expect； be eager for； anticipate期待；盼望
*Frank was looking forward to that evening's date．弗蘭剋期待著那天晚上的約會。
*Jim has been working hard and looks forward to spending his vacation lying on the beach doing nothing．吉姆一直工作努力，他渴望能躺在海邊什麼也不幹，度過假期。make a short visit；drop in拜訪On his way downtown， Jim looked in on his aunt．吉姆在進城的路上順道看望了他的嬸母。
*I'll look in on you again sometime，Mary！Bye for now！過些時候我會再來看你的，瑪麗！再見！face bravely or without shame；meet with a steady look勇敢對待；直視；面對
*Mary looked the gangster in the eye， and he turned away without hurting her．瑪麗面對歹徒面無懼色，結果歹徒逃走，沒有傷害她。
*I promised to write to Julie while I was on vacation，and if I don't do it， I won't be able to look her in the eye．我答應在假期中給朱麗寫信，如果不寫，我將不好意思見她。
*He had an easy conscience and could look everybody in the face．他心中坦然，什麼人都敢正視。1．examine；inspect；investigate 調查；研究
*He promised me to look into the matter．他答應我調查此事。
*Mr． Jones said he was looking into the possibility of buying a house．瓊斯先生說他正在研究買房子的可能性。
*The government will look into how to reduce unemployment．政府將研究如何降低失業率。
*Thank you very much for the information，sir；I'll get one of our detectives to look into the matter．非常感謝你提供這些情況，先生，我將指派一名偵探調查此事。
2．dip into（a book，etc．）；consult （a book， etc．） in a rapid or cursory manner瀏覽（書等）；快速或草率地查閱（書等）
*I usually look into a book before deciding whether to read it．我通常在決定是否讀這本書之前先瀏覽一下。
3．make a brief call or visit to；enter（a house， etc．） for a few moments in passing對…作暫短的訪問或參觀；順便進入（房屋等）看看
*I'll look into the library on the way home to borrow some books for my children．在回家的路上，我將順便去圖書館給孩子們借幾本書。
*I must look into the garage on the way home to book a service for the car．回家時我得順路到汽車修理廠去預約檢修汽車的事情。face朝向
*This building looks on to the public centre square．這個建築物面朝中心廣場。1．be careful；watch 小心；注意Look out！ A train is coming．注意！火車來了。
*Look out when you're crossing the street．過馬路要小心。
2．search for尋找
*Go through the books in our library and look out any that you would like to borrow．到我們的圖書館去仔細找，把你要借的書挑出來。
*She's looked out some clothes for her trip．她為自己的旅行挑選了幾件衣服。1．watch out for；keep a watch for 密切注意；提防
*When you're eating fish，look out for the bones．吃魚的時候，當心魚刺。
*You must look out for catching cold．你得小心，不要感冒了。
2．seek if one can find尋找
*Will you go to the station and look out for your uncle？你去火車站找你叔叔嗎？
*We have been looking out for a new house， but the ones we've seen have all been too expensive．我們一直在找一所新房子，但是我們看的幾所房子都要價太高。
3． take care of照顧；照看
*You needn't worry about me， I can look out for myself．你不用替我擔心，我會照顧自己的。
*If you're catching the same train as me，I'll look out for you．如果你要和我同乘一次火車，我會照料你的。face；overlook面對
*Their rear windows look out upon a lovely garden．他們的後窗面對一個美麗的花園。
*Our apartment looks out on a river．我們的公寓房間面對一條河。1． examine carefully or fully全面或仔細檢查
*They have looked over the accounts．他們已經查過帳目。
*I want to look over these exercises before I give them to the teacher．交給老師之前，我要把這些作業檢查一遍。
*The manager has looked over your work and has some comments to make．他仔細地檢查了你的工作，並且要提出一些看法。
2．fail to see or notice ； pass over without punishing忽略；寬恕
*He has done wrong but the teacher will look over it this time．他做錯了，但老師這次將原諒他。
*I'll look over your carelessness this time，
*but be more careful in future．這次我原諒你的粗心大意，但以後得細心點。
3．revise複習
*I should look over my notes before the exam．考試前我得複習我的筆記。
4． inspect by making a tour of（a house，etc．）仔細查看；巡視
*We must look the school over before sending our son there．我們得先去仔細考察一番這所學校，再決定是否把兒子送去學習。
*You should look over the house before you decide to move in．在決定搬進去之前，你必須先去看一下房子。
5．peer over從…上面看過去
*The thief pulled himself to the top of the wall and looked over．小偷爬上牆頭觀望。1．examine possibilities before deciding sth．事前仔細考慮；慎思而後行
*Don't make a hurried decision； look round well first．不要忙於做決定，先好好考慮一下。
2． look in all directions四下環顧
*Don't look round； I don't want him to notice us．不要四下張望，我不想讓他注意我們。
3．go about observing in；visit；inspect； go sightseeing四處遊覽；參觀；視察
*Do we have time to look round before lunch？午飯前我們還有時間逛逛嗎？
*The party was looking round the factory．這一行人在參觀工廠。hurry趕快
*Look sharp！ We haven't much time to waste．趕快！我們沒多少時間可以浪費。1． study； examine溫習
*Look through your notes before the examination．考試前把你的筆記從頭至尾看一遍。
2．inspect carefully仔細查看
*I looked through my drawer， but I could not find my keys．我仔細查過抽屜，但是找不到鑰匙。
*You have to look through those reports before you attend the meeting．開會前，你必須把那些報告看一遍。
3．not see sb． or sth． that is clearly visible； deliberately ignore sb．one can plainly see故意視而不見
*I met him on the way home yesterday，but he just looked straight through me．昨天我在回家的路上碰見了他，但他卻故意不理睬我。
*You must be blind，I was standing ten yards away， and you looked straight through me．你一定瞎眼了，當時我站在離你只有10碼遠的地方，你竟看不到我。
4． survey or scan（a book， paper，etc．） often briefly粗略地檢查、瀏覽或翻閱
*I usually look through newspapers after supper．晚飯後我常常瀏覽一下報紙。1． attend to ； take care of ； give attention to照管；照顧；注意
*The president assigned a man to look to our needs．總統派了一個人來對我們要求的東西作出安排。
*We must each look to our own work．我們每個人都必須負責自己的工作。
*Look to it that this doesn't happen again．注意不要讓這種事再發生。
*Look to your manner，my boy，don't be so rude．注意禮貌，孩子，別這麼無禮。
2． depend on； turn to for help依賴；指望
*They all look to you for help．他們全都依賴你的幫助。
*He is ashamed to look to others for assistance．他不好意思求別人幫助。
*We looked to him to settle most of the troubles that arose among us．我們都指望他來解決我們中間產生的大部分問題。
3．look forward to； expect預期；期待
*We look to the day when world peace will be a reality．我們期待著世界和平實現的一天。
*We looked to her for a solo．我們希望她來一個獨唱。
4．（a house， a building， etc．） face 面向；朝向
*The house looks to the south．這房子朝南。1．call on sb ； pay a visit訪問或拜訪某人
*Do look me up next time you are in town．下次進城請一定來看我。
*I must look up Uncle George．I've heard he's in bed with arthritis．我應該去看看喬治叔叔，聽說他因關節炎臥床不起了。
2．search for in a dictionary，a reference book， etc．查閱字典或參考書等
*Can you look up the time of the next train to Beijing？你能查一查下一趟去北京的火車時間嗎？
*I'll look it up in the encyclopaedia．我將在百科全書中查閱它。
*If you don't know the meaning of a word， look it up in the dictionary．如果你不懂一個詞的意思，就查一查詞典。
*He is looking a name up in the telePhone directory．他在電話簿裡找一個人的名字。
3． rise in price上漲
*The price of goods is looking up．物價正在上漲。
4．be improving；promise more success好轉；漸有起色；進步
*The weather is looking up at last．天氣終於好起來了。
*Share prices are looking up again！So is business．股票行情又見漲！生意也有了起色。
*The first year was tough， but business looked up after that．頭一年很困難，但後來生意就興旺起來了。
5．raise eyes仰望
*She looked up and saw me．她抬頭看見了我。
6．seek and find尋找
*While he was in Chicago Henry looked up a friend of college days．亨利在芝加哥時，尋找一位大學時代的朋友。
*If I had known you were in the office building， I would have looked you up．如果知道你在辦公樓裡，我就來找你了。admire；respect highly尊敬
*Mr． Smith had taught for many years， and all the students looked up to him．史密斯先生執教多年，他的學生都非常尊敬他。
*He was always taught to look up to older people．他接受的教育總是要尊敬老人。look-alike
