C
1 a. 使…成為…; 使…顯得…
Flowers help to ~ a room more cheerful.1． make less by a very small amount； reduce slightly略為減少
*The boy shoveled and shoveled， but he didn't seem to make a dent in the pile of sand．這男孩鏟了又鏟，可他好像並沒有把沙鏟走多少。
2． make a first step towards success in取得進展
*Peter studied all evening，but hardly made a dent in his homework．彼得整晚都在學習，但他的作業似乎沒有進展。be of importance關係重大；重要
*It does make a difference．那確實是很重要的。
*John's score on the test will make the difference between his passing or failing the course．約翰這次考試的得分關係著他這門功課能否通過。make faces做苦臉；扮鬼臉
*She made a face when I told her to take the medicine．我要她吃藥時，她做了個鬼臉。
*The child made a face when he was scolded．這孩子被訓時做了一個鬼臉。trick；deceive愚弄；欺騙
*He did not know his roommate was making a fool of him．他不知道他的室友在愚弄他。gain wealth；become rich發財
*He went to Australia and soon made a fortune．他去澳大利亞，不久便發了財。show unnecessary nervousness or excitement大驚小怪
*Please don't make a fuss over such a thing．請不要為這點小事大驚小怪。
*She made a tremendous fuss about it．這件事她鬧得滿城風雨。cause to be a success；produce good results使成功
*In brief， we should make a success of the conference．總之，這次會議我們要開好。
*Several times I thought in despair，「It's no good， we'll never make a go of it．」有好幾次我絕望地想：「毫無辦法，我們決不會成功的。」say sth． briefly長話短說
*Make a long story short，John；there isn't much time left．長話短說吧，約翰，時間不多了。1． regard as necessary or very important； lay streaa on重視；強調
*John makes a point of reading a fresh book every month．約翰堅持每月讀一本新書。
2． be careful to； be sure to特別注意地做；有意識地做
*Punctual people always make a point of being a little early．準時的人總是有意識地稍微早一點兒。
*He made a point of thanking his hostess before he left the party．離開宴會前他特地去感謝女主人一番。
*He always made a point of helping old ladies cross the road．他總是小心翼翼地幫助老太太們過馬路。
*If someone sends you a gift， make a point of thanking them the next time you meet．當有人送你禮物時，下次見面時一定要謝謝他。
*Because I was late for class， I made a point of apologizing to the teacher after class．因為我上課遲到了，下課時我特意向老師道歉。
3． try hard to； take pains to努力去做
*He made a point of remembering to get his glasses fixed．他讓自己務必記住去修眼鏡。
*Since she couldn't put up with him at all， she made a point of ignoring him altogether．她一點也不能容忍他，因此她總是千方百計地迴避他。make a habit of養成…的習慣
*Make a practice of being on time for work．要養成按時工作的習慣。
*They made a practice of taking a walk together every evening．他們每天傍晚總是一起散步。chase； follow追逐
*He made after the enemy officer regardless of the danger to himself．他不顧個人安危追逐敵軍官。1． take into consideration考慮（到）
*The tailor made allowance for the growth of the boy and didn't cut his coat small．裁縫考慮到孩子會長大，沒有把他的外衣裁小。
*The court was asked to make allowances for his age．法院被要求考慮他的年齡。
*It would be sensible to add a further￡200 to the budget to make allowance for inflation．考慮到漲價的因素，在預算之外再追加英鎊是一個明智之舉。
2．excuse for原諒
*You must make allowance for his ill manners．你必須原諒他的不禮貌。
*They esteemed each other and made allowances for each other．他們互敬互諒。punish sb． as a warning to others 殺一儆百
*The teacher made an example of the boy who copied from another student during the test．老師懲罰了考試中抄襲別人試卷的男孩以警告別的學生。
*The headmaster made an example of Jane to try to stop misbehavior by the other pupils．校長對簡作了懲罰，以儆戒其他同學不要調皮搗蛋。1． have a strong influence on使深受印象
*His speech made a strong impression on the audience．他的演說給聽眾留下了深刻的印象。
2． have an effect on對…有效
*Punishment seemed to make no impression on the child．懲罰似乎對這小孩不產生效果。make and break
電流斷續器start to attack襲擊
*The prisoner made at the guard with a knife．囚犯用刀襲擊看守。1． steal and hurry away with攜…而逃
*He made away with a large amount of money．他竊走了一大筆錢。
*Two masked men held up the clerk and made away with the payroll．兩個戴面具的匪徒截住了職員，搶走了薪水冊。
2．spend花掉；浪費
*He soon made away with his fortune．他很快就把財產揮霍一空。
3．eat up吃完
*The kid made away the whole pie．那小孩把整整一大塊餡餅都吃光了。
4．destroy毀滅；消除
*He tried to make away with the proof．他企圖消滅罪證。
5．kill殺死；謀殺
*The poor fellow made away with himself unnecessarily for he was proved innocent．這個可憐人無謂地自殺了，因為他已被證明是無罪的。
*Our neighbor tried to make away with herself by drinking posison．我們的鄰居試圖服毒自殺。
*They made away with their opponents．他們暗殺了他們的對手。1． pretend假裝
*He made believe not to be aware of my presence．他假裝不知道我在場。
*Let's make believe that we're Red Indians．讓我們假扮成印第安人。The boys made believe that they were explorers in the African forests．孩子們假裝他們是非洲森林裡的探險家。
2． imagine as if sth． is true while you know it is not幻想
*She used to set the table for two and make believe that her husband was with her again．她過去總是擺兩個人的飯，幻想她丈夫還同她在一起。make sure（of）弄清楚；確定
*Make certain where we are going．弄清楚我們去哪兒。
*Have you made certain of the time of the train？火車的時間你已弄清楚了嗎？clarify； explain解釋
*The meaning of the story is made clear in the introduction．這個故事的含意在引言中已說清楚。make smaller使…變小
*Can you make the dress down for her younger sister？你能把她妹妹的這件衣服做小點嗎？
*The eldest girl's frocks can be made down for her sisters．那最大女孩的外衣可以改小給她妹妹們穿。make fast
『航海』縛定
(浮標、柱子、椿等)

fasten firmly繫緊
*Tie the rope round the pole and then make it fast．把繩子繞在桿子上，然後繫緊。
*I forgot to make fast the back door．我忘了把後門關好。1． go in the direction of向…前進After the concert the crowd made for the nearest door．音樂會結束後，人群湧向離他們最近的門。
*As the mother came into the room，her little girl made straight for her．當母親走進房間時，她的小女孩直向她撲去。
2．promote對…有益
*Does early rising make for good health？早起可以增進身體健康嗎？
*What you've said will make for the good relations between our two people．你講的話有助於發展我們兩國人民的友好關係。
3． attack ； rush violently攻擊；襲擊
*When I was half way across the field the bull made for me and I had to run．當我走到田中間時，那頭公牛向我衝來，我只得跑開。1． take or use without asking隨便用
*Bob makes free with his roommate's clothes．鮑勃隨便穿他室友的衣服。
*Your friends at the party who made so free with the drinks weren't invited！你的那些在晚會上擅自喝酒的朋友竟然不請自來。
2． act in a rude way無禮
*The girls don't like Ted because he makes free with them．女孩子們不喜歡泰德，因為他對她們無禮。become friendly with與…交友
*Within two days she made friends with everybody on the boat．兩天之內她便同船上的每個人交了朋友。
*Chuck's made friends with several people at work．查克跟好幾個一同工作的人交上朋友。joke about； laugh at開玩笑James was making fun of the new pupil．詹姆士在與那位新生開玩笑。
*People enjoy making fun of the clothes I wear， though they seem all right to me．他們愛拿我穿的衣服開玩笑，雖然我的衣服對我似乎很合適。1． do what one promises to do遵守諾言
*The government still has to make good many promises it made at the last election．政府仍然必須兌現它在上次選舉中做的許多承諾。
*He made good his word and arrived at the conference in time despite many difficulties．他遵守諾言，克服了困難，準時到會。
*Joe made good his boast to swim across the lake．喬吹牛說要游過湖去，他真的那麼做了。
2． pay for the loss賠償
*The insurance company will make good your loss．保險公司將賠償你的損失。
3．succeed成功
*I am sure he will make good．我相信他會成功的。
*The story is the traditional one of a local boy from a poor background who dreams of glory and eventually makes good．這是一個傳統的故事，講的是當地的一位少年出生貧寒，渴望榮耀，最後終於如願以償。travel rapidly at good speed按規定的速度迅速前進
*We made good time on our trip to Florida．我們很快抵達佛羅里達旅遊。move fast； hurry趕快
*Mary saw that she had hurt John's feelings， and made haste to say she was sorry．瑪麗見她傷害了約翰的感情，連忙說對不起。
*The shepherds made haste to gather their sheep before dark．牧羊人在天黑之前匆匆把羊群趕在一起。1． be successful成功
*It's a very difficult examination；are you sure you can make it？這次考試很難，你肯定能通過嗎？
*It's natural to have dreams of success and fame，but only a few people in this world actually make it．夢想成功和追求名利是很自然的，但這世界上只有為數不多的人能真正做到。
2．get to a destination or an appointment in time及時到達目的地或及時約會
*The bus goes in ten minutes；you must hurry or you won't make it．汽車還有10分鐘就要開了，你必須快一點，否則就趕不上了。
*You can't make it to the other shore in this weather．天氣惡劣，你到不了對岸。
3．recover痊癒；復原
*The doctor knew that the man was unlikely to make it．醫生知道這人很可能治不好了。consider unimportant；minimize the importance of．輕視；看不起
*The soldier made light of his wound．這個士兵沒把傷當一回事。
*Tom made light of his mistakes，but his teacher didn't at all．湯姆對他的錯誤不當一回事，可他的老師對他的錯誤卻很認真。
*In fact， she suffered great inconvenience， but she made light of the whole affair when I asked her about it．事實上，她遇到了很大麻煩，可我向她提起此事時，她卻一點都不放在心上。1．treat as of little importance輕視
*She makes little of walking fifty kilometres in a day．她一天走50公里是不在乎的。
*He made little of his illness．他認為自己的病無關緊要。
2．hardly understand簡直弄不懂I could make little of what he was saying．我簡直弄不懂他在說些什麼。have fun尋歡作樂
*The young people made merry at the picnic．那些年輕人在野餐時盡情歡樂。lay much emphasis on特別強調
*The report made much of the fact that there had not been enough cooperation among the department heads．該報告強調各部門負責人沒有盡力合作。
*He makes much of his upperclass background when you talk to him．當你同他談話時，他總是強調他上流社會的家庭背景。
*Don't make too much of Sally's harsh manner ；she's really quite gentle one you get to know her．別太計較薩利粗暴的態度，一旦你瞭解她，就會知道她實際上是一個相當溫和的人。be unimportant無關緊要
*It makes no difference which road you take；both lead to the city，and they are equally long．你走哪條路都無關緊要，二者都通往城裡，而且一樣長。1． treat as of no importance認為不重要
*He made nothing of the injury and went on working．他受了傷卻全不在意，繼續幹活。
*It's strange that he should make nothing of others' opinions．真奇怪，他對別人的意見居然毫不重視。
2． not understand不瞭解；不懂
*I can make nothing of what he says．我不懂他的話是什麼意思。go or run away逃走
*When the deer saw the hunter，it made off at once．當那頭鹿看見獵人時，拔腿就跑。
*The thieves ran out of the jeweller's and made off in a stolen car．竊賊們溜出珠寶行，坐上偷來的汽車逃走了。1．steal and hurry away with偷走
*The cashier made off with all the money in the safe．出納員偷走了保險箱裡所有的錢。
2．carry off攜走；拿走
*He made off with the first prize in the table tennis tournament．他在乒乓球聯賽中獲得第1名。
*Someone has made off with my pen．有人把我的鋼筆拿走了。make a reputation出名
*Shakespeare made his mark as a playwright．莎士比亞作為一個劇作家享有盛名。
*You've made your mark in the engineering world，you ought to be content．你已在工程學方面取得了成功，你該滿意了。
*Norman quickly made his mark and was the company's top salesman．諾曼很快做出了成績，成為公司第一流的推銷員。1．go forward with difficulty艱難地向前走
*As soon as he saw us， Henry made his way through the crowd to greet us personally．亨利一看見我們就從人群中擠過來，親自迎接我們。
*In the evening we made our way to the appointed meeting place． 到了晚上我們就向約定會面的地方趕去。
2． do many hard things to earn a living自力更生；自食其力
*He doesn't have the determination to make his way in the world．他沒有努力上進的決心。
*She was anxious to finish school and make her own way in the world．她渴望早點畢業好在社會上謀生。feel comfortable，as though one were in one's own home感到自在
*When people come to our house，we like them to make themselves at home．當有人來我們家時，我們願意他們像在自己家裡一樣感到自在。1． fill out填寫
*The teacher made out the report cards and gave them to the students to take home．老師填好成績單，交給學生帶回家。
*Will you please make out my bill？請把我的帳單開給我好嗎？
2．understand理解；瞭解
*I couldn't make out what he was saying．我不明白他在說什麼。
*I never could make Janet out． Why does she always annoy people who try to help her？我永遠也不可能理解珍妮，為什麼她總要使那些想幫她忙的人感到不愉快呢？
3． distinguish辨認
*I can't make out what that sign says； it's still too far away．我無法看清那個標記，它距離我太遠了。
4．try to prove企圖證明
*Charles and Bob had a fight， and Charles tried to make out that Bob started it．查爾斯和鮑勃打了一架，查爾斯竭力說是鮑勃先動的手。
*He made out that he had never been to the place before．他企圖證明他從未去過那個地方。
5．represent；represent as being聲稱；把…說成
*They make themselves out to be poorer than they really are．他們把自己說得比實際上要窮些。
*He made me out to be a hypocrite．他把我說成是偽君子。
6．progress進展
*He is making out very well in his new job．他那項新工作幹得很不錯。
*He seems a little bit irresponsible now，but I think he will make out all right．目前看來他有點缺乏責任感，但我相信他會變好的。
7．pretend假裝
*They made out they were weavers．他們假裝是織布工人。
*He made himself out to be interested in our planned trip．他假裝對我們計劃中的旅行感興趣。
8．complete（a total）湊足（總數）
*I cannot make out the required sum to settle this account．我湊不出這筆款子來還帳。
*Several other items were added to make out a round number． 加了幾個別的項目以湊足一個整數。1．produce from用…製成
*The cottage was made out of logs．那小屋是用圓木建成的。
2．change…to把…培養成；使…變成
*It was the school's responsibility to make good citizens out of the students．學校的職責是把學生培養成良好的公民。
*They made an illiterate out of my daughter．他們使我女兒變成了文盲。1． alter and make like new（particularly of clothes）翻改（衣服）
*Do you think you can make over this old coat？你看你能把這件舊上衣改一下嗎？
*The house has been made over into a school．這座房子已改建成一所學校。
2．transfer轉移
*Mr．Brown has made over his business to his son．布朗先生已經把公司移交給了他兒子。
*he has made over his property to a hospital．他把他的財產捐給了一家醫院。be on good terms（with）（與…）和好；（與…）講和
*The leaders of the two nations decided to make peace．兩國領導人決定議和。
*Has Philip made peace with Rosemary or are they still arguing？菲利浦已經同羅斯瑪麗握手言好了，還是他們仍在爭吵不休？make ready
『印刷』墊版
(開始印刷之前用上襯及下襯將印版和印刷機墊平)1． arrange space for為…騰出空地
*We can easily make room for you at this table．我們很容易就能在這張桌上為你騰出位置。
2．be replaced by被…所替代
*It's in the very nature of things that the old eventually makes room for the new．舊事物終將被新事物所代替，這是必然的。make sb． angrg激怒
*When someone called him a liar it made his blood boil．當有人說他是個扯謊的人時，他十分惱火。
*It made Mary's blood boil to see the children make fun of the crippled girl．瑪麗看到孩子們在取笑那位殘廢的女孩時，勃然大怒。1． be sth． you can understand or explain能理解；合理
*What he said just doesn't make sense．他講的那番話簡直不知所云。
*She doesn't talk much， but what she says makes sense．她不多講話，但言之有理。
2． seem right； sound reasonable or practical可行；合乎情理
*Does it make sense to let little children play with matches？讓孩子們玩火柴能行嗎？understand； interpret successfully 理解
*Even though the speaker had a strong accent，
*Henry could catch on to his story， but Tom couldn't make sense of it at all．儘管演講者地方口音很重，但是亨利能聽懂他的話，而湯姆卻一點兒也聽不懂。
*Can you make sense of what he said？你聽懂他說的話嗎？
*I can't make sense of either the Chinese or Korean language，and that's why I can't tell them apart．我既不懂漢語，也不懂朝鮮語，這就是我分不清這兩種語言的原因。substitute one thing for another用一物代替另一物
*If there's no cream for the coffee，we'll just have to make milk do．如果沒有奶油放在咖啡裡，放牛奶也可以。be sure or certain務必
*Father makes sure that all the lights are off before he goes to bed．父親在確認所有的燈都關了以後才上床。
*Let's make sure that it has been finished．讓我們搞清楚這工作是否確實已完成。
*We must make sure of the facts．我們必須把事實搞清楚。1．try to use to the best advantage 盡量利用
*With the government cutbacks， the hospital will just have to make the best of the limited resources at its disposal．當政府削減撥款時，這家醫院就只能充分利用那些有限的財力。
*You should make the best of this valuable opportunity．你應該充分利用這寶貴的機會。
2． accept cheerfully欣然接受
*He has bad luck，
*but he always makes the best of everything．他運氣不佳，但他總能坦然接受一切。
*Since we can't get any new equipment right now， let's make the best of what we have．既然現在搞不到新設備，我們就先將就著用現有的設備吧。1． make good； succeed成功
*Mr． Baker made the grade in the insurance business．貝克先生在保險業務上幹得很不錯。
2．meet a standard； qualify夠水準；合格
*After repeated trials the new calculators eventually made the grade．通過反覆試驗，那種新計算器終於達到了標準。
*He tried several times to enlist， but first he was too young，
*then too thin， to make the grade．他幾次報名參軍，但都不合標準，先是由於他年齡大小，而後又由於他個子太瘦。get as much as possible out of a situation充分利用
*George studied hard． He wanted to make the most of his chance to learn．喬治學習很努力，他想利用一切機會學習。
*The doctors have told him he's only got six months to live， so he's making the most of them．醫生已經告訴他，他只能活6個月時間了，所以他在充分利用這段時間。1．invent；fabricate編造
*Jane made up stories to amuse her little brother．簡編故事逗她的小弟弟。
*He's very good at making up songs．他很善於編歌。
2．constitute組成
*A car is made up of many different parts．汽車由許多零部件組成。
*Peasants make up over 80 percent of the Chinese population．農民占中國人口的百分之八十以上。
3．repay； compensate補償
*We have to drive fast to make up the hour we lost in Boston．我們的車得開快一點，好補回我們在波士頓丟掉的時間。
*By hard work they made up the loss of time．由於努力工作，他們彌補了失去的時間。
4．apply cosmetics化妝
*Tom watched his sister make up her face for her date．湯姆望著他姐姐化妝去赴約。
*She spent two hours making herself up before the party．她在參加聚會前用了兩個小時化妝。
5．become friends again after a quarrel復交；和解
*Why don't you make up with her and forget all about your quarrel？你為什麼不能同她和解並忘掉你們吵架的事呢？
*Has Ray made it up with Ros yet？雷跟羅斯還沒有握手言好嗎？
6．complete完成；湊成
*She has a lot of work to make up．她有許多事要做。
*We still need 50 yuan to make up the required sum．我們還需50元來湊足需要的款項。
7．arrange bedclothes鋪床；（臨時）搭床鋪
*Make up your bed before you sleep．睡前要鋪床。
*She made up a special bed for her sick mother．她為生病的母親搭了個特製的床。
8．prepare sth．， esp．medicine，by putting different things together配製
*Please call at the drugstore and have this prescription made up for me．請去藥店照這張方子給我配些藥來。
*He made up a bottle of cough medicine．他配製了一瓶咳嗽藥水。
9． add fuel to a fire， boiler， etc．加燃料使（火）不熄；生（火）
*If the stove isn't made up， it'll soon go out．不給火爐加點燃料的話，火很快就會滅。
*He made up a fire．他生了堆火。
10． wrap up；fasten up包紮；把…打成包
*She made up a big bundle of all her old clothing．她把她所有的舊衣服紮成一大包。
*The shop assistant made up the parcel expertly．那個店員把小包捆得乾淨利落。
11． make（cloth）into a garment 縫製
She would like to have this piece of cloth made up into a skirt．她想用這塊布做條裙子。
*This material will make up into two dresses．這塊衣料可做兩件女裝。compensate彌補
*Hard work can often make up for a lack of intelligence．勤奮工作往往可以彌補智力的不足。
*His strong personality makes up for his ugly appearance．他堅強的性格彌補了他醜陋的外表。
*Your kind behavior now more than makes up for your rudeness last week．你此刻的善良舉止大大地彌補了你上周的野蠻粗魯。decide；choose what to do； determine決心
*They made up their minds to sellthe house．他們下決心要把房子賣掉。
*Look， I've thought about it a lot，and now I've made up my mind－you can borrow my car！瞧，這件事我已想了許多，現在我主意已定，你可以借用我的車了。1．advance to；approach接近；向…前行
*It was easy to make up to him．他是容易接近的。
*A suspicious boat made up to us．一艘行跡可疑的船向我們駛來。
2．flatter奉承
*She started making up to him the day she learnt that he was a millionaire．從她開始得知他是個百萬富翁那天起，她就巴結他。
*She makes up to her boss all the time．她總是討好她的老闆。
3． repay補償
*How can we make it up to them for all the worry we've caused them？我們害得他們如此焦慮不安，要怎樣才能彌補呢？
*He lost some money， but his father made it up to him．他丟了些錢，可是他父親給他彌補了這筆損失。use；utilize利用；使用
*You must make good use of any opportunity to practise English．你必須好好利用任何機會練習英語。stand aside讓路
*When older men retire they make way for younger men to take their places．年長者退休時為年輕者讓路，讓他們接班。
*All traffic has to make way for a fire engine．所有車輛都得給消防車讓路。make-believe
