見Marcus Antonius1．lower the price of減價
*All our stock has been marked down thirty percent．我們的所有存貨都已減價百分之三十。
*I wonder why these dresses have been marked down．我不知道這些衣服為何降價。
2．note down with a mark作記號
*The teacher immediately marked down the students'suggestion in his notebook．老師立即將學生提出的建議記在筆記本上。
3．single out選出
*He has been marked down for assassination．他們事先定下來要暗殺他。
*He marked down that house for his headquarters．他選那所房子作他的指揮部。lay out in sections劃出界線
*The fiela will be marked off in accordance with the special track events which will take place tomorrow．場地將按照明天的特殊徑賽項目而劃分。
*This feature marks him off from other boys．這個特徵使他和別的孩子有所區別。1．put lines on to indicate limits劃線
*The tennis court has been freshly marked out．網球場新劃了線。
*The site of the new chemical fertilizer plant has been marked out．新的化肥廠的地界已經劃出來了。
2．chart the course of制訂
*They have marked out a general course of action．他們已經擬訂了一個行動計劃。
*The directions of urban development have been marked out．城市發展的規劃已制訂出來了。
3．select sb．for special treatment 選定
*Three of his paintings have been marked out for exhibition．他的3幅畫已被選出，準備送去展覽。
*He was marked out as the most promising young soldier in the whole army．他被認為是全軍最有前途的青年軍人。1．be idle；wait for等待
*The teacher marked time until all the children were ready for the test．老師一直等到所有孩子都作好了考試準備。
*Business is fairly slow；we're just marking time till the economy improves．現在生意相當蕭條，我們正等待經濟的好轉。
2．move the feet up and down as in marching，but not going forward原地踏步
*The captain ordered his men to mark time．上尉命令士兵原地踏步。Mark Twain
[`mɑrk`twɑn; ˋmɑ:kˋtwɑin]
<<名詞>>
馬克吐溫
(1835-1910; 美國作家; 本名 Samuel L. Clemens[`klmnz; 'klemnz])1．put up with a mark記分；在…上作記號
*The child used his new crayons to mark up the kitchen walls．小孩用新蠟筆在廚房的牆上畫。
*They marked up the score on the scoreboard．他們把得分記在記分牌上。
2．decide the price at which to sell sth．給…標價
*If we mark them up at that price，we'll never sell them．如果我們標那樣的價，那這些貨永遠也賣不出去。
*They have marked up all these items．他們把這些商品通通標了價。
3．raise the price漲價；加價Everything in the shop will have to be marked up if the tax is increased．如果稅收增加的話，商店裡所有的物品都得加價。
*They marked up the prices of those rare books．他們提高那些珍本書的定價。
4．add（an item） to a store account；give credit for記帳；賒欠
*I shaved a gentleman who asked me to mark it up．我替一位先生修了面，他要我記帳。
*A man bought an umbrella from us and asked us to mark it up．一個男人向我們買了一把傘，叫我們記帳。
5．increase the marks awarded to （a student，a class，etc．）增加（學生等的）分數
*If we mark up Jones on two papers he will just scrape a pass．要是我們給瓊斯的兩份卷子加分，他也只能勉強及格。Mark, Saint
馬可
(聖經馬可福音之作者)mark.down
