<<可數名詞>>
1 (美) (運動的) 競賽大會,大會( (英)meeting) 
an athletic ~ 
運動會
2 (英) (出去打獵前的獵人、獵犬等的) 會合,集合
3『幾何』交點,交線1．keep one's promise承諾（約言、契約）
*He has met his engagements．他已履行了他的契約。
2．make payment付款
*He has not enough money to meet his engagements．他沒有足夠的錢來償清他的債務。compromise；come to an understanding with sb． when opinions differ妥協；和解
*In an effort to end the strike，the owners agreed to meet the strikers halfway．為了努力結束這場罷工，老闆自己和罷工者和解了。
*The two sides finally met halfway －the workers gave up their pay claim but got the cut in working hours that they wanted．雙方最後都作出了讓步－工人們放棄增加工資的要求，但得到了他們想要的勞動時間的減少。
*John has definite ideas about things，but he's not unreasonable，he always tries to meet you halfway．約翰對事情有明確的意見，但他不是不講理的，他總是努力和你折衷一下。meet by accident遇到；接觸
*The family would have arrived on time，but they met up with a flat tire．要不是在路上壞了一隻車胎，他們一家人是會準時到的。
*It was some years before we met up with each other again．幾年之後我們才再度邂逅。1．meet，usu．by accident（偶然）遇見
*In the woods， he met with two strangers．在樹林裡他遇上了兩個陌生人。
*I met with an old friend at the meeting．我在會上碰到了一個老朋友。
2．meet together，usu．by plan （按計劃）約見
*The two scouts went to meet with the officers to talk about plans for the march．兩位偵察員前去會見軍官，討論行軍計劃。
*I met with him at the bus stop and together we went to dine at a restaurant．我和他在汽車站碰頭，然後一起去飯館吃飯。
3．experience經歷；遭受
*The farmer met with misfortune；storm．這位農場主遭受了不幸，他的莊稼被一場暴風雨毀了。
*On every battle field the enemy met with defeat．敵軍在各個戰場上都吃了敗仗。
4．agree with；be in accord with 符合（某種意見）；獲得（同意）
*The suggestion met with unanimous approval．該項建議獲得一致通過。
*The plan you submitted seems to meet with the committee's ideas on the subject．你提出的計劃似乎符合委員會對這個問題的主張。meet.ing
