1．confuse混亂；搞混
*The airline staff mixed my luggage up with yours．飛機航班服務員把我的行李和你的混淆了。
*People are always mixing me up with my twin brother．人們總是分不清我和我的孿生弟弟。
*We got mixed up in our directions，took the wrong road，and drove many miles out of our way．我們搞錯方向上錯了路，結果繞開正路開了許多英里。
*Even the twin's mother mixed them up．甚至這對雙胞胎的母親也會把他們搞混。
2．mix thoroughly；mingle together攪勻；拌和
*She mixed their medicine up in a glass．她在杯子裡調勻他們的藥。
*Dinner will be ready as soon as I finish mixing up this salad dressing．我把色拉調料一調好，咱們就吃飯。
3．involve使捲入；使牽連進
*How did you become mixed up in such affairs？你怎麼會牽涉到這些事情裡面去的？
*They advised him not to ger mixed up with such people．他們勸他不要和這種人搞在一起。mix-up
