4 <與其…> ?more dict.
亦作 mor.dict『處方』按處方指示
(=in the manner directed)very often常常；多半
*More often than not，I take a cold bath every evening in summer．夏天我常常晚上洗個冷水澡。
*During foggy weather，the trains are late more often than not．有霧時，火車常常誤點。
*He is a fairly good runner． He wins more often than not．他是一名相當好的賽跑運動員，常常跑贏。1．a little；somewhat有點
*He is more or less selfish．他多少有點自私。
*The road runs more or less parallel to the Bell Street．這條路基本上是和貝爾大街平行的。
*By September we knew more or less what our income would be for the whole year．到9月份，我們就大概知道了我們全年的收入是多少。
2．nearly大約
*It's a mile，more or less，from his home to school．從他家到學校大約有一英里遠。more sol.
亦作 mor.sol.『處方』依常法
(=in the usual manner)1．very（後接形容詞，表示被修飾的形容詞的強烈程度）非常；十分；不僅僅
*He was more than upset by the accident．他為此事故深感不安。
*They were more than glad to help us．他們非常樂意幫助我們。
*In doing experiments，you must be more than careful with the precision instruments．在做實驗時，你必須特別小心這些精密儀器。
*Such work requires more than indomitable will．這項工作不僅僅需要堅韌不拔的意志。
2．rather（後接副詞或分詞）簡直；十分；不止…
*The girl was more than slightly hurt．這女孩傷得可不輕。
*She behaved more than fairly to him．她對他十分公正。
*I was more than surprised；I was astonished．我不止是詫異，簡直是大吃一驚。
3．nearly（後接動詞）十分；綽綽有餘；大大地；幾乎
*He more than hesitated to promise that．他幾乎是拒絕答應那件事。
*It was a moonless night，but the brilliant stars more than made up for the want of moonshine．晚來無月，但繁星點點，皎潔明亮，足補月亮之缺而有餘。
4．not only（後接名詞，或名詞從句）不只是…；不僅僅…；非但…尤其…
*He is more than a friend to me．他對我不只是一個朋友。
*My trip to Beijing is more than sightseeing．我到北京的旅行不僅僅是觀光而已。
*The stars are something more than huge inert masses；they are machines in action，generating and emitting the radiation by which we see them．星星不只是某種巨大的惰性物質，它們是運動著的機器，產生和放出我們藉以看見它們的光。
5．over（後接數詞）…以上；不只
*We have studied English for more than ten years．我們學英語已經10多年了。very十分
*If you tell your father what you've done，he'll be more than a little angry．如果你把你所幹的事情告訴你父親，他會很生氣的。cannot簡直不；難以
*His insolence is more than I can stand．他的傲慢使我難以忍受。
*The beauty of the park is more than words can describe．這個公園的美不是語言所能描繪的。
*The traveller entertained his host with stories，some of which were really more than could be believed．這個旅行者講了一些故事給他的主人聽，其中一些簡直難以置信。More, Hannah
