(1) (經常) 在動 [在旅行] 的
(2)<事情>在進行[發展]中的; 活動[活潑]的 (active) 
The stock market is on the ~. 
股市旺盛 [交投熱絡]move a little挪動一點
*The girls were so startled that they did not move a muscle．女孩子們驚訝之極，在那兒一動也不動。
*The robber said he would shoot the bank worker if he moved a muscle．強盜說銀行職員若敢動一下，他就開槍。1．travel about到處旅行；走來走去；搬來搬去
*He is a great traveller and has moved about all over the world．他是個大旅行家，走遍了全世界。
*I can hear somebody moving about upstairs．我聽見樓上有人走動。
*Before liberation his family was moved around a good deal．解放前他的家老是搬來搬去。
2．be restless坐立不安
*The children kept moving about．孩子們總動個不停。1．transfer one's possessions to where he is going to live搬進；遷入
*Our new neighbours are moving in tomorrow．我們的新鄰居明天搬來。
*They decided to move the luggage in while there was time．他們決定趁還有時間把行李搬到屋子裡去。
2．take possession of a place佔據某地
*The enemy moved in last night．敵人昨晚佔領了那個地方。1．approach；enter or attack an area when trying to get control of it向…移近；向…進逼；為捕獲而逼進
*The army has begun to move in on the defenders．部隊開始圍殲守敵。
*The camera moved in on the hero for a closeup sequence．攝影機向男主角移近，準備拍一組特寫鏡頭。
2．take control of；take over控制；佔有
*He moved in on my girl friend and now we're not talking to each other．他搶走了我的女朋友，現在我們互不理睬對方。
*The gang has decided to move in on the slot machine business．那夥人決定控制自動售貨機的生意。1．depart（開始）離開
*The troops moved off at dawn．部隊在黎明時出發了。
*The train moved off．火車開動了。
2．be sold rapidly暢銷
*The first edition moved off within a week．第1版不到一星期就銷完了。
3．die死
*Whether from the fall or the fright，the Major moved off in a month．也不知道由於跌倒還是由於驚嚇，少校不到一個月就死了。1．proceed；advance前進；繼續前進；繼續進行
*Medical science has moved on a lot since I was a boy．從我孩提時起，醫學就一直發展得很快。
*We'll now move on to your next proposal．我們現在接著討論你的下一個建議。
2．change the discussion， conversation，etc．to sth．else改換（新的東西）
*I think we've talked enough about that subject；let's move on．我看那個題目我們已經談得夠多了，讓我們換換話題吧。
3．depart；start離開；出發
*It's time to be moving on．該走啦。1．move or cause to move from a house，etc．搬出
*The tenants of that old house are moving out to the new flats．那座老房子的住戶將搬到新公寓去。
*They're having to move out because they can't afford the rent．因為交不起房租他們只得準備搬家。
2．quit；leave離開
*The troops have moved out．軍隊已經開拔了。
*Tell the men to pack their kit；we're moving out．通知大家打好背包，我們要出發了。1．move farther in the direction indicated沿著指定的方向往前移動
*Move up in front，we haven't any room to sit．往前移點兒，我們沒地方可坐了。
*Would you mind moving up a bit to that I can sit down？能不能挪點地方讓我坐下來？
2．rise in rank；promote升職；提升
*He's moved very rapidly up the promotion ladder．他步步高陞。
*She's learnt so fast that we can now move her up to a more advanced class．她學得很快，我們可以把她調到高班去。
3．（an exchange rate，etc．） rise （兌換率等）升高
*The exchange rate of the pound moved up sharply．英鎊的兌換率急劇上升。
4．move into a battle area進入戰鬥區
*Two companies were moved up under cover of darkness to reinforce the front line．兩個連在夜幕的掩護下增援前線。move-in
