(2) 為<動物>清除 [打掃] 窩棚
(3) 清除 [打掃] (馬) 等1．spend time in an aimless or idle way閒蕩；混日子
*If I were you，I'd stop mucking about and look for a job．我要是你的話，就不再整天無所事事，而去找一份工作干。
*The square was full of people mucking around．廣場上儘是些閒逛的人。
2．handle sth．playfully or in a clumsy way瞎弄；亂弄
*He keeps mucking about with things he doesn't understand．他總是瞎弄他所不明白的東西。
*Someone has been mucking about with my bicycle．有人在瞎搞我的自行車。
3．irritate激怒
*He seems to enjoy mucking me about．他似乎以氣我取樂。
*He hates customers who muck him about．他恨那些使他生氣的顧客。
4．behave in a silly，playful or foolish way胡鬧
*I'll send the pair of you to see the headmaster if you don't stop mucking about．你們要是不停止胡鬧，我就把你們兩個都送去見校長。take part參加
*You don't want people to think that you are too proud to muck in，do you？你不想讓人認為你這人很高傲而不想加入，是嗎？
*They've mucked in with each other ever since childhood．他們倆自幼相處，關係一直很好。1．make dirty弄髒
*He fell down and came home with his clothes all mucked up．他摔了一跤，回家時衣服都弄髒了。
*Clean your shoes on the mat，or you'll muck up the floor．把鞋子在墊上擦乾淨，否則你會把地板弄髒的。
2．spoil；make a mess of搞糟
*The hairdresser has really mucked my hair up this time．He's cut it much too short．理髮師這次真把我頭髮弄壞了，他剪得太短了。
*They have mucked my plan up completely．他們把我的計劃全搞亂了。muck-up
