nail up
(1) 釘牢 <窗戶等> 
(2) 將<畫等>釘於 (牆等的高處)nail clipper
<<可數名詞>>1．make secure by using nails用釘子釘住
*If the corner of the carpet curls up，nail it down．要是地毯的角捲起了，就把它釘牢。
2．settle definitely；make sure確定；肯定
*Joe had a hard time selling his car，but he finally nailed the sale down when he got his friend Sam to give him＄300．喬的車很難脫手，在他朋友山姆出價300元時，他終於做成了交易。
*Our company has just managed to nail down a new，contract worth ￡60，000．我們公司剛設法確定了一份價值6萬英鎊的合同。
3．make sb．express his position，opinion，etc．要（某人）把話講明
*It's impossible to tell how much truth there is in his allegations as he refuses to be nailed down．要說出在他的斷言中有多少真實性是不可能的，因為他不肯講明白。
*The more we try to nail her down，the more she refuses even to talk about the issue．我們越是想讓她講明白，她越是拒絕談論這個問題。
4．insist on sb．keeping a promise，an undertaking，etc．堅持要（某人）遵守諾言等
*I'm not going to be nailed down to a particular date for completing the work．我不打算受在某個特定日期完成任務的約束。
5．make agree使同意；使應允
*See if you can nail him down to accepting our offer．看你能否使他同意接受我們的幫助。
*I nailed him down to coming at six．我讓他一定在6點鐘來。nail enamel
