←→ on)not regularly；occasionally時輟時續的
*It rained off and on all day．雨斷斷續續地下了一整天。
*He wrote to a girl in London off and on for several years．他與倫敦的一位姑娘斷斷續續地通了幾年信。
*We don't go to the theatre regularly，just off and on．我們不常去看戲，只是偶爾看看罷了。1． not in balance失去平衡
*Paul was speeding along on his bicycle，when an unexpected hole in the road caught him off balance．保爾飛快騎著自行車，沒料到路上的一個坑使他失去平衡，從車上摔下來。
2．not prepared； not ready無準備地；不防備地
*Our surprise attack caught the enemy off balance and threw them into confusion．我們的突然襲擊把敵人打了個措手不及，他們頓時亂作一團。
*The teacher's surprise test caught the class off balance，and nearly everyone got a poor mark．老師突然抽考，使全班毫無防備，幾乎每個同學成績都很差。not agreeing with fact； wrong與事實不符的；錯誤的
*So far as I know， what he said at the meeting is off base．據我所知，他會上所講的那番話與事實不符。
*Any man who said such a thing is certainly off base．說這事的人都是沒有根據的。off chance
<<名詞>>
