I wrote the letter on the ~ of its reaching him [that it might reach him]. 
我抱著也許他能收到信的渺茫希望寫信給他unwell； in low spirits氣色不好；身體有點不舒服；神情沮喪
*I'm off color today．今天我感到不舒服。
*「You're looking a bit off color yourself，Mr．Young．」「Oh， I feel very tired， doctor．」「楊先生，你看上去氣色有點不好。」「噢，醫生，我感覺很累。」off day
不當班之日; 休息日not at work不值班；下班
*He is off duty today．他今天不值班。
*It seems that all the taxis in New York are off duty whenever it rains．雨天，紐約所有的出租車似乎都休息了。in a careless attitude疏忽；不提防
*Tim's question caught Jones off guard．蒂姆提的問題令瓊斯毫無準備。
*He struck me while I was off my guard．他乘我不備打了我一下。off limits
<<形容詞>>
(美)禁止入內的,禁區的
(cf. on limits) 
The bar was (declared) ~ to athletes in training. 
正在集訓的選手不得進入該酒吧1．done完成
*The responsibility is off my hands．我已完成那項任務。
2．disposed of售出
*He had a lame horse which he wished to get off his hands．他有一匹瘸馬要賣。
3． no longer in sb．'s care or possession不再由（某人）照管或負責
*Now my two sons are off my hands：one of them is working in a factory and the other teaching in a school．現在我兩個兒子都自立了，一個在工廠做工，一個在學校教書。1．（of an airplane） not in the radio beam that marks the path to follow between airports（飛機）脫離航向
*The pilot received a warning that his plane was flying off the beam．飛行員接到了他的飛機偏離了航向的警告。
2．wrong； mistaken錯誤的
*I've come to realize what I said at the meeting was off the beam．我已經認識到我在會上所講的話是錯誤的。
*Jim was off the beam when he said that the girls didn't like him．傑姆說那些女孩都不喜歡他，他是錯了。1．not wellknown； not visited by many people不出名；人們不常去的
*I know a nice place for a picnic that's off the beaten track； hardly anyone goes there．我知道一個野餐的好地方，那兒很少有人去。
*This theatre is off the beaten track．這家劇院並不出名。
2．unusual不尋常
*The workers went off the beaten track and designed a newtype grinder．工人們打破常規，設計了一台新型磨床。without preparing ahead of time what one will say無準備地；即興地
*He is always at his best when he speaks off the cuff．他即席講話總是講得很出色。
*Considering that the speech was off the cuff，it was rather good．由於這發言是毫無準備的，所以它還算是不錯的。making progress進展
*Our plans for a party didn't get off the ground because no one could come．我們聚會的計劃未能實現，因為沒人前來參加。
*Make sure your project gets off the ground at the start．一定要使你們的工程一開始就進行得順利。out of trouble； out of an awkward situation擺脫窘境
*Seeing that he couldn't answer the question， I tried to get him off the hook by changing the subject．看到他那個問題答不上來，我就設法換個話題讓他擺脫窘境。
*As soon as he saw her smile he knew he was off the hook．他一看到她的笑臉，就明白他已沒麻煩了。remote偏遠的
*Our house is rather off the map． I think it would be best for me to meet you at the station．我們的房子在很偏遠的地方。我想最好是我到車站去接你。not related to the subject離題的；不切題的
*I understand what you are trying to say，but I think it's off the point．我知道你想講什麼，但是我認為你要講的與本題無關。confidentially；not for official publication不可記錄或引用的；不公開
*The president told the reporters that his remarks were strictly off the record．總統告訴新聞記者，他的談話嚴禁公開發表。without thinking hard； quickly不加思索地
*He didn't prepare his lecture beforhand， but only talked off the top of his head．他事先沒有準備，在講演時只是想到哪裡講到哪裡。
*Jim answered the teacher's question off the top of his head．吉姆回答老師的問題時不大動腦筋。1．following a wrong line of action 出軌
*The train ran off the track．火車出軌了。
*Our effort proved fruitless because we were off the track from the very beginning．我們一開始路子就邁得不對，所以一番功夫盡付東流。
2．away from the subject離題 The speaker was a long way off the track．演講者離題太遠。off year
