It was well on in theliving on a limited list of foods and drinks按規定進食
*You'd better give her something else but candy and chocolate because she is on a diet．你最好不要給她糖和巧克力而給些別的，因為她在節食。1．as interim payment預付
*Give the driver ten dollars， and tell him it is on account．給司機10美元，告訴他那是預支的。
2．in the creditor's book分期付款
*John paid ＄10 down and ＄5 on account each month for his bicycle．約翰購買自行車時先付了10美元，以後每月按5美元分期付款。as a result of； because of因為
*The picnic was held indoors on account of the rain．由於天下雨，野餐在室內進行。
*Flights were delayed two hours on account of the thick fog．由於大霧，班機推遲了兩小時。1．on all four legs ；on hands and knees匍匐而行
*Alice's father got down on all fours and gave the baby a ride．艾麗絲的父親趴下，讓她騎在背上。
*The baby crawled around the floor on all fours．那嬰孩在地板上到處亂爬。
2．in agreement with一致的
*Your argument is on all fours with mine．你的論點和我的一致。
*This simile is not on all fours with the thing that it is supposed to illustrate．這個比喻同那個要說明的事物不太貼切。in a wellordered way or condition； orderly有條不紊地；安定 When the discussion seemed to be getting out of hand the chairman got things back on an even keel．眼看爭論激烈得要難以收場時，會議主席設法使大家平靜下來。in most cases；usually通常
*On an average Don's mother has to ask him three times before he helps wash dishes．通常唐的母親叫他3遍他才幫助洗盤子。
*On the average the machine turns out one bottle every two seconds．這台機器平均每兩秒鐘生產1只瓶子。continuously連續不斷地
*She talked on and on about her son．她不停地談到她的兒子。with the understanding that the thing may be refused（商品）供試用的；包退包換的
*The corporation offered to send us samples on approval．公司提出要向我們提供一些試用樣品。
*Mr．Grey bought his camera on approval．格雷先生買的相機包退包換。1．as a representative代表
*John accepted the championship award on behalf of the team．約翰代表球隊領取冠軍獎。
2．for the good of為了… 的利益
*He rendered many valuable services on behalf of justice and freedom．他為正義和自由做了許多有意義的事情。
*They worked hard all their lives on behalf of the poor．他們畢生為窮人的利益而辛勞。on a ship or train在（船、火車）上
*A ship was leaving the harbor，and we saw the people on board waving．船緩緩地離開港口，我們看見船上的人在揮手。
*Jack wasn't on board the ship when it sailed．啟航時，傑克不在船上。for the purpose of doing business 有事；因公
*Are you here on business or for pleasrue？你來這兒是有事還是消遣呢？
*The secretary told the visitor that the manager was out on business．秘書告訴來訪者說經理出差去了。ready and available隨叫隨到的 The doctors in our clinic are on call day and night．無論白天黑夜，我們醫務室的醫生總是隨叫隨到。
*The money is payable on call．這筆錢可以隨時支付。if；provided that假如；在…條件下
*I will lend you the money on condition that you pay it back in one month．假如你在一個月內能還我錢，我就借給你。
*You can go there on condition that you don't come back late for dinner．你可以去那兒，條件是回來吃飯不能太晚。promising to pay at some future time賒欠
*I bought it on credit．這是我賒帳買的。
*Goods in our shop are not sold on credit but have to be paid for in cash．本店貨物現金交易，概不賒欠。1．on the open floor of a ship在甲板上
*Shall we go up on deck？我們到甲板上去好嗎？
2．ready to do sth．準備好
*Every employee had to be on deck at nine o'clock．每個僱員都必須在9點鐘到。
*Everyone was on deck for the dress rehearsal．大家都為綵排作好了準備。in bank存款
*The children saved their pennies and each month placed them on deposit．孩子們省些零錢每月存入銀行。
*He has almost ＄400 on deposit in his account．他帳戶上大約有400美元的存款。being shown publicly陳列著；在展覽
*Stop crying if you are not going to have yourself on display in shame！你不想丟人現眼的話就不要哭了！
*Samples of all major export commodities will be on display at the fair．主要出口商品的樣品將全部在交易會上展出。on dit
[әn`di; ʒnˋdi:]
(pl. on dits [n`d  (z) ; n'di: (z) ])
『法』
1 他們說; 據說
(=they say; it is said)
2 傳聞; 謠傳
I thought it was a mere on dit. 
我以為那只是謠傳doing one's job ；at work上班
*Don't talk with him． He's on duty now．不要跟他說話，他正在值班。
*Policemen are not allowed to smoke while on duty．警察上班時不許吸煙。1． in the world在世界上
*Honolulu boasts that it has the best weather on earth．檀香山以氣候最佳誇稱於世。
*They consider themselves the wisest men on earth．他們自認為是世上最聰明的人。
2．ever究竟
*Where on earth did you find that cap？你究竟在哪兒找到那頂帽子的？
*How on earth did you manage to do that？你究竟是怎樣設法做那件事的？rather rich生活優裕；富裕的
*After her success in several films，Mary found herself on easy street．成功地拍攝了幾部影片之後，瑪麗發現自己的生活頗為優裕。
*They have been living on easy street since the family business began to prosper．自從家庭生意開始興隆以來，他們就過著富裕的生活。excited or nervous；irritable興奮；緊張；煩躁不安
*The magician kept the children on edge all through his show．魔術師在他的整個表演中使孩子們興奮不已。
*Most people feel on edge before exams．考試前大多數人感到很緊張。
*Everyone was on edge to hear the verdict．每個人都迫切地要聽到裁決。1．continously連續不斷地
*The play is so successful that it has run for years on end．這齣戲非常成功，連演幾年不衰。
*There has been no rain for weeks on end．持續幾個星期沒下雨了。
2．upright豎著地
*We had to stand the table on end to get it through the door．要讓桌子從門裡進，我們只好把它側著豎起來。
*Please put the barrel on end．請把這只桶豎起來。
*on even terms（with）
*at the same level（with）（與…）不相上下
*They are on even terms．他們不相上下。without question or proof毫無疑問；無需證據
*He looked so honest that we accepted his story on faith．他看上去極為誠實，我們也就毫不懷疑地相信了他的話。stored in a file存檔
*This card should be kept on file for reference．這張卡片應該存檔以備參考。
*Our documents on file may throw some light on the matter．我們保存的文件也許會對這件事有所啟示。1．burning著火；失火
*We saw a house on fire when we passed the road．我們經過這條路時，看到一所房子失火了。
2．in a rage憤怒；急切
*They were on fire with zeal to defend their native land．他們熱血沸騰，決心捍衛自己的祖國。
*He was on fire to rejoin his family after an absence of five years．他急切地想和闊別5年的家人團聚。1． by walking步行
*Sally's bicycle broke and she had to return home on foot．薩莉的自行車壞了，她只好步行回家。
2． being planned在計劃中
*Plans have been set on foot by the 
*company for a party，because Miss Jackson is retiring．公司已經計劃舉辦一次聚會，以歡送傑克遜小姐退休。
*A plan's on foot to invite the Minister of Health to visit our hospital．邀請衛生部長來我們醫院訪問的準備工作正在進行。enjoying friendly relations（with）（與…）和睦相處
*The two neighbouring countries are on good terms．這兩個鄰國和睦相處。
*The two brothers had not been on good terms since their father died，and there was a dispute over the will．兄弟倆自從父親死後一直不睦，他們對遺囑有爭議。
*We are not on very good terms with the people next door．我們和鄰居關係不太好。watchful警惕；警戒
*The police warned people to be on guard for pickpockets during the Christmas rush．警察警告人們在聖誕購物高潮時謹防小偷。
*Be always on guard against complacency．要時時警惕自滿情緒。1．nearby；within reach附近；在手頭
*Do you happen to have any aspirin on hand？I seem to be getting a headache．你身邊有阿斯匹林嗎？我似乎頭痛。
*Alwaya have your dictionary on hand when you study．學習時要隨時將詞典放在手邊。
2．present出席；在場
*You'd better wait here so you'll be on hand when you're needed．你最好在這兒等著，以便需要你的時候你在場。
*Mr．Baker's secretary is always on hand when he appears in public．貝克先生出現在公眾面前時，他的秘書總是在場。
3．in stock；available現有（存貨）
*We have some new woollen goods on hand．我們現有一些新羊毛織品。
*The department store has a large stock of goods on hand．這家百貨商店現有大量存貨。1．sure to be won有獲勝（成功）的把握
*With their lead they had the game on ice．由於他們得分領先，他們有了贏得這場比賽的把握。
2．away for safekeeping or later use留待後用；擱置
*The plan for the new book is on ice at the moment． I've been busy with too many other things．寫新書的計劃暫停。我一直在忙於做太多其它的事。
*He will have to put his vacation plans on ice until his debts are paid．在還清債務之前，他只好擱置度假計劃。absent with permission請假；休假
*The soldier is absent from his regiment on leave．這位士兵休假，不在隊上。on limits
<<形容詞>>
(美)開放的,准許進入的
(cf. off limits)upon my word發誓；一定
*I promise on my honor not to betray the secret．我發誓不洩露機密。definitely not決不
*On no account should we go out in this big storm．我們決不能在這場大暴風雨中外出。
*Don't on any account leave your baby alone in the house．切不可將嬰兒獨自留在家裡。occasionally； now and then偶然地；有時
*I went swimming on occasion in summer．夏天我有時去游泳。
*I meet him on occasion at the club or in the theatre．我在俱樂部或戲院裡有時能遇到他。
*On occasion we feel like celebrating and have a party．我們有時喜歡來個聚會慶賀一番。behaving right行為規矩
*While his father was around，the boy was on his good behavior， but when the father left， the boy soon got into mischief．父親在場時，這孩子規規矩矩，但父親一走，他馬上就調皮起來。
*The naughty boy is on his best behavior today．今天這個調皮鬼表現很好。1．standing or walking站立或步行
*Before the teacher finished asking the question， George was on his feet，ready to answer it ．老師的問題還沒問完，喬治就已經站起來準備回答。
*How do you keep on your feet so long？你怎麼堅持站了這麼長時間？
2．recovering恢復（身體）
*Jack is back on his feet after a long illness．傑克病了好長時間，現在恢復健康了。easily易如反掌地
*When asked if he could lift the big stone，the boy said he could do it on his head．當有人問那男孩能否舉得起那塊大石頭時，他說這不費吹灰之力。1．being very proud and scornful 趾高氣揚；自高自大
*I don't like him：he's always on his high horse， thinking he can order 
*everyone else about．不喜歡他，他總是趾高氣揚的，以為什麼人都得聽他的。
*Martha was chairman of the picnic committee， and at the picnic she was on her high horse， telling everyone what to do．瑪莎是野餐會的主席，在野餐時她盛氣凌人地指揮每個人怎麼做。
2． in a bad temper發脾氣．The girl was on her high horse because she found her boyfriend insincere．姑娘發現她的男友不誠實，非常生氣。trusted信任
*The students were not supervised during the examination．They were on their honor not to cheat．學生考試時沒人監考。老師相信他們不會作弊。1． pleading； begging very hard求饒
*The children were on their knees for hours before their parents agreed to their camping plans．孩子們求了幾個小時家長才同意讓他們去野營。
