2．in written words以書面形式
*We must get the agreement down on paper．我們必須將此協議形成文字。
3． in theory理論上；從文字上看
*The idea sounds good on paper，but I'm not sure whether it will really work．這個主意從字面上看是很好的，但我不敢肯定它是否真正能行得通。
*The applicant looks good on paper．從書面材料看，這個申請人的情況很不錯。worried焦慮；坐立不安
*Jane was very late getting home from school， ane her mother was on pins and needles．簡放學很晚才回家，她媽媽焦急不安。
*The wounded soldier was on pins and needles， wanting to know the fate of his comrades．那位傷員因急於想知道戰友們的情況而焦慮不安。as a moral matter按道理；原則上
*He drinks a cup of hot milk every night on principle．他每晚照例喝一杯熱牛奶。
*I dislike going out for meals in restaurants on principle； why should you pay so much money for food that you could prepare yourself？我就是不喜歡去外面餐館吃飯，幹嗎要花那麼多錢去買那些自己能做的食物呢？intentionally故意地
*Jimmy hit his little brother in the eye， but he didn't do it on purpose．傑米打了他弟弟的眼睛，但他不是故意的。
*She did not forget her coat； she left it in the locker on purpose．她並未忘記要帶外衣，她是故意放在鎖櫃裡的。
