*Sally's boyfriend got on Father's bad side by keeping her out too late after the dance．薩莉的男朋友在舞會後沒帶她早點回家，她的父親因此不喜歡他。
*The boy's on his mother's bad side because he is lazy．媽媽不喜歡那男孩，因為他懶。feeling worried or upset心中有事；悶悶不樂
*Jane looks unhappy because she has the quarrel with Sue on her chest．簡顯得不高興，因為她和蘇吵了架，心裡有些煩悶。friendly with sb．； liked by sb．與人友善；被人喜歡
*Diligent pupils get on their teachers'good side．老師總是喜歡勤奮的學生。
*Successful workers stay on the good side of their bosses．成功的工人總給老闆留下一個好印象。resting on sb． as a responsibility 在某人手中；成為某人的負擔
*After everyone had bought a ticket to the dance， the club treasurer had over＄100 on his hands．每人買了舞會票以後，俱樂部財務主管手頭還有100多美元。
