*His job at the hospital did not pay much，so he found another on the side．他在醫院工作的報酬不多，所以他另外找了一份兼職。
*Besids fruit，he bought some candies on the side．除了水果，他還買了些糖。supporting支援；輔助
*He was on the side of the oppressed．他站在被壓迫者一邊。secretly偷偷地
*The boy smoked on the sly． 這男孩偷偷地抽煙。
*She recerived letters， on the sly，from young men．她暗地裡收到一些男青年的來信。1． just there正在那裡；在場
*The police were on the spot within a few minutes of hearing about the crime．警察在接到犯罪消息的幾分鐘內就趕到了現場。
2．without waiting立刻；當即
*The news of important events is often broadcast on the spot over television．重要事件的新聞總是通過電視立即廣播。
*Anyone breaking the rules will be asked to leave on the spot．任何人違反規則，立即勒令退場。
3． in trouble， difficulty or embarrassment在困難中；在危險中
*The question put me on the spot； I couldn't make an excuse or lie． 這個問題搞得我很尷尬，我既無法推托，又無法撒謊。
*Bob was on the spot because he was unable to pay the money he owed．鮑勃陷入了困境，因為他無力償還欠下的錢。
4．in danger of being murdered有被暗殺的危險
*After he talked to the police， the gangsters put him on the spot．他報告警察後，歹徒們就決定置他於死地。honest誠實的
*You need have no doubt of Jack's honesty．He is completely on the square．你不必懷疑傑克是否誠實，他絕對忠實可靠。
*You must act on the square when negotiating for contracts．在簽訂談判合同時，你必須處事公道。
*Can we trust them to act on the square？我們能夠相信他們處事公正嗎？1．in a sudden impulse一時高興或衝動
*He had not planned to take the trip； he just went on the spur of the moment．他事先沒有計劃這趟旅行，只是一時高興就走了。
*I've accepted the offer of a job abroad． I decided on the spur of the moment to go．我已接受了國外的工作並決定馬上就走。
*He acts on the spur of the moment．他憑一時衝動行事。
2． on the spot當場；即席
*He can invent any number of excuses on the spur of the moment．他能當場謅出許多托辭。
*Though quite unprepared，he was nevertheless able to sing a folk songon the spur of the moment．儘管毫無準備，他還是能即席演唱一首民歌。in or into the work of being an actor or actress當演員；登台演戲
*She has been on the stage for many years．她已經當了多年演員了。
*He went on the stage shortly after he left high school．他中學一畢業就當了演員。with faith or trust in依靠；憑借
*On the strength of the Committee's report，we have decided to carry out the reforms proposed．根據委員會的報告，我們決定實行所建議的各項改革。
*On the strength of Bill's promise to guide us，we decided to climb the mountain．由於比爾答應帶我們，我們才決定登山。under sb．'s influence or control唯命是從；在…支配下
*She was pretty and popular，with two or three boys on the string all the time．她漂亮又活躍，始終有兩三個男孩圍著她轉。trying to find尋找
*The lawyer is on the track of new proof in the case．律師正在這樁案子中尋找新的證據。1．in a state of continuous activity 忙個不停
*I could do with a rest for a while；I've been on the trot all the morning．我真想休息一會兒，整個上午我一直在忙個不停。
*The job kept me on the trot most of the week．我大半個星期都在忙著這件工作。
2．one after another接連地；一個接一個
*They have won three races on the trot．他們在賽跑中接連贏了3次。
*She didn't sleep well for four 
*nights on the trot．她已連續4個晚上沒睡好覺了。1．about to turn or change正在轉變中
*The tide will soon be on the turn and then we can make a start．形勢馬上會變，然後我們就可以開始干了。
2．（of milk）on the point of becoming sour（牛奶）正在變酸
*The milk is on the turn；you'd better not drink it．牛奶變味了，最好別喝它。1．honest誠實的
*You can take his word for it．He has always been on the upandup．你可以相信他的話，他一向老實可靠。
*This information is on the upandup．這消息完全可靠。
2．improving；succeeding走上坡路的；越來越好的
*From now on，everything is on the upandup．從現在起，一切事情都會好轉。
*The guy's on the upandup and I know it．這小伙子步步高陞，這我是知道的。near；close to快要；瀕於
*When I went into her room I found her on the verge of departure．當我走進她房間時，發現她正準備出發。
*He was on the verge of bankruptcy．他瀕臨破產。1．very angry非常生氣
*The police are on the warpath because the suspect is at large．警察當局極為惱火，因為嫌疑犯還逍遙法外。
2．fighting；making an attack攻擊；作戰
*The government is now on the warpath against pollution．政府現在正著手解決污染問題。alert；watchful留心；警戒
*The customs inspector was on the watch for diamond smugglers．海關檢查人員留心是否有寶石走私犯。while travelling or going在途中
*The train left and Bill was on the way to New York．火車離開了，比爾踏上了去紐約的路途。
*These machines are already on the way out．這些機器很快就要過時了。1．usually；in most cases通常
*On the whole，children begin walking when they are about one year old．一般來說，小孩1歲左右開始走路。
*On the whole，men are stronger than women．一般來說，男人比女人強壯。
2．generally speaking；in the most important things大體上；總的說來
*On the whole our stay there was quite enjoyable．總的說來，我們待在那裡是很開心的。
*On toe whole we're happy living here，but it is a long way away from my parent'home．總的說來，我們住在這兒很愉快，但就是離我父母家太遠了。1．always very busy忙碌不停
*Susan was on the wing doing things to get ready for her trip．蘇珊忙個不停，為旅行作準備。
*He was on the wing early．他很早就起來活動了。
2．travelling；going somewhere在旅行中
*We stayed in Britain for a week and then we were on the wing again．我們在英國逗留了一個星期，然後又上路了。punctually；promptly準時
*They forecast the weather accurately and on time．他們預報天氣既精確又準時。
*If the train is on time，I should reach home before dark．如果火車不誤點，我應該在天黑前到家。
*The train left on time．火車准點發車。1．on one's toes with the rest of the feet raised above the ground以趾尖（行走、站立）
*He left the room on tiptoe so as not to disturb his roommates．為了不打擾同室的人，他輕手輕腳地離開了房間。
*All the crowd stood on tiptoe to have one more look at her．所有的人都踮腳站著，希望能多看她一眼。
2．eager；excited渴望的；殷切期望的；激動的
*With the Spring Festival coming，the children were on tiptoe．春節快到了，孩子們殷切地盼望著。
*She was on tiptoe on the morning of her wedding．舉行婚禮的那天早晨，她非常激動。
*We were on tiptoe to learn the result of the election．我們迫切希望知道選舉結果。1．above在…之上
*A submarine is a ship that can run under water as well as on top of water．潛水艇可行水下，亦可行水上。
*Just put the dictionary on top of those books．把這本字典就放在那堆書上。
2．very close to靠近
*The elevator was so crowded that everybody was on top of each other．電梯非常擁擠，大家你擠我，我靠你。
*When I turned the corner，I was right on top of the post office．我一轉彎，郵局就在我眼前。
3．in control of管理；控制
*Although his new job was very complicated，John was on top of it within a few weeks．儘管約翰的新工作非常複雜，但他幾星期之內就掌握了。
*He acted like a man on top of his job．他裝得像對自己工作很內行一樣。
4．in addition to；along with此外；還有
*He promised to help us and on top of that he lent us many reference books．他答應幫助我們，並把許多參考書借給我們。
*He came late，and on top of that he didn't bring the papers．他遲到了，而且也沒有把文件帶來。
5．knowing all about通曉；十分瞭解
*He is always on top of the latest developments in his field of work．他總是通曉自己業務領域內的最新發展情況。
*Joan stays on top of the news by reading newspapers and magazines．瓊看報紙與雜誌，所以瞭解各種新聞。feeling pleased and happy；feeling successful非常高興；覺得成功
*The sea and the warm sun made them feel on top of the world．大海和溫暖的陽光使他們感到無比的快樂。
*Having won the first prize，he is on top of the world．他得了一等獎，欣喜若狂。1．on probation試驗；試用
*The new clerk was found on trial to be incompetent．這個新職員試用後被發現不合格。
*You may take it on trial；if you like it，then buy it．你可以把它拿去試用，要是你喜歡，就買下來。
2．in a court of law受審
