公開信open market
自由市場have an opening or outlet to；give access to通往；有出口和…相通
*All the rooms open onto a long hall．所有房間都和長廊相通。
*The French windows open onto the garden．落地長窗通往花園。1．become wider，esp．of a road，river，etc．變寬；打開
*At the foot of the mountain，the river suddenly opens out into a broad estuary．這條河流經山腳時突然向寬闊的港灣伸展開去。
2．develop發展；發育
*In the warmth of the room，the roses opened out in a few days．在室內溫暖的空氣中，玫瑰幾天內就開花了。
*Her good qualities opened out as she grew in years．她的優秀品質隨著年齡的增長而更趨完美。
3．become visible over a wider area 展現；顯示
*As we climbed higher，a wonder ful view opened out before us．當我們再爬高一些時，一派美好的風光展現在我們眼前。
*Just over the hill the countryside began to open out，and we had our first glimpse of the sea．就在山那邊我們看到了鄉村的景象，而且第一次看見了那片大海。
4．become less shy or nervous in public變得不那麼害羞；直言；暢談
*He's opened out a lot since he went to university．上大學後他健談多了。
*They opened out to each other．他們相互暢談。open plan
<<可數名詞>>
『建築』沒有明顯隔間的房間設計open port
