對新會員之加入無嚴格限制的工會Open University
<<名詞>>1．unwrap；undo（a parcel，etc．）打開；解開
*The surgeon opened up the man's stomach to get at the source of the trouble．外科醫生切開了這個人的胃來查清病源。
*Open up the boot of the car，and let me look inside．打開汽車的行李箱，讓我看看。
2．begin to fire開火；發動攻擊We held our ears as the machine guns opened up．機槍開火時我們堵住了耳朵。
*Our players opened up with forward passes．我方球員向前傳球，發動了攻勢。
3．make clear；reveal揭示
*After hours of grilling the prisoner opened up．幾小時的審訊後，犯人終於把秘密說了出來。
*Einstein's theories opened up a whole new area for study．愛因斯坦的理論揭示了一個全新的研究領域。
4．make sth．available for use or development開發；開闢
*The building of the railway opened up new land to the pioneers．鐵路的建成為先驅者們開闢了新的土地。
*We're being forced to move because the council wants to open up the whole area for redevelopment．我們只好搬家，因為委員會準備對這個地區再開發。
5．talk frankly and honestly直率、坦誠地說
*After a few drinks he opened up and told us all his problems．酒下肚後，他才開口說話，把他所有的問題都告訴了我們。
*After John trusted Mr．Jones，he opened up and told him how he felt．約翰信任瓊斯先生之後，便與他直言相談，告訴他自己的感受。
6．develop，arise or emerge，esp．of possibilities，prospects，opportunities變得有可能；出現（機會）Quite unexpectedly a chance has opened up for Henry to go and work abroad．出乎意料，亨利得到了去國外工作的機會。
7．open the door開門
*Mother，open up！I'm home．媽，開門！我回來了。
8．speed up加速
*He opened up and drove straight towards the stadium．他加快車速，直駛體育場。
*When they got out on the highway，the driver opened up and drove at 60 miles per hour．他們一上公路，司機便加快車速，車速竟達每小時60英里。open verdict
