說!extreme；complete；thorough完完全全；徹頭徹尾
*He was an opportunist out and out．他是個徹頭徹尾的機會主義者。
*It was out and out robbery to charge twice the usual price for eggs just because they were scarce．因為缺貨，雞蛋就索價兩倍之高，簡直是搶劫。unconscious；in a faint失去知覺；
*陷入昏迷
*A brick hit him in the head and he was out cold for half an hour．一塊磚砸到了他的頭，他昏迷了半小時。
*They tried to lift Julie when she fell down，but she was out cold．他們想把倒下的朱麗扶起來，但她已經昏迷了。taking part in參加
*He is out for the basketball team．他加入了籃球隊。free from sth．that worries sb．；finished擺脫困境的；完結的
*With so much work to do，I feel I'll never be out from under．我要做的事太多了，總感到沒完沒了的。
*George had so many debts that he couldn't get out from under．喬治債務纍纍，簡直無法還清。1．far from the right answer；wrong錯的；錯得離譜
*She tried to answer the teacher's question，but she was way out in left field．她想回答好老師的問題，可她答非所問。
*Philip tried to guess what the surprise was but he was way out in left field．菲利浦想猜出是什麼驚喜，但他猜錯了。
2．speaking or acting very queerly；crazy瘋的；舉止怪異的
*After her father was killed by a group of bandits，the girl was out in left field．自她父親被一群匪徒殺害後，那女孩就瘋了。alone；not included被忽視；孤單
*Everyone made plans for the National Day but he found himself out in the cold．每個人都計劃國慶節怎麼過，只有他一個人孤零零的。
*She was so talkative that she was often left out in the cold．她太饒舌了，常常搞得沒有人願搭理她。1．fast asleep酣睡；很快睡著的
*As soon as the lights were turned off the little boy was out like a light．燈一關，那小男孩就呼呼入睡了。
2．in a faint；unconscious昏迷；失去知覺
*When she heard that her son died in the war，she was out like a light．當聽到兒子在戰爭中死去的消息時，她昏了過去。out of
[`aJtˏv; ˋautɒv]
<<介係詞>>
1 從…裡面向外,向…外面
( 
←→ into) 
~ doors 
向門外
Two bears came ~ the forest. 
兩隻熊從森林裡出來
2 從<某數>當中
one ~ many 
多數中的一個
nine cases ~ ten 
十之八九
one chance ~ ten 
十次中有一次的機會
pay ten dollars and fifty cents ~ twenty dollars 
由二十元中付出十元五角
3 在…的範圍外; 在…達不到之處
~ sight 
看不見,在視線外
Tom was already ~ hearing. 
湯姆已經走到聽不到的地方
O~ sight, ~ mind. (
諺)眼不見,心不想; 去者日以疏; 離久情疏
4 a. 離開,脫離<…的狀態>; 沒有…,失去…
~ date 
過時的
~ danger 
脫險
~ breath 
氣喘地,喘不過氣來
~ humor 
不高興,生氣
~ one's mind [head] (
口語)瘋狂,失去理性
~ doubt 
無疑地,確實
~ the question 
根本不必討論; 不可能
~ work [a job] 
失業
b. <東西>缺乏,沒有…
We are ~ coffee. 
我們沒有咖啡了
We have run ~ tea. 
我們的茶葉用完了
5 用… (做材料) 
(
→ make v.t. A l c) 
What did you make it ~?. 
你用什麼材料製造它?
6 由於…,為了…
~ curiosity [kindness] 
由於好奇心 [出於好意] 
We acted ~ necessity. 
我們是因需要而做的
7 
a. 從…
drink ~ a cup 
用杯子喝
come ~ a poor family 
出身於貧窮家庭
a passage ~ Milton 
密爾頓著作中的一段
~ one's (own) head 
出於自己的思考,用自己的頭腦
b. <馬等>由…所生
8 a. 失去…
cheat a person ~ money 
騙取某人的金錢
He was swindled ~ his watch. 
他被騙走了手錶
b. 拿…,脫去…
I helped her ~ her clothes.

1．from從…中
*Choose one out of these paintings．從這些畫中選一幅。
*He picked the girl out of the crowd．他從人群中把這女孩挑了出來。
2．from the inside to the outside of自內而出
*She walked out of the room，all smiles．她笑容滿面地從屋子裡走了出來。
3．from（a source）從；自
*His dog and cat eat out of the same dish．他的狗和貓從同一盤子裡進食。
*The teacher gave a test to see what the students got out of the lesson．老師測驗學生從課上學到了多少。
4．in a place away from不在He is out of town this week．他這星期不在城裡。
*Our house is ten miles out of town．我們家離鎮上有十里路。
5．beyond sb．'s reach在…達不到的地方；非…所能及
*The target is out of reach of the gun．那靶子在槍的射程以外。
*The train is out of sight now．火車已看不見了。
6．without；not having沒有；缺乏
*He is out of work．他失業了。
*We are out of firewood；let's go and gather some．沒柴禾了，我們去撿一點吧。
7．not；no；used up沒有
*The car has run out of gas．車子沒有汽油了。
8．because of因；為了
*They helped us out of pity．他們出於同情幫助我們。
*She asked the question out of curiosity．她出於好奇提出了這個問題。
9．by the use of用…做材料
*She made a hat out of bits of old materials．她用零碎的舊料子做了一頂帽子。
*The house is built out of stone．房子是用石頭造的。
10．beyond超出；不容
*The machine is out of control．這台機器失控了。
11．from a particular condition or situation；not in脫離某狀況；脫離They finally talked him out of his fears．他們終於使他克服了恐懼心理。
*The sick man was out of danger at last．病人最後終於脫險。not working；not functioning不能工作；失（去）效（能）
*Three trains went out of action yesterday when the severe cold ruined the engines．昨天因天氣奇冷致使發動機凍壞，3趟列車停止運行。1．outside of the boundary lines in a game；not on or inside the playing field越軌；超出規定範圍
*He was out of bounds when he called his opponent names in the debate．他犯規了，在辯論中謾罵了對方。
2．outside of the place where sb．may go禁止入內
*The teacher told the students that the new gymnasium being built on the school grounds was out of bounds．老師告訴同學們正在興建中的體育館是禁止進去的。not breathing easily喘不過氣來The fat man was out of breath after climbing the stairs．那個胖子爬完樓梯就喘不過氣來。not in agreement with sb．'s character or personality；unsuitable for a part or character不符合（某人的一貫習性等）；（與所演的角色）不適合
*One of his traits is his honesty；few people have ever seen him out of character．他的特性之一是誠實，幾乎沒有人發現他不是這樣。
*The young actress said that it was out of character for her to play an old woman．那位青年女演員說她不適合扮演老太的角色。not out in the company of friends，other people，and groups；not active不和（朋友等）在一起；不活躍
*John was out of circulation with his friends when he was ill．約翰生病時沒有和朋友們來往。1．retired from active military service退役；不再執行任務
*When the war was over，many warships were placed out of commission．戰爭結束後，許多戰艦都退役了。
2．not in use or working不能使用；損壞
*Some of the bridges were out of commission．有一些橋樑不能使用
*She had to go to school on foot because her bike was out of commission．因為自行車壞了，她只得步行去學校。not healthy不健康；身體不好
*She is out of condition．她身體不好。unfashionable陳舊的；過時的
*The furniture is out of date．這家俱過時了。
*Your methods have long gone out of date；you will have to modernize or risk failure．你的這些方法早已陳舊，你應當用現代化的方法，否則有失敗的危險。
*out of favor（with）
*not well regarded（by sb．）失寵（於…）；不受（…的）歡迎
*Sir Walter is out of favor with the King．瓦特爵士已在國王面前失寵。
*He was out of favor in Paris and went to London．他在巴黎不受歡迎就到倫敦去了。1．promptly立即
*The situation needs to be dealt with out of hand．這個情況需要立即加以處理。
2．out of control失控
*The meeting was broken up by the chairman when the discussion got out of hand．當討論失控時，主席宣佈休會。
*The difficult class got out of hand when an inexperienced teacher was put in charge．一位缺乏經驗的老師任教時，這個差班就失控了。not pleasant；not in good mood不高興的；情緒不高的
*He was probably still out of humor over the affair of this morning．他大概還在為早上的事悶悶不樂。
*Why is she so out of humor today？她今天為什麼不高興？not proper不協調；不合適
*Loud talk is out of keeping in the library．高聲交談不符合圖書館的規定。
*These actions are out of keeping with his character．這些行為同他的性格不符。1．not balanced right不均衡；不平直
*The wheels of my bike were out of kilter after it hit the wall．我的自行車撞在牆上後，前後輪失去了均衡。
2．needing repair；not working right需要修理；失靈
*My watch is going too fast；it must be out of kilter．我的表走得太快，肯定出毛病了。1．not in a straight line；away from the true line不直的；不成一直線的
*The official ordered the soldier who was out of line to get properly lined up．軍官命令未對齊的士兵排好。
2．not obeying or agreeing with what is right or usual不守常規；越軌的；不適宜的
*I must say your behavior at the meeting was a bit out of line．老實說，你在會上的舉止有點不恰當。
*We told him not to tell the joke for it was out of line．我們告誡他別開那玩笑，因為太過火了。not in agreement with不同意；與…不一致
*The price of the bicycle was out of line with what Bill could afford．自行車太貴，比爾買不起。unfortunate；unlucky不幸
*Mr．Baker missed his train and was out of luck in getting to the ball game on time．貝克先生誤了火車，沒能及時趕去看球賽，他的運氣真不佳。
*When it comes to getting theatre tickets，we're usually out of luck．每次買戲票，我們的運氣總是不好。separate from sb．'s feelings，interests or desires忘懷；驅除
*When Tom moved to the city，he couldn't get the country out of his blood．湯姆搬進城以後，對農村仍無法忘懷。outside of one's natural surroundings在不適宜的環境裡；不得其所
*Wild animals are out of their element in cages．野生動物不習慣籠中生活。
*I'm out of my element when people start talking about music．人們一談起音樂，我就是外行了。acting in a crazy way行為瘋狂；特別地
*He must have been out of his mind to say something like that．他說出那樣的話來，一定是精神錯亂了。
*The patient was feverish and out of his head and had to be watched．病人發高燒，神志不清，需要守護。
*Sam was out of his senses with grief and rage．山姆由於悲痛和憤怒而失去理智。out of one's shyness or silence不羞怯沉默；開懷暢談
*John wouldn't come out of his shell and talk to the boys and girls at the party．約翰放不開羞怯沉默的性格，無法與聚會中的人交談。1．mad發瘋
*He is out of his wits．他瘋了。
*His provocative remark nearly drove me out of my wits．他的挑釁性的話簡直把我氣瘋了。
2．greatly upset不知所措
*He was frightened out of his wits．他被嚇得不知如何是好。
*The enemy，scared out of their wits，were routed，and all of us laughed for joy．敵人嚇得驚慌失措，潰不成軍，而我們卻高興得放聲大笑。1．in the wrong order次序錯了
*Peter wrote the words of the sentence out of order．彼得寫的句子詞序不對。
*The room was out of order．整個房間亂七八糟。
*I checked the papers that were to be printed and noticed that one or two were out of order．我檢查要印的文件，發現有一兩處次序混亂。
2．in poor condition壞了
*Our television set is out of order．我們的電視機壞了。
*Because the lift was out of order，we had to walk up the stairs．由於電梯壞了，我們只好走上樓去。
*It is no use phoning．The line is out of order．打電話沒有用，線路壞了。
3．against the rules；not suitable 違反規則；不宜
*Such attire is out of order for an occasion like this．這種場合穿這衣服不適宜。
*「You are out of order，」shouted the Chairman．「Kindly sit down．」 主席喊道：「你違反了規則，請坐下。」1．in the wrong place位置不對
*Your books are out of place．你的書放錯了位置。
2．improper不合適
*It was out of place for Russsell to laugh at the old lady．拉賽爾取笑這位老太是不對的。unable to do sth．well because of lack of practice久不練習；荒疏She is out of practice，so she can't sing as well as before．因久不練習，她歌唱得不如以前好了。
*He used to be good at cricket，but now be's out of practice．他過去擅長於打板球，可現在已荒疏了。no longer obtainable from the publisher because the printed copies have been sold out；no longer printed絕版；停印
*The book you want is out of print，but you may get a copy from a dealer in used books．你要的那本書已絕版，不過你或許可以從舊書商那裡買到一本。
*I'm sure the work you mention is out of print．我可以肯定你提到的那部著作已絕版了。undoubtedly無疑
*It is out of question that he will work his way through college．毫無疑問，他會完成大學學業的。rid of as a nuisance擺脫；甩開煩惱
*Harry got the children out of his hair so he could do some reading．哈里擺脫了孩子們的糾纏，可以讀點東西了。beyond sb．'s ability力所不及
*Reading twenty pages a day is simply out of his reach．一天讀20頁對他來說簡直不可能。
*Prices are rising so fast that the kind of house we want to buy keeps getting out of our reach．價格上漲太快，我們想買的房子老是買不起。1．making room for sb．or sth．給…讓開路
*When the fire engine came down the street，all the traffic got out of its way．當消防車沿街駛來時，所有的車輛都為它讓路。
2．not bothering不要打攪
*Tom wishes that his little brothers were out of his way，so that he can finish his paper．湯姆希望他的弟弟不要打攪他，這樣他就可以完成他的論文。not in the time for hunting，fishing，etc．不適時
*The boys were caught fishing out of season．孩子們在禁止釣魚時間釣魚被抓住了。
*Peaches are out of season now．現在桃子下市了。1．not looking the same；changed不成形；走樣
*The box was crushed out of shape．箱子已被壓得歪歪斜斜了。
*The front wheel of the bicycle was out of shape；and several spokes were broken．自行車前輪變形了，還斷了好幾根鋼條。
2．not able to perform well競技狀態不好
*He is out of shape，that's why he can't play as well as he used to．他競技狀態不佳，所以打得不如從前那麼好了。
3．not in good condition身體不佳；生病
*I get tired easily；I must be out of shape．我動不動就感到疲倦，一定是病了。
*She went to school as usual though she had been out of shape for several days．儘管身體不舒服已好幾天了，她還是照常上學。not to be seen看不見
*The plane was soon out of sight．飛機很快就看不見了。1．not in good condition身體不舒服
*I'm a little out of sorts today．我今天有點兒不舒服。
2．in an angry or unhappy mood 心情不好；發脾氣
*I really enjoy my work and if I miss it I am out of sorts．我確實很喜歡我的工作，假如我不做它，我就不痛快。
*Tom was out of sorts and would not say goodbye．湯姆心情不好，不想說再見。
*Bob was out of sorts because he didn't get a bicycle for his birthday．鮑勃因過生日時沒有得到一輛自行車而發脾氣。worried憂愁
*He was out of spirits as if he had something on his mind．他憂心忡忡，好像有什麼心事。1．not keeping pace with步調與…不一致
*George always marches out of step with the music．喬治的步子總是和音樂不合拍。
2．out of harmony不協調
*Just because you don't smoke，it doesn't mean you are out of step with other boys and girls your age．不抽煙，並不意味你就跟不上和你同齡的少男少女。
*His methods are out of step with the times．他的那些方法與時代不適應。sold out缺貨
*So many children have bought balloons that the store is now out of stock．買氣球的孩子太多，那家商店現已缺貨。
*We do sell this item，but it is out of stock at the moment．我們確實出售這種商品，但目前脫銷。unfashionable過時的
*My dress is out of style．我的衣服過時了。angry發脾氣
*He is out of temper．他發脾氣了。
*He is clearly out of temper and you should have a talk with him．他顯然是生氣了，你應該找他聊聊。without any warning；unexpectedly出其不意地；忽然
*You may want to spend time with a longlost friend who drops in out of the blue．如果有一位久已失去聯繫的朋友突然來訪，你會很想同他多呆一會兒。
*The cowboy thought he was alone but suddenly out of a clear sky there were Indians all around him．牛仔以為只有自己一人，誰知忽然間身旁出現了許多印第安人。without looking at sb．or sth．directly or openly從眼角處看；窺伺
*The cat looked at the mouse out of the corner of its eye．貓暗地裡注視著老鼠。
*As the little boy spoke to his mother，he looked out of the corner of his eye at his elder brother waving to him from outside the window．那個小男孩在跟他母親說話時，用眼梢瞟著站在窗外向他招手的哥哥。1．with a score better than zero in a game；eyen with an opponent 打破零分；扳回平手
*It took us a long time to get out of the hole in the card game．我們打牌打了很長時間才沒得零分。
*The team played very hard，but could not get out of the hole．該隊打得很賣力，但仍然不能打成平手。
2．out of debt不欠債
*The first year was bad，but after that he got out of the hole．第1年情況不太好，但第2年他就還清了債。
*Jack got out of the hole after he found a job in the bank．傑克在銀行找到工作後很快就還清了債務。outside or beyond common experience；unusual不同凡響；出眾：不尋常
*This is indeed out of the ordinary and unheard of．這真是聞所未聞的咄咄怪事。
*In our grand father 'time it was quite out of the ordinary for a woman to go to college．在我們祖父的時代，婦女上大學是很不尋常的。
*Has anything out of the ordinary happened since I've been away？我不在的時候，有沒有發生什麼不尋常的事？impossible不可能的
*To get there before seven is out of the question．7點以前趕到那兒是不可能的。
*What you say is out of the question．你說的那事是辦不到的。
*An expensive holiday abroad was out of the question on his salary．按他的工資水平，要花很多錢去國外度假是不可能的。having no chance to win 無取勝的希望
*It was clear from the start that Enoch was out of the running in the Congressional race．一開始就很明顯，伊諾先生在這次議會竟選中是沒有獲勝希望的。
*His sudden illness put him out of the running in the contest．他突然病倒了，使他在比賽中獲勝的希望成了泡影。not doing what others are doing；not active in business or social affairs不熟悉情況；不合潮流
*We're new to the district and out of the swim．我們是新來這個地區的，情況還不熟悉。
*The toy manufacturer who is out of the swim will lose money．玩具製造商如果趕不上潮流，就要虧本。1．not where people usually go；difficult．to reach偏僻的；人跡罕到的
*This village is very much out of the way．這個村子非常偏僻。
2．not what is usual or proper；strange不尋常的；奇特的
*I did not notice anything out of the way．我沒有注意到有什麼不尋常的事。
3．not in sb．'s way不妨礙人的
*Please put these odds and ends out of the way．請把這些零碎東西放到一邊去。
*I'll stand this box in the corner，it will be out of the way there．我來把這個箱子豎放在角落裡，這樣就不會礙手礙腳了。
4．not proper不恰當的；不禮貌的
*Have you heard him say anything out of the way？你聽他說過不恰當的話嗎？
*To leave before the guest of honour would be out of the way．先於主客離去是很不禮貌的。
5．not able to stop or bother sb．離開（不煩某人）
*Bill wished the visitors were out of the way so that he could have time to study．比爾希望來訪者離去，這樣他就有時間學習了。from nowhere沒有根據；無出處
*The teacher criticized Dick because his story was made out of thin air．老師批評了狄克，因為他編的故事毫無根據。wonderfully good；satisfying十全十美；極其優美
*The dress in the store window was out of this world．商店櫥窗裡的那件女服實在太好看了。
*Her cooking is really out of this world．她的烹調技術確實太出色了。losing touch沒有聯繫
*Fred has got out of touch with people in his hometown．弗雷德與他家鄉人失去了聯繫。1．out of proper musical pitch音調不准；走調
*The band sounded terrible because some instruments were out of tune．樂隊演奏得太差勁了，因為有些樂器走調了。
2．not in agreement；not going well together不協調；不一致
*His ideas were out of tune with the period in which he lived．他的思想同他所處的那個時代格格不入。
*His speech at the meeting was out of tune with the remarks of the other speakers．他在會上的講話同其他幾位發言者所說的精神不一致。1．out of the correct order不按順序的
*You'll get your chance．Just wait and don't speak out of turn．你會有機會的。等一等，不要搶先發言。
*The students were told not to enter the meeting room out of turn．學生們被要求依次進入會議室。
2．at an unsuitable time or in an unsuitable way不合時宜地；魯莽地
*Jack loses friends by speaking out of turn．傑克說話輕率，因此失去了朋友。
*I hope I haven't spoken out of turn；I didn't know it was supposed to be secret．我希望我沒說漏嘴，我不知道這是該保密的。1．needing repair；not working right需修理；出故障的
*My stomach is out of whack．我的胃不舒服。
*I can't do any typing today；my typewriter has got out of whack．我今天打不了字，我的打字機壞了。
2．not going together well；not in agreement不相稱；不一致
*The things he does are out of whack with what he says．他的言行不一致。
*The TV report on the weather is always out of whack with the weather we actually get．電視天氣預報總是和實際天氣有出入。1．in a dangerous position處境危險
*The company overextended itself and was soon out on a limb．該公司擴展得太快，很快便陷入困境。
*You'll be putting yourself out on a limb if you undertake to defend such an unpopular act．如果你同意為這樣一種不得人心的行為作辯護，就會使自己陷於困境。
2．with one's beliefs and opinions openly stated公開發表
*The President went out on a limb and supported a foreign aid bill that many people were against．總統公開表示自己的見解，對許多人反對的援外法案表示支持。out sister
(住在女修道院內但負責院外事務的) 外務修女inattentive；daydreaming心不在焉
*What't wrong with him？He seemes to be out to lunch today．他怎麼了？他今天似乎心不在焉。out-
