The whoin a helpless condition；trapped受牽制的；無能為力
*I have to obey him because he's got me over a barrel．我被他所控制，只好服從他。too old；above the legal age太老；超齡
*Father wanted to fight in World War Ⅱ，but he couldn't because he was over age．二戰時父親想參軍，但因年紀太大而未成功。
*She wasn't allowed to sit for the college entrance exams as she was over age．她因超齡而未獲准參加大學入學考試。besides此外
*We gave them two tons over and above the amount agreed to．除了商定的數字外，我們又多給了他們兩噸。
*The basic cost will be＄1，000．Over and above this there will be my expenses－say another＄300．基本的費用將是1000美元。除此之外，我還花費了300美元。
*Over and above injured，he was also insulted．他不僅受了傷，還遭受到了侮辱。repeatedly一遍遍地
*The doctor has warned him over and over again to stop smoking，but he doesn't take any advice．醫生多次告誡他戒煙，可他就是聽不進去。
*I have warned you over and over again not to do that．我已再三警告過你不要做那事。1．not understandable不可理解
*The lesson today was too hard；it went over my head．今天的課太難，我不懂。
*His writings go over my head．他寫的東西太深，我理解不了。
2．to a more important person in charge；to a higher official越級報告或請求
*The thing was settled over his head．這事沒與他商量就處理了。
