1 不發出腳步聲輕輕地走<along>
2 不發出腳步聲輕輕地走 [路] [along]1．fill out with extra material用額外的材料充填
*The tailor padded out the shoulders of the coat．裁縫給這上衣做墊肩。
2．make a sentence， story， etc．longer by adding unnecessary detail用不必要的材料拉長；添湊
*Her letter to her aunt was not long enough，so she padded it out with information about the weather．她給她姨媽的信不長，她又添加了些有關天氣的內容。
*My advice is not to pad out your story with irrelevant details．我的意見是別用不相干的細節來拉長你的故事。
*paddle one's own canoe work without help； earn one's own living獨立自主；依靠自己
*After his father died，he had to paddle his own canoe．他父親死後，他只好自己謀生。
*Don't worry about your son． He's old enough to paddle his own canoe．不要為你兒子擔心，他已到了足以自力的年齡了。Pa.dang
