他看電視度過那個晚上
5 a. (用手) 遞<東西>; 傳遞 < (餐桌上的) 食物等> <on,around,round,along> 
Will you ~ the pepper?. 
請你把胡椒粉遞給我好嗎?
The photograph was ~ed round [around] for every one to see. 
那張相片被1．go by度過；過去
*We had so much fun that the weekend passed away before we realized it．我們玩得非常開心，週末不知不覺就過去了。
*He passed the evening away playing caras．他打了一晚的牌。
2．end；disappear結束；消失
*When automobiles became popular，汽車普及後，人們就不再用馬了。
*He felt dizzy after the accident，but the doctor assured him the dizziness would soon pass away．事故以後他感到頭暈，可醫生告訴他說這種現象很快就會消失的。
3．die 逝世
*I'm sorry to hear that your grandmother has passed away．聽說你奶奶不在了，我很難過。
*Mary passed away in her sleep last night．瑪麗是在昨晚睡覺時去世的。1． go past走過
*He passed by without greeting me．他經過我面前時沒打招呼。
*A bus passed by just a moment aso．一輛公共汽車剛開過去。
2．（time）elapse ：（chance or opportunity）slip by（時間）過去；（機會）錯過
*The patient grew steadily better as the days passed by．一天天過去了，病人逐漸好轉起來。
3．overlook； ignore忽略
*We'll pass that matter by for the moment．我們暫時不去考慮那件事。
*In making the selection we passed this short piece by quite inadvertently．在挑選時我們完全由於疏忽而漏過了這篇短文。pass degree
<<可數名詞>>
(英國大學中的) 普通學士學位hand or transfer sth．（from one generation to another）把…往下傳遞
*The craft of candlemaking has been passed down for mang generations．蠟燭製作的工藝流傳了許多代人。be taken for被當作
*Do you think he will pass for a cook wearing that hat？你以為他戴上那頂帽子就會被當作廚師了嗎？
*He would never pass for an Englishman；his pronunciation gives him away．人們決不會把他當成英國人，他的發音就聽得出來。1． go into進入
*He passed into the college by the narrowest possible margin．他十分勉強地考進了這個學院。
*Patients under hypnosis pass into a trancelike state．被催眠的病人都進入昏睡狀態。
2．become gradually 逐漸變成
*When water boils it passes into steam．水沸騰後變成蒸汽。
*His words may pass into a proverb．他的話可能會流傳為諺語。
*On his death， the farm passed into the hands of the state．他死後，農場歸國家所有。
3．record into載入
*The general's brilliant military achievements have passed into history．將軍的輝煌軍事成就已成了歷史。pass a test or check up； be good enough通過考核；及格；符合要求
*Such excuses will not pass muster with him．這種借口在他面前是通不過的。
*After a period of practice，he was able to pass muster as a qualified lawyer．他實踐了一段時間以後，便成了一名合格的律師。1． pretend假裝
*He passed himself off as a doctor until someone checked his record．在人們查閱他的檔案之前，他一直偽裝成醫生。
*They resorted to the trick of passing off fisheyes as pearls．他們使用了魚目混珠的伎倆。
2． disappear 消失
*Mrs．White's headache had passed off by that night．懷特太太到了夜裡頭痛便消失了。
*A few minutes after we started，the fog began to pass off．我們動身後幾分鐘，霧就開始散去。
3．reach an end；last through to completion；take place完成；舉行
*The party passed off well．聚會開得很成功。The organisers were pleased that the demonstration passed off without any police arrests．組織者們很高興警察沒有在這次遊行中抓人。
4．ignore；treat as unimportant忽視；把…看作無關緊要
*She hated his familiarity，but passed it off as a joke．她討厭他那種親暱的態度，但一笑置之。
*His rude remark was passed off by the host．主人並沒有把他的粗魯的話放在心上。1．hand…on傳授；傳遞
*He was a simple man， content to pass on his learning to new generations．他是一位純樸的人，以傳授學問給後輩為滿足。
*Please read this notice and pass it on to others．通知看後請傳給其他人。
2．die死
*He passed on quietly at his home last night．昨天他在寓所安詳地死去。
3．move on； go on繼續下去；前進
*I have said enough o this subject，now let me pass on．關於這個問題，我已經談了不少，現在我接著談下面的問題。
*Time passed on like an arrow．光陰似箭。
4．give an opinion about；judge提議；審核
*The jury will pass on the case next week．陪審團將在下星期對這個案件作出裁決。
*Will you pass on the authenticity of this painting？請你鑒定一下這幅畫是不是真的？1．lose consciousness；faint昏迷
*The atmosphere in the crowded hall became so stifling that two of the women passed out．擁擠不堪的大廳裡悶得令人窒息，兩個婦女暈了過去。
*She passed out while we were waiting for the doctor．我們正在等大夫時，她暈過去了。
*She went back to work while she was still sick，and finally she just passed out．她帶病重返工作，最後暈了過去。
2．distribute分發
*The salesman passed out cigarettes to everyone in the restaurant．推銷員給飯店裡所有的人發了香煙。
*The exhibitors at the trade fair pass out free samples to stimulate interest．參加交易會展出的廠商免費贈送樣品以引起人們的興趣。
3．die死
*Mr．White passed out last，night．懷特先生昨晚去世。
4．graduate畢業（尤指軍事院校）
*Just over fifty students will be passing out at the end of the semester．有50多名學生在本學期末將學成畢業。1．cross橫過
*We must take care in passing over the road．我們過馬路時必須小心。
2．forgive寬恕
*I cannot pass over his fault．我不能寬恕他的過失。
*I'll pass it over this time； but don't do it again．這回我饒恕你，但下次不可這樣。
3．overlook；pay no attention to 對…置之不理
*I cannot pass the matter over．我不能對此事置之不理。
*You can't pass over these painful sources of conflict and hope they'll naturally disappear．你不能迴避這些令人痛苦的衝突根源而希望它們會自然消失。
*I wonder what made the reviewer pass over this aspect of the book in silence．我不知道書評作者為什麼隻字不提該書的這一方面。
4．review or summarise sth．briefly回顧；瀏覽
*He quickly passed over the decisions which had been made at the last meeting．他很快把上次會議作出的決定回顧了一下。
*I have read the first two chapters and passed over the rest of the book．書的第1、2章我已閱讀過了，其餘部分我只粗看了一遍。
5．not promote or choose sb． who feels he should be promoted不予考慮（提升、任命）
*Did you hear that they've passed over poor old Henry for a newcomer？你聽說了嗎，他們沒考慮提升可憐的老亨利，而提升了一個新來的？
*He was passed over by the Army Promotion Board．他未被陸軍晉級委員會考慮提升。make sb． decide sth．or accept a responsibility or give orders instead of doing it oneself推諉；推卸責任
*The favorite game in that office is passing the buck． Everybody refers you to somebody else．那個辦公室的拿手好戲是推諉責任，大家都叫你去問別人。
*Although it was his fault，he tried to pass the buck on to someone else．雖然那是他的過錯，可他卻竭力推卸責任，怪罪別人。say hello to sb．寒暄；打招呼
*She is so haughty that she will scarcely condescend to pass the time of day with people when she meets them．她非常傲慢，每次碰到人幾乎都不願和他們打招呼。
*They met at the corner and paused to pass the time of day．他們在拐角處相遇，停下來寒暄了幾句。1．experience 經歷；經過
*The country is passing through an economic crisis．這個國家正在經歷一場經濟危機。
*This soldier passed through many dangers．這個士兵經歷了許多危險。
2．travel through經過
*I passed through a picturesque village on my way here．在來這裡的路上，我經過一個風景如畫的鄉村。
*He passed through the doorway and entered the room．他穿過門口進入室內。
3．complete a course of training at 在…學完訓練課程
*He passed through a university course in Beijing．他在北京修完了大學的課程。
*After passing through college，he was assgned to work in a big factory．大學畢業後，他被分配到一家大工廠工作。1．let go放棄
*John was offered a good job in California，but he passed it up because he didn't want to move．約翰在加州得到一份好工作，可他放棄了，因為他不想搬家。
*He passed up the chance of going to New York for a year．他放棄了去紐約一年的機會。
2．hand to sb．above oneself 把…向上遞
*Pass up the paint pot and brush，and I'll put another coat on the ceiling．把油漆桶和刷子遞給我，我要把天花板再上一層漆。
3．decline；reject謝絕；拒絕
*Mary passed up the dessert because she was on a diet．瑪麗沒吃甜食，因為她在節食。pass-fail
