<<形容詞>>
1 收費的call on 訪問
*I paid a visit to Mr．and Mrs．Smith yesterday afternoon．昨天下午我去拜訪了史密斯夫婦。pay cash；pay at once當場付清；銀貨兩訖
*It's best to pay as you go；then you will not have to worry about paying debts later．最好能當場付清，這樣就不必擔心日後負債了。place importance on注意
*Please pay attention to the use of this word．請注意這個詞的用法。
*Economists are paying close attention to the latest developments in the Middle East．經濟學家們正密切注視著中東的最新發展。
*Pay attention to uniting and working with those who differ with you．注意團結那些和自己意見不同的人一道工作。1．return punishment報復
*He paid me back by not coming．他採取不來的方式向我報復。
*We'll pay them back for their insults one day．總有一天，我們將對他們的惡意中傷進行報復。
2．return（money）還錢；還債
*I'm certain that he will pay back every cent he owes you．我敢肯定他會分文不差地把欠款還給你。pay dirt
<<不可數名詞>>
(美)
1 值得開採 [有利可圖] 的礦砂 [礦石] ,有希望的礦脈
2 (口語)有利可圖的東西; 意外之財; 撿到便宜的好東西
strike [hit] ~ 
有利可圖 [有價值] 的發現; 找到值得開採的礦脈; (投資生意等的) 押中1．pay in cash；pay on the spot付現款；當場支付
*She pdid the money down and took the goods．她當場付了錢，並取走了貨物。
2．pay（part of the purchase price）at the time of purchase as a deposit 先支付（部分貨款）
*How much did you have to pay down on the car？你買這部汽車得先付多少貨款？
*You pay down only ten dollars and then you pay five dollars a month for eight months．你只需先付10美元，然後分8個月每月付5美元。pay envelope
<<可數名詞>>
(美)薪水 [工資] 袋( (英)pay packet)1． give money for付錢
*I have paid for these pens．我已付過這些鋼筆的錢了。
*You pay for it at the time you order it．你訂購時就得付款。
2．have trouble because of因…而付出代價
*When Bob could not get a good job，he realized he had to pay for all the years of fooling around instead of working hard in school．當鮑勃找不到理想的工作時，他意識到了這些年來他游手好閒，在學校不用心讀書，因而得付出代價。
*If you don't work now， you'll pay for it later when you fail your exams．你現在不好好學，到考試不及格時就得為此而付出代價。pay list
<<名詞>>
= payroll1．pay the wages of付工資
*The men were paid off just before the holiday．剛好放假前，這些人領到了工資。
*They're usually paid off at weekends．他們一般在週末領工資。
2．discharge a debt completely償清（債務）
*It took them three years to pay off their debts．他們付了3年才付清了債務。
*You must pay off your old loan before you can obtain a new one．你必須還清舊債才能再借款。
3．be rewarding有報償
*John studied hard before the examination，and it paid off．約翰考試前學習很刻苦，因而得到了回報。
*It has been rather costly to install the machinery， but it should pay off in the long run．安裝機械的代價很高，但從長遠看是划算的。
4．pay and discharge from a job發薪遣散
*The manager paid off the redundant employees．經理將冗員的工資付清後把他們解雇了。
*The whole ship's crew were paid off at the end of the voyage．遠航結束時全船員工拿到工資後就被遣散了。
5．get revenge on報復；報仇
*You'll be paid off for negligence．你將因失職而受到處罰。
*Joel wanted to pdy William off for backbiting him．喬爾因威廉在背後說他壞話而要對他進行報復。
6． give money to sb． to stop him from threatening給（某人）錢使其不做危害自己的事；賄賂
*He agreed to pay the gang off if they promised not to burn down his shop．如果匪徒們答應不燒燬他的商店，他同意給他們錢。
*The inspector won't be paid off to let that go through．檢查員是不會受賄而讓那件事通過的。1．pay one's daily expenses without going into debt 付清日常消費；不負債
*I paid my way through college by acting as a guide．我靠當導遊自己負擔上大學期間的全部費用。
*He earns barely enough money to pay his way．他賺錢僅足餬口。
2．meet one's obligations盡自己的責任
*He is useful and goodnatured；he is a man who pays his way．他很能幹，個性又好，是一個盡職的人。
3．be profitable；be valuable to an employer有盈利；值得僱傭
*We had to offer our new manager a high salary， but he was a capable man and paid his way．我們只得給新經理高薪，不過他很能幹，請他值得。
*It will take time for the restaurant to begin paying its way．這家餐館還要經營一段時間才能盈利。1． give money付出錢
*You can either draw the money in monthly installments until it is exhausted，or you can be paid out here and now．你可以把錢分月提取，直到取完為止，也可以當場一次提完。
*He must have paid＄ 50 out on repairing that house this month．他這個月一定已經付了50美元來修理這所房子。
2．take revenge on向…報復
*Wrongdoers are usually paid out in the end．幹壞事的人通常到最後會受到懲罰。
*I've paid him out for the trick he played on me．他捉弄了我，我已進行了報復。
3．cause a rope， cable，etc． to run throngh one's hands放鬆；放出（繩子）
*The kite climbed steadily higher until there was no more string to pay out．風箏平穩地越飛越高，直到手上再也放不出線來。
*The fish which was hooked darted away so rapidly that we were obliged to pay out the line fast．我們釣住的那條魚逃得很急，我們只好加快速度放長釣線。pay packet
