peg down
(1) 把 <帳篷等> 用木樁固定在地面等
~ down a tent ( 
釘木樁) 掛帳篷
(2) 約束<某人>[to]
~ down a person to a specific job 
把某人羈絆於特定的工作
(3) 壓低<物價等>
(4) 看清…; 判斷…<為…>,斷定 <as> 
We haven't yet pegged down what it is that he wants. 
我們尚未看出他要的是什麼
peg out
(1) 以木樁標出 <採礦權土地、房屋、庭園等> 的界限
(2)(英口語)死亡; <機器等>故障work hard and steadily at sth．堅持不懈地工作
*He found maths difficult but he pegged away at it every evening and passed the exam．他覺得數學很難，但他每天晚上都用功，最後通過了考試。
*To write a novel， one must keep pegging away at it consistently．要寫小說，必須不斷地辛勤勞動。1．fasten down with pegs用木樁固定
*They pegged down their tent，ready for the night．他們用木樁把帳篷固定，準備過夜。
2．make sb． keep to a certain line of action；restrict sb． to the rules 約束（某人）的行動
*It's proving very difficult to peg him down to a definite date for completion．硬要他定期完成任務，顯然是很困難的。
*When it comes to getting a clear promise，he's very hard to peg down．想叫他明確答應下來，那實在很難。peg leg
<<可數名詞>>
(口語)
1 義肢
2 裝有義肢的人1．mark out the boundaries of with pegs fixed in the ground用木樁在地上標出
*The surveyor pegged out the plot of land．測量員用木樁標出這塊地。
2． faint or collapse from exhaustion精疲力盡；暈倒
*He'll never give up work；he'll go on until he pegs out．他決不中途放下工作，定要干到精疲力盡為止。
3．die死
*At this height， a climber can peg out from lack of oxygen．在這樣的高度，爬山者會因缺氧而死去。peg-leg.ged
