pick
<<名詞>>
1 緯紗
2 投梭
<<及物動詞>>
(picked,picking,pciks)
1 投 (梭) 
2 『古』投; 擲
as high as I could ~ m lance. (Shakespear) 
有如我所能投矛之高select with much care挑三揀四
*Some people pick and choose to get something perfect，and some just because they can't make up their minds．有些人挑剔是想得到完美的東西，而有的人只是因為拿不定主意。
*You haven't time to pick and choose from among so many pictures．這麼多的圖片，你是沒有時間從中細選的。1．tear into pieces撕成碎片；拆散
*As this skirt fits badly，I'll pick it apart and remake it．這條裙子不合身，我要把它拆了重做。
2．criticise harshly；find fault with 猛烈批評；找岔子
*He is always picking apart every girl he meets．Naturally ever yone has some faults．他每遇到一個姑娘總愛挑剔，其實每個人都會有缺點的。
*After the dance， the girls picked Mary apart．舞會後，女孩們都責備瑪麗。1．eat without appetite挑食
*Stop picking at your food， Janet！
*Eat it all up or you won't have any pudding！珍妮，不要挑食！全部吃下去，否則就不給你吃布丁了！
*She had no appetite and only picked at food．她食慾不振，只吃了一點點食物。
2．find fault with對…吹毛求疵
*They showed their displeasure by continually picking at her．他們不斷挑她的毛病以示他們的不滿。
*She'd been picked at so often by parents and teachers that she didn't know how to behave．家長和老師經常對她吹毛求疵，她簡直不知怎麼辦才好。1．take off； remove with the fingers脫下
*The insecticide might harm the flowers Let's pick off the insects by hand．殺蟲劑可能會傷害花朵。我們還是用手把蟲捉下來吧。
*Don't pick off any of these flowers．這些花一朵也不要摘。
2．shoot or bring down singly or selectively逐個地或有選擇地射中或打下
*They picked off the officers first，so as to throw the enemy troops into confusion．他們首先把軍官一個個地擊斃，使敵軍陷入混亂。1．annoy使煩惱
*The children picked their father on until he agreed to have a ride．孩子們一直纏著父親，直到他同意開車出去兜風。
*Little Tom complained that his mother was always picking on him．小湯姆抱怨說，媽媽老是挑他毛病。
2． choose選擇
*He visited a lot of universities，and finally picked on Stanford．他去了許多大學，最後選擇了斯坦福大學。
*Why do they always pick on her to do the difficult tasks？他們為什麼老是找她去幹困難的工作？advance with care謹慎前進
*After nightfall we drove slowly along，picking our way until we found the right building．天黑後，我們駕車慢慢地往前開，直到發現了我們要找的大樓。
*The driver picked his way across the rough and rocky hillside．司機小心地越過崎嶇的山坡。1．choose挑選
*It took Mary a long time to pick out a new dress at the store．瑪麗在商店裡花了好長時間才挑中一件新衣服。
*You may pick out any two books listed here．你可以在這圖書目錄中任選2本。
2． tell from others區分
*We could pick out different places in the city from the airplane．從飛機上我們可以辨認出這座城市裡的不同地方。
*Although he had not seen his sister for twenty years，he picked her out as soon as she got off the plane．儘管他和妹妹有20年沒見了，可她一下飛機他就認出了她。
*He has such a distinctive appearance that I could pick him out anywhere．他的樣子非常特別，不論在哪裡我都可以認出他來。
3．tell the meaning領會；弄明白
*In spite of the difficulty of the passage，we succeeded in picking out its sense by our concerted efforts．這段文字雖然難懂，但我們通過共同努力還是弄懂了它的含義。
4．play a tune by ear on a musical instrument憑聽覺記憶在樂器上奏出曲調
*As soon as she'd sung the first verse， he picked out the tune on the piano．她一唱完第一部分，他就在鋼琴上把它彈奏了出來。
5．relieve（the ground color）with another color（用不同的顏色）襯托（底色）
*The ancient cloister was a structure of red brick picked out with white stones．這個古老的修道院是一座白石襯托紅磚的建築物。
*All the important passages in the article were picked out in red．該文的重要段落均用紅筆勾出。select the best of選出最好的
*She picked the apples over and threw out the bad ones．她把好蘋果挑出來，把壞的扔掉。
*We picked over the cotton seeds before sowing．我們將那些棉籽經過挑選之後才播種。steal扒竊（某人的東西）
*Thieves pick the pockets of unwary people．小偷扒竊粗心大意的人口袋裡的東西。
*The guy was given a good talkingto when he was found picking a customer's pocket in the shop．那傢伙在商店裡行竊時被當場發現，挨了一頓訓斥。1．lift；take up；raise after a fall 拾起；拿起；跌倒後爬起
*The children picked up many sea shells at the seashore．孩子們在海邊拾到很多貝殼。
*During the morning Mrs．Carter picked up sticks in the yard．早上卡特太太在院子裡拾柴。
*He fell but at once picked himself up．他跌了一跤，但馬上又爬了起來。
2． pay支付
*After lunch in the restaurant，Uncle Bob picked up the check．在餐館吃完飯後，鮑勃叔叔付了飯錢。
*They offered to pick up the bill for all the expenses of the trip．他們表示願意把全部旅行費用的帳單接受下來。
3．take on（開車）帶人
*The train stopped to pick up passenger．火車停下來讓乘客上車。
*I'll pick you up at your office．我到辦公室來接你。
*At the corner the bus stopped and picked up three people．在街拐角處汽車停下來讓3個人上車。
4． collect收集
*They picked up some rumours that the firm was going to close down．他們聽到一些關於公司要倒閉的謠傳。
*They are trying to pick up information．他們在設法收集情報。
*He picked up rare coins in seaports all over the world．他在世界各港口收集稀有硬幣。
5． gather together收拾；整理
*It's almost dinner time， children．Time to pick up and get ready．快到吃飯時間了，孩子們。收拾收拾，準備開飯。
*Let's pick up the room before everyone arrives．我們在大家來之前把房間整理好吧。
*It's time to pick up tools and go home．現在是收拾工具回家的時候了。
6．get，learn accidentally 偶然得到（或學到、找到）
*He never studied Japanese；what he knows is what he picked up while living in Japan．他從未正式學過日文，他所懂的一些日文是他居住在日本時隨便學來的。
*He picked up a beautiful statue when he was in Rome．他在羅馬時買到了一尊美麗的塑像。
*I picked up that volume in a secondhand book shop．那本書是我偶然在一家舊書店裡找到的。
*He has picked up some bad habits at that club．他在那個俱樂部沾染上了一些壞習氣。
7．make friends with與…交朋友
*Mother told Mary not to walk home by herself from the party be cause some strangers might try to pick her up．媽媽告訴瑪麗舞會後不要獨自步行回家，因為會有陌生人與她搭訕。
*I think she picked him up at a dance．我想她是在舞會上與他認識的。
8．arrest逮捕
*The main suspect in thr murder case was finally picked up by police in London yesterday．謀殺案中的主要嫌疑犯昨天在倫敦被警察抓住了。
*police picked the man up for burglary．警察因這男子盜竊而逮捕了他。
9．receive radio signals收到信號
With my new radio I can pick up stations all over Europe．我的新收音機可接收到歐洲所有的電台。
*The enemy planes are picked up by our radar installations．敵機被我們的雷達發現了。
10．rescue sb．from the water從水上救起
*AirSea Rescue picked up the downed airman after receiving an SOS message．空海營救隊接到呼救信號後，在海上救起了被擊落的飛行員。
*They picked up the survivors in the lifeboat．他們救起了救生艇裡的倖存者。
11．find and travel along（a route，a trail， etc．）發現（道路、蹤跡等）並沿著走
*State police picked up the bandits'trail．州警察發現了土匪的蹤跡。
*We picked up the trail of the fugitives and soon overtook them．我們找到逃亡者的蹤跡，不久就追上了他們。
12．continue or return to sth． after a break or interruption重新開始
*He picked up the story where he had left it the day before．他接著往下講前天沒講完的故事。
*I found it difficult to pick up the discussion again after lunch．我發現午飯後再繼續討論很困難。
13．make sb．feel better使感覺好些
*Catherine was feeling very bad yesterday but has picked up a lot today．凱瑟琳昨天身體很不好，但今天覺得好多了。
*A bit of exercise will pick you up．你稍微運動運動會恢復健康的。
*A little food will pick you up．吃點東西會使你感覺好些。
14． become faster加快
*About a mile out of the station the train began to pick up speed．出站大約一英里，火車開始加速。pick-and-shovel
