(8 reals)1． put together from many different pieces拼湊；使…連起來
*You must piece out the full story from your own imaginations．整個故事情節得通過你的想像才能串連起來。
*They pieced out a meal from leftovers．他們把剩餘的飯菜拼湊出一餐來。
2．make larger or longer by adding one or more pieces加長；加大
*The boy grew so fast that his mother had to piece out his coat．孩子長得太快了，他母親只好把他的衣服接長。piece rate
<<可數名詞>>
論件計酬時之報酬put together piece by piece 一片片拼合；拼湊
*She pieced together a blanket from odds and ends of wool．她用零碎毛料拼湊成一床毛毯。
*One cannot write a good narrative simply by piecing together the details．只是把細節拼湊起來並不能寫出一篇好的記敘文。
*I managed to piece together what had happened frow what he told me．我終於按他講的情況把事情經過貫穿了起來。patch up修補；接合
*Let's piece up this broken tyre．我們來把這個破輪胎修補一下。
*He was trying to piece up those fragments．他在設法把那些碎片拼合起來。
*pile in（to）
*1．push， crowd into （a car， room，football ground，etc．）擠進；擁入
*All five of us piled into George's car．我們 5個人全都擠進了喬治的汽車。
*Reports of bumper harvests came piling in from all parts of the country．豐收的消息從全國各地湧來。
*2． eat吃
*The meal is ready， pile in．飯好了，吃吧。
*3．attack violently猛烈攻擊
*John piled into his opponent， almost knocking him down at the first assault．約翰猛擊對手，第1次攻擊就幾乎把他打倒在地。piece.meal
