打樁機exaggerate；stretch the truth誇大
*Stop piling it on； it's not half as bad as you make it appear．別誇大其辭了，情況遠沒有你描述的那麼糟。
*pile on（to）
*put on in a heap堆上
*Why is it that all the extra work gets piled onto me at Christmas time？為什麼聖誕節期間把所有額外工作都堆在我身上？
*Pile on more coal；the fire is going out．火快滅了，再加些煤。push out（of a car， room， etc．）擠出去；蜂湧而出
*We piled out of the back of the car and stretched our cramped limbs．我們爭先恐後地從後面下車，活動一下被擠得動彈不得的四肢。1．grow into a big heap積聚
*He didn't go into his office for three days and his work kept piling up．他3天沒去上班，工作積了一大堆。
*Don't let your work pile up； never leave till tomorrow what you can finish today．不要積壓工作，今天能處理的決不要拖到明天。
*They had piled up a lot of earth in one corner of the garden．他們在花園一角堆積了很多土。
*He has piled up a lot of troubles for himself．他給自己找了一身麻煩。
2．crash衝撞
*Several cars and lorries piled up on the motorway in thick fog this morning．今天早上，高速公路上有好幾輛小汽車及卡車在大霧中相撞。
*One car made a sudden stop and the two cars behind it piled up．一輛小汽車突然停住，後面的兩輛撞了起來。pi.le.a
