2 將…壓在[某處],使…動彈不得 [to,against,under] 
The tree fell and ~ned him to the ground. 
樹倒下來把他壓在地上
The child was pinned against the wall. 
那小孩被按在牆頭動彈不得
3 把 <信念、希望等> 寄托[在…][on]
The widow pinned her hopes on her only son. 
那個寡婦把希望寄托在獨子身上
pin down
(1) 用針釘住…
(2) 使<人>固守[約定], [用合約、條約] 束縛<人>[to]
(3) 要求 [逼迫] <某人>[就…]詳細說明[to]
(4) 使<事實等>清楚,清楚地說明 [查明] …pin clover
見 alfilariapin curl
<<可數名詞>>
(固定髮型的) 卷髮器 [發卷]1．fix by means of a pin；fix immovably用針固定住；壓住
*They seemed to have pinned his legs down under a heavy weight．他們似乎用很重的東西把他的雙腿壓得不能動彈了。
2．bind使受約制；使受限制
*They managed to pin him down to a particular time and place．他們設法給他規定一個時間和地點。
*He agreed to lecture here next year， but I couldn't pin him down to a firm date．他答應明年來講學，但我無法叫他定出一個具體的日期。
3． get sb． to make a definite statement使表明態度
*We did try to pin him down on his plans for the swimming pool，but he remained evasive．我們的確想要他對他所擬訂的游泳池計劃表明態度，但他總是閃爍其辭。
4． accurately define or determine sth．確定；證實
*It was impossible to pin down exactly what it was that he was trying to say．不可能完全弄明白他想說的是什麼。
*pin one's faith on／upon／to trust 信任
*Don't pin your faith on his promises；he is known to be a rogue．不要相信他的諾言，大家都知道他是個無賴。
*I shouldn't pin my faith to what he says．我不該盲目相信他的話。pin money
