播放唱片
~ some popular music (on1．amuse oneself in a lighthearted way輕鬆愉快地玩
*The children are playing around in the garden．孩子們在園子裡玩耍。
2．toy；meddle玩弄；瞎弄
*The school told him that if he didn't stop playing about，he would fail in his exams．校方告訴他，要是他還瞎混的話，他考試會失敗的。
*She is playing around with a man twenty years younger than she is．她跟一個比她年輕20歲的男人鬼混。1．keep sb． waiting for an answer or a decision使（某人）焦急地等候
*You've played him along for some time now， without telling him what you really want．你們沒告訴他你們需要什麼，使他焦慮地等待了許久。
2．cooperate合作
*We felt that the best way to get what we wanted was to play along with them．我們覺得要達到我們的願望，最好的辦法是同他們合作。
*He plays along with his boss all the time，but I'm sure he does not really agree with him．他跟他老闆一直合作著，但我敢肯定他並不真正與他老闆意見一致。1．play（ball，card，etc．）打（球、牌等）
*They are playing at hockey．他們正在打曲棍球。
2．play the game of makebelieve of作假裝…的遊戲
*Let's play at being pirates．讓我們來假裝海盜。
*We watched the kindergarteners playing at camping out this afternoon．今天下午我們看了幼兒園的孩子們做野營遊戲。
3．do sth．in a halfhearted way 不認真做
*You must settle down and concentrate．You're only playing at doing your homework．你做作業一點也不認真，你要定下神來專心做你的作業。
*This is a job that needs to be tackled wholeheartedly－not played at．這件工作需要全神貫注認真對待，不能敷衍了事。replay放錄音
*We recorded our English lesson and then played it back．我們把英語課內容錄了下來，然後就放錄音聽。I'm going to play back the first half of Act One．我打算重放第 1幕上半部的錄音。1．begin play in a ball game開始賽球
*When the umpire calls「play ball，」the game begins．裁判一叫「開始比賽，」球賽就開始了。
2．join in an effort； cooperate 合作
*They said if we would play ball with them， this could be brought off with great success．他們說如果我們注意與他們合作，這件事情就能出色地完成。
*We need the Committee's approval for this scheme． Do you think they'll play ball with us？我們這項計劃需要委員會批准。你認為他們會跟我們合作嗎？1．play a musical instrument by remembering the tune憑聽覺記憶演奏
*She plays the piano entirely by ear．她不用樂譜，完全憑聽覺記憶演奏鋼琴。
2．decide what to do as one goes along酌情而定
*We don't know what may crop up，so you'll have to play it by ear．我們不知道會出現什麼情況，因此你得見機行事。tease or fool by pretending to let sb．go free and then catching him again欲擒故縱
*The policeman decided to play cat and mouse when he saw the woman steal the dress in the store．警察發覺那女人在商店偷衣服時，他欲擒故縱，暫時先不抓她。make sth． less important貶低；縮小
*He gave all the credit to the others and played down his own part in the work．他把功勞都歸於別人，而對自己的作用則輕描淡寫，一帶而過。
*The doctors thought it necessary to play down the serious nature of her illness．醫生認為把她的嚴重病情說得輕一些是必要的。
*The newspaper reports played down the actor's unattractive past．新聞報道對於該演員不光彩的過去很少提到。deliberately talk to or behave towards so that sb．doesn't feel inferior in order to win support or favor故意擺出平易近人的樣子
*Right before the election， the Labour candidate played down to the voters in order to win their support．就在大選前夕，工黨競選人裝出一副平易近人的姿態，以取得選民的支持。do what is right to others；act in a fair and truthful way公平；舉止正派
*He is a hardnosed man， but you can be sure that he'll play fair with you．他雖是一個頑固的人，但是你放心，他一定會公平對待你的。
*It wouldn't be playing fair if you were to break your promise at the last minute．你如果在最後關頭失信的話，那就不近情理了。
*play false cheat；deceive欺騙
*Don't try to play me false； I can see you don't mean what you said．別想騙我，我看得出來你講的跟你想的不是一回事。
*Good faith was not in him；he played anyone false who trusted him．他一點也不老實，專門欺騙那些信任他的人。repeatedly change one's attitude反覆無常
*He played fast and loose with several women's affections．他玩弄了好幾位女士的感情。
*No one can place any reliance on a person who plays fast and loose．沒有人能夠信賴反覆無常的人。
*He should not play fast and loose with the company's good name．他不應該拿公司的好名聲當兒戲。make sb．the victim of a trick or joke；make fun of和…開玩笑
*Mark Twain liked very much to tell funny stories and he also liked to play jokes on his friends．馬克?吐溫很喜歡講有趣的故事，他也喜歡開朋友的玩笑。
*Though he knew they were playing tricks on him， he pretended not to notice it．他心裡明白他們是在捉弄他，但他佯裝不知。1．put sb．in competition with sb．else，so to benefit from it在…之間挑撥以從中獲利
*She was always playing her two brothers off against each other．她總是在她兩個兄弟之間挑起爭端。
*The practice of playing off one great power against another is not new．挑撥一個強國對抗另一個強國並不是什麼新的手法。
2．play or complete the playing of （an interrupted or delayed match）； break（a tie） by playing once more舉行或完成（中斷了的比賽）；（平局後）再賽以決勝負
*Smith and Peter will play off next week．史密斯和彼得下周舉行決賽。
*The visitors came back the next Saturday to play off the game stopped by rain．客隊下星期六來進行因雨天而停止的比賽。
*When each player had won two matches，the championship was decided by playing off the tie．兩個選手都各贏兩局後，再賽一局以決定冠軍。
3．make fun of取笑
*Jones always tried to play off poor old Smith who stammered badly．瓊斯總想嘲弄可憐的老史密斯，因為他口吃得很厲害。
4．pretend假裝
*The man is not ill； he is playing off．這人沒病，他是在裝病。1．perform to the end把…進行到底
*In spite of the heavy rain they managed to play out the football match．儘管雨下得很大，他們還是堅持把球踢完。
*The actors played out the comedy and the audience applauded．演員們演完喜劇後，觀眾拍手喝采。
2．exhaust疲倦
*I'm always played out by the time I finish work on Fridays．每到星期五這時候，所有的事情都做完了，我總會感到精疲力竭。
*The work was strenuous for John，and each day he would arrive home all played out．對於約翰來說，這工作實在太吃力了，他每天回到家裡，總是精疲力盡。
3．become ineffective已不適用
*Such methods soon played out．這些方法很快就不適用了。play tricks for one's own gain玩弄權術；操縱
*The attorney for the union accused the Mayor of playing politics in the strike．工會律師譴責市長在這次罷工中玩弄權術。
*In order to get elected，he had to play politics with both the unions and the bosses．為了要當選，他得同時與工會和老闆們達成協議。1．pretenb to be asleep裝睡；裝傻
*The boy seemed to be fast asleep，but I knew he was playing possum．這孩子看上去像是睡熟了，但我知道他是裝的。
*Don't let his silence fool you；he's just playing possum．別被他的沉默騙了，他只不過是裝傻。
2．stay quiet for selfprotection；try to escape attention by inactivity 不動聲色；不引起注意
*The rabbit played possum under the bushes， hoping the hunter would not see him．兔子靜待在灌木叢中，希望獵人看不見它。be very careful求穩；不冒險
*Tom didn't know what the other driver would do，so he played safe and stopped his own car．湯姆不知道另一個司機要幹什麼，為安全起見他就停下車子。
*I don't think it will rain today，but I'd better play safe and take a raincoat．我看今天不會下雨，不過為穩妥起見，我還是帶件雨衣好。act a smaller part居次要職位；當副手
*I'm tired of playing second fiddle to George－why can't I run the business？老是給喬治當副手我煩死了，為什麼我就不能管事呢？
*He was only too glad to play second fiddle to Professor Smith at the symposium．他非常樂意在討論會上當史密斯教授的助手。play street
遊戲街道
(臨時禁止車輛出入使兒童能安全在戶外遊戲的街道)cause confusion in；upset擾亂；破壞
*The high winds played the devil with my new hairstyle．大風吹亂了我的新髮型。
*Mother's illness played the devil with our party．由於母親生病，我們取消了聚會。obey the rules； do right符合規則；做事公道
*Tom told the teacher what had happened，but all his friends thought he had been unfair and that he hadn't played the game properly．湯姆把所發生的一切告訴了老師，但他的朋友都認為他不公正，太不光明磊落了。
*I hold her in high esteem，since she is an honest person and has always played the game．我非常尊敬她，因為她是個誠實的人，一向辦事公道。try to make money on the stock market by buying and selling stocks玩股票
*Sometimes Mr．White makes a lot of money when he plays the market，and sometimes he loses．懷特先生玩股票有時賺大錢，有時則賠本。try to get the approval of the audience討好（低級趣味的）觀眾；迎合大眾的口味
*In the past few years，television has been playing to the gallery．過去幾年裡，電視一直在迎合大眾的口味。
*The speaker played to the gallery by indulging in vulgar jokes．為了譁眾取寵，那位演講者大講粗俗的笑話。1．emphasize強調
*The coach played up the possibilities of success．教練竭力強調成功的可能性。
*In the article he plays himself up and plays the others down．在文章中他抬高自己，貶低別人。
2．play well； do one's best賽好；加油
*I expect them to play up this afternoon．我希望他們今天下午賽出水平來。
3．behave mischievously；cause trouble調皮；折磨；製造麻煩
*The new teacher didn't know what to do when the class started playing up．班級開始亂哄哄時，新來的老師不知該怎麼辦。
*The old wound has been playing up again lately．近來舊傷又在折磨人。
*Those children do play their parents up．那些孩子確實給父母惹麻煩。
*The engine began playing up．引擎開始出毛病了。
4．（a band） begin to play（樂隊）開始演奏
*The band played up the national anthem．樂隊奏起了國歌。flatter討好
*He is always playing up to the pretty girl students．他總是向那些長得漂亮的女學生獻慇勤。
*He always plays up to his political boss．他總是對他的政界上司獻媚。
*He is the sort of man who dislikes being played up to．他是那種不願被奉承的人。1．have fun with和…玩
*The boy is playing with his new toys．這小男孩在玩他的新玩具。
2．trifle with輕率對待；玩弄
*She's not a woman to tolerate being played with．她不是一個容忍別人玩弄的女人。
*He's been playing with the idea ofleaving his job and buying a farm，but he'll never do it．他一直在考慮離開現在的工作，去買一個農場，但他永遠也不會這樣做。take risks；put oneself in danger 冒險；引火燒身
*He loved driving fast，even though he knew he was playing with fire．即使他知道開快車是很危險的，但他還是喜歡這麼幹。
*He who plays with fire gets burned．玩火者必自焚。play-by-play
