<<可數名詞>>
關於議事程序的問題a way of considering or judging a thing，person，event，etc．觀點
*From my point of view it would be better if you could come tomorrow，but you may not want to．從我的觀點看，你明天最好來，但你可能並不想來。
*You've given me quite a new point of view．你給我提供了一個新的看法。

point of view
1 立點; 觀點
2 對事物之態度1．explain解釋
*He pointed out that it was not his fault．他解釋說這不是他的過錯。
*I pointed out the advantages of the plan．我說明了這計劃的優點。
2．call to attention喚起注意
*The policeman pointed out that the law forbids public sale of firecrackers．警察指出法律禁止公開銷售鞭炮。
*It was pointed out to him that his application had arrived too late．有人向他指出，他的申請交來太晚了。
*When the mistake was pointed out to him he hastened to correct it．人們向他指出錯誤時，他趕緊糾正。point switch
<<可數名詞>>
『鐵路』轉轍機point system
<<可數名詞>>
1 (盲人的) 點字法
2 (學業成績的) 分數制度
3 (記錄汽車駕駛員違規的) 記點制度1．direct to指向
*The needle of a compass points to the north．羅盤的指針指向北方。
*Not far from there，you'll see a signpost pointing to the town you want to go to．離那兒不遠，你就可以看到一個路標，指明你所要去的那個鎮的方向。
2． direct attention to指明；表明
*Everything points to his guilt．一切表明他有罪。
*Everything points to a bright future for us all．種種跡象表明我們都有光明的前途。show clearly清楚地表明
