top of the pops → toppay a visit casually 順便經過；順道來訪
*I'll pop along to the post office and mail the package for you．我順便去郵局幫你把包裹寄走。
*I may pop in to see you next month．我也許下個月來看你。pop art
<<不可數名詞>>
『美術』普普 [大眾] 藝術 (pop) 
(從 1962 年左右起以紐約 (New York) 為中心,採用廣告、漫畫等技巧的前衛派美術運動)pop fly
<<可數名詞>>
『棒球』內野高飛球1．go away hurriedly趕緊離開
*I must pop off now．我得走了。
*Where has he popped off to？他匆忙去哪裡了？
2．die死
*I'm not going to pop off just now，so you needn't worry．我還不會死，你不用著急。
*He popped off at the age of twenty．他在20歲時突然死去。
3．fire放（槍、炮等）
*The children were running about popping off their toy guns．孩子們奔跑著，劈哩啪啦地放玩具槍。1．go out hurriedly匆匆出去
*I'm sorry to have kept you waiting；I just popped out for a few moments．抱歉，勞你久等了。我剛才匆匆出去了一會兒。
2．come out with a sharp explosive sound砰地一聲出來
*The cork popped out and the champagne gushed from the bottle．軟木塞撲地一聲跳出來，香檳酒從瓶裡湧了出來。
3．protrude from the sockets突出
*His eyes popped out in surprise．他驚訝得眼睛瞪得大大的。ask sb．to marry one求婚
*After the dance， he popped the question．舞會後，他向她求婚。rise or appear suddenly or unexpectedly；show up突然出現
*I haven't seen him for weeks， but I'm sure he'll pop up one of these days．我好幾個星期沒見他了，不過我肯定他這幾天會來的。
*He pops up all over the place， so you never know where to look for him．他什麼地方都去，所以你不知道去哪裡找他。pop-eyed
