5<人>剝削[欺騙][某人][on, upon]1．hunt and kill（animal）for food 捕食
*Cats prey on mice．貓捉老鼠。
*What does the owl prey on？貓頭鷹捉什麼東西吃？
2．rob； take advantage of劫掠
*The robbers living in the mountains preyed on any traveller who wandered into their land．住在山裡的那幫強盜對進入他們地區的任何遊人都要搶劫。
*It was hard to believe that these little boats were being preyed on by pirates．很難相信海盜對這些小船都要搶劫。
3．trouble or worry sb．使痛苦；折磨
*His fears and worries preyed so much on his mind that eventually he committed suicide．恐懼和焦慮經常折磨著他，最後他自殺了。
*Ill health has preyed on him for years．疾病折磨了他許多年。prf.
