pull off
(1) (急忙) 脫下<衣服>
He ~ed1．pull in different directions拖來拖去
*He pulled the flowers about until he ruined them all．他把那些花拖過來拽過去，結果全搞壞了。
2．handle roughly猛力推搡；虐待
*They pulled him about rather violently．他們相當凶狠地推搡著他。
*He got angry when people started pulling him about．人們開始粗暴待他時，他惱火了。overtake sb．or sth．超前
*The winner of the men's 400 metres pulled ahead in the last 50 metres．男子400米的獲勝者在最後50米衝到了最前面。
*That driver's trying to overtake．Slow down a bit and let him pull ahead．那個司機想超車，開慢一點讓他超過去吧。1．separate by pulling把…撕開；拆開；扯斷
*The table is so made that you can easily pull it apart．這張桌子是可以隨意拆開的。
*As the curtains were pulled apart，we saw the actors on the stage．帷幕拉開時，我們看到了台上的演員。
2．criticize sb．or find serious faults in an idea， plan， piece of work，etc．把…批評得一無是處
*He pulled my argument apart and made me feel very stupid．他把我的論點說得一無是處，使我感到像是個傻瓜。
*The professor proceeded to pull apart the student's paper．教授進而指出那個學生作業中的許多錯誤。1．drag forcibly at用力拉
*Mary pulled at his sleeve and led him boldly upstairs．瑪麗拉了拉他的袖子，大膽地領他上樓。
*The dog pulled at the rope as though he knew alife depended on his exertions．這條狗用力拉繩，好像知道它用力與否關係到一條性命似的。
2．take a drink from； draw from by sucking深吸（煙）；大口喝（酒）
*The old man sat in the corner，pulling at his pipe．老人坐在角落裡，抽著煙斗。1． cause to be down from its place by pulling把…拉下
*His hat was pulled well down over his eyes so that nobody would guess his true identity．他把帽沿拉得很下，幾乎遮住了眼睛，使人猜不清他是誰。
2．destroy；demolish（a building）破壞；拆毀（建築物）
*It is easy to pull down the old world than to build the new．破壞舊世界容易，但要建設新世界就難了。
*They pulled down the old shop and built a supermarket．他們拆掉了舊商店，建起了一個超級市場。
3．earn掙得
*He pulls down quite a lot of money in his new job．新工作使他掙了許多錢。
*Tom always pulled down the highest grades in school．湯姆在學校總得最高分。
4．weaken（sb．） in health使身體虛弱
*A really bad cold pulls you down and leaves you feeling very miserable．重感冒會使你身體虛弱，讓你感到很難受。
*That long spell in hospital pulled him down a lot．那次長時間生病住院使他的體質大大變差了。
5．humiliate羞辱；批評；降低地位
*They intend to pull him down a bit．他們想挫挫他的銳氣。
*One is not sorry to see the proud pulled down．看到自高自大的人被拉下來，誰都不會惋惜。1．reduce one's boast；calm down from a quarrel收斂言語；停上吵架
*He pulled in his horns when he realized that his boasting was not impressing me．當他意識到他的自吹對我不起作用時，就縮回去了。
2．reduce spending or activity縮減開支或活動
*After the business failed，father had to pull in his horns．經營失敗後，父親只得縮減開支。criticize very badly；find serious fault with駁得體無完膚；說得一無是處
*Politicians always try to pull their opponents'ideas to pieces．政治家們總是把他們對手的觀點駁得體無完膚。
*The famous scientist pulled the new theory to pieces because it was very unscientific．這位著名的科學家把這條新理論說得一無是處，因為它很不科學。1．arrive到達
*The lorry driver pulled into the side of the road to get a cup of tea．卡車司機把車子停靠在路邊去喝杯茶。
*The train from Edinburgh pulled in five minutes late．從愛丁堡開出的列車晚點5分鐘進站。
2．seize（a possible criminal）抓獲（嫌疑犯）
*The police pulled those youths in for questioning after the robbery．搶劫案發生後，警察把這些年輕人拘留起來審問。
3．attract吸引
*The Beatles always pulled in enormous crowds．甲殼蟲樂隊總是吸引成千上萬的人。
*They need to have a high rate of interest in order to pull in money from investors．他們需要高利率來誘使投資者投入資金。
4．reduce one's expenses；restrain 緊縮開支；限制
*You must pull in now，or you'll be asking for trouble．你應當節約，不然你會自找麻煩。
5．earn掙得
*He pulls in quite a lot as a milkman．他當牛奶工掙了不少錢。
*They're pulling in a lot of overtime on that job．他們做那工作得了很多加班費。complete or perform（sth．） successfully使（某事）成功
*He has pulled off some remarkable shots in the match．在比賽中，他幾次因精彩的投籃而得分。
*How did you manage to pull off the deal without offering them more money？沒有出更多的錢，你是怎樣把這筆生意做成的？get control of oneself；get into a mood of preparedness振作起來；做好…的思想準備
*Stop crying and pull yourself together！ You're not a baby any more．別哭了，冷靜點！你不再是個小毛孩了。
*Pulling himself together，he dismissed the matter from his mind．他振作起來，不再想這件事。1．take（sth．） out拿出；拔出
*Putting his hand in his pocket， he pulled out a handkerchief．他把手伸進口袋掏出一塊手帕。
*He pulled out the pistol and aimed at the enemy officer．他拔出手槍，對準敵軍官。
*I'll have to have this tooth pulled out．我的這顆牙要拔掉。
2．move away離開
*We reached the station too late，just as the train was pulling out．我們到達車站太遲了，當時火車正出站。
*The train for Beijing will pull out in 10 minutes．去北京的火車還有10分鐘就要開了。
3．leave；cause to leave離開；退出
*Jim saw that the firm was going to be ruined，so he pulled out．吉姆眼看公司即將垮台，於是就退了出來。
*The government pulled the army out of the troublespot．政府把部隊撤出有爭端的地區。
4．recover from illness恢復健康
*John did not feel very well， but soon he pulled out．約翰感到身體不太舒服，但不久就康復了。drive towards the roadside開向一邊
*Everyone pulled over to let the ambulance pass．大家都把車子開到路邊，讓救護車開過去。1．help（sb．） to pass safely through a difficulty幫助…度過難關
*Their courageous spirit pulled them through the darkest days of the war．他們的勇敢精神使他們度過了戰爭中最黑暗的日子。
*Good nursing will pull him through．好好護理可以使他恢復過來。
*The company was in great difficulties this year until a gift of money from the government pulled it through．今年那家公司一直困難重重，直到政府資助後才度過難關。
2．recover from an illness恢復健康
*He was very ill but he eventaully pulled through．他病得很重，但最後還是康復了。
*The competent doctor pulled the patient through his serious illness by giving him the best possible attention．那位能幹的醫生給病人以無微不至的關懷，使其從重病中康復了。1．cooperate合作
*People often pull together in a crisis．人們在危機中往往是團結一致的。
*We must pull together， or we will fail．我們必須齊心協力，否則就會失敗。
*We must all pull together if we are to win this election．如果我們想在這次選舉中獲勝，就必須通力合作。
*It's hoped that the new coach may be able to pull the football team together．希望新教練能使這個足球隊重振雄風。
2．make oneself regain one's courage振作起來
*It took some time for him to recover from the shock and pull himself together．過了一些時候，他才從震驚中恢復過來，重新鎮靜下來。
*After breaking down and weeping，she tried hard to pull herself together．失聲痛哭一陣之後，她竭力振作起來。1．raise（sth．） by pulling拔出
*You'll find my mother in the garden as usual， pulling up weeds．你會像平時一樣在花園裡找到我的母親，她在拔草。
2．（cause to） come to a stop（使）停止
*A lorry pulled up as I was walking along the footpath， and the driver asked me the way to the soft drinks factory．我沿著小路散步時，一輛卡車停了下來，司機問我去軟飲料廠的路。
*The policeman pulled up the motorist and asked to see his licence．警察讓那個駕駛員停車，要看他的執照。
*The car pulled up when the light turned red．紅燈亮時，那輛轎車停了下來。
*I wanted to keep on speaking but the chairman pulled me up short．我想繼續講下去，但會議主席把我打斷了。
3．improve提高
*His mark in English pulled him up several places．他的英語成績使他的名次提前了好幾名。pull-in
