英口語)危急時,臨危,緊急時
if [when] it comes to the push 
臨到緊要關頭 [危急] 時bully；order about驅使；擺佈
*I'm not going to be pushed about by anybody．我不準備受任何人的擺佈。
*Paul is always pushing the smaller children around．保爾總欺侮比他年紀小的孩子。1．go on resolutely堅決前進
*It's getting on for noon；we must push ahead to our destination as quickly as possible．快中午了，我們必須盡快到達目的地。
*If you want to push on with the decorating， we can leave dinner until later．你要是想繼續裝飾的話，晚飯我們可以晚點吃。
2．ambitiously draw attention to （oneself）故意引人注目
*He doesn't like pushing himself forward on public occasions．他不喜歡在公開場合拋頭露面。1．impel along；continue one's way 繼續前進
*He pushed the work along．他抓緊進行工作。
*We were tired but managed to push along to the next village．雖然我們很疲勞，但還是竭力趕到了下一個村子。
2．leave；go離開；去
*It's time for us to push along now．我們該走了。push button
<<可數名詞>>
按鈕strive for爭取；強烈要求
*The miners are pushing for more money and less work．礦工們強烈要求增加工資，減少工作。
*People living near the airport are pushing for new rules about night flights．機場附近的居民正在強烈要求制訂新的夜航規則。1．set sail in a small boat乘船出發
*We pushed off frow the shore and were soon out to sea．我們乘船駛離岸邊，不久就到了海上。
2．leave or go away離開
*I must be pushing off now！ It's getting late．現在我得走了！天已很晚了。
*Push off！ Can't you see I'm busy？走開！你難道看不見我很忙嗎？1． make a passage through擠過去
*He tried in vain to push through the crowd．他怎麼也無法從人群中擠過去。
2．gain acceptance of a bill， proposal使…被通過
*In spite of a lot of resistance，we managed to push the proposal through．雖然有許多阻力，我們還是設法使這個議案通過了。
*We're trying to push the legislation through before the Christmas recess．我們力爭在聖誕節休會前通過這法令。
3．cause sb． to pass or succeed in doing sth．設法完成
*By giving him extra lessons，we managed to push him through his exams．通過給他額外加課，我們終於使他通過了考試。cause sth．to rise or increase 上升；提高
*Wage increases keep pushing up the cost of living．工資的增加使生活消費不斷上漲。
*The hot bath has pushed her temperature up．熱水澡使她身上暖和多了。
*I can't reach the branch．Will you push me up？我夠不到那樹枝。你把我托上去好嗎？push-button
