(put; put.ting)
1 放置
【同義字】
put 放置
set 鄭重其事,放於「固定位置」
place 放在正確的位置
lay 橫放
a. 把<東西、人>放在 (某場所) ,擱
P~ your pencil down. 
把你的鉛筆放下來
P~ the chair here, please. 
請把那張椅子放在這裡
She ~ the dish on the table. 
她把盤子放在桌子上
b. 把<東西、人>置於 (某位置) ,使<人>陷入 [處於] (某種處境,情況) 
You should ~ your happiness first. 
你應該把你的幸福置於第一位
(你應該最先考慮你的幸福)
This case will ~ him in a serious position. 
這個案件將使他陷入困境
Just ~ yourself in his place. 
請你設身處地替他想想
c. 把…置於 (…狀態、關係) ,使…成為 (某種狀態、關係) 
~ names in alphabetical order 
把名字依字母順序排列
~ a law in force 
執行法律,實施法律
~ something in motion 
使東西移動
~ a person in (a) good humor 
使某人興高采烈
~ a person in charge of the work 
使某人負責那件工作
~ a person out of temper 
使某人發脾氣 [發怒] 
d. 把…弄<成…>
She ~ his tie straight. 
她把他的領帶弄直
His report ~ the matter wrong. 
他的報告把那件事弄砸了
2 移動
a. 使…移 (至…) ,使…朝向,把…放進
He ~ the pail down the well. 
他把水桶放入井中
You mustn't ~ your finger into your mouth. 
你不可把手指放進嘴裡
He ~ the book in his bag. 
他把那一本書放進他的書包裡
They ~ the man into jail. 
他們把那個男子關進牢裡
b. 把<東西>安裝[接][在…],使…貼近,使…接近[to]
The driver ~ the horse to his cart. 
馬車伕把馬套在貨車上
He ~ his eye to the telescope. 
他把眼睛貼在望遠鏡上
He ~ spurs to his horse. 
他以踢馬刺刺馬
c. 把…打入[…],將…灌入[…] [into,in,through] 
~ a nail into a board 
把釘子打入木板
~ a satellite into orbit 
把衛星射入軌道
~ a knife into a person 
把刀子刺入某人身體
~ one's pen through a word 
在某字上畫線 (刪除) 
What ~ such an idea into your head?. 
何事把如此念頭灌入你的腦子裡?
(你腦子裡怎麼會有如此念頭?)
3 
a. 使<人>承受[痛苦],接受 [考驗等] [to,on,through] 
~ a person to torture 
使某人受折磨
~ a person to great inconvenience [much trouble] 
給某人很多麻煩,給某人帶來諸多不便
~ a person to death [the sword] 
處死 [殺死] 某人
~ a person on trial 
使某人受審判
~ students through an examination 
使學生接受考試
→ PUT a person through it.
b. (為某種目的而) 送 [載] … [到某場所] ,使…去[…][to, on]
~ one's son to school 
使兒子就學
~ one's children to bed 
使孩子們就寢
~ one's son to a trade 
使兒子從事某種生意
~ a play on the stage 
上演一齣戲
c. 使<某人>著手[工作等][to]
~ a person to work 
使某人工作
~ the group to digging 
使那群人去挖掘
d. [~ oneself]著手[…],開始[to]
~ oneself to work 
開始工作 [用功] 
4 投入
a. 把 <注意力、精力等> 投入[…][to, into]
~ one's mind to world economics 
把心思投注於世界經濟
~ all one's energies into one's study 
傾全力於研究
b. 把<錢>投資[於…][in, into]
~ one's money into land 
把錢投資於土地
c. 把<錢>賭在[…上][on]
He ~ his last penny on the horse. 
他把最後的錢賭在那匹馬的身上
5 
a. 把…交給[…],委託,托付 [in,into,under] 
~ matters in [into] the hands of the police 
把事情交給警方 (處理) 
~ one's child under the care of the doctor 
把孩子交由那位醫生治療
b. 把<責任等>歸於[…],把…歸咎[於…][to, on]
He ~ his failure to my carelessness. 
他把自己的失敗歸咎於我的粗心
You must not ~ the responsibility on any other person. 
你不可把該責任推給其他任何人
c. [對…]課 <稅> ,加以 <侮辱> [on, upon]
~ a tax on an article 
對物品課稅
~ an insult on a person 
侮辱某人
d. [對…]予以 <信任> ,將 <信任> 寄予[某人][in]
~ one's trust in a person 
信任某人
6 
a. [向…]提出,提起 <問題、議案等> [to,before] 
He ~ the motion to [before] the committee. 
他向該委員會提出那項動議
He ~ several questions before me. 
他向我提幾個問題
I ~ it to you that you have told a lie. 
我要你承認你說了謊話
b. [對…]設 <限> ,做 [了結] [to]
~ an end [a stop] to 
?對…打上休止符,使…結束
~ an end to one's life 
結束自己的生命
c. 抑制[…],[對…]施加 <壓力> [on]
~ a check on one's enthusiasm 
抑制某人的狂熱
7 
a. [在…]寫 [簽] <名字等> [to]
I ~ my signature to the document. 
我在文件上簽名
b. 列 <名字等> [於表等上] [on]
He ~ the n1．spread a rumor，piece of news，story，etc．傳播；散佈
*They've put it about that the Government's going to resign．他們謠傳說政府將集體辭職。
*Someone has been putting rumors about that we are leaving．有人散佈謠言說我們要走了。
2．trouble；distress麻煩
*Please don't put yourself about because of me．請別為我麻煩了。
*He was very much put about by the news of the illness of his fellow worker．聽到同事生病的消息他很難過。
3．cause to change direction改變方向
*The captain put the ship about and headed for safety．船長將船轉航，駛向安全水域。1．fulfil sth． successfully做成
*The director put the business deal across in record time．廠長在極短的時間內就把生意做成了。
2．make understood使…被理解
*He was too full of emotion to put across his ideas properly．他太激動了，沒有把他的意思表達清楚。
*He was having difficulty putting his case across．他當時很難講清自己的情況。1．make sth．end；cause to end使…停止
*It's up to the police to put an end to these robberies．杜絕這類搶劫案是警察的事。
2．destroy or kill毀掉或殺死
*The new highway took most of the traffic from the old road and put an end to Mr．Hanson's motel business．舊路上的大部分車輛都轉移到新公路上，漢森先生的汽車旅館生意也因此而終止。1．place sth．on one side放在一邊
*She put her sewing aside when the telephone rang．電話響時她把縫紉活放在一邊。
2．save or reserve節省或存儲
*He tries to put aside a little money every month．每月他都努力省些錢下來。
3．ignore不予理會
*During the war everyone put their political differences aside and worked together．戰爭期間大家都放棄政治分歧通力合作。1．put sth．in a proper place收拾（東西）
*Please put those tools away after you finish the work．幹完活後請把那些工具收起來。
2．save（money）存（錢）
*I have put some money away in the bank．我已在銀行裡存了點錢。
*How much have you put away for your holiday？你為度假存了多少錢？
3．stop thinking about停止考慮
*Put away those foolish ideas．放棄那些可笑的想法吧。
*She put away the idea of going home on holiday．她放棄了回家度假的念頭。
4．place in prison監禁
*The judge put the criminal away for ten years．法官判這名罪犯服10年刑。
5．eat or drink吃或喝
*He put away nearly half a bottle of whisky last night．昨晚他喝了近半瓶威士忌酒。
*How can they put away so much rice？這麼多的飯，他們怎麼能吃光？
6．kill；kill to prevent suffering處死；殺掉
*The dog was so old and ill that it had to be put away．那條狗年老多病，只好處死。
*Douglas put away Collins in cold blood．道格拉斯蓄意殺死了柯林斯。1．reset the hands of a clock or watch to an earlier time撥回
*My watch was ten minutes too fast，and I put it back．我的表快了10分鐘，我把它撥回去了。
2．put off推遲；延誤
*The meeting has been put back until next week．會議已推遲到了下個星期。
*We had iniended to get married in April but we had to put the wedding back to September．我們原打算4月份結婚，但後來只好推遲到9月份。
*The strike has put back production considerably．罷工已經大大地耽誤了生產。1．lay aside儲備
*We should put by something for a rainy day．我們應該未雨綢繆。
*We have put by some medicine for emergencies．我們儲存了一些藥品，以備急用。
2．leave out of consideration；evade sth．把…擱在一邊；迴避
*We may shelve the difficulties for a while，but they cannot be put by inde finitely．我們可以暫時不考慮這些困難，但要永遠迴避是不可能的。
*He put the idea by until he was at leisure to consider it carefully．他把這個想法擱在一邊，直到有空時再去仔細考慮。1．stop by force；crush武力鎮壓
*In 24 hours the general had entirely put down the rebellion．在24小時內，這位將軍就把叛亂完全鎮壓下去了。
2．write a record of記錄
*Make sure that you put down every word she says．務必記下她所說的每一個字。
3．name sth．as a cause歸因於
*I would put his bad manners down to tiredness．我認為他的無禮是因為他太疲勞了。
*I don't think you can put all his success down to pure luck．我認為你不能把他所取得的全部成就歸結為僥倖。
4．charge sth．to a particular account把（開支）記在…帳上
*She put the dress down to her mother's account．她把買衣服的錢記在母親帳上。
5．stop and let a passenger get out of a vehicle讓乘客下車
*Where would you like me to put you down？你要我在哪兒讓你下車？
*The bus stopped at the station to put down one or two passengers．公共汽車到站停下，讓一兩位乘客下車。
6．land or cause sth．to land使…降落
*The pilot put the plane down safely，despite the storm．儘管有暴風雨，飛行員還是安全地降落了飛機。
7．humiliate sb．駁斥；使啞口無言
*He seems to enjoy putting his wife down in public．他似乎喜歡在大庭廣眾之下把妻子弄得啞口無言。
*He was put down in the argument．他在辯論中被駁得無言以對。
8．dig；drill挖；掘
*They're engaged in putting down a well．他們正在挖一口井。
9．pay a deposit付定金
*She put down ＄100 on some furniture．她買家俱付了100美元定金。
10．kill an animal殺死
*If the horse't leg is broken，it'll have to be put down．要是馬腿斷了，那只能把它殺了。
11．regard sb．as認為…是
*The man looked so uneasy that I put him down for a criminal．那個人看上去非常不安，我便以為他是個罪犯。
12．write the name of sb．as willing to give（an amount of money）寫出…名字以示願出（多少錢）
*I have put you down for￡5，is that all right？我已記下你的名字，你願出5鎊，對嗎？
13．put on a waiting list for申請
*If only he had put down for that job，he might have been a director now．要是他申請了那個工作，他現在或許就是個主任了。
*You have to put down for government housing well in advance．你必須提前申請政府住房。1．produce（leaves）長出（葉子）
*In spring the trees put forth new leaves．樹在春天長出新葉子。
2．bring（strength）into action；show；display使出勁；做出努力
*Putting forth a great effort，he uprooted the tree．他費了好大勁才把那棵樹連根拔起。
*Students who put forth much effort will get ahead．勤奮的學生是會取得進步的。
*In the contest，our team was trying for the prize，so we put forth a lot of effort．在比賽中，我們隊力爭要得獎，所以我們作了很大努力。
3．state；propose；offer（a plan）陳述，提出（計劃等）
*The heads of government of many countries have put forth a better system for preventing world war．許多國家的政府首腦提出了阻止世界大戰爆發的更好辦法。
*The President put forth his best plan for cutting down on in flation．總統提出了控制通貨膨脹的最佳方案。1．propose or suggest提出
*The students put forward new proposals on the running of the college to the College Education Committee．學生們向學院教育委員會提出了管理學院的建議。
*I have put your name forward as the best for the job．我已提議你為這項工作的最佳人選。
2．move the hands of（a clock or watch）to a later time往前撥（鐘錶）
*My watch was slow so I put it forward three minutes．我的表慢了，因此往前撥了3分鐘。
3．move an event，appointment，etc．to an earlier time or date把…提前
*We had to put our holiday forward one month．我們不得不把我們的假期提前一個月。
*The warm weather has put the crops forward by a month．暖和的天氣使莊稼早熟了一個月。1．cause to be in；add使加入；使進入
*You find the tea too strong？Just put in more water．你覺得這茶太濃嗎？多加些水進去就是了。
*He put his head in at the window．他把頭伸進窗口。
*It's a pity that he forgot to put in some of the important details in his report．很可惜，他忘了把一些重要細節寫進報告裡。
2．spend time doing sth．花費（時間）；度過（時間）
*Altogether，he has put in about four years'work on his thesis．他總共用了4年時間研究他的課題。
*There's still a quarter of an hour to put in before the class begins．還要過一刻鐘才上課。
3．make a request or application提出申請或要求
*If any of the goods arrive in a damaged condition，you must put in a claim within three days．如果到的任何貨物有受損情況，你必須在3天內提出賠償要求。
*You won't get the money if you don't put in for it．你如果不提出要求，這筆錢你就得不到。
4．recommend sb．for sth．推薦
*His commanding officer is putting him in for the Victoria Cross．他的司令官推薦授予他維多利亞十字勳章。
*We are thinking of putting John in for the 100 metres．我們考慮提名約翰參加百米賽跑。
5．do；perform干；做
*She always puts in an hour's piano practice after supper．她每天晚飯後練一小時的鋼琴。
6．install；fix or supply sth．安裝
*We put central heating in when we moved into our new house．我們搬新家時安裝了中央供暖裝置。
7．elect使人當選；選舉
*Voters put a Conservative government in at the last election．上次選舉中，保守黨入選了。
8．appoint任命；委派
*A security man was put in to check on doors and windows．委派了一個安全人員檢查門窗。
9．enter sb．or sth．in a competition參加比賽
*She put herself in for the marathon．她報名參加馬拉松比賽。
10．enter a port進港
*The vessel put in at Xiamen during the storm．船進廈門港躲避暴雨。
11．cut in插話
*「Don't forget us，」she put in．「別忘了我們。」她插話說。say sth．in favor of sb．or sth．為某人或某事說話
*If you have a chance to put in a word for me when you speak to the boss，I'll appreciate it．你和老闆交談時，如果能為我美言幾句，我會非常感激。
*His uncle put in a good word for him and he got the job．他叔叔為他說情，他才得到這份工作。
*She was so unpopular that on one could be found to put in a word for her．她太不得人心了，替她說情的人一個也找不到。remind sb．of使…想起
*She puts me in mind of my sister．她使我想起了我的姐姐。
*The way he behaves when he is angry puts me in mind of his father．他發脾氣時的那付樣子使我想起他的父親。perform；fulfil實施
*We have made our plans；now we must put them into practice．我們已經制定計劃，現在該付諸實施了。1．pretend假裝
*He says he's unwell，but I think he is putting it on．他說他有病，可我認為他是在裝病。
*He is a pretty good dancer，but he was putting it on to impress his girlfriend．他跳舞跳得相當不錯，但為了給女朋友留下深刻印象，他故意賣弄了一番。
2．boast吹牛；誇張
*That's rather putting it on．那是誇大其詞。
*It wasn't as hard as you claimed；you were putting it on．這並不像你說的那麼難，你在誇大其詞。1．take off脫去
*As it got warmer，I put off my overcoat．天氣暖和了些，我脫去了大衣。
2．postpone推遲
*Never put off till tomorrow what may he done today．今天可以幹的事絕不要拖到明天。
*The concert had to be put off because the main singer was ill．由於主要歌唱演員病了，音樂會不得為延期。
*He had to put off his trip to Japan for two weeks．他只好把去日本的行期推遲兩周。
3．distract使分散
*The slightest noise puts me off when I am concentrating．當我精神高度集中的時候，很輕的聲音都會使我注意力分散。
*I don't like people talking when I'm writing a letter；it puts me off．我寫信時不喜歡別人談話，那會使我分心。
4．embarrass；displease使為難
*Don't be put off by his appearance；he's nice when you get to know him．不要對他的外表反感，當你與他熟悉後，你會覺得他為人很好。
*Don't let his rough manners put you off．不要對他的粗魯態度不高興。
*I was very hungry but the smell of rotten eggs put me off．我非常餓，但臭雞蛋味使我倒胃口。
*I was rather put off by the shamelessness of his proposal．我對他的無恥建議深感不安。
5．move out to sea出海航行
*They put off in small boats to meet the coming ship．他們分乘小船出海去迎接那隻大船。
6．avoid推脫；迴避
*He put her off with the excuse that he had too much work to do．他以有很多工作要做為借口來搪塞她。
*They refused to have their demands put off．他們不許人家對他們的要求加以搪塞。
7．discourage sb．or cause sb．to lose interest in sth．使洩氣；阻止；勸阻
*I wanted to say something，but her face quite put me off．我本來要說幾句，但看到她的神情，又沒有勇氣開口了。
8．let or make sb．get out of a vehicle讓人下車
*Ask the conductor to put you off at the next stop．告訴售票員在下一站讓你下車。
9．get rid of丟棄；拋掉
*He decided to put off all personal considerations and accept the task assigned to him．他決定拋棄一切個人打算，接受交給他的任務。
*He had put off all personal cares．他已擺脫了一切個人的煩惱。
10．send to sleep；anaesthetize使入睡；使麻醉
*This medicine will soon put you off．這種藥會使你迅速入睡。1．dress oneself in穿戴
*He put his coat on hurriedly and ran out of the house．他匆忙穿上外套，衝出了屋子。
2．turn on開
*He opened the door and put on the light．他開了門，打開了燈。
3．pretend假裝
*He was not really angry．He was putting it on．他並不真生氣，他是假裝的。
4．present（a performance）上演
*The actor put on a fine performance．這位演員的表演非常精彩。
*The senior class put on a dance．高年級學生舉行了一次舞會。
5．gain（weight）；increase增加（體重）；增添；上漲
*She put on a lot of weight last winter．去年冬天她體重增加了很多。
6．force acceptance of sth．on sb．強迫某人接收
*In those days various sorts of exorbitant taxes and miscellaneous levies were put on the people from time to time．那時候，不時有各種苛捐雜稅加在人民的身上。
*Why do you put the blame on me？你為什麼責怪我呢？
7．deceive欺騙
*I don't believe you；you are just putting me on．我不相信你，你不過是在騙我。
8．move forward（a clock or the hands of a clock）往前撥（鐘錶）
*He forgot to put the clock on last night．他昨晚忘了把鍾往前撥了。
*The English people will put on their clocks one hour for summer time the day after tomorrow．英國人後天實行夏令時間，將把鍾往前撥一小時。
9．bet or risk money on sth．下…賭注
*Richard put on＄5 and lost it all．理查德押了5美元，結果全輸了。pretend to be very grand擺架子
*She puts on airs all the time to try to inpress new acquaintances．她總是擺架子，以期給新結識的人留下印象。
*I'm tired of those who put on airs．我討厭擺架子的人。find exactly準確查出；找到
*The engineers couldn't put their fingers on the reason for the rocket's failure to orbit．工程師們查不出火箭沒能進入軌道的原因。make a strong resolution下決心
*I'll have to put my foot down and stop this nonsense．我將下決心阻止這種胡鬧。make a foolish remark or make an awkward mistake說錯或犯了令人困窘的錯誤
*You certainly put your foot into it when you told the teacher that you hated homework．你對老師說你討厭家庭作業，你這是犯了一個愚蠢的錯誤。1．extinguish（a fire）撲滅（火）；熄滅
*The fire brigade soon put out the fire．消防隊員很快就把火撲滅了。
*She put out the light and closed the door．她關掉燈，然後帶上了門。
2．force to leave逐出；趕走
*If you keep talking in class，I'll have to put you out．如果你上課再講話，我就把你趕出去。
*He put out the cat．他把貓趕了出去。
3．make angry使生氣
*He never compromises on matters of principle and doesn't care who he puts out．在原則問題上他從不妥協，不怕得罪人。
*She was so put out by the man's rudeness that she didn't know what to say．那個男子的無禮使她非常生氣，以致於不知該說什麼是好。
4．stretch out伸出
*It is rude to put out your tongue at people．對別人伸舌頭是不禮貌的。
*She put out her hand in welcome．她伸出手來歡迎。
5．set sail出航
*The ship put out to sea at dawn．這條船在黎明時啟航了。
6．publish；broadcast出版；廣播；發表
*For years he had put out a weekly newspaper．多年來他一直在出版一種週報。
*The government is about to put out a statement on its wages policy．政府將對工資政策發表聲明。
7．exert（strength，etc．）使出力量
*Let's put out all our strength to do it．讓我們全力以赴去做。
*Never had our supporters put out so much effort．支持我們的人從來沒有出過這麼大的力。
8．produce；generate；provide生產；產生；供應
*The company puts out 900 cars a week．這家公司一星期生產900輛汽車。
*The enging of a fighter puts out more than one thousand horsepower．一架戰鬥機的發動機輸出功率高達1千多匹馬力。
*This eatinghouse puts out meals at moderate prices．這家餐館供應廉價飯菜。
9．sprout new shoots，leaves，etc．，esp．of a tree or plant（植物）長出（芽、葉）
*The trees start putting out their fresh green shoots in the spring．春天，樹木開始長出鮮嫩的綠芽。
10．cause sb．to become unconscious使昏迷
*He put out his opponent in the seventh round．在第7回合中他把對手擊昏倒了。
*He was put out by acupunctural anaesthesia．針刺麻醉使他失去了知覺。
11．dislocate a part of the body使脫臼
*She fell down and put her shoulder out．她摔了一跤，把肩膀跌脫了臼。
*12．cause figures，results，calculations，etc．to be wrong or inaccurate使誤差
*The rise in transportation costs has really put our estimate out．運輸費的上漲使我們的預算產生了誤差。
*The final totals can have been put out by as much as five per cent．最後的總數可能誤差達百分之五。
13．inconvenience sb．麻煩（某人）；使某人不便
*You're not putting us out at all！On the contrary，we're glad to see you．你一點也沒打攪我們！相反，見到你我們真是很高興。
*It won't put us out a bit if we drive you home．我們開車送你回去，一點都不麻煩。
14．lend money to sb．in order to get interest on it放款；投資
*The banks have started putting out money to people wanting to buy their own houses．銀行已開始借款給那些想買房子的人。kill殺死
*The old dog was very sick，and Father had the animal doctor put him out of the way．那條老狗病得很厲害，父親就請獸醫把它弄死。
*Many patriots were put out of the way because of their opposition to the government．許多愛國者由於反對政府而被殺害了。1．（a boat，etc．）go across（船等）開到對面去
*The boat has put over to the other side of the harbour．小船已開到港口的對面去了。
2．postpone推遲
*The discussion of this problem will be put over to next week．這個問題將推遲到下周討論。
*The weekly meeting was put over because of the bad weather．周會因天氣不好而推遲了。
3．cause sth．or sb．to be accepted or understood表達思想；使受歡迎
*He wasn't elected because he didn't put his ideas over clearly enough．他沒有當選，因為他沒有把自己的主張說清楚。
*She has put herself over the audience．她博得了觀眾的歡迎。
4．deceive欺騙
*He is not the sort of man you can put something over on．他不是你能隨便騙得了的那種人。
*Mrs．Wang believed everything the antique dealer told her until she discovered that nothing he said was true．「He tried to put something over on me，」she said．王太太起先非常相信這個古玩商，後來發現他所說的全是假話。她說：「他騙了我。」1．mend修理
*The washing machine broke down again，so I called the repairman to see if he could put it right．洗衣機又壞了，我請修理人員看看能否把它修好。
2．correct糾正錯誤
*If I make a mistake when I read out the results，please put me right．我在宣讀結果時如果有誤，請幫我更正。
*She likes to put other people right，but will，never admit making an error herself．她喜歡找別人的錯，但從來都不承認自己有錯。
3．make sb．feel better使身體變好
*This medicine will quickly put you right after your illness．這藥會使你病後的身體很快恢復健康。criticize sb．for impolite boldness；deflate使（某人）不敢越軌；使（某人）守本分
*She was a teacher who could put an impolitely bold boy in his place with just a glance．她是個瞪一眼就能叫無禮的男生聽話的老師。
*If he dares to be impudent with me again，I'll put him in his place．要是他再敢對我無禮，我就要對他不客氣了。1．complete successfully順利完成
*He put through an important business deal yesterday．昨天他做成了一筆大生意。
*We can put this task through tomorrow．我們明天可以完成這項工作。
2．cause to pass or succeed使通過；使成功
*Ten U．S．senators helped to put the bill through Congress；the president was very grateful for this special support．10個美國參議員使這項議案在國會裡通過了，總統對此特殊的支持深表感激。
3．connect sb．by telephone接通電話
*Can you put me through to this number？你能替我接通這個電話嗎？1．submit a question，belief，proposal，etc．to sb．for consideration 提出（問題等）
*I would like to put a question to the speaker，if I may．如果可能的話，我很想向演講者提個問題。
*I put it to you，Minister，that unemployment will continue to rise．部長，我提請您注意，失業率將繼續上升。
2．ask sb．to decide sth．；resolve sth．by voting or discussing把…委託…表決
*May we put the proposal to the meeting？我們能把這個提議在會上表決嗎？
*The committee will put your proposal to a vote．委員會將把你的建議付諸表決。
3．subject sb．to a lot of worry，trouble，distress，etc．使遭受
*You can't imagine the trouble we've been put to by him．你很難想像他給我們帶來的麻煩。set sail；start a voyage啟航
*The captain said the ship would put to sea at six in the morning．船長說船於早晨6點啟航。assemble組裝
*It's easier to take a machine to pieces than to put it together again．拆卸機器比重新安裝要容易。
*He put the story together by asking lots of people what had happened．通過向許多人瞭解所發生的事，他把故事串連了起來。make effective use of；utilize well 充分利用；使用
*Smart businessmen put their money to use in the best investment．精明的商人把錢用在最賺錢的投資上。
*If you want to draw value from your education，put your study time to good use．如果你想從教育中得益，就要充分利用你的學習時間。1．build；construct建造；搭起
*They are putting up several new buildings in that block．他們正在那一街區建幾幢樓房。
*Several tents have been put up to accommodate the party．搭起了幾個帳篷來給這一行人住。
2．provide food and lodging for sb．為…提供食宿
*Yes，we can put you up for a night or two．是的，我們可以安排你住一兩夜。
*We shall be happy to put you up when you come to town next month．你們下個月到城裡來時我們將很樂意為你們提供膳宿。
*You're welcome to put up in my home for the night．歡迎你們在我家過夜。
*They put Frank up at a good hotel．他們安排弗蘭克住在一家很好的旅館裡。
3．preserve（food）；lay aside保存（食品）；把…擱置起來
*The fans have been put up for the winter．冬天人們把扇子收了起來。
*The farmers put up the apples in barrels．農民用桶保存蘋果。
4．provide（money needed）in advance預先提供（所需的錢）
*He promised to put up the money for the scheme．他許諾要為這項計劃提供資金。
*He is willing to put up money on the local team．他樂意把賭注下在本地球隊上。
5．offer for sale出售
*She put the house up for sale．她的這幢房子待售。
6．increase the price of sth．提高價格
*Universities have just put up their fees．大學剛提高了收費標準。
7．offer oneself as a candidate for an election參加競選
*He is putting up for Parliament next year．他準備明年參加議會選舉。
*Has your father been put up to serve on the committee？你父親已被選為委員會成員了嗎？
8．pack up包裝
*They usually put up six packs to a carton．他們通常把6包裝成1盒。
*They're busy putting fish up in barrels．他們正忙著裝魚入桶。
9．offer a struggle，resistance，defence，etc．進行鬥爭、抵抗等
*The militia put up a stout resistance．民兵進行了頑強的抵抗。
10．display；show顯示出；表現出
*I think he's only putting up a bluff．我想他不過是虛張聲勢。
11．place（a notice，etc．）so as to be seen張貼；公佈
*The names of the successful candidates will be put up on the College notice board．錄取名單將公佈在學院佈告欄裡。
12．put to the original place放回原處
When you have done with the book，please put it up in its place．書用完後，請放回原處。
13．put forward提出
*I'd like to put up an idea for your consideration．我想提個意見供你考慮。
14．make up sth．準備（飯菜）；配製（藥品）
*Would you be so kind as to put up a quick meal for me？勞駕來一份快餐好嗎？
*The druggist put up the medicine that the doctor had prescribed．藥劑師把醫生開的藥配製出來。1．encourage；entice唆使；鼓動
*They put me up to it！It wasn't my idea to make trouble．是他們煽動我鬧事的，這本不是我的主意。
*Older boys put us up to painting the statue red on Halloween．大些的男孩鼓動我們在萬聖節前將雕像漆成紅色。
2．offer sth．to sb．for consideration將…提交考慮
*Your idea is good；I'll put it up to the manager tomorrow．你的想法不錯，我明天提請經理考慮。suffer or bear patiently；tolerate 容忍
*I cannot put up with all this noise．我無法忍受這些噪音。
*I can't put up with their bad behavior any longer．我再也不能忍受他們的惡劣行為了。
*No longer able to put up with my toothache，I went to consult a dentist．我再也忍受不住牙痛，於是就去請牙科醫生診治。put-down
