*If you read between the lines，this letter is really a request for money．如果你細心體會一下，這封信實際上是要錢。
*Read between the lines，and you'll find out what's at the back of his mind．從字裡行間去體會他的言外之意，你就會發現他頭腦裡究竟在考慮什麼。give an interpretation to（a statement，a situation，etc．）；add more than is justified對（聲明、形勢等）加以解釋；自以為有某種含意
*He read into the statement a deep insult．他認為該聲明含有極大的侮辱。
*You are reading into the situation more than the facts warrant．你對形勢的估計比實際情況誇大了。
*Too much should not be read into the minister's statement；we can't expect a sudden easing of the situation．不要對部長的講話亂加解釋；我們不能指望形勢會突然緩和下來。
*Don't read things into what I say．不要對我講的話妄加解釋。expel from，or declare no longer to belong to（some organization）by proclamation of any kind宣佈除名；自（政黨等）逐出
