If you want to start a business now, you'll have to ~ with a harsh economic limate. 
如果你現在想創業,你就必須考慮到嚴苛的經濟環境
reckon without ?
忽視…,不考慮到…
How can we ~ without him?. 
我們怎能夠不考慮 [忽略] 他?
reckon without one's host→host1．trust信賴
*You can always reckon on me．你總是可以信賴我。
2．expect（sth．to happen）；base one's assumption on盼望（某事發生）；沒想到
*You can't reckon on seeing him．你不要指望能見到他。
*She didn't reckon on six dinner guests．她沒有預料來赴宴的客人會有6個。1．deal with對付；處理
*I have to reckon with many problems every day．我每天必須處理許多問題。
*I wouldn't like to reckon with the director when he is in a bad temper．主任脾氣不好時我不想與他打交道。 
2．consider carefully；include in consideration or planning認真考慮；考慮到
*We must reckon with all possible difficulties when we are considering the contract．在考慮合同時，我們要把所有可能的困難都估計到。
*Before you do anything，you must reckon with the danger that may arise there from．無論做什麼事，都必須估計到可能因此而產生的危險。
3．settle accounts or claims with 結算賬目；結賬
*It is a long time since I reckoned with the merchant．我已經很久沒有和那個商人結賬了。
4．punish懲罰
*All those who opposed us have now been reckoned with．所有反對我們的人都已受到了懲罰。reck.on.er
