我們無法說明這兩種現象之間的關係
2 使… 有親戚關係[to]
B
1 敘述,講 <事、經驗等> 
(
→ tell 【同義字】) 
He ~d a strange story. 
他說了一個奇怪的故事
2 [對人]敘述,說<事>[to]
Tom ~d some amusing stories about his classmates to his parents. 
湯姆把一些有關同學們的趣事說給他父母聽
<<不及物動詞>>
1 有關聯,有關係[to]
She won't notice anything but what ~s to herself. 
她只注意與自己有關之事
2 有關,指[to]
This report does not ~ to him. 
這項報告並不是在說他
3 與[他人]友好地相處, (互相) 合得來[to]
She does not ~ very well to her husband. 
她和丈夫感情不好
Strange to relate. 
說來奇怪1．tell sth．to sb．向…講述
*The children enjoyed relating their imaginary adventures to the visitors．孩子們喜歡向來客講述他們幻想中的冒險故事。
*He related to his students his adventures vividly．他向學生們生動地敘述了他的奇遇。
2．understand and like sth．理解並且喜歡
*I can't relate to loud modern music．我不喜歡喧鬧的現代音樂。
3．have a friendly and sympathetic relationship with sb．與…有友好和諧的關係
*This boss is best at relating to his employees．這位老闆很善於和他的僱員們相處。
*A good teacher is one who can relate to the students，not just one who has a lot of information．一個好老師應該能夠與學生和諧相處，而不僅僅是個知識的擁有者。
4．be concerned with；be in relationship with關於；涉及；與…有關
*He sent me a letter relating to his son's marriage．他給我來信講了關於他兒子的婚事。
*She is only concerned with things relating to herself．她只關心與她自己有關的事情。
*The unemployment figures are not necessarily related to the rise in prices．失業數字不一定與物價上漲有關。
5．connect by family與某人有親戚關係
*How are you related to her？你和她是什麼親戚關係？
*Jim is related to Jack；Jack is his uncle．吉姆和傑克是親戚，傑克是吉姆的叔叔。re.lat.ed
