岸邊巨瀾的回流; 激流1．steal；rob偷竊；搶劫
*He was caught ripping off books from the library．那個傢伙在圖書館偷書時被抓住了。
2．tear off with an effort用力撕掉
*He ripped the paper off．他用力把紙撕掉。
3．defraud；exploit詐騙；敲詐；剝削
*I don't shop at that small store any more；they're known for ripping off the customers whenever they get a chance．我再也不在那家小店買東西了，他們一有機會就敲詐顧客已經出了名了。
*We are really ripped off by the baker who gave us zero nutritional value for our money．我們確實上了那家麵包商的當，他用毫無營養價值的東西來騙我們的錢。

rip off
(俚)
1 倫竊
He was ~ped ~ by burglars. 
他被竊賊偷了
2 剝削; 敲詐; 詐欺
They were ~ped ~ by bakers. 
他們被麵包師傅騙了1．utter angrily， as with an oath or exclamation 憤然說出；詛咒
*He has a hot temper and is likely to rip out with unseemly language；you would do well not to say anything at all．他脾氣急躁，很可能破口說出不體面的話，你最好什麼都不說。
2 ．tear out with an effort 撕碎；拆除
*He ripped out the pockets of the coat．他撕掉了上衣的口袋。
*The criminals have ripped the telephone wires out，so we can't call the police．罪犯把電話線拉斷了，因此，我們無法給警察打電話。1． bring to recollection； recall回憶；追想
*He ripped up all he had done in the past．他回憶自己過去所做的一切。
2．tear up with an effort；vigorously renounce or tear up（a treaty，etc．）撕毀（條約等）
*He ripped up the documents．他把文件撕碎了。
*Whoever rips up the agreement will be condemned．不管誰撕毀協議都要受到譴責。
*rise in sb． 's opinion improve or go up in sb． 's estimation 獲得某人的重視或好評
*She has risen in my opinion．我對她的評價有所提高。Rip van Win.kle
