*Round off the corners of the table please．請把桌子的角刨成圓形。
*Take a piece of sand paper and round off the edges of the frame．拿一張砂紙把這個框架的邊擦光滑。
2．finfish off well；bring to completion，esp． in a fit manner圓滿結束；完成
*We rounded off the party by singing popular songs．我們唱著流行歌曲結束了晚會。
*Thry have rounded off their work and will write a detailed report．他們圓滿結束了工作並將寫出詳細的匯報。
*Their day's outing was rounded off with a visit to the theatre．他們到一家戲院看了一場戲，從而圓滿結束了這一天的外出遊玩。1．complete or perfect；finish very fully 完成；使圓滿；完全結束
*He rounded out his education by spending a year in Paris．他在巴黎住了一年，完成了學業。
*He needs only one or two more stamps to round out his collection of postwar Chinese stamps．他還需要一兩張郵票即可將戰後中國的郵票集全了。
*They intend to round out their work be fore presenting their final analysis．他們打算在全部工作完成之後再提出最終分析。
*The scheme was rounded out with suggestions from the veteran technicians．由於採納了經驗豐富的技術員的建議，這個計劃就更完善了。
2．fill out； become rounder使飽滿；使變圓；使胖起來
*She was very thin a fter her illness，but is rounding out nicely now．她病後很瘦，可是現在胖起來了。
*As she grew older，she rounded out in the right place．隨著年齡的增長，她的身材變得豐滿勻稱起來。
