(阿拉伯半島東南部內陸大沙漠,佔地約250,000平方哩; 亦稱Empty Quarter)1．（of a person） manage to exist；pass one's time with too much difficulty；live day to day in a more or less satisfactory but unexciting manner（指人）無太大困難地過活；馬馬虎虎度日；平平淡淡過日子
*With the money my mother earned we just managed to rub along．靠媽媽掙來的錢，我們馬馬虎虎地湊合著過日子。
*He is not a good student；he can only just rub along in class．他學習並不好，在班上只是勉強過得去。*「How are you getting on nowadays？」「Oh，just rubbing along．」「你近來好嗎？」「哦，馬馬虎虎過得去。」
2．（of two or more persons）live without quarrelling，etc．和諧相處
*We manage to rub along together．我們相處得還算不錯。
*Except for the first two months they rubbed along quite happily．除了頭兩個月以外，他們相處得頗為融洽。1．clean and dry the body（of an animal or person） by rubbing擦乾
*The athletes rubbed themselves down with coarse towels．運動員們用粗毛巾擦身。
*She rubbed the horse down．她把馬梳洗乾淨。
2．rub and press with the fingers on the body（of a person）to loosen muscles or prevent stiffness；massage按摩（人體）使肌肉放鬆
*The athletes were rubbed down after the training．訓練結束後，運動員們都要按摩一下，以放鬆肌肉。
3．reduce by friction or abrasion ；take off roughness磨光；磨平
*He rubbed the chair down with sandpaper．他用砂紙把椅子磨光。
4．search sb．by passing the hand all over the body and limbs遍身搜查（某人）；對（某人）搜身
*The policeman rubbed down the suspicious stranger，who turned out to be a spy．警察搜查了那個陌生人的全身，原來他是個間諜。keep talking about sth．that another person wants to forget反覆講別人不願聽的事
*「I am really surprised that you failed exams．」「OK，don't rub it in！」「我沒想到你會考試不及格。」「好啦，別再提啦！」1．remove with a rubber； erase擦掉
*He rubbed off the finger mark from the painting．他擦去了畫上的指印。
*He rubbed off what he had written and started again．他把他所寫的擦掉後又開始重寫。
2．appear or cause to appear less bright，remarkable or praiseworthy （使）減色With the passing of time some of the glitter of the champion's success has rubbed off．隨著時間的推移，這位冠軍的成績已不那麼驚人了。
3．stick to sth．touched（接觸時）粘住
*His dress touched the door that the worker was painting，and some paint rubbed off on it．他的衣服碰到了工人正在油漆的那扇門，沾上了油漆。
*Don't touch that charcoal；it will rub off．不要碰那煤炭，會弄髒你的手。
4．pass to sb． near as if by touching傳給別人
*We all hoped he would stay with us longer so that some of his good qualities might rub off on us．我們都希望他能和我們在一起多呆些日子，這樣我們可以從他身上學到一些優秀品質。
*Mr．Li is very lucky； I wish some of his luck would rub off on me．李先生運氣真好，我希望他的運氣能傳些給我。1．destroy completely；kill；eliminate毀滅；殺死；消除
*The gangsters rubbed out four policemen before they were caught．匪徒們在被捕前打死了4名警察。
*The city was rubbed out in the earthquake．這座城市在地震中毀滅了。
2．erase ； obliterate擦去；把…磨掉
*The ink won't rub out．這種墨水擦不掉。
*He rubbed out his name and wrote his father's name in its place．他擦去他自己的名字，寫上了他父親的名字。
*rub shoulders/elbows be in the same place（with others）；meet and mix 互相接觸；在一起；與他人往來
*We don't rub shoulders with such arrogant people．我們不和這種狂妄自大的人來往。1．polish by rubbing 擦光；把…磨光滑
*When you have put the polish on the silver，rub it up with a clean dry cloth．在銀器上打上擦光劑後，要用塊乾淨的干布把它擦亮。
*He rubbed the vase up until it shone．他把花瓶擦得錚亮。
2．excite；rouse to action； revive or refresh one's knowledge of 激起；喚起；複習
*Your French needs rubbing up．你的法語需要複習一下。
*I cannot find a recipe which I cut from the paper ；I must rub up my memory and recall where I laid it．我從報上剪下來的一張配方找不到了，我得好好想想放在哪裡了。1． rub against sth．in passing擦上；相磨擦
*Look at the spot on your skirt！You must have rubbed up against wet paint somewhere看看你裙子上的髒斑！你一定是在什麼地方碰上沒干的油漆了。
2．meet or come into contact with by accident 偶然相遇
*You occasionally rub up against most interesting people in unlikely Places．有時在意想不到的地方會遇上很有趣的人。rub-a-dub
