sail in
(1) 進港
(2)(口語)熱烈地展開議論 [活動 (等) ] 
sail near [close to] the wind→ wind1． enter a port進港
*It was on June 3rd that our ship sailed in．我們的船是6月3日進港的。
2．（ladies，etc．）enter in a stately or dignified manner（貴婦人）儀態萬方地走進
*They were talking of Mrs．Swift when she sailed in．他們正談論著斯威夫特夫人時，她風姿綽約地走了進來。
3．take decisive action 採取斷然行動
*He sailed in and finished the job．他一鼓作氣，完成了任務。
4．enter an argument or dispute energetically 起勁地參加爭論
*Just as we thought the heat had gone out the discussion，Mrs．Hughes sailed in．在我們感到討論陷入冷場時，休斯太太興致勃勃地加入了討論。1．enter in a dignified or stately manner 大搖大擺地走進來；儀態萬方地走進來
*She sailed into the hall with her head held high．她昂著頭傲慢地走進了大廳。
2．attack with great strength 猛擊
*George grabbed a stick and sailed into the dog．喬治抓過一根棍子，猛打那條狗。
3．criticize hard 嚴厲批評
*I could hear Mother sailing into the children for bringing mud into the house．我聽見母親在狠狠責備孩子們把泥帶進了屋裡。sail lizard
