[sєv; sәiv]
<<介係詞>>
(文語)除…以外 (except) 
the last ~ one 
倒數第二
We all went ~ him. 
除他以外我們全去
The store is open ~ on Sundays. 
那一家店舖除星期日以外都營業
save for ?
(文語)除了… (except for) 
conj
1 [~ that] (文語)除…外
There was not a sound ~ that from time to time a bird called. 
除了偶而有鳥叫聲外,一點聲音也沒有
2 (古)除非…save one's good reputation，popu larity，or dignity when sth．has happened or may happen to hurt sb．保全名譽；保全面子
*They gave him a choice of resign ing，to save face．他們給了他自動辭職的機會以保全他的面子。
*I think it would be better if you admitted your mistake instead of trying to save face．我認為你還是認錯的好，不要死要面子了。keep silent because talking will not help 省點力氣別開口；免開口
*What you are saying will not make any difference to me，so you may as well keep your breath．你所說的對我不會產生任何作用，所以你最好是免開尊口。
*Save your breath．There is no chance that he will agree． 省點力氣吧，他是決不可能同意的。save from danger or trouble 免於遭殃；使擺脫困境
*He's saved his neck，thanks to his counsel，but people will always suspect him．多虧他的辯護律師才使他免受絞刑，但人們將永遠以懷疑的眼光來看他。
*You really saved my neck by help ing me check up on many details in my paper；otherwise I couldn't have got the work done in time．你替我核對了這篇論文中的許多具體細節，真是幫了個大忙，否則我根本不可能及時完成這篇論文。bring about victory or success，esp．when defeat is likely 反敗為勝；轉危為安
*The forest fire was nearly out of control when suddenly it rained heavily and saved the day．森林火災幾乎無法控制，但一場瓢潑大雨，把它澆滅了。
*They were ready to retreat，but re inforcements arrived in time and saved the situation．他們正準備撤退時，增援部隊及時趕到，一下扭轉了局勢。keep up for future use 儲存
*Tom was saving up for a new bicy cle．湯姆在攢錢準備買輛新自行車。
*You should save some money up，instead of spending it all．你應該存一些錢，不要全花光。save-all
