see
[si; si:]
(saw[s; s:]; seen[sin; si:n]) )
<<及物動詞>>
1 (指映在視覺上的) 看見
a. <人等>看見,看得見
I ~ some people in the garden. 
我看見一些人在花園裡
Can you ~ the dog over there?. 
你看得見在那兒的那條狗嗎?
b. 看見<某人><做…>
(
→ 1 c{用法}) 
I saw him enter the room. 
我看見他進入房間
c. 看見<某人><在做…>
I can ~ some little fish swimming about in the water. 
我看到一些小魚在水裡游來游去
She was seen walking along the street with a gentleman. 
有人看見她和一位男士沿著街道走
d. 看見 <某人、事、物> <被…>
Have you ever seen a man murdered?. 
你見過人被殺害嗎?
I have twice seen a bribery overlooked. 
我曾目睹兩次賄賂被放過(未加追究)
e. 參照,參閱
(略作 s.)
S~ p. 56. 
參照第五十六頁
2 仔細看
a. 弄清楚,查明
Let me ~ your passport. 
讓我看一看你的護照
b. 仔細看,看清楚
S~ how I operate this machine. 
仔細看我如何操作這部機器
S~ how to operate the machine before turning it on. 
開電源以前先弄清楚這部機器如何操作
Go and ~ if the door is locked. 
去看看門是否上了鎖
3 看了…而知道
a. (在報紙上等) 看到,讀到
I saw the report of his death in today's newspaper. 
我在今天的報紙上看到他死亡的報導
b. 看到,知道<…事>; (在報紙上) 讀到<…事>
I ~ that you have given up smoking. 
我知道你已戒煙了
I saw in the paper that another earthquake had occurred in Italy. 
我從報紙上得知義大利又發生了另一次地震
4 瞭解
a. 明白,瞭解,發覺
Do you ~ the point of my remark?. 
你明白我所說的重點嗎?
I ~ what you mean. 
我明白你的意思
b. 知道 <…的事> 
He didn't ~ that she was mistaken. 
他並不知道她弄錯了
c. (文語)知道…<是…>
I saw him to be a liar. 
我知道他是個扯謊者
d. 知道
I don't ~ why he is absent. 
我不知道他為什麼缺席
I don't ~ how to avert it. 
我不知道如何去避免它
5 
a. 遊覽,參觀 <名勝等> 
~ the sights 
遊覽名勝
Have you ever seen Rome?. 
你遊覽過羅馬嗎?
b. 看,觀賞 <戲劇、電影等> 
~ a movie 
看電影
I'm going to ~ a baseball game. 
我要去看棒球賽
c. 看 <電視、節目> 
Did you ~ the baseball game on TV yesterday?. 
你昨天看了電視轉播的棒球賽沒有?
6 
a. 會見<某人>,和<某人>見面
I am glad [pleased] to ~ you. = It's nice to ~ you. 
我很高興見到你; 幸會
→ see much [nothing,something] of,see you (later,soon) .
b. 去會見<某人>,訪問,探望<某人>,看 <醫生> 
You'd better ~ a doctor at once. 
你最好立刻去看醫生
I'm ~ing my client today. 
我今天要和我的客戶見面
7 a. 送,護送<某人>
Let me ~ you home [to your car]. 
讓我 (護) 送你回家 [到你停車的地方] 
→see off (1),see out (1).
b. (幫助或加以留意等) 對<某人>照顧 [負責] 到底<through>
I'll ~ you through. 
我會幫你幫到底
c. 幫助<某人> [使度過…] [through]
Father is ~ing me through college. 
父親供我念大學
8 經歷過,遭遇到
He has seen a lot of life [the world]. 
他已經見過不少世面
(他已積有很多的人生經驗)
She has seen better days. 
她過去過得不錯
(現已落魄)
I have seen the time when it didn't rain for a month. 
一個月不下雨的日子我已經歷過
He will never ~ 50 again. (
口語)他年過五十
It was the worst heat wave that the nation ever seen. 
那是該國前所未有的最熱的熱浪
This coat has seen hard wear. 
這件上衣已經穿得很舊了
9(文語)
a. <在某時代、某地> 發生 <事件、事態等> 
The nineteenth century saw the Industrial Revolution. 
十九世紀發生了工業革命
The autumn saw a cruel recurrence of Spanish flu. 
那年秋天西班牙流行性感冒再度肆虐
b. <某時、某地> 使<某人>經歷…
The following day saw us flying northward. 
第二天我們向北飛行
10 a. 留意,注意,負責,查看
S~ that he does it properly. 
注意要他做好那件事
S~ that the window is shut. 
留意把窗戶關好
b. 注意,處理期使 <某人、事物> …
~ a thing done 
留意 [監督] 使人確實做某事
~ justice done 
期使正義伸張; 報復
11 a. 看,想,判斷
as I ~ it 
就我所見
I ~ things differently now. 
我現在對事情有不同的看法
b. 把 <某人、事物> 認為…視…<為…>
Some saw the affair as a tragedy. 
有些人把這件事視為一場悲劇
c. [常 will[would]~] (輕微的斥責) 希望<某人><被…>
I'll ~ him hanged [blowed, damned] (first). 
那種事我絕不干
I'll ~ him damned before I lend him money. 
我絕不借錢給他
12 a. 想像,預料
~ a catastrophe in the near future 
預料不久的將來1．make arrangements for 安排
*It is time for me to see about（cook ing）dinner．我該準備飯菜了。
*I think I'd better see about the tick ets．我看我最好去把車票的事辦一下。
2．consider further 進一步考慮
*There are all kinds of things that have to be seen about．有各種各樣的事情需要考慮。
*We cannot give an answer yet，but we shall see about it．我們現在還不能答覆，但我們會考慮的。look after 照顧
*John's mother told him to see after his younger brother．約翰的母親告訴他要照顧好弟弟。
*Who'll see after the house when you are gone？你外出時誰來替你照看房子？agree fully 完全一致
*Mother did not see eye to eye with Father on where we would go for our vacation．關於我們究竟到哪兒去度假，父母意見不一致。
*After repeated discussions，we be gan to see eye to eye on that matter．經過反覆討論，我們逐漸對那個問題取得了一致意見。1．study；investigate 研究；調查
*The director has promised to see in to the matter for us．主任已答應替我們調查此事。
2．know or understand the real na ture or meaning of 理解…的性質或意義；看破
*Suddenly the teacher saw into Linda's strange actions．突然間老師明白了琳達的古怪行為。
*It's difficult for me to see into his full meaning．我很難弄清他的全部意思。See of Rome
羅馬教廷go to say or wave goodbye to sb．upon his departure 為…送行
*Wives used to see their husbands off to work at the front door，but this is no longer common．妻子們過去習慣在門口目送丈夫們去上班，這在現在已不常見了。
*We saw the visitors off at the bus stop．我們把客人送到汽車站。
*When Marsha flew to Cleveland，Flo saw her off at the airport．瑪莎去克利夫蘭時，弗羅在機場為她送行。1．accompany to the door，etc．送…到門口
*Please don't get up，I'll see myself out．請不必起來，我自己能出去。
*Miss Jones will see you out of the building．瓊斯小姐將送你出這座大樓。
2．stay and witness（sth．）to the end 看完
*We saw out the long play．我們看完了那個長劇。
*Peter's assignment was hard but he saw it out to the end．彼得的作業很難，但他堅持把它做完。
3．last until the end of sth．幹到底；用到底；堅持到底
*We have enough food to see out the winter．我們的食物足夠過冬了。
*I am ninety on my next birthday，but I hope to see a few more years out yet．下次過生日我就滿90歲了，我希望再多活幾年。
*It may take a long time，perhaps five years，but we will see it out．這也許要花很長的時間，可能要5年吧，但我們要幹到底。inspect（a building，an estate，etc．）in order to buy，rent，etc．察看；視察
*I should not think of making an of fer for the house until I had seen over it．我要看過房子，才考慮給這房子出多少錢。
*I'd like to see over the house．我想檢查一下這房子。1．publish 出版；問世
*These famous letters first saw the light about fifty years ago，when they were discovered and pub lished．這些著名的信件大約是50年前問世的，那時候它們被發現並出版了。
2．understand or agree；accept sb．'s explanation or decision 領悟；接受別人的意見
*We've been telling him all along that he ought to make the store more attractive，I guess he's finally seen the light．我們一直對他說他應該把商店搞得更吸引人一些，我想他終於明白了這個道理。
*He wouldn't agree，no matter how hard we argued，but eventually he saw the light and changed his mind．不管我們怎麼講，他總是不同意，但後來終於領悟並改變了自己的主張。1．understand or not be deceived by（a trick）識破（詭計）；不上當
*Mother saw through Johnny's ex cuses not to go to bed on Christmas Eve．She knew he wanted to stay up to see Santa Claus．母親看穿了約翰尼在聖誕夜不睡覺的借口。她知道他是想等著看聖誕老人。
*We easily saw through the man and his lies．我們輕而易舉地看破了這人和他的謊言。
2．do until sth．is finished 做完（某事）
*Once Charles started a job，he saw it through until it was finished．查爾斯一旦開始一項工作，就要把它做完。
*Before I leave，I would like to see the project through．我要把這任務完成後再走。
3．help（sb．）through difficulty 幫助（某人）度過難關
*His business was about to fail，but his banker saw him through．他的生意行將失敗，但他的財東幫助他度過了難關。
*She was very upset when her hus band died but her friends saw her through．丈夫的去世使她非常難過，但她的朋友們幫她度過了悲傷時期。
4．be enough for or last 夠用
*This money will see us through the week．這筆錢夠我們用一個星期。
*I think we have enough bread to see us through the weekend．我看現有的麵包足夠我們吃到週末了。attend to or deal with 照料或處理
*While Donna bought the theatre tickets，I saw to the parking of the car．唐娜買戲票，我則負責停車。
*The telephone out of order again？Why，it was only last week that it was seen to．電話又出毛病了？嗨，上個星期剛剛找人看過。make sure；take the responsibility務必使；負責
*See to it that the door is safely locked．務必鎖好門。
*We saw to it that the child was fed and bathed．我們負責給孩子餵飯、洗澡。see-through
