sell
<<名詞>>
<<形容詞>>
<<代名詞>>
『蘇』=selfsell out
1 賣完; 完全脫手
This edition of the dictionary is sold out. 
本版字典已經賣完
2(俚)出賣; 背叛
He committed suicide rather than sell out to the enemy. 
他寧願自殺而沒有向敵人投降

1．sell all of 賣光
*The shop sold out all their shirts．商店賣完了所有的襯衫。
*The day after the blackout，most stores sold out their entire stock of flashlights within a few hours．停電後的這一天，大部分商店在幾個小時之內就賣光了他們所有庫存的手電筒。
*Tickets for the football match were sold out in two hours．足球比賽門票兩小時內就售完了。
2．be disloyal or unfaithful to 背叛
*He can't be trusted not to sell out his friends if he is in a position to make a profit．我們不要指望他在有利可圖的情況下不出賣朋友。1．sell one's major assets 變賣主要財產
*The new supermarket has been so successful that some small shop keepers have had to sell up．那家超級市場經營非常成功，使得一些小店主不得不歇業。
*After farming for over ten years in Britain he sold up and went abroad．他在英國務農10多年後，變賣財產出國去了。
2．sell sb．'s property for payment of debt 將某人的財產變賣抵債
*Old Williams went bankrupt，and was sold up by his creditors．老威廉斯破產了，他的全部財產被債權人變賣了。sell-off
