set
<<名詞>>
1 一連串之境況、事件等
2 (方塊舞中之) 基本對數,基本隊形1．begin 開始
*Benjamin Franklin set about learn ing the printer's trade at an early age．本傑明?富蘭克林早年就開始學習印刷術。
*I'll set about preparing supper．我去做晚飯。
2．attack 襲擊
*When I refused to give him mon ey，he set about me with a stick．我不給他錢，他就用棍子打我。
*They set about each other furious ly．他們使勁地扭打起來。1．balance against sth．用（某物）抵消
*Certain business losses can be set against taxes．有些經營損失可以用來抵稅。
2．oppose sth．firmly 堅決反對
*Mary's father was set against the marriage from the beginning．瑪麗的父親從一開始就堅決反對這樁婚事。
*All those who set themselves against the people will come to no good end．一切與人民為敵的人，都沒有好下場。1．reserve 留出；撥出
*They decided to set a day apart for the work．他們決定撥出一天的時間來幹這項工作。
2．make sb．or sth．special or dif ferent from others 使突出；使…不平常
*His intelligence set him apart from the other boys in his class．他的才華在班上的男孩中很突出。
*Her bright red hair sets her apart from her sisters．她頭髮緋紅，同姐妹們迥然不同。1．keep or choose（money or time） for some purpose 特意留出（錢或時間）
*The busy executive set a weekend aside for a small trip with his family．這位繁忙的官員騰出一個週末和家人一起作了一次短途旅行。
*Every month we tried to see aside a few dollars．每個月我們都設法積蓄幾美元。
2．pay no attention to；reject 不理睬；拒絕
*The complaint was set aside as of no importance．這個投訴被認為不重要，因而不被理睬。
*I'm afraid we must set aside your request fot more equipment．恐怕我們要拒絕你要求更多設備的申請了。
3．annul 廢止；宣告無效
*The Supreme Court set aside the decision of the lower courts．最高法院駁回了下級法院的判決。1．delay the progress of sth．延期；耽擱
*The snow this winter set back the building of our new house by two months．今冬的一場雪使得我們新房子的修建耽擱了兩個月。
*The harvest was set back by bad weather．由於天氣惡劣，收割推遲了。
2．put back 撥回；使回轉
*Let's set back the clock half an hour．咱們把鍾撥回半個小時。
*It's impossible to set back the clock of history．要使歷史車輪倒轉是辦不到的。
3．cost 花費
*Her new boots set her back 70 dol lars．她花了70美元買了雙靴子。
4．position well back 使縮進去
*The house is set back some distance from the street．這房子造得離街面有一段距離。set chisel
一種寬刃鑿刀1．let sb．out of a bus or other ve hicle 讓…下車
*The driver will set you down just outside our house．司機會送你到我們家門口的。
2．place；put down 把…放下
*She set down the tray on the table and went out．她把盤子放在桌上就出去了。
*Set down your bags and take a rest．把包放下來，歇一會兒吧。
3．write down 定下；記下
*I will set down the story as it was told to me．我將按我聽說的情況寫。
*He was good at setting his thoughts down on paper．他善於把自己的想法記錄在紙上。
4．consider；attribute 認為；把…歸因於
*He set her attitude down to shy ness．他把她的態度歸因於害羞。
*when he heard the man speak，he set him down as a fool．他聽了那個人講話後，認為他是個傻瓜。
*The failure was set down to bad planning．這次失敗是由於計劃不周全而造成的。see 看到；望到
*None of us had ever set eyes on a generator before．我們過去誰也沒有見過發電機。
*When she set eyes on the green hills，she felt deep excitement．當她見到了翠綠的小山時，感到異常激動。cause to burn；start a fire 使燃燒；點燃
*The sparks set fire to the carpet．火花燃著了地毯。
*NO one knows who set fire to the building．沒人知道是誰放火燒了那棟樓。arrive at；step into 進入；踏上
*From the moment you set foot in this house you've been grumbling－now what's wrong？你進屋後就一直在嘮叨，到底出了什麼事？
*Armstrong was the first man to set foot on the moon，in July 1969．阿姆斯特朗是第1個登上月球的人，時間是1969年7月。
*I left him，determined never to set foot in that house again．我離開了他，決心再也不進那屋了。1．explain exactly or clearly 闡明
*The President set forth his plans in a television talk．總統在電視講話中闡明了他的計劃。
*She willingly set forth her opi nions．她主動提出了她的意見。
2．start to go somewhere 出發
*The troops set forth on their tenmile hike early．部隊一大早就進行10英里的行軍去了。1．promote 推動
*Their enterprise was set forward by the increase of capital．資本的增加促進了他們企業的發展。
2．put forward 提出；宣佈
*He set forward his proposition in no uncertain terms．他毫不含糊地提出了自己的建議。
*The proposal she set forward is practicable．她提出的建議是可行的。
3．cause to indicate a later time 撥快
*He set his watch forward five min utes in order not to be late．為了不遲到，他把表撥快了5分鐘。release；give freedom 釋放；使獲自由
*Someone has slipped into the prison cell and set the prisoners free．有人溜進牢房，放走了犯人。
*Following the Civil War，the Southern slaves were set free．美國內戰後，南方奴隸獲得了解放。set function
『數』集合函數begin；start 開始
*Before the boat could reach shore， a storm had set in．小船還未靠岸，暴風雨就來了。
*The rainy season has set in．雨季開始了。
*He didn't keep the wound clean，so infection set in．由於沒有保持清潔，傷口開始發炎了。1．decorate through contrast 襯托
*The bright colors of the birds were set off by the white snow．白雪的襯托使這些鳥的顏色顯得更加鮮艷。
*A red flower needs to be set off by green leaves．紅花還需綠葉扶持。
2．balance 彌補
*Her great wealth，as he thought， set off her plain face．正如他所想的那樣，她的巨大財富彌補了她相貌平淡的不足。
*You can set the heavy expenses off against a probable increase in sa lary．薪水可能會增加，這樣你就能彌補開支的嚴重不足。
3．start to go 出發
*They set off for the West in a wagon．他們乘馬車去西部。
*Having said farewell to their friends，they set off for home．向朋友們告別後，他們動身回家。
4．cause to begin 引起
*A letter from home set off an at tack of homesickness．一封家信一下子喚起了他的思鄉之情。
*Don't mention Italy；you'll set him off on his holiday adventures again．不要提意大利，這會使他又談起他度假時的冒險經歷。
*She had stopped crying but his shouting set her off again．她已止住了哭，可他的叫喊使她又哭了起來。
5．cause to explode 使爆炸
*On July 4 we set off firecrackers in many places．7月4日這一天，我們在許多地方燃放爆竹。cause to burn 使燃燒；點燃
*Be careful with the candle，you will set those curtains on fire．當心蠟燭，你會把簾子燒著的。begin；cause to start 開始；使開始
*Plans have been set on foot for a party for Miss Jackson，because she is retiring．已經計劃為傑克遜小姐舉行一個聚會，因為她要退休了。1．want very much 很想要（或很想得到）
*He set his heart on that bike．他很想要那輛自行車。
2．hope very much to succeed in doing sth．很希望成功地做某事
*He set his heart on winning the race．他很希望能贏得這場比賽。pull all one's efforts into doing sth．專心於；一心想
*Nothing in the world is difficult for one who sets his mind to it．世上無難事，只怕有心人。
*If he sets his mind on doing some thing，it takes a lot to dissuade him．如果他下決心要做某事，要花很大努力才能說服他不去做。1．leave on a journey or voyage 啟程或啟航
*The Pilgrims set out for the New World．英國清教徒們啟航駛向「新大陸」。
*He will set out tomorrow on his journey to Beijing．他明天動身去北京。
2．attempt 試圖
*George set out to improve his pitch ing．喬治試圖提高他的投球技術。
*He set out to do a lot of things，but didn't succeed．他原打算做許多事，但都未成功。
3．plant in the ground 種植
*The gardener set out some tomato seedlings．這位園丁種植了些西紅柿苗。
4．display 陳列；佈置
*The goods are set out in the shop window．商品陳列在商店的櫥窗裡。
*It took them an hour to set out the room ready for the reception．他們花了一小時把房間佈置好，準備開招待會。
5．start to do sth．開始；著手
*They set out to perform the opera tion．他們開始動手術。
*They are setting out on a new ex periment．他們正著手進行一項新的試驗。
6．state；describe；define 陳述；敘述；說明
*He set out his ideas in simple Eng lish．他用簡單的英文表達了他的想法。
*He carefully set out all the facts．他仔細陳述了全部事實。set piece
<<可數名詞>>
1 花式煙火
2 (藝術、文學等流於固定型的) 一般化作品
3『足球』(英)定位進攻
(如角球 (corner kick) 、自由踢 (free kick) 等)
