<<可數名詞>>
『網球』決勝得分
(決定該場比賽勝利的關鍵性得分)begin a sea voyage 啟航
*The ship set sail for Europe．這船啟航駛往歐洲。set scene
<<可數名詞>>
舞台上之立體佈景set shot
<<可數名詞>>
『籃球』原地投籃
(罰球線外或從球場一隅之立穩長射)set theory
<<不可數名詞>>
『數學』集合論1．start to do sth．eagerly 積極地做某事
*They set to and cleaned the whole house in two hours．他們開始打掃屋子，兩個小時就打掃完了。
2．begin arguing or fighting 開始爭吵或打架
*The boys set to and the teacher could hardly separate them．男孩們打架了，老師簡直無法把他們分開。1．put upright；raise 豎立；升起
*They set up some stones as land marks．他們豎起一些石頭當界碑。
*An improvised platform was set up in the market square．集市場上搭起了一座臨時講台。
*They set up a notice on the wall．他們在牆上貼出一張通告。
2．construct；found 建立；設立；創立
*They set up a committee to investi gate the matter．他們成立了一個委員會來調查這件事。
*The school has set up a special class to help poor readers．學校專門辦了一個班來幫助閱讀能力差的學生。
*The government has set up a tri bunal to examine the problem．政府設置了專門法庭來審查這個問題。
3．achieve or establish 創造（紀錄等）
*The French team set up a new record at tonight's meeting．在今晚的會上法國隊創了一個新紀錄。
*They have set up a new record for the flight to Beijing．他們創造了一項飛往北京的飛行紀錄。
4．put forward；propose 提出；提議
*They have set up a new opinion re garding the case．他們對此事提出了一個新的意見。
*What defence did his counsel set up in the trial？審判時他的律師提出了什麼辯護？
5．extol as a model 樹立；推崇
*He is setting up an example by persisting in manual labour．他在堅持體力勞動方面樹立了榜樣。
6．help sb．start a business by pro viding the money required 幫助（某人）從事（某種）職業
*His father set him up in a restau rant．他父親幫他開了個飯店。
*Jack was set up in business by a rel ative．傑克在一個親戚的資助下開始經商。
7．make proud or vain 使居高自傲
*Don't be set up about your success．不要有了成就就驕傲自滿。
8．make a claim 自稱；自命為…
*He sets himself up as an expert in this field．他自認為是這個領域的專家。
*He set himself up to be a graduate of a medical school，but he was not．他自稱是醫科畢業生，其實不是。
9．cause or produce sth．引起；產生
*The heavy rain set up dangerous conditions on the motorway．大雨造成了公路上的危險狀況。
*Ocean tides are set up by the pull between the earth and the moon．海潮是地球與月球之間的引力引起的。
10．cause to be heard 大聲發出
*She set up a shout that might have frightened anyone．她扯開嗓子大喊了一聲，聲音之大真會把人嚇一跳。
11．make sb．feel healthier，hap pier，etc．使振作；使高興
*My holiday really set me up for the winter．我的休假確實讓我在冬天變得強壯。
The boy was set up by the unex pected praise．意想不到的表揚使這個男孩感到振奮。
12．make a gift of；treat 饋贈；請…客
*He set me up to a nice dinner that night．那天晚上他請我吃了一頓豐盛的晚飯。
13．put in type 排版；印刷
*He has set the text up．他把文稿排完了。
*The book will be published shortly；the type is being set up now．這本書正在排印，不久就可以出版。set-a.side
