c. <霧等>降[於…]; <寂靜、黑暗等> 籠罩[…]
[on, upon, over]
A strange calmness ~d upon her. 
她表現出一種奇異的平靜
Dusk was settling over the city. 
都市籠罩在漸暗的天色之中
6 a. <液體>澄清; <渣滓> 沉澱
The wine [coffee] will soon ~. 
葡萄酒 [咖啡] 很快就會澄清
b. <灰塵等>落,積[在…][on, upon, over]
Dust has ~d on the furniture. 
傢俱上積著灰塵
7 a. <天氣等>變穩定
b. <吵鬧、興奮等> 靜下來,變平靜
8 <地層、地基等> 下陷
settle one's affairs
(1) 處理工作
(2) (尤指完成遺書等) 妥善處理身邊的工作
settle down
(1)[~ oneself] (舒適地) 坐下
He ~d himself down into his chair. 
他 (舒適地) 坐在椅子上
(2) 使<人>安靜,使…平靜
She tried to ~ the baby down. 
她試著使嬰兒安靜
(3) 坐下
(4) 安心 [於新職業、生活等] [to]; 定居; 成家
~ down to a new life 
習慣於新生活而安定下來
All his daughters have married and ~d down. 
他所有的女兒都結了婚而且安定下來
(5) 穩定地開始,定心去做[…][to]
They quickly ~d down to business. 
他們很快地定下心來做生意
(6)<鳥等>棲息
(7)<船>在下沉,傾斜
(8)<霧等>籠罩[…][on, upon, over]
(9) 變安靜,靜下來
S~ down!. 
安靜!
settle in
遷入 (新居) 安頓下來
把<人>安頓於 (新居等) 
settle up
償還 [欠…的] 債,清帳[with]pay what one owes 同…算清賬
*He used to settle accounts with the grocer at the end of each month．他總是每月底同雜貨商結賬。1．have a regular place to live and a regular job；begin a normal，sta ble life 生活和工作安頓下來；安居樂業
*John will settle down after he gets a job and gets married．約翰在找到工作並且結婚以後才會安頓下來。
*Many people settle down in San Diego because of the fine weather．許多人在聖地亞哥安居下來，因為那兒的氣候宜人。
2．become calm，quiet or peaceful安靜下來
*The house settled down for the night after the children were put to bed．夜晚孩子們被安頓上床後，這所房子就平靜下來了。
*The children settled down when their teacher entered．老師進來以後，孩子們就安靜下來了。
3．begin to concentrate on 開始專心於
*There were so many distractions that we were unable to settle down to studying．有那麼多令人分心的事，我們無法安下心來學習。
4．sit or lie comfortably 舒服地坐著或躺著
*She settled down in the back of the car and fell asleep quickly．她舒服地坐在汽車後座上，很快就睡著了。accept sth．which is not as good as one hoped for 接受；滿足於
*She wanted to be a lawyer but she had to settle for being a secretary．她想當一名律師，但後來甘願當了名秘書。
*He is so keen to sell his houses that he is willing to settle for less than the asking price．他急於想出售他的房子，所以他願意接受低於開價的價格。move in and put things in order 遷入新居並安頓好
*You must come and see our new house when we've settled in．等我們安頓好了，你一定來看看我們的新居。
*They got into Dolon and settled in at an outoftheway inn．他們來到多倫，在一家偏僻的旅店裡住了下來。1．decide or agree on 決定或達成一致意見
*She wanted blue and I wanted yel low，so we settled on green．她要藍的，我要黃的，最後我們決定要綠的。
*I don't know what dress she finally settled on．我不知道她最後選定了什麼樣的衣服。
*We finally sttled on Greece for our holiday．我們最後決定去希臘度假。
2．land on 降落於
*The bird settled on the branch and folded its wings．鳥落在樹枝上，收起了翅膀。
3．give（money or property）for mally to sb．正式把（錢、財）給予
*She settled a small sum on each of her children．她給每個孩子一小筆錢。pay a bill or debt 結帳或付債
*He asked the waiter for the bill，and settled up．他向侍者要來了帳單，結了帳。
*You paid for the theatre tickets and the meal．I'd better settle up with you now．你付了戲票和飯錢，現在我們最好把帳結了。take revenge on 向…報復
*I'll settle with him one day for telling people I am a thief．我總有一天會向他報復的，因為他對別人說我是個小偷。set.tled
