<<可數名詞>>
1 
a. 搖動,搖一下
with a ~ of the head 
搖一搖頭(表示「不」的動作)
gshake down
1 搖落; 搖下
2 使安頓; 使安居
3 試驗
shake down a ship 
試航一艘船
4(俚)勒索; 敲詐
5(俚)搜查 (某人)

1．cause to fall by shaking 搖落
*He shook some pears down from the tree．他從樹上搖落下幾個梨子。
2．become used to a new place of work，way of living，etc．適應下來
*You'll soon shake down at the new post．你很快就會適應新的工作崗位的。
*The boy will soon shake down at his new school．孩子很快就會適應他的新學校。
3．take up temporary quarters；sleep 臨時寄宿；睡覺
*Let's spread the blankets on the floor；we can shake down on them for the night．我們在地板上鋪了幾條毯子，這樣就能在地鋪上過夜了。
*Let's shake down here．我們就睡這兒吧。1．remove by shaking 抖落
*He stamped his feet to shake the snow off his boots．他跺了跺腳，把靴子上的雪抖掉。
*The dog shook off the drops of water．那狗抖落掉身上的水珠。
2．escape from sb．逃脫
*After a threemile chase through the woods，he was able to shake off the police．他在樹林中被警察追了3英里，終於把他們甩掉了。
*Our pilot dived into a bank of cloud and shook off the enemy fighters．我們的飛行員駕機鑽入雲層，甩掉了敵人的戰鬥機。
3．free oneself from（trouble，ill ness）擺脫（麻煩、病）
*I can't seem to shake off this fever．這次發燒我似乎好不了。
*Only in this way can we shake off their evil influence．只有這樣我們才能擺脫掉他們的惡劣影響。
*She found it difficult to shake off this feeling．她感到很難擺脫這種情緒。1．shake as fully as possible 搖勻；搖松
*You must shake up the medicine each time before you take it．每次服藥前都必須把藥搖勻。
*Shake them all up together．把它們搖勻。
2．disturb；agitate 干擾；震動；震驚
*The notice about a cut in pay shook up everybody in the office．減薪的通知使辦公室裡人人憂心忡忡。
*The news shook him up a bit．那消息使他有點震驚。
3．rouse by shaking 激勵；使振作
*Shake yourself up，young man．振作起來，年輕人。
*I hope her closeness to failure in the exam will shake her up．我希望她這次考試幾乎失敗能使她清醒起來。shake-up
