shoot
[ɑut; ʃu:t]
《shit 的委婉語》<<感歎詞>>
(美口語)哇!可惡!哎呀!1．bring down by shooting 擊落
*They shot down three enemy planes in their first engagement．在第1次空戰中，他們擊落了3架敵飛機。
2．criticise and dismiss an idea，suggestion，etc．極嚴厲地批評
*The headmaster shot down my plan for making money for the school．校長極嚴厲地批評了我那為學校賺錢的計劃。
*Why did you shoot him down like that？你為何那麼嚴厲地批評他？emerge quickly and suddenly from somewhere 猛然出現
*Rice was shooting out into ears．稻子已經抽穗了。
*The snake shot out its tongue．蛇猛地伸出舌頭。
*He was shot out of the seat as the two cars collided．兩車相撞時，他被甩出了座位。1．grow rapidly 迅速成長
*When he was thirteen years old，Billy began to shoot up．貝利從13歲起，個子就開始猛長。
2．arise suddenly 突然升起
*As we watched，flames shot up from the roof of the house．我們看著看著，火焰突然從屋頂竄起來。
*Rents in that city have shot up in the last few months．最近幾個月那城市的房租又漲了。
3．shoot recklessly and hurt badly亂槍射傷（射壞）
*The gunfighters shot up the town．持槍者開槍掃射整個城鎮。shoot'emup
