廣告; 招貼; 海報lead in/out 領進（或領出）
*The usher showed us in to our seats．引座員領我們進去找到了座位。
*The guards showed the visitors out．警衛領著客人出去了。show jumping
<<不可數名詞>>
『馬術』超越障礙比賽Show Me State
為Missouri之別稱1．put out nicely for people 展出
*The Science Fair gave Julia a chance to show off her shell collec tion．科學博覽會使朱莉婭有機會展出她所收集的貝殼。
*He enjoys showing off his new car to people．他喜歡向人們顯示他的新車。
2．display to excess one's ability or possessions 炫耀
*Joe has not missed a chance to show off his muscles since that pretty girl moved in next door．自從那個漂亮的姑娘搬進隔壁以來，喬從未放棄過任何機會來炫耀自己健美的肌肉。show with direction 帶…參觀
*They were taken to the house and shown round．他們被領著四處參觀那座房子。
*If you are free on Wednesday，I'll be delighted to show you round the place．你要是星期三有空，我很樂意帶你去遊覽那個地方。show trial
公審1．make known the real truth about 使瞭解真相；揭露
*The man said that he was a mind reader，but he was shown up a fake．那人說他能知道別人在想什麼，但他實際上是一個騙子。
*All their deceptions have been shown up by their own deeds．他們的種種欺騙都被自己的行為揭穿了。
2．become or make easy to see 使顯露
*The detective put a chemical on the paper，and the fingerprints showed up．偵探在紙上塗了化學試劑，指紋就顯示了出來。
*The sun shows up the dirt on the windows．陽光下，窗戶上的污跡都顯露了出來。
3．appear；come 出席；到來
*We had agreed to meet at the gym，but Larry didn't show up．我們商量好在體育館見面，但拉裡沒有來。
*We thought that you were never going to show up．我們以為你永遠都不會露面了。
*He showed up an hour late．他來了，遲到了一小時。
4．make sb．feel shame 使…難堪
*When we go to dinner parties my husband always shows me up with the rude jokes he tells．每次我們去參加宴會，我丈夫總是開些粗俗的玩笑，使我很難堪。
*He showed his parents up rather badly．他給他父母丟盡了臉。
*My friend always shows me up by laughing too loudly in the theatre．我朋友總在電影院裡放聲大笑，使我很尷尬。show window
