(6) 使<人>坐起來
sit up and take notice
(口語)吃驚,興奮,害怕sit and do nothing懶洋洋地閒坐
*She sat around all day and watched me clean the house．她整天閒坐著看我打掃房子。
*Don't just sit about and dream！不要只是呆坐著夢想！1．relax and do nothing休息
*It's marvellous to be able to sit back after a day's hard work．一天辛勞工作後能坐下來休息休息真是太美妙了。
*Get on with the work；this is not time to sit back．幹活吧，這會兒可不是坐下來休息的時候。
2．be inactive；become a spectator 不採取行動；旁觀
*He's happy just to sit back and let others make the decision．他真樂意袖手旁觀而讓別人作決定。
*Do you expect me to sit back and do nothing？你希望我袖手旁觀什麼也不幹嗎？1．stay near；watch and care for 守護照料
*Mother sat by her sick baby all night．母親通宵在生病的嬰兒身邊照料。
2．observe but fail to act as needed 袖手旁觀
*Even when his daughter was in trouble，he just sat by and did not help．即使他女兒陷入困境時，他也袖手旁觀不予支援。
*Don't just sit idly by while the other children are all busy．別的孩子都正忙著，你不要閒著什麼也不幹。1．sit on a seat or resting place坐下
*After the gym class Jim was tired and was glad to sit down and rest．體育課結束後，吉姆很累，因此很高興能坐下來休息。
2．sit on the ground to express opposition靜坐反對
*All the students sat down and refused to leave the building．所有的學生都靜坐，拒絕離開大樓。
3．suffer without protest or complaint逆來順受
*I couldn't sit down any longer．我再也無法忍受下去了。1．take an examination應（考）；參加（考試）
*His teachers said he should sit for university．他老師都說，他應該參加高考。
*He sat for a scholarship and got one．他參加了爭取獎學金的考試，並得到了獎學金。
2．be a member of parliament for a certain place代表…在議會佔一個席位
*He sits for a town in Cambridgeshire．他是劍橋郡一個市鎮選區選出的議員。1．sit in a place，for a special purpose為某一特殊目的而坐在某處
*He sits in with the patients while the nurse has a rest．護士休息的時候，他坐在那兒照看病人。
2．replace臨時代替
*The president is ill tonight so the secretary will be sitting in for her as chairman at the meeting．主席今晚生病，因此秘書將代她主持會議。
3． demonstrate by sitting in a place坐某處示威
*The students have been sitting in for the last two weeks．上兩個星期學生一直在靜坐示威。
4．babysit替人臨時照看嬰孩
*When her son and daughterin一law went to the cinema，she had to sit in with their child．她兒子、兒媳去看電影時，她得替他們照看孩子。attend as a visitor or an observer 作為來訪客人參加
*The professor said I could sit in on his linguistics lectures．教授說我可以旁聽他的語言學課程。
*Our teacher was invited to sit in on the conference．我們的老師應邀列席會議。
*She sat in on the whole debate．整個辯論她都在場。1．continue to sit繼續坐著
*She sat on until someone agreed to help．她一直坐到有人同意幫忙為止。
2．delay taking action on sth．擱置；壓下
*They have been sitting on my job application for weeks．他們把我的求職申請壓了好幾個星期。
*For weeks they did nothing about my case；they just sat on it．他們好幾個星期拒不審理我的案子，他們就是拖。
3．serve as a member of當…的一個成員
*Mr． Brown sat on the jury at the trial．布朗先生擔任陪審員。
*He has been sitting on the English committee ever since he came to university．一進大學他就成了英語協會的一員。
4． quickly subdue sb．who behaves rudely or impertinently申斥；壓制
*Her brother sat on her firmly whenever she was too noisy or silly．每當她太吵或太蠢時，她哥哥都要訓斥她。
*The teacher sat on Jack as soon as he began showing off．傑克一開始賣弄小聰明，老師就馬上加以制止。1．remain seated during a dance坐著不跳舞
*I think I'll sit out the next dance；I'm tired．下一個舞我不想跳了，我很累。
2． stay until the end of（a play）看完（戲）
*I decided to sit out the rest of the film although I was not especially enjoying it， but my friends were．雖然我並不太喜歡這部電影，可是我的朋友們喜歡，因此我決定還是把它看完。
*It was a tedious show and very few people sat it out．那部電影冗長乏味，很少有人堅持看完的。
3． stay longer than比…留得久
*It was her turn to leave， but she decided to sit the other women out．該她走了，可她卻決定等其他婦女都走後再離開。
*I wonder which of the visitors will sit out the other．我不知道兩位客人中哪一位坐得更久。
4． sit out of doors坐在室外
*Isn't it nice when the sun is warm enough for us to sit out？太陽暖洋洋，我們坐到室外去不是很好嗎？watch or listen until sth． is finished看完或聽完
*Though he was busy，he sat through the performance of the play．儘管忙，他還是堅持看完這劇的演出。
*We had to sit through the first half of the film without the sound．電影的前半部分我們是在無聲中看完的。1．make no move or change坐著不動
*Mother told her little son to sit tight until she came back．母親告訴孩子坐著不要動，等她回來。
*Sit tight；I'll be ready to go in a few minutes．等等，我一會兒就走。
2．stick to one's opinion堅持意見
*I was unable to dissuade him． He is still sitting tight with regard to his opinion that he ought to leave his present job．我無法勸阻他，他仍然固執己見，要辭去他現在的工作。
*Both of them sat tight with their own arguments．他倆各執己見，互不相讓。1．move into a sitting position坐起身來
*Joe sat up when he heard the knock on his bedroom door．喬聽到有人敲寢室的門，就坐起身來。
*She sat the old man up in bed．她扶老人起來坐在床上。
2．stay awake instead of going to bed遲睡；熬夜
*Mrs．Jones will sit up until both of her daughters get home from the dance．瓊斯夫人要等到她兩個女兒跳舞回來後再休息。
*I'll be late tonight． Don't sit up for me．今晚我回來得遲，不要等我。
3． be surprised驚訝
*Janice really sat up when I told her the gossip about Tom．當我把有關湯姆的流言蜚語告訴詹妮絲時，她確實很驚訝。
*You should have seen them all sit up as soon as I mentioned money．你應該注意到，當我一提起錢的時候，他們個個都警覺了起來。1．be accepted by被接受（常用於否定句或疑問句中）
*Did your story sit with your mother？你編造的假話你母親相信嗎？
*Bob's poor sportsmanship does not sit well with the coach．鮑勃不守運動道德，教練對此很惱火。
2．nurse or attend sb． who is ill照看病人
*You go to bed for an hour；I'll sit with your mother while you are asleep．你去睡一小時，我來幫你照看你母親。sit-down strike
靜坐罷工
