slap down
(1) → v.t. 2 a
(2) 用力 [粗暴] 地壓制,制住
<<副詞>>
1 啪一聲地,用力地,猛然
hit a person ~ in the face 
啪一聲掌摑某人的臉
2 迎面地,正面地,直接地
run ~ into 
?與…撞個正著1． slam down砰地摔下
*A boy in uniform came into the shop， slapped a telegram down on the counter，and went out without waiting for a reply．一個穿制服的小伙子走進店舖，把一封電報啪地一聲放在櫃檯上，不等答話就走了。
2．firmly prevent sb．from doing sth．堅決阻止；斥責
*He soon slapped her down when she wanted to speak．她想說話時，他很快阻止了她。
*Anyone who speaks out of turn in the Old Man's presence is liable to be slapped down．誰要是在老闆面前隨隨便便說話都會遭到嚴厲訓斥。
*Any attempt at reform was quickly slapped down．進行改革的任何企圖都很快地遭到壓制。
3．reduce in stature or humiliate，as if by slapping滅…的威風；羞辱
*It's time someone slapped him down．該是殺殺他威風的時候了。1．an insult；a disappointment侮辱；失望
*The minister's decision was a slap in the face to those who had tried to change his mind．部長的決定等於是在那些企圖使他改變主意的人的臉上打了一記耳光。
*Susan thought it was a slap in the face when her boyfriend invited another girl to the dance．蘇珊認為她男友邀另一女孩去跳舞對她是一種侮辱。
2．insult；embarrass；make feel bad侮辱某人；使某人不快
*I don't want to slap her in the face by not coming to her party．我不想由於不參加她的晚會而使她掃興。slap-up
