[slIp; slip]
<<可數名詞>>
1 a. 細長片,紙片
a long narrow ~ of paper 
一條細長的紙片
b. 傳票,便條紙
2『園藝』插穗,插枝
3 (罕)瘦小的年輕人[of]
a (mere) ~ of a boy [girl] 
一個瘦削的男[女]孩1．leave quietly悄悄離開
*I'd like to slip away before the end of the meeting，so I'll sit at the back．我想在會議結束前溜走，因此我要坐在後排。
2．（of time） pass quickly（時間）過得很快
*The summer has simply slipped away，but we've had such fun！夏天就這麼過去了，可我們玩得真痛快！pass away quietly（時間）悄悄過去
*As the years slipped by，I thought less about her．隨著歲月的流逝，我越來越不想她了。
*The afternoon slipped by very pleasantly．一個下午很愉快地就過去了。slip carriage
(英)滑脫車廂
(火車過站不停時所滑脫之車廂)1． enter by sliding滑過
*The car turned on the wet road and slipped into the fence．汽車開上潮濕的路面，滑進了圍欄。
*As the door closes the catch slips into place．門一關上，門扣就自動扣緊。
*Be careful not to let errors slip into the proofs．注意不要讓校樣中出現差錯。
2．enter silently or secretly 悄悄溜進 I have to come late，so I'll slip into the room at the back if you will save me a place．我會來遲一點，如果你願意給我留個位子，我就從後面溜進屋去。
*Later，Mother slipped into the children's room to make sure they were all asleep．過了一會兒，母親悄悄走進孩子們的房間，看看他們睡著了沒有。
3．pass…into secretly悄悄把…放入
*She slipped a note into my hand when the teacher wasn't looking．老師沒注意看的時候，她把一張條子悄悄地塞進我的手裡。
*He slipped a coin into the old man's hand．他把一枚硬幣塞入老人手中。
4． put on quickly匆忙穿上
*After supper， he slipped into his overcoat and went out．一吃完晚飯，他就披上大衣，出去了。the mistake of writing sth． different from what one should or what one planned筆誤
*That was a slip of the pen，I meant to write September，not November．那是筆誤，我原意是要寫9月，不是11月。
*It was by a slip of the pen that his letter was addressed to Hanzhong Road instead of Hankou Road．由於筆誤，他的信寄到了漢中路而沒有寄到漢口路。the mistake of saying sth． one had not wanted or planned to say； an error of speech一時說錯；失言
*I didn't mind what he said， because I knew it was only a slip of the tongue．對他的話我並不介意，我知道他不過是一時說漏了嘴。
*She didn't mean to tell our secret；it was a slip of the lip．她無意洩漏我們的秘密，她是不小心說漏了嘴。1．fall off by sliding unintentionally不慎滑落
*I thought I was safe on the branch，until my foot slipped off and I fell to the ground．我本來認為我在樹枝上很安全，但沒想到我的腳滑了一下，摔到了地上。
*The blanket slipped off the bed．毯子從床上滑落下來。
2．leave quietly悄悄溜走
*Mary couldn't bear the party， so she slipped off while no one was looking．瑪麗不想再在晚會上呆下去，於是她趁沒人注意時溜走了。
*He slipped off without waiting for a reply．他不等答覆就溜走了。
3．remove（clothes） quickly急急脫掉（衣服）
*He slipped his coat off and jumped into the river to save the drowning child．他匆忙脫掉外套，跳入河中去搶救落水兒童。
*He slipped off his clothes and went into the bathroom．他迅速脫掉衣服走進浴室。put on（clothes，etc．） quickly迅速穿上
*She slipped her shoes on．她迅速穿上了鞋子。
*Slip your clothes on and come with me．快穿上衣服跟我走。slip ring
