a slowly increasing feeling of anger 漸漸的發怒
*The boys kept teasing John，and watched him do a slow burn．男孩們一直戲弄約翰，看他逐漸憤怒起來。
*Her slow burn ended when I explained everything that led to the misundersanding．我講明誤會的來由後，她臉上的慍色漸漸退去。（cause to）go more slowly than usual減速
*The road was slippery so Mr．Jones slowed down the car．路面太滑，於是瓊斯先生就放慢車速。
*There were signs at every curve in the road warning motorists to slow down．每個轉彎處都有要司機減速的標誌。
*You should slow down a bit and lead a less hectic life．你應該悠著點，過比較安靜的生活。
*He has slowed down a lot since his heart attack，自從心臟病發作以來，他行動遲緩多了。
*Their objections are slowing down the progress of the engotiations．由於他們的反對，談判進展緩慢。
*We should find some way to slow him down；he is taking on far too much work．我們必須設法讓他放鬆一點，他的工作太重了。stupid；dull愚笨
*He is somewhat slow in his wits． 他有點笨。slow match
