~.nessget rid of difficulties or problems 消除（困難）；排除障礙
*With a bit of effort，we will smooth away any problems we encounter．只要花一點努力，我們就能克服面臨的任何困難。
*Her touch seemed to smooth away all his problems．她的撫摸似乎消除了他所有的疑慮。
*The attendant smoothed away the slight irregularities in the running track．跑道稍有一點不平，勤務人員就給平整過來。smooth breathing
1 希臘文中表示不送氣母音之符號(')
2 不送氣母音smooth dogfish
星鯊
(學名 Mustela canis,產於美國大西洋海岸,身形小,背鰭前面無刺; 亦稱 smooth dog)1．make smooth把…弄平
*She smoothed her hair down．她把頭髮撫摸平整。
2．make calm； calm down使平靜；安靜下來
*She tried to smooth down his temper．她盡量使他心平氣和下來。
*I hope he can smooth the whole matter down．我希望他能使這件事完全平息下去。
*The sea gradually smoothed down．海面逐漸平靜下來。
*Affairs have smoothed down since the cause of trouble was removed．自從糾紛的起因消除後，事態就緩和下來了。smooth muscle
『解』平滑肌1． smooth until flat弄平
*Mother brushed off the breadcrumbs and smoothed out the cloth．母親把麵包屑刷掉，把桌布拉平。
*The child was told to fold up the quilt and smooth out the bedsheets，after he got up in the morning． 孩子被要求早上起床後，自己把被子疊好，把床單鋪平。
2．remove（difficulties，etc．）消除（困難等）
*She is good at smoothing these little problems out．她善於解決這些小問題。
*There are some technical problems to be smoothed out before we can fly．我們起飛前，還有一些技術問題要解決。make smooth；put right調停；解決；掩飾
*He was asked to smooth things over between them．他被請來給他們調解糾紛。
*Bill tried to smooth over his argument with Mary by making her laugh．比爾試圖逗瑪麗發笑，以緩和他倆之間的爭吵。smooth-faced
