<<副詞>>
啪噠 [啪,劈啪] 一聲地
<<感歎詞>>
(英)
1 相同!同點!
(玩紙牌的 snap 遊戲時,出現兩張同點紙牌時說的話)
2 (口語)一樣! 完全相同!1．grab eagerly急切地抓住（接受）
*She snapped at the chance of going to America．她急不可待地抓住了去美國的機會。
*He snapped at the offer I made him．他連忙接受了我提供給他的東西。
2．answer rudely無禮地回答
*Don't try to be friendly to him；you'll only be snapped at．對他不要客氣，他只會對你很無禮。
*She snapped at him when he asked her what she was going to do．當他問她要幹什麼去時，她厲聲回答了他。
3． make a biting movement towards對著…咬
*The dog snapped at the stranger．那狗朝著陌生人咬。
*The fish snapped at the bait．魚咬住了魚餌。snap bean
<<可數名詞>>
『植物』青豆; 菜豆snap fastener
(美)按扣snap link
彈簧扣snap lock
彈簧鎖show contempt for；show no respect for蔑視；漠視
*Don't snap your fingers at his proposal；I think it at least merits our consideration．不要小看他的建議，我認為至少值得我們考慮考慮。
*John snapped his fingers at the sign that said〞 Don't enter〞， and he went into the door．約翰漠視「不准進入」的牌子，進去了。change quickly from a bad habit，mood，or feeling to a better one擺脫某種精神狀態；打起精神來
*The coach told the lazy player to snap out of it．教練要這個懶惰的球員改變作風。snap roll
