快槍射擊1．take or buy sth．quickly and eagerly把…搶到手；爭購
*She snapped up a lot of bargains in the sales．在拍賣中她搶到了許多便宜貨。
*If you don't marry me soon， I'll be snapped up by somebody else！如果你還不快點娶我，我就會被別人搶走了！
2．interrupt sb． sharply搶白；突然打斷（某人）的話
*I don't mind a person criticizing me，but I do object to being snapped up in that fashion．人家批評我，我沒意見；可像那樣搶白我，我反對。
*The counsel snapped up the witness who had made a slight slip in his statement．當證人的證詞略有差錯時，律師就狠狠地打斷了他的話。snap-brim
