sort out
(1) → v.t
(2) 把…[從…中]分開,挑出[from]
~ out the sheep from the goats 
分開山羊和綿羊(區別善人與惡人)
She ~ed out her summer clothes. 
她挑出夏季衣服
(3) 歸納<想法等>; 改善<事態>
(4)(英口語)整理,整頓; 解決 <問題、糾紛等> 
(5)(英俚)嚴懲 [幹掉] <某人>rather；to some extent有點；在某種程度上
*I sort of thought this would happen．我有點兒覺得這件事會發生。1． arrange things neatly or into groups分類
*The child was sorting out the bricks into different colors．那孩子在把磚分成不同的顏色種類。
*These things will take some sorting out．這些東西要清理一陣子呢！
2．resolve an argument解決；澄清
*You will have to sort out your differences yourselves．你們得自己解決你們的分歧。
*You'd better send somebody over there to sort the situation out．你最好派個人去那兒把情況弄清。
3．organize整頓（人員等）
*He took just one month to sort out his new office and the secretarial staff．他僅用了一個月就整頓好了他的新辦公室及秘書人員。
*She told him to sort himself out or she would leave him．她告訴他把自己管好，否則她將離開他。
*The school was sorted out in a matter of two months．那所學校用了差不多兩個月的時間就整頓好了。
4． attack sb． either verbally or physically懲處；懲罰
*If you don't stop fighting， I shall come and sort you out．你們要是繼續打架，我就要出來懲治你們了。sort-out
