speak to?
(1) → v.i. 1 b
(2) → v.i. 2
(3) → v.i. 3a
(4) 在會議上等談[論]關於…
Next he rose to ~ to the matter. 
接著他站起來談論該問題
(5)(委婉語)申斥,忠告<某人>
(6)<事物>動<人>心弦
The music ~s to me. 
那音樂打動我的心
speak up
更大聲地說
speak well for?
<行為等>成為對<某人>的有利證據; 證明對…好
His work ~s well for him. 
他的工作足以證明他的優秀
speak well[ill]of ?
說…的好[壞]話; 稱讚 [誹謗] …
He is spoken well [ill] of by everybody. 
他受到大家的稱讚
to speak of
值得說 [一提] 的,重要的
That's nothing to ~ of. 
那不值得一提 [芝麻小事] 
She has no voice to ~ of. 
她沒有值得一提的嗓子; 她的聲音沒什麼特別talk about談及；談論
*We won't speak about the unfortunate period in your family history．我們不會談及你家的那段不幸歷史。1．support支持
*At the meeting John spoke for the change in the rules．約翰在會上支持改變規則。
*He was asked to speak for the motion that nuclear weapons should be abolished．他被要求支持廢除核武器的動議。
*Although most members of the committee spoke for the bill，a few still held different views．雖說委員會中的多數成員贊同這項議案，但還有一些人持不同看法。
2． act as a representative for sb．，so as to give his views代表…發表意見
*I speak for my wife as well as myself when I thank you all for your great kindness．我代表我妻子和我本人感謝你們大家的巨大幫助。
*Just be quiet a minute and let Johnspeak for himself．靜一會，讓約翰為他自己辯解。
*Have you got anyone to speak for you？你找到人代表你發言了嗎？
*What others think I do not know； I can only speak for myself．別人怎麼想我不知道，我只能代表我自己講話。
3．ask for索要
*The teacher was giving away some books? Fred and Charlie spoke for the same one．老師正在分發書，弗萊德和查理要的是同一本。
4．give an impression of留下…印象；證明；表明
*Facts speak for themselves．事實本身就是很好的說明。
*His patient nursing speaks for his comradeship．他的耐心護理足以說明他的同志情誼。
5． book or reserve訂購
*All the rooms in the hotel have been spoken for by the organizers of the conference．旅館所有的房間都被會議的組織者們預訂了。
*They have spoken for five tickets in the front row at the theatre．他們已預定了5張前排戲票。express a bad opinion of講…的壞活；貶損；中傷
*Never speak ill of people behind their backs．千萬別在背後說人家壞話。
*Don't speak ill of the dead．不要貶損死者。1．mention；talk about提及；談到
*The book speaks of the writer's childhood．這本書談到了作家的童年。
*He speaks very highly of the boy's behaviour．他高度讚揚那男孩的行為。
*In his lecture， he spoke of the increasing use of computers．他在演講中談及了計算機日益廣泛的使用。
2．suggest the idea of說明；表明
*This gift of money speaks of your generosity．你捐贈這筆錢說明你很慷慨。
3．be worth mentioning值得一提
*The town had no industry to speak of before liberation．解放前這個小鎮沒有工業可言。say openly what one thinks說心裡話；暢所欲言
*When we asked the students what they thought of the new plan， they spoke their minds freely．當我們徵求學生們對新計劃的意見時，他們都暢所欲言。
*John thought it was wrong to keep Jack out of the club and he spoke his mind about it．約翰坦率指出摒傑克於俱樂部門外是不對的。1． talk to對…說
*Don't speak to that rough boy．不要跟那個無禮的男孩講話。
*She sometimes blushes when spoken to in the street．當有人在街上跟她打招呼時，她有時會臉紅。
2． talk about談論
*We haven't much time； please speak to the subject．我們時間不多了，請談正題吧。
*I'll speak to that point later．我在後面會說到那一點。
3．scold責備；批評
*The boy was late again today；it's time you spoke to him．那男孩今天又遲到了，你該批評批評他了。
*I'll speak to him about his rudeness at the meeting．他在會上太不禮貌了，我非責備他不可。
4． be attractive to對…有吸引力
*I am afraid this kind of art doesn't really speak to me．恐怕這種藝術對我沒有吸引力。
*Great music speaks directly to the emotions．偉大的音樂能直接打動感情。1．speak in a loud or clear voice大聲而清楚地說
*The teacher told the shy boy to speak up．老師叫那個靦腆的男孩講得響一點。
*Would you please speak up，as we can't hear you？我們聽不清楚，請大聲點說，行嗎？
2．express one's opinion fearlessly大膽發表意見
*Ed spoke up against letting girls join the club．艾德反對讓女孩參加俱樂部。
3．say for sb．為某人辯護；替某人說好話
*Since he was a complete stranger in the town，there was no one to speak up for him when he was brought into court．因為他在這個鎮上是一個完全陌生的人，所以當他受到控告時，沒有人替他講好話。express a good opinion of稱讚
*Everyone that knows him speaks well of him．瞭解他的人都稱讚他。speak.easy
