在拼字比賽中擊敗1．read sth．very slowly and with difficulty緩慢而費力地讀
*He is eight now，but he still has to spell out nearly everything he reads．他已8歲了，可他看書的時候，還是要費力地才能把所看的東西讀出來。
*It took the boy an hour to spell out a page of French．那男孩花了1小時才吃力地讀完一頁法文。
2．explain sth．in a very clear and simple way清楚地說明；講清楚
*He is so stupid that you have to spell out the most basic things to him．他真笨，連最基本的東西都得給他解釋。
*His speech spelt out the Government's plans for the army．他的演說清楚地講明了政府對軍隊的計劃。
*Must I spell out ever ything to you？我有必要把每件事情都一五一十地跟你講嗎？
*I wish someone would spell proposals out for us．但願有人能給我們把這些建議講明白。spell.bind
