2．disperse；scatter分散；散佈
*The men spread out over a wide area．人們分散在一塊很寬闊的區域裡。
*The work has to be spread out over several weekends．這項工作不得不分散到幾個週末去做。
3．develop發展
*Our foreign trade is spreading out in all directions．我們的對外貿易正向各方面發展。
*A scene of prosperity spreads out before us．一幅欣欣向榮的景象展現在我們面前。1．cover；scatter over覆蓋；散佈於
*The water spread over the floor．水溢到了地板上。
*His interests now spread over several subjects．眼下他的興趣遍及好幾門學科。
2．（cause to）last for（a period of time）（使）持續（一段時間）
*Their friendship spread over many years．他們的友誼持續了許多年。
*The grammar lectures spread over into the next term語法課延續到下個學期。
*You don't need to pay back the money you borrowed all at once；the repayment can be spread over a number of years．你借的錢不用一次全部還清，可以分幾年償還。spread-eagle
