<<可數名詞>>
(美口語)公平而正直的人pay sb．money that one owes結帳；付帳
*Will you square up with the waiter while I go and get the car？我去把車開過來，你來和侍者結帳好嗎？
*Let's square up，how much is the bill？我們結帳吧，帳單金額多少？1．stand as if ready to fight sb．擺好架勢
*The boys squared up to each other，but the teacher stopped them．男孩們擺好架勢準備打架，但老師制止了他們。
*The fighters squared up and began to trade blows．拳擊手面對面站好，接著就開始對擊。
2．acknowledge or accept misfortune in a courageous way勇於面對
*He squared up to the possibility of losing his job．他正視失業的可能性。
*The little boy squared up to his tormentors．小男孩勇敢地面對折磨他的人。1．agree with與…一致（或協調）
*His actions do not square with his principles．他的行為與他的原則不一致。
*His theory squares with the facts．他的理論與事實相符。
2．finish paying sth．付清…的帳
*I should be able to square with you at the end of the month．我在月底就能付清你的帳。
3．arrange（things）with sb．與…把…安排好
*Can you square things with the director so that the worker won't be punished for his accidental damage？你與主任商量一下，不要使這個造成意外損失的工作人員受到處罰，行嗎？square yard
