Who ~s to gain by his death?. 
誰會因他的死亡而得到好處呢?
5 a. 保持have a possibility or opportunity可能；可能獲得
*Weak and lame in one leg，Tom never stood a chance of getting that job．身體較弱，一條腿又拐的湯姆永遠不可能找到那份工作。
*We stand a good chance of seeing Mary at the party．我們很有可能在晚會上見到瑪麗。1．（cause to）lean or take a position against倚靠著
*The ladder stood against the wall，making it easy for thieves to enter the house．椅子靠在牆上，這使小偷很容易就能進入屋子。
2．oppose反對
*I stand against all forms of cruelty，especially cruelty to children．我反對各種形式的殘暴行為，尤其是對兒童的摧殘。stand out of the way站到一邊
*The crowd were asked to stand aside to let the players go in．人群被要求站到一邊讓運動員們進去。
*He never stands aside when he is needed to lend a helping hand．無論什麼時候需要他幫助，他從不袖手旁觀。1．stand to the rear向後退
*Stand back and let the car pass．退後一點，好讓汽車開過去。
*The policeman asked the spectators to stand well back．警察要求圍觀者靠後站。
2．be situated some distance from sth．位於後一點的地方
*The house stands back from the main rood．那房子離幹道有一段距離。
3．distance or detach oneself from sth．退讓；擺脫
*Sometimes an administrator must stand back from daytoday business to grasp the wider pattern of events．有時一個行政管理人員必須擺脫日常事務以便掌握大局。1．be close beside or near緊靠在旁邊
*Mary could not tell Jane the secret with her little brother standing by．瑪麗不能把秘密告訴簡，因為她的弟弟當時站在旁邊。
*The house stands by the river．房屋位於河邊。
2．watch sth．and do nothing袖手旁觀
*He could not stand by and watch the boy being beaten．他不能袖手旁觀孩子被打。
*Don't just stand by．Can't you lend a hand？別袖手旁觀，你不能幫一下忙嗎？
3．be near；wait to do sth．when needed在附近等待做某事；準備行動
*The policeman in the patrol car radioed the station about the robbery，and stood by for orders．巡邏車裡的警察用無線電向總部報告有關搶劫案的情況，然後等待行動命令。
4．follow or keep（one's promise）信守（諾言）
*He is a boy who always stands by his promises．他是個信守諾言的男孩。
*I stand by every word I said．我信守我說的每一句話。
5．be loyal to；support忠於；支持He is the sort of person who will always stand by a friend．他是那種永遠忠實於朋友的人。
*When three big boys attacked Bill，Ed stood by him．當3個大男孩襲擊比爾時，艾德幫助了他。1．leave the witness box in a court of law離開證人席
*If there are no more questions，the witness may now stand domn．沒有更多問題的話，證人可以退席了。
*He asked the witness to stand down．他要求證人離席。
2．withdraw from sth．，esp．in favor of sb．else退出競爭或競賽
*He stood down as a candidate because he felt a younger man would be more suitable．他退出了競選，因為他覺得年紀輕一點的人更合適。
*I'm not going to stand down for him．我不打算給他讓位。1．represent；mean象徵；代表；意指
*The letters「U．S．A．」stand for 「United States of America」．字母U．S．A．表示美利堅合眾國。
*I hate the woman and everything she stands for．我恨那個女人以及她所代表的一切東西。
2．speak in favor of sth．支持
*John always stands for what is right．約翰總是支持正確的事。
*We stand for equality among all nations，big or small．我們主張大小國家一律平等。
3．try to be elected for競選
*Three men from London are standing for Parliament．3 位倫敦人參加議會競選。
*She's standing for governor in the next election．她準備參加競選下一任州長。
4．permit；tolerate允許；容忍
*The teacher will not stand for fooling in the classroom．老師不允許在教室裡開玩笑。
*I will not stand for behavior of that kind in my house．我不允許在我家出現那種行為。
*She stands for a lot of abuse from those children．她忍受了那些孩子的許多辱罵。stand in
(拍影片時在燈光等佈置好以前) 代替演員站好位置

take sb．'s place or job for a short time代替
*she often stands in before a scene is being fimed．在正式拍攝一個場景前，她經常充當演員的替身。
*He said be would stand in for me any time．他說他隨時都願意來替代我。
*I'm standing in for the secretary while she is sick．秘書生病了，我在頂她的位置。line up排隊
*The children stood in line until the teacher said they could move．孩子們列隊站著，直到老師說他們可以走動了才解散。1．be in conspiracy with；go shares with與…合謀；同…分擔
*He stands in with those people．他跟那些人勾結。
*Let me stand in with you if it is expensive．如果貴的話，我來同你分擔。
*The politicians stand in with the saloonkeepers．政客與酒吧老闆有勾結。
2．be on good terms with和…友好
*John stands in well with the teacher．約翰和老師相處得很好。stand off
1 疏遠; 不親近; 遠離
2 離岸駛行
3 暫時解雇
4 避開 (債主、攻擊者等) ; 擋開

1．stay apart不靠近；呆在遠處．
*At parties Mr．Jones goes around talking to everyone but Mrs．Jones is shy and stands off．晚會上瓊斯先生走來走去與大家交談，可瓊斯夫人卻總是很靦腆地呆在一邊。
2．keep sb．or sth．from coming near or winning使…不能靠近；使…不能贏
*The other schools wanted to beat our team and win the championship，but our boys stood them all off．別的學校想擊敗我校球隊而奪取冠軍，但我校球員們把他們打得無一得逞。
3．dismiss，esp．for a short time，when there is no work to do解雇
*The management had to stand off a hundred men this week．資方本周不得不臨時解雇100個員工。
*If the slump continues，more will be stood off．如果繼續不景氣的話，就會有更多的人被解雇。stand oil
熟油 (一種致干性油,如亞麻子、桐或大豆等加熱但盡量減免氧化,使變濃,用於亮漆或油墨中) ; (用於平版印刷之) 凡立油depend on oneself獨立；不依賴別人
*After his father's death，Bob had to stand on his own feet and earn his own living．父親死後，鮑勃只得自立謀生。
*He offered to help me，but I said I would rather stand on my own feet．他提出幫我，但我說我寧願自己幹。stick to one's rights堅持自己的權利
*Although the teacher criticized her，she stood on her rights and argued back．儘管老師批評她，但她堅持自己的權利並予以反駁。1．stay and fight instead of running away堅守陣地
*The enemy attacked in great numbers but our men stood their ground．敵人大舉進攻，但我方戰士仍堅守陣地。
2．insist on one's opinion堅持自己的觀點
*John's friends said he was mistaken，but he stood his ground．約翰的朋友說他錯了，但他仍堅持自己的觀點。stand out
1 突出; 伸出
2 繼續抵抗; 支撐
The troops ~ against the enemy until their ammunition was exhausted. 
這支軍隊繼續抵抗敵人,直到彈藥援絕時
3 傑出; 顯著
She ~s ~ in a crowd. 
她在人群中很出眾
4『航海』 (離岸) 駛去
~ from the shore 
駛離海岸

1．project伸出；突出
*The pot has two handles standing out．這個壺有兩個突出的柄。
*Her pale face stood out in the lamplight．在燈光下，她臉色顯得特別蒼白。
2．be noticeable；outstanding引人注目
*They were all pretty，but she stood out among them．她們都很漂亮，但她卻特別突出。
*The primary colors stand out clearly from the others．主色襯著其它顏色特別醒目。
*He is a tall，distinguished looking man who stands out in any crowd．他是一個魁梧英俊的人，在任何人群中都很突出。
*It stands out a mile what has to be done．應該做什麼再也明顯不過了。
3．go on resisting or refuse to yield堅持抵抗或拒不妥協
*He stands out against all persuasion．他堅持不聽一切勸說。
*The soldiers stood out against the enemy as long as they could．戰士們全力抵抗敵人。
*The workers are standing out for higher wages and better conditions．工人們正在堅持爭取提高工資和改善生活條件。1．watch closely嚴密監視
*Ted's mother had to stand over him to get him to do his homework．泰德的母親得監督他做家庭作業。
*I hate having someone standing over me all the time．我討厭別人總監督我。
2．be held over for later action推遲處理
*The committee decided to let the proposal stand over until its next meeting?委員會決定把這項建議推遲到下次會議討論。
*The project is to stand over till next yedr．這項工程將延期到明年。1．prepare for action準備行動
*The troops were ordered to stand to in case of attack．為了防備敵人的襲擊，部隊已接到命令準備行動。
*He told his men to stand to．他告訴他的屬下準備行動。
2．keep（one's promise）信守（諾言）
*I'll stand to my promise and tell you everything about her．我會信守諾言，把她的情況全都告訴你。
*He always stands to his promise．他一貫遵守諾言。
3．stick to（one's post，duty，etc．）堅守（崗位、職責等）
*Everyone of us should stand to his duty．我們每一個人都應堅守自己的職責。
4．persist in；give support to堅持；支持
*We always stand to the oppressed nations．我們永遠站在被壓迫民族一邊。
*In defiance of public opinion he stood to his guns．他無視公眾輿論，固執己見。
*We stand to it that whatever work we do，we must do it well．我們認為，無論做什麼工作，都要把它做好。follow as a matter of course理所當然地（會）做
*If he supports the trade unions，then it stands to reason that he will vote Labour．如果他支持工會的話，那麼他理所當然會支持工黨。
*Joe is intelligent and studies hard；it stands to reason that he will pass the examination．喬既聰明又用功，他考試肯定會及格的。stand up
1 站起; 向上升起; (使) 豎立
~, please. 
請起立
2 站得住腳; 經得起磨損
a proof that would ~ in court 
在法庭上可站得住腳的證據
3『俗』不守與 (某人) 訂好的約會

1．rise to or be on one's feet起立
*Stand up when the judge enters the court．法官到庭時要起立致意。
*He told the men to stand up straight．他要那些人站直。
2．remain upright聳立；立起
*The church tower stands up very well．教堂的尖塔高高地聳立著。
*He stood the statue up in a corner．他把塑像豎在屋角。
3．withstand use or wear耐用（穿）
*De you think this dress material will stand up well under such conditions？你認為這種衣服料子在這樣的環境下是否很耐穿？
*The leather in these shoes will stand up much better than the leather in those you just tried on．這雙鞋子的皮質比你剛才試穿的那雙鞋的皮質要耐穿得多。
4．fail to appear；leave sb．waiting at an appointment失約
*Jim said he'd be at the station，but he stood me up．吉姆說他要去車站的，但他失約了。
*After waiting for two hours，John began to realize that Helen had stood him up．等了兩個小時以後，約翰開始意識到海倫失約了。
5．be accepted as true or be able to withstand an investigation站得住腳
*The charges against him will not stand up in court．對他的指控在法庭上將站不住腳。
*What is false can never stand up．假的東西總是站不住腳的。1．support；speak in favor of支持；替…說話
*Will you stand up for me？你會支持我嗎？
*When the boss wanted to dismiss Bill the other workers all stood up for him．當老闆要開除比爾時，其他工人全部為他說話。
2．defend；insist upon保護；堅持
*He always stands up for women's rights．他一貫維護婦女的權益。
*We must stand up for truth and correct mistakes．我們必須堅持真理，修正錯誤。1．resist；face抵抗；勇敢地面對；經受住
*Mary finds it difficult to stand up to her husband．瑪麗發現她很難對付得了她丈夫。
*Will the chair stand up to your weight？這椅子能吃得住你的重量嗎？
*They launched fierce attacks on Mary，but she stood up to this undaunted．他們對瑪麗進行了猛烈攻擊，但她毫不畏懼地頂住了。
2．match in quality同…相抗衡
*This doesn't stand up to the products of other firms．這種產品無法與其他公司的產品抗衡。stand-in
