What a ~ youbegin a return journey開始返回
*What time do we have to start back？我們必須什麼時候回去？
*They started back immediately when they got the news．他們聽到消息後就立即返回去了。1．begin a journey to a place出發
*When do you start for london？你何時動身去倫敦？
*He started for home at 6 p．m．他下午6時動身回家。
2．become a candidate for參加…的競選
*He has started for a seat in the National Assembly．他已開始競選國民大會代表。1．come out of quickly從…很快出來
*Blood started from the wound．血從傷口流出。
2．begin a journey from從…出發
*The climbers started from the village at daybreak．登山隊員們黎明前從那村莊出發了。1．set to work，etc．開始（工作等）
*She started in as a typist but soon became a secretary．開始她當打字員，不久就任秘書了。
*It started in to rain again．又下起雨來了。
*He started in drinking again．他又開始喝酒了。
2．give a first job to（使）開始任職
*The bank started him in as a clerk．這家銀行雇他先當辦事員。
3．begin to criticize，scold，etc．開始批評、責備等
*The boys were hardly settled in the classroom when the monitor started in on them for coming late．男孩們還沒在教室裡坐定，班長就開始責備他們，說他們來遲了。1．begin a journey；depart離開；出發
*Having missed the last bus，we had to start off walking．我們沒有趕上最後一班車，只得步行。
*We started out at 8 a．m．and arrived at7p．m．我們早上8點出發，下午7點到。
2．begin doing sth．開始Whatever you do，don't start off crying again．不管幹什麼，可別再哭了。
*The writer started out to write a novel．那位作家著手寫一部長篇小說。
*The dictionary starts off with the letter A．詞典是從字母A開始的。
*Don't let him Start off on his holiday stories again or we'll be here all night．不要讓他再談他的假期經歷，否則我們又得在這兒呆一個晚上。1．make a sudden movement due to surprise，alarm，pain，etc．驚跳起來
*A hare started up at his feet and raced off．有隻兔子突然從他腳邊一蹦就跑掉了。
*He started up from his seat．他一驚，從椅子上跳起身來。
2．begin to function開始運轉At six o'clock the moter started up．6點鐘馬達開動起來。
*The factory will start up tomorrow．工廠明天開工。
3．come into existence suddenly or unexpectedly突然出現
*Many difficulties have started up．一下子冒出了許多困難。
*He seemed to have started up from nowhere．他似乎是忽然從天而降。
4．begin a career，business，working life，etc．開始從事
*The merchant from New York was thinking of starting up in the fruit and vegetable trade．這個紐約商人正在考慮經營蔬菜水果業。
*He's thinking of starting up as a private consultant．他在考慮當一名私人顧問。begin with以…為開端
*In teaching English，we usually start with listening and speaking．學習英語我們往往從聽說開始。
*His illness started with a slight cough．他的病開始只是一點咳嗽。start-up
