<<名詞>>
~.erleave quietly and often secretly溜掉
*He stole away while everyone else was watching the film．別人都在全神貫注看電影時，他悄悄溜走了。
*The enemy stole away under cover of night．敵人趁夜黑逃遁。
*Time stole away．時問不知不覺地過去了。walk into quietly and secretly偷偷進入
*He stole into the room while I was writing a letter．我寫信時，他悄悄地進了房間。
*The thief stealthily stole into the house．小偷悄悄地潛入房子。leave silently and secretly偷偷走開
*Jim stole off without anyone seeing him．吉姆偷偷地走開了，誰也沒看見。slowly and quietly take hold of不知不覺地襲來；悄悄地呈現
*A feeling of happiness stole over the girl when she thought about the days ahead．當女孩想到未來的日子時，臉上不禁露出了一種幸福感。
*A smile stole over his face．他臉上隱隱現出笑容。
*Mist stole over the valley．霧漸漸瀰漫了整個山谷。do or say sth．that sb．has planned to do or say先人一著
*John announced the news before Peter had a chance，stealing his thunder．約翰在彼得之前宣佈了那則消息，搶了個先。
*He stole his oppoent's thunder by proposing a toast for the distinguished visitor．他搶在對手之前向貴賓祝酒。attract attention away from sb．or sth．that people should be watching搶鏡頭；引起注意力
*She was on the stage for only a few minutes，bat I thought she stole the show．她僅出場幾分鐘，不過我認為她搶先出了風頭。
*Just as the speaker began，a little dog ran up the aisle，and stole the spotlight from him．正當演說者開始演說時，一隻小狗跑上通道，把人們的注意力吸引了過去。approach sb．slowly and quietly悄悄地走近；偷襲
*Her friend stole up on her and made her jump．她的朋友悄悄走近她，使她跳了起來。
*A small party stole up on the bridge under cover of darkness．一支小分隊趁黑夜偷襲這座橋。steal.age
