(1) (暫時) 離開屋子[房間],外出
(2) 放大腳步; (加快) 腳步
Let's ~ out. 
我們加快腳步吧
(3)(口語)出去尋樂 [玩耍,跳舞,遊蕩] 
(4) → v.t. 2
step out of line
(1) 採取與別人不同的行動
(2) 做出意料之外的事
step out on?
(口語) <對妻子、丈夫> 不忠實,背叛…
step up
(1) → v.i. 2 a
(2) 增加 <速度,電壓等> 
(3) 促進<工作>,提高 <生產等> 
Production must be stepped up. 
必須增產,非促進生產不可1．move to one side讓到一邊
*Would you mind stepping aside to let this old lady off the bus？請讓一讓，讓這位老太太下車好嗎？
*Step aside and make room for us．靠邊，給我們騰個地方。
2．move from a position of authority讓位
*They expect him to step aside and make way for a younger man．他們希望他讓位，好給一個年輕些的人接班。
*He was willing to step aside in favor of a more dynamic leader．他願意讓位給更強有力的領導人。1．yield ground by moving to the rear；recede後退
*He stepped back to admire the painting．他退了幾步來欣賞這幅畫。
*We stepped back politely to let the ladies pass．我們禮貌地後退，讓女士們過去。
2．move backwards from surprise，shock，etc．由於吃驚而後退
*When he saw it，he stepped back in surprise．他一看到它，就吃驚得往後退。
*She stepped back，hardly able to believe her ears．她吃驚地往後退縮，簡直不能相信自己的耳朵。gradually逐步地
*Step by step I'll learn to do the work．我將逐步地學會幹這項工作。
*A foreign language can't be learned rapidly；it must be learned step by step．學外語不能急，只能按部就班地學。1．walk down走下來
*As soon as the train stopped，the conductor stepped down to help the passengers off．火車一停，列車員就下火車幫乘客下車。
2．move to a lower level；retire or leave a top position降低；辭職；讓位
*I've spent so many years as chairman that I feel it's time I stepped down．我當了這麼多年的董事長，現在我覺得該退下來了。
*Next May our company's president will step down，and we will have to elect a new one at the next stockholders'meeting．明年5月我們公司的總經理任職期滿就要退下來了，我們將要在下一次的股東會議上選舉一個新的總經理。
3．slow down放慢
*For lack of raw materials they had stepped down production．由於原料缺乏，他們不得不放慢生產進度。

step down
1 退讓
2 放棄; 辭去
3 逐漸降低 (電力等)step function
『數』階躍函數; 階梯函數step in
1 參與
2 介入; 干預; 干涉
Father ~ and forbade me to go camping. 
父親出面干預,不准我去露營

1．walk in走進
*Would you mind stepping in for a moment？進來坐一會好嗎？
*The clerk stepped in and asked for Mr．Black．辦事員走進來要找布萊克先生。
2．intervene either to help or hinder插進來（幫助或阻止）；干預
*If the government does not step in，there will be no trains on Monday．政府要是不干預的話，星期一將沒有任何火車。
*The police are reluctant to step in．警察不願插手干預。
*Father stepped in and forbade me to go campimg．父親進來干預不准我去野營。1．go out from a place走出去
*He just stepped out for a breath of fresn air．他只是出去換換新鮮空氣。
*I'm just going to step out for a minute．我正要出去一會兒。
2．walk fast快走；加快步伐
*As it was getting dark we stepped out so as to reach the village．天快黑了，我們快點走，好趕到村裡。
*Step out，you still have a long way to go．走快點，你還得走很長一段路呢。
3．engage in social activities；enjoy oneself socially出去娛樂
*She'really stepping out these days：the theatre last night，dinner tonight and dancing tomorrow．她這幾天確實交際很多：昨天去看戲，今晚參加晚宴，明天又要去跳舞。
*You're all dressed up，Mary；you must be stepping out tonight．你穿得這樣漂亮，瑪麗，今晚想必有什麼約會。step rocket
『太空』多級火箭step turn
