*Stick the flap down with tape or glue or something．把這信封口蓋用紙條或膠水之類的東西粘上。stick figure
<<可數名詞>>
棒線畫
(人或動物等的略圖)1．be hard to accept難以接受
*Having to pay out￡50 for such a small thing really sticks in my throat．為這個小東西要付50英鎊的錢太讓我難以接受了。
*It's his treatment of his aged mother that really sticks in my throat．他對待自己年邁母親的那種做法實在使我很反感。
2．be hard to say難以啟齒
*Jane wanted to ask the teacher's pardon，but the words stuck in her throat．簡想請求老師原諒，卻又難以說出口。stick insect
<<可數名詞>>
『昆蟲』竹節蟲1．protrude or make sth．protrude or project突出；伸出
*Don't stick your tongue out at me．不要對我伸舌頭。
*An arm was sticking out from the hole．有只胳膊從洞中伸出。
2．be noticeable醒目
*The author's outlook sticks out on every page．書的每一頁都清楚地顯示出作者的觀點。
*My house is the only brick one on the street．It sticks out and you can't miss it．我的房子是這條街上唯一的一棟磚房，它很顯眼，你不會找不到的。
3．endure or tolerate sth．to the end堅持…到底；忍受
*Try to stick out the party for another hour and then we can go home．設法在聚會上再堅持一個小時，然後我們就回家。
*If you can stick it out a bit longer，everything will be all right．如果你能再忍耐一會兒，一切都會正常的。
*Mathematics is hard，but if you stick it out you'll understand it．數學是困難的，但如果你努力學習，堅持到底，自然就會瞭解它。
4．wait stubbornly for sth．that has demanded to be allowed or given堅持要
*The union are sticking out for a twenty per cent increase．工會要求工資增加百分之二十。
*They say she's too young but she's sticking out for the job．他們說她太年輕了，可她還是堅持要做這件工作。stick shift
<<可數名詞>>
(美) (汽車的) 手操作變速器,手排擋persevere；adhere to堅持
*I shall stick to my decision．我將堅持我的決定。
*If you stick to it long enough you can find the answer to that problem．如果你堅持一段時間，你就會發現那個問題的答案。
*I hate listening to him；he never sticks to the point．我不喜歡聽他說，他從不堅持自己的觀點。
*I hope you will stick to the point in the debate．我希望你在辯論中能抓住要害。
*If you stick to the truth，you've nothing to fear．你要是堅持真理，就可以無所畏懼。remain close together in a situation 團結
*Stick together，and don't let anything divide you．要互相支持，不要讓任何東西影響團結。
*They stuck together through thick and thin．不管有什麼艱難險阻，他們都緊密團結在一起。stick up
『俗』搶劫; (尤指) 槍械槍劫

1．protrude突出；豎起
*Stick up your hand if you know the answer．知道答案請舉手。
*Her hair keeps sticking up no matter how often she combs it．不管她怎麼勤梳頭，她的頭髮總是豎著。
*The pillars of the wharf are still sticking up in the water．碼頭的樁子仍在水中豎著。
2．rob搶劫
*The owner of that store was stuck up three times in the last six months．那家商店老闆在過去6個月中曾3次遭搶劫。defend；support保護；支持
*She always sticks up for her friends．她總是支持她的朋友。
*Can't you stick up for yourself sometimes？有時候你難道不能為自己辯護一下嗎？stick-at-it
