<<不及物動詞>>
1 使身體變直<up>
2 變端正<out, up>1．solve；make less confused解決；使清楚
*I hope the misunderstanding will soon be straightened out．我希望誤會很快就會澄清。
*He said we needed some straightening out on one or two points．他說我們需要澄清一兩點問題。
*I could not grasp the theory until Dr．Rose straightened me out on it．羅斯博士解釋後，我才弄懂了那種理論。
2．put right恢復正常；使好轉
*I'll try to straighten the matter out once and for all．我要竭力把這事情辦好。
*I'm only a little tired；a night's sleep will straighten me out．我只是有點累了，睡一晚就會好的。1．become erect or upright；make straight挺直身子
*I told him to straighten up．我叫他要挺直身子。
*He straightened himself up and looked them squarely in the eye．他直挺挺地站著，瞪著眼睛盯著他們。
2．make tidy整理
*Mrs．White straightened up the house before the guests came．懷特太太打掃好房子準備接待客人。
*He straightened up the papers．他把文件弄整齊。
