那男孩 (伸開四肢) 直躺在草地上
c. 把<某人>擊倒,使<某人> (成大字形地) 趴倒<out>
A blow behind the ear ~ed him (out) on the floor. 
耳後的一擊使他趴倒在地板上
3 
a. 曲解; 濫用; 誇張
~ a point 
作牽強附會的說明; 破例作讓步
~ the law 
歪曲法1．extend 伸出
*The little boy stretched out his hands to catch the toy．小男孩伸出雙手去抓玩具。
*He stretched out his arms and embraced me tightly．他伸出雙臂緊緊擁抱了我。
2．extend one's body or part of it for relaxation 伸直四肢
*He stretched out on the grass in the sunshine．他舒展著身子躺在陽光下的草地上。
*The cat stretched out in front of the fire．貓伸直身體躺在爐前。
3．be enough or cause sth．to be enough 使夠用
*Will the food stretch out？Tonight we've got three extra guests for dinner．飯菜夠吃嗎？今晚我們多了3個客人吃飯。
*I don't see how I can stretch out the housekeeping to the end of the month．我不知道家用錢要怎麼安排才能維持到月底。stretch receptor
