14 『軍』攻擊<敵人等>
B
1 a. 打動<某人>的心,使<某人>銘感 [印象深刻] 
What ~s me most about America is its crime. 
美國給我最深刻印象的是該國的犯罪 (率) 
I was struck by her charm. 
我被她的嫵媚迷住了
b. 使<人>覺得<…>,產生<…>印象
She struck me as being very practical. 
她使我覺得她很實1．attack 進攻
*Many newspapers struck at his latest plan．許多報紙都攻擊他的最新計劃。
*He struck at me but missed．他動手打我，但是沒打著。
2．attempt to destroy 企圖毀壞
*Each of the two theories seems to strike at the foundation of the other．這兩種理論似乎從根本上相互排斥。return an attack 還擊
*In reply to last night's bombing attack，our planes this morning struck back at the enemy port．為了回敬昨夜的空襲，我機今晨對敵機場進行了還擊。
*When he attacked me，naturally I struck back．他既然攻擊我，我當然還擊。strike benefit
<<名詞>>
=strike pay1．cause to fall by a blow 擊倒
*The man struck down by lightning during the storm was taken to the hospital．在暴風雨中被雷電擊中的人被送進了醫院。
*With one blow he struck down his opponent．他一拳就把對手擊倒。
2．make sb．unable to lead a full，active life 使受到摧殘
*He was struck down by a heart attack at the age of forty．他40歲時得了心臟病。
*He is struck down with flu．他患流感。make unable to speak 使啞口無言
*His eloquence struck them dumb．他的雄辯使他們啞口無言。
*The news of his financial losses struck him dumb．他財務損失的消息使他目瞪口呆。strike figure
『地質』=percussion figurestrike fund
罷工資金interrupt suddenly 突然插話
*Someone struck in with a question．有人插進來提出了一個問題。
*「I know where she was．」Jane struck in．簡突然插話說：「我知道她在哪兒。」strike leader
罷工領導人strike measure
平斗; 斗刮量法1．remove 刪去；除去
*He promised to strike off the interest of the first debt．他答應免去第1筆債的利息。
2．remove by cutting 斬去；砍去
*The boy was striking off all the flowers with a stick．小男孩在用棍子把花全部打落。
*He struck off the enemy's revolver．他一拳打掉了敵人的左輪手槍。
3．print 印刷
*They struck off 5，000 copies of the election leaflet．他們印了5000張關於選舉的傳單。
*Another hundred thousand copies of the novel have been struck off since last yedr．自去年以來，那部小說又印了10萬冊。think of or get suddenly or unexpectedly 偶然想起；偶然得到
*He struck on a way of making diamonds．他突然找到了一種製造鑽石的方法。
*We struck on the idea when at work yesterday．我們昨天上班時忽然想到了這個主意。
*He struck upon the book in a secondhand bookstore．他在一家舊書店裡偶然發現了這本書。1．remove 刪去；塗去
*You had better strike out the fourth paragraph．你最好刪去第4段。
*She struck out the sentence she had just written and added a new one．她把剛寫的那句話刪掉了，另加了一句。
2．dawn on 想起；明白
*He struck out a plan of doing the work well．他想出一個做好該工作的計劃。
*He struck out a plan for himself for the next year．他為自己擬訂了下一年的計劃。
3．start to do sth．new and different，esp．on one's own自成一路；創新
*He decided to leave his father's firm and strike out on his own．他決定離開父親的公司，出去開創一條自己的路。
*He struck out a path through the thicket．他開闢了一條穿過灌木林的新路。
4．try to hit sb．in a wild or uncontrolled way用力打
*The little boy was frightened and struck out madly．孩子非常害怕，用手亂打。
*He lost his temper and struck out wildly．他動了肝火，大打出手。
5．move quickly in a certain direction 向…快速走去；用手腳使勁划水
*He dived off the boat and struck out for the island，他從船上躍入水中，朝島上用力游去。
*She stood hesitant for a minute and then struck out for the bus stop．她站在那兒遲疑了片刻，然後拿定主意向汽車站疾步走去。strike pay
