*They strung up the ham for the winter．他們把火腿懸掛起來留到冬天吃。
2．kill sb．by hanging 絞死（某人）Two of the rebel leaders were strung up as a warning to the others．叛變首領中的兩名被絞死，以做傚尤。
3．make tense，excited 使緊張；使振奮
*On the evening of his big speech he didn't seem at all strung up．他在作重要講話的那天晚上似乎一點也不緊張。
*He strung up his nerves to do it．他打起精神來幹那件事。string-clo.ored
