*Mind your language！Don't swear at him．說話要小心，不要惡語傷人。
*He resented being sworn at．他憎恨別人罵他。praise or recommend極力推薦；極其信賴
*She swears by aspirin as the best remedy for a headache．她極力推薦阿斯匹林治頭痛。
*I always swear by their products．我一貫信賴他們的產品。make sb．take an oath to be truthful，loyal，obedient，etc．宣誓就職
*The new president was sworn in last week．新總統上星期宣誓就職。
*He was sworn in shortly after the election．選舉後不久他就宣誓就職了。vow to abstain from 發誓不再；發誓戒掉
*He finally made up his mind to swear off smoking．最後他決心戒煙。
*Since his illness，he has sworn off drinking．生病以後，他已發誓戒酒。assert with great conviction 斷言；發誓肯定
*I can't swear to it，but I don't think he would lie to me．我不敢斷言，但我認為他不會對我撒謊的。
*I was sure I locked the door when I left the room，but I can't really swear to it．我離開房間時肯定是鎖了門的，但我不能把話說死。swear.er
