『航空』 (飛機之) 尾翼; 尾部1．diminish；grow progressively smaller in number，size，etc．變得越來越少、越來越小等
*The numbers in the procession began to tail away．隊列中的人數開始減少。
*Orders for goods of this kind usually begin to tail off towards the end of the year．這類貨物的訂單通常在臨近年終時就開始漸漸減少了。
2．lessen；decline in quality；grow progressively fainter or more scattered 降低；質量下降；變得越來越輕、越來越弱、越來越分散
*The work of some students begins to tail off as they approach their examination．在快要考試的時候，有些學生的作業質量在下降。
*My enthusiasm has tailed off．我的熱情越來越低了。
*She was too shy to speak，and after a few words her voice tailed off into silence．她靦腆得話也說不出來，講了幾句話，話音就越來越低，最後乾脆不吭聲了。
*Your work has been tailing off this year；we expect you to keep up your former standard．今年你的工作質量在下降，我們期望你保持原來的工作水平。tail beam
