c. 佔領 <要塞、城市等> ,攻取,奪取
~ a fort 
攻取要塞
3 
a. 獲得<獎賞等>,得到,把…拿到手
~ a degree 
取得學位
~ a bribe 
收賄
His team took (the) first prize at the contest. 
他的隊在競賽中獲得第一名
b. [從…]接受,賺取[from]
He ~s 600 dollars a week (from his job). 
他拿六百美元的周薪
T~ that! (. 
一邊揍著對方) 收下這個 (拳頭) !
I'm not going to ~ any more of your insults [any more insults from you]. 
我已受夠了你的侮辱 [我不想再忍受你的侮辱] !
c. [~ it](口語)接納,採納,承諾,收下,承受,接受
TAKE it or leave it. 
要嘛接受要嘛放棄,不容討價還價
4 
a. 買<物>
I'll ~ this hat. 
我要買這頂帽子
b. 訂購<報紙等>,預訂 <票、座位等> ; (訂合約) 租用<房屋等>
What paper do you ~?. 
你訂什麼報紙?
We have taken a cottage by the sea for the holidays. 
我們在海邊租了一間小別墅供度假之用
5 a. 攝取 <藥、飲料、食物等> ,吃,喝,服用
~ medicine 
服[吃]藥
Not to be taken internally. 
不可服用 (只可注射或塗敷) 
I don't ~ coffee. 
我不喝咖啡
b. 將 <牛奶、糖等> 放入[…中][in]
~ sugar in one's coffee 
把糖放入咖啡中
c. 吸入<空氣>
~ a deep breath 
做深呼吸
→ take the AIR.
6 a. 採用<人>,錄取; 收<學生>; 收容 <房客> ; 娶 <妻> 
~ pupils 
收學生
~ lodgers 
收容房客
~ a wife 
娶妻
b. 將<人>納入[…中],接納…為新會員[to, into]
We took him into our plans. 
我們吸收他參與我們的計畫
7 
a. 採取 <手段等> 
~ measures [steps] 
採取措施[手段]
b. 使用<機會等>,利用…
I'll ~ (advantage of) the next opportunity. 
我要利用下次機會
T~ your time before answering. 
慢慢想再回答(不用急)
c. 舉… (作例子) 
T~ Susan for [as an] example. 
舉蘇珊作例子吧
8 
a. (選) 用…,採用…
I usually ~ size nine shoes. 
我平常穿九號鞋子
b. <機器>使用…
This vending machine ~s any coin. 
這種自動販賣機可以使用任何硬幣
9 
a. 修 <學科、課程等> ; 上 [受] <課>
~ dancing lessons 
學跳舞 [上舞蹈課] 
~ biology 
修生物學
b. 徵求 <專家的意見> ,請教
~ medical [legal] advice 
接受醫師的診斷 [請教律師] 
10 
a. [從…]得…[from]
This medicine ~s its name from the inventor. 
這種藥的名稱取自發明者的名字
b. [從…]引用…,借用[from]
This line is taken from Shakespeare. 
此行引自莎士比亞
11 a. <恐怖、疾病、情緒等> (突然) 侵襲<人>
Fear took him.= He was taken with fear. 
他忽然感到恐懼
She was taken with sickness [illness]. 
她生病了
b. 使<人> <生病> 
She was taken sick [ill]. 
她生病了
c. [在某種狀況下] 襲擊,突襲<人> [by,at] 
~ a person by surprise 
突然襲擊某人
~ a person at a disadvantage 
趁其不備襲擊某人
12 <人>患 [罹] <疾病等>,引起,感染
~ (a) cold 
患感冒
13 吸引 <耳目、關心> ; 使<人>喜悅,使<人>銷魂,迷住<人>
~ a person's eye 
吸引某人的注意力
The song took my fancy. 
這首歌深受我喜愛
I was much taken with [by] her beauty. 
我深深地被她的美貌所吸引
14 
a. 著<火>
~ fire 
著火
b. 吸收 <染料、氣味等> 
The milk has taken the smell of fish. 
這牛奶沾有魚腥味
c. 收 <磨、擦拭等的> 效果
Marble ~s a high polish. 
大理石可以磨得極為光滑
15<魚>咬上 <餌> 
16<男人>與<女人>性交
17(俚)欺騙<人>
18『文法』字尾加…, (後面) 要有…
Ordinary nouns ~ -s in the plural. 
一般名詞的複數字尾加 -s.
B
1 (從某處) 拿去,帶去
(
→ bring 【同義字】) 
a. 將<物>拿去 (…) ; 將<人、動物>帶去 (…) ; <交通工具、道路> 將<人>運往 (…) 
He took sweets home to his children. 
他帶糖果回家給他孩子們
Please ~ these dishes away and wash them. 
請你把這些盤子拿去洗一洗
My father often ~s me to the zoo. 
我父親時常帶我去動物園
Will thaccept a poorer or lower position；be second to sth．or sb．else；take second place 接受較差或較低的位置；成為次要的人或事情；退居其次
*With no hope of winning，he had to take a back seat in the contest．眼看自己在比賽中無望獲勝，他只得甘拜下風。
*During the war all manufacturing had to take a back seat to military needs．在戰爭期間，一切生產都要服從軍事需要。sit down 坐下
*After she had taken a chair，we started to watch TV．她坐下來以後我們就開始看電視。1．be against；disapprove of 反對；不贊成
*All the family members took a dim view of his rash action．所有家庭成員都反對他的輕率舉動。
*John's father took a dim view of his wanting to borrow the car．約翰的父親不肯將車借給他用。
*Helen approves of many things her sister does，but she takes a dim view of the way Edith is raising her children．海倫贊成她妹妹做的許多事情，但是她不贊成埃狄斯扶養孩子的方法。
2．have doubts about；feel unsure or anxious about 對…持懷疑或悲觀的看法
*Tom took a dim view of his chances of passing the exam．湯姆對通過這次考試的可能性持悲觀態度。
*They hope to go on a picnic，but they take a dim view of the weather．他們希望去野餐，但是又怕天氣有問題。like 喜歡
*From the start，he took a fancy to Mary．從一開始，他就喜歡瑪麗。
*All the students have taken a fancy to their new teacher．所有的學生都喜歡他們的新老師。participate in 參與；介入
*He wanted to take a hand in the activity．他想參與這項活動。make a firm decision；hold a strong opinion 作出有力的決定；持有明確的意見
*The lazy man didn't want to deal with the problem，so he refused to take a stand on it．那個懶人不想處理那個問題，因此他拒絕表態。
*The American people expect the President to take a stand on every important national issue．美國人民希望總統對國家的每一個重要問題都有明確的意見。accept the risk of failure or loss（as in planning or starting sth．）；
*gamble on；venture on 打賭；冒險；碰運氣
*Won't you take a chance on the price？你願對這個價格打賭嗎？
*You're taking a chance if you go out in weather like this without an umbrella．這樣的天氣出門不帶傘，你有點僥倖心理。
*I don't think I'll get the job but I'm willing to take my chance and ask for it．我想我難以謀得那份工作，但我想碰碰運氣提出申請。surprise；astonish 使…吃驚；使…驚異
*They were taken aback by his unexpected appearance．他的突然出現使他們大為吃驚。show round a place 領…參觀
*There is no need to take me about seeing the sights．不必領著我去觀光了。take into consideration 考慮
*We'll take account of your suggestion．我們將考慮你的建議。
*I don't take much account of myself，but I have never let myself be duped．我不大考慮我自己的利益，可是我也從來不肯受騙。use for one's own benefit 利用
*He takes advantage of his fine secretary by leaving all the work to her and doing nothing himself．他利用他那位能幹的秘書，把所有工作都丟給她幹，自己卻什麼也不幹。
*He always takes full advantage of the mistakes made by his rivals．他總是充分利用對手的失誤。
*They decided to take advantage of the beautiful weather and go to the country．他們決定利用這麼好的天氣到鄉村去。
*He was always good to people，and there were those that took advantage of him．他總是待人很好，所以有人總想佔他的便宜。1．resemble sb．in appearance，personality or character（在外貌、品格和性格方面）與…相似
*He takes after his father in mathematical ability．他在數學方面的才能很像他的父親。
*Peter doesn't seem to take after either of his parents；the person he resembles most is his uncle John．彼得長得似乎不像他的父母親，而最像他的叔叔約翰。
2．follow as an example；imitate 學…的榜樣；倣傚
*Though he is fairly well off，he is very frugal；he takes after his father in that respect．雖然他相當富裕，但他非常節約，在這方面他是向他父親學習的。
*Try to take after your mother who is an honest hardworking woman．向你媽媽學學，她誠實而且勤勞。misunderstand；interpret（remarks，conduct，etc．）unfavourably 誤解
*I think you have taken my word amiss；that was not my meaning．我想你誤解了我的話，那不是我的意思。
*His joke was taken amiss by some of the company．他開玩笑得罪了幾個同伴。
*I hope you will not take it amiss that I venture to make a few criticisms of your article．我冒昧地對你的文章提出幾點批評意見，希望你不至於生氣。1．separate into parts 拆開
*We have to take the whole engine apart to discover the cause of the trouble．我們必須將整個發動機拆開，查明故障的原因。
*He took the machine apart to clean and oil the parts．他拆開機器，把所有的部件都擦淨並上了油。
*It's much easier to take a clock apart than to put it together again．把鍾拆開比重新裝上要容易得多。
2．treat roughly or rudely；defeat utterly；punish severely；criticize harshly 粗暴對待；徹底打敗；嚴厲批評
*He had a rough time in his first fight．He was drawn opposite a real old pro who took him apart inside two rounds．他在第1場拳擊比賽中吃了不少苦頭，他抽籤碰上的對手是一名副其實的職業選手，不到兩個回合他就被打得一敗塗地。
*The critics really took the novel apart，but I thought it quite good．那些批評家簡直把這部小說說得一無是處，不過我覺得還可以。1．withdraw 收回；撤銷
*I take back what I said just now．我撤回剛才說的話。
*He would neither apologize nor take back what he had said．他既不肯道歉，又不肯收回他說過的話。
2．regain possession of 重新獲得；取回
*Do you mind taking the children back in your car？你可以讓孩子們搭你的車回來嗎？
3．agree to receive back again；permit to come back 同意收回；同意退回；允許…回去
*This shop promises to take back any good that don't satisfy the person who buys them．這家商店允許顧客退回他所不滿意的商品。
*The chair was defective and the dealer was obliged to take it back．這把椅子有毛病，商人不得不同意把它收回。
*Lindsay was fired twice but both times taken back under the pressure from the union．林賽兩次被解雇，但在工會的壓力下，兩次都被允許回去工作。
4．remind of earlier time；cause to remember 使回想
*This picture took me back to my own childhood．這張照片使我回憶起我的童年。1．fill with surprise or amazement；astonish 使吃驚；使驚奇
*Your good examination results have taken all the teachers by surprise．你考試的好成績使得所有老師都感到吃驚。
*When our teacher quit in the middle of the year to work for the government，it took us all by surprise．我們的老師在年中辭職去政府部門供職時，我們都感到吃驚。
2．appear in front of sb．suddenly；come before sb．is ready 出其不意地出現；在（某人）未準備妥當之前來到
*The passenger took the thief by surprise．He caught the latter's hand as it sneaked into his pocket．那位旅客在扒手剛把手伸進他的口袋裡的時候，突然抓住了他。
*Our guests came half an hour early，taking my mother by surprise．我們的客人提前半小時來了，弄得我媽媽措手不及。be careful 當心；注意；小心
*In busy city streets special care should be taken．在繁忙的城市街道上，應該特別小心。
*Care should be taken to see that a letter is properly addressed．要注意把信封上的地址寫對。
*Take care that you don't slip on the icy roads．注意，不要在結了冰的路上滑倒。
*Take care not to make the same mistake again．當心，不要再犯同樣的錯誤。1．take charge of；look after 照顧；照看
*The nurse takes good care of the baby．保姆把嬰兒照顧得很好。
*「Don't worry about me while you're away；I'll be taken good care of by our neighbours．」「你外出期間不要掛念我，鄰居們會很好地照顧我的。」
2．be responsible for 負責
*Will you take care of buying the wine for tonight's party？你負責為今晚的聚會買酒好嗎？
*Don't worry about this．I'll take care of it．這事不要擔心，我會負責處理的。
3．be careful of 當心；注意
*You must take much care of your handwriting；it's so illegible．你得特別注意書法，你的字跡太潦草了。
*She never takes care of her wording．她從來不注意自己的措辭。1．take the management of；become responsible for 負責
*Professor Smith takes charge of the literature class．史密斯教授負責文學班。
*The secretary took charge of the matter until her boss returned．秘書負責這件事直到老闆回來為止。
*She offered to take charge of all the arrangements for the conference．她主動提出來負責會議的一切安排。
2．assume control of控制
*When the fire started，the police and firemen quickly took charge of the situation．著火時，警察以及消防隊員很快就控制了火勢。find delight in喜歡
*Some people take delight in harming others．有些人以害人為樂。
*Our monitor takes delight in helping others．我們的班長樂於助人。
*He takes delight in playing chess．他喜歡下棋。1．remove；get by lifting down 移動
*Please take down the books from the shelf．請把書從架上取下來。
2．write in shorthand；write down；record 用速記記錄；記錄；速記
*The policeman took down all particulars of the accident．警察把事故的所有細節都記錄下來了。
*She took down the speech in short hand．她用速記法把演講記了下來。
3．diminish the pride or arrogance of；humiliate 挫某人的傲氣；挫銳氣
*A person who is always trying to take other people down gets himself disliked．老是企圖讓別人丟面子的人不討人喜歡。
*Margaret has too high an opinion of herself．Someone must take her down a bit．瑪格麗特太自負了，應當有人挫一挫她的傲氣。
4．dismantle；pull or take apart 拆卸；拆散
*The workmen are now taking down the scaffolding round the building．工人們正在拆卸建築物周圍的腳手架。
*Carpenters took down the old house in order to build a new one．木工們拆掉那老房子，以便建一幢新房。
5．fall sick；become ill 病倒
*He was taken down with fever．他因發燒而病倒了。
6．cheat 欺騙
*The plausible rogue took me down over that bargain．這花言巧語的流氓在那宗交易中欺騙了我。
*Only when he got the camera home and began to examine it did he realize that he had been taken down at the pawnbroker's．當他回家檢查買回來的照相機時，才發覺自己在當鋪裡受騙了。
7．swallow with difficulty 困難地吞下
*Take the medicine down and do not stop to think about it．把藥吞下去，吞的時候不要停下來想它。1．become effective 生效
*The medicine took effect two hours ago．藥兩小時前就產生了效果。
2．go into operation 實施
*The new rule took effect last month．新規則上個月開始實施了。
*When does the new law take effect？這項新法律什麼時候生效？disagree with；dislike 不同意；不喜歡；對…表示異議
*In his speech，the economist put unemployment above inflation but other experts took exception to his statement．在演講中，這個經濟學家把失業問題看作比通貨膨脹問題更重要，但是其他專家不同意他的觀點。
*Great exception was taken to his remarks by all the older members of the family．家裡的老人對他的談話很不高興。
*There was nothing in the speech that you could take exception to．這篇演講無可非議。1．mistake for 誤認為
*I am sorry，I took you for your brother．對不起，我把你誤認為你哥哥了。
*What does he take us for？他把我們當作什麼人？
*When he worked in the countryside，he used to take wheat for barley．當他在農村勞動時，經常把小麥看成大麥。
*At first they took him for a foreigner．最初他們把他當成了外國人。
2．assume to be假定是；認為是
*I took it for the truth．我認為那是真的。
*Make no mistake．Don't take him for a fool；he is anything but that．別搞錯了，不要把他當傻瓜，他決不是那種人。play a trick on；fool 愚弄（某人）；欺騙（某人）；尋開心
*When he told me I had passed the exam，he was actually taking me for a ride．他告訴我說我已通過了考試，其實他是在騙我。
*The girls told Mary that her mother had come to see her，but she did not believe them；she thought they were taking her for a ride．女生們告訴瑪麗說她媽媽來看她了。但她不相信，認為她們是在拿她開玩笑。1．suppose or understand to be true 假定是真的；對…信以為真
*He took for granted that the invitation included himself．他認為他自己一定是在被邀請之列。
*A teacher cannot take it for granted that students always do their homework．老師不能假定學生們一定會做家庭作業。
2．assume；accept as a fact that does not need any confirmation or verification 假定；認為理所當然
*I take it for granted that he will come．我認為他當然會來的。
*We take it for granted that they would consent．我們認為他們一定會同意的。
*Excuse me for not introducing you to Kermit．I took it for granted that you two knew each other．對不起，我沒有把你介紹給凱米特，我想當然地認為你們互相認識。
*All particulars should be carefully checked and verified；nothing should be taken for granted．所有的細節都應當仔細查對、核實，任何一點都不能想當然。1．grasp；seize 緊緊抓住
*Please take hold of the rope．請抓緊繩子。
2．take advantage of 利用
*We will take hold of this good opportunity．我們將利用這個好機會。be hurt or offended 受…傷害；對…生氣
*When he heard of his dismissal，he took the news ill．聽說被解雇，他受到很大刺激。
*Don't take it ill．不要生氣。1．attend 出席
*Let's have lunch here and then take in a movie．我們在這兒吃午飯，然後去看場電影。
2．deceive；cheat 欺騙
*The salesman finds it easy to take in old ladies．營業員發現很容易欺騙老年婦女。
*He certainly took us in with his stories about his experiences in Mexico．他一定是用他在墨西哥的經歷來欺騙我們。
*Don't trust that fellow；he'll take you in if he gets the chance．別相信那個傢伙，他一有機會就會使你上當。
*We were completely taken in by his story．我們完全被他的謊言欺騙了。
3．receive and accommodate as a guest or as a boarder in one's house；give shelter to 在家裡接待客人或搭伙者；收容
*Our hotel is full，we can't take in any more guests．我們的旅館已經客滿，不能再接待客人了。
*After the death of her husband she had to take in boarders．在她丈夫死後，她不得不接納搭伙的人。
*The kind old lady offered to take in the poor homeless child．這位好心的老太太主動提出收留那個無家可歸的窮孩子。
4．understand；grasp 理解
*We need some time to take the situation in．我們需要一些時間來弄清情況。
*This book is so difficult that I'm tired；I can't take in what the author means．這本書很難，我無法理解作者的意思。
*I tried my best to explain the matter to him，but he still couldn't take in what I was saying．我盡最大努力向他解釋這件事，但他仍然不能理解我在說什麼。
5．accept（work）into one's house to be done for pay 接活在家做
*She scraped along by taking in sewing．她在家替人做針線活勉強餬口。
6．include 包括
*The study of physics takes in many different subjects．物理學的研究包含了很多不同的科目。
*I think this list takes in everybody．我想這個名單是包括了所有的人。
*This love of our country takes in our families，relations，friends and acquaintances．這種對我們國家的愛也包括了對我們的家庭、親戚、朋友以及我們所認識的人的愛。
7．make narrower；make smaller；reduce the size or measurement（of garments）改小（服裝）
*This skirt is too loose at the waist；I shall have to get the dressmaker to take it in．這條裙子腰圍太寬了，我要讓裁縫改小一點。
*This dress needs to be taken in a bit at the neck．這件衣服的領子要改小一些。
8．see at a glance；observe keenly 一眼看清；敏銳地觀察到
*He took in what was happening and decided to get away quickly．他一眼就明白了是怎麼回事，於是決定立即脫身。
*The police officer took in every detail of the room at a glance．警官一眼就把屋裡的每個細小的地方都敏銳地看到了。
9．subscribe to；receive and pay for regularly 訂閱
*Which newspaper do you take in？你訂閱什麼報紙？
*I take in China Daily．我訂《中國日報》。
10．accept without question；believe 毫不懷疑地接受；輕信
The poor man takes in all the lies 
*she tells him．那可憐的人相信了她告訴他的所有謊言。
*The magician did many tricks，and the children took them all in．魔術師變了許多魔術，孩子們都信以為真。consider seriously；take account of仔細考慮
*When you are planning a picnic，you will have to take weather into account．準備野餐時必須考慮到天氣情況。
*I know I was wrong to do that，but please take the special circumstances into account before you decide on the punishment．我知道我做錯了，但你在決定給我懲罰之前請考慮當時的特殊情況。
*When deciding what to do we must take into account all the difficulties．在決定做某件事情的時候，我們必須把所有的困難都考慮進去。relax；avoid hard work or worry；have an easy time；live in comfort 輕鬆一點；不要太緊張；不要太勞累；不要操心；放心；休息
*Take it easy，there is no need to be nervous．放鬆一點，沒有必要緊張。
*You've been working hard all afternoon，Steve．Sit down and take it easy for a few minutes．斯蒂夫，你已經辛苦了一個下午，坐下放鬆一會兒。
*The doctor said that Bob would have to take things easy for a while after he had his tonsils out．醫生說鮑勃割過扁桃腺之後要休息一段時間，不要勞累。obtain an equivalent for a loss sustained 獲得等值補償
*The salesgirl could find no small change to give me，so she let me take it out in some sweets．那個女售貨員找不出零錢，就給了我一些糖果。
*The laborer has worked for the merchant a month，and now he will take it out in articles for the store．那個工人已經替這家商店工作了一個月，他要在店中取得等值的商品作為工資。1．administer castigation；beat揍；打
*He threatened to take it out of the boy's，hide．他威脅說要揍那小孩一頓。
2．exact payment for；penalize 向…報復；懲罰；找…出氣
*They took it out of his pay．他們扣了他的薪水作為處罰。
*If he has been annoyed by anything at the office，he takes it out of his wife and children．如果上班時被什麼事情惹火了的話，他就找妻子和孩子出氣。
3．exhaust；tire 使疲勞；使體弱無力
*That long climb took it out of me．爬那麼高的山使我精疲力竭。
*The hot weather takes it out of me；all I want to do is to sit about doing nothing．炎熱的天氣使我疲乏不堪，我只想坐著什麼也不幹。cause sb．else to suffer for one's own misfortune or dissatisfaction 向某人發洩自己的不幸或不滿足的感情；向…出氣
*Having had a quarrel with his wife John left home in a bad temper，and then took it out on his subordinates at the office．約翰跟妻子吵了一架以後，怒氣沖沖地離開了家，到辦公室對自己的部下出氣。
*He came home angry upon losing his job and took it out on his children．他失業了，很生氣地回到家，在孩子身上發洩自己的怒氣。say goodbye to告別
*Before he went back home， he took leave of all his friends．他回家之前向朋友們一一道別。
*It was going to be very difficult，after such a close working partnership， to take our leave of each other．我們經過一段親密無間的合作以後，一旦要分別，實在是令人難受。be free with 對…舉止隨便；調戲
*The rascal was punished for taking liberties with a girl．那個流氓因調戲一位姑娘而受到了懲處。
*You must stop taking liberties with her．你切勿對她太隨便。
*Don't take liberties with the young lady．不要調戲那位小姐。notice；pay attention to注意
*Did you take note of the man speaking at the meeting this morning？你注意到今天上午在會上發言的那個人沒有？pay attention to；heed 注意；留意
*He passed by me without taking any notice of me．他從我旁邊走過，一點也沒有注意到我。
*If you hear the fire alarm at ten o'clock this morning，don't take any notice of it；the engineers are merely testing it．如果你們今天上午10點鐘聽到火警，請不要在意，工程師們只是在做試驗。
*She passed me in the street，but took no notice of me．她在街上碰到我，但是她不理我。
*He never takes notice of what I say．他從不理會我所說的話。1．remove 脫下
*Help me to take this handle off．幫我取下這個把手。
*Take your coat off and sit down．脫掉外衣坐下吧。
2．leave the ground and go up（飛機）起飛
*The plane is taking off．飛機要起飛了。
3．imitate；give an amusing imitation of 模仿
*Mary can take off her English teacher perfectly．瑪麗模仿她的英文老師維妙維肖。
*He takes that comedian off beautifully．他學那個喜劇演員學得極像。
4．reduce；subtract as a discount；deduct 減少；減去；打折扣
*They took off 25 per cent discount for each．他們每一個都打七五折。
*As the cover of the book was torn，the bookseller took 50p off．因為那本書的封皮已破，店主把書減價50便士。
5．remove from service or circulation；discontinue 取消班車等服務；中止
*Some local trains have been taken off，as there was no demand for them．一些區間火車已被取消，因為用不著了。
*The 7 a．m．express to London will be taken off next month．上午7點開往倫敦的快車下月將取消。
*The play was taken off after six performances．這齣戲演了6場後停演了。
6．amputate 截除
*The surgeon took off his arm．外科醫生截除了他的手臂。
7．lead away 帶走
*The child was taken off by kidnappers．那孩子被綁匪拐走了。
*The guard took him off to prison．看守人員把他帶到監獄去了。
8．leave hurriedly；depart 急忙離開；啟程
*He took off yesterday for Beijing．他昨天啟程去北京了。
*The sharp criticism made him take off in a fit of temper．尖銳的批評使他忿然離去。
*He grabbed his bag and took off for the meeting．他抓起包就匆匆忙忙地去開會了。
9．reduce（weight）減輕（體重）
*She took off three pounds last month．她上個月體重減輕了3磅。
*To take off pounds，you don't have to cut down the amount of food you eat，but the number of calories．為了減輕體重，你不必減少食量，只需減少飲食中的熱量就行了。
10．remove by death；kill 殺死；致死
*He was taken off by cholera．他被霍亂送掉了性命。
*Millions were taken off by the plague．那場瘟疫奪走了成百萬人的生命。
11．have（a period of time）as a break from work or as a holiday；absent oneself from work；ask for leave 有（一段時間）的休息或休假；不去上班；度假；請假
I took a week off in March and I'm taking Easter off，too．我在3月份休息了一周，還要在復活節休假。
*I was tired out，so I took the day off．我疲勞極了，所以那天我休息了一天。
*I'd like to take next Monday off to visit my sister in hospital．我想下星期一請假去醫院看我姐姐。
12．drink off；swallow 飲盡；吞下
*He took off a bottle of beer at one draught．他一口氣喝完了一瓶啤酒。give honor，praise and respect to 向…致敬；稱讚；頌揚
*He was indeed a courageous man and I took off my hat to him．他確實是個勇敢的人，我佩服他。
*You've done a remarkably fine job－I take off my hat to you．你幹得太出色了，我向你致敬。become angry with 對…發怒
*She took offence at what he did．她對他的所作所為感到惱火。
*He always takes offence at any kind of criricism．他總是對批評意見感到生氣。
*She took offence at what I said，but I meant no offence．她對我的話生了氣，但我無意冒犯她。1．employ僱傭
*Our factory will take on twenty more workers next month．我們廠下個月將再僱用20名工人。
*No more workers are being taken on at present．眼下不再招收工人。
2．undertake 承擔
*She takes on extra work on Sundays．她星期天還承擔了額外工作。
*Is he willing to take on the responsibility？他願意承擔責任嗎？
*I'll take the work on，but I can't tell you exactly when I'll finish it．我會承擔這項工作，可我不能確切地告訴你什麼時候完成。
*You should never take on more than you can do．你切莫承擔力不能及的工作。
3．become excited；show great emotion（excitement，grief or anger）激動；表現出強烈的感情（激動、悲痛、氣憤等）
*At the news of her husband's death she took on like a mad woman．聽到丈夫逝世的消息，她傷心得像瘋了一樣。
*She took on something dreadful when she was accused of telling lies．當被指控說謊時，她的臉部表情很可怕。
*She took on terribly when her sister was so badly hurt．妹妹受傷這麼厲害，她傷心得不得了。
*The indignant passenger took on about the rudeness of the bus conductor．憤怒的乘客對公共汽車售票員的粗魯無禮發起火來了。
4．put on；take the appearance of；start to have the look of披上；帶上；呈現面貌
*Our institute has taken on a new look recently．我們學院最近面目一新。
*The city took on a festive air．全市呈現出一派節日景象。
*After the students put up Christmas decorations，the classroom took on a holiday appearance．同學們掛上聖誕裝飾後，教室裡呈現出一片節日的景象。
*His writing has taken on a very peculiar style．他寫的作品體現了一種非常獨特的風格。
5．be generally adopted；become popular 被普遍接受；受大家的歡迎
*The idea somehow failed to take on．那主意不知為何未被大家接受。
*The new style didn't take on，so it was quickly dropped．這種新式樣沒有能夠流行，於是很快就被淘汰了。
*I didn't expect pointed shoes to take on，but they have．我原來以為尖頭皮鞋不會流行，可還真的流行了。
6．accept as an opponent in a contest；accept the challenge of（在競賽中）接受…作為對手；接受…的挑戰
*We knew their football team was bigger and stronger，but we took them on anyway and beat them．我們知道他們的足球隊比我們強大，但是我們仍然和他們比賽，而且把他們打敗了。
*I don't mind playing against a beginner，like myself，but I'm not going to take on someone who has been playing chess for years．跟一個像我自己一樣的初學者比賽我不反對，但是我不會接受和一個下了多年棋的對手進行比賽。
7．load; receivefor carrying； be loaded with； allow to enter裝載；接納；允許進入
*The tanker took on water at that port．油船在那個港口加了水。
*A big ship was at the dock taking on automobiles in crates to carry overseas for sale．一艘大船停在碼頭上裝載用板條箱運送的汽車，將它們運到海外去銷售。
*The bus driver stopped to take the children on．公共汽車停下讓孩子們上車。
8．absorb; acquire吸收；獲得
*The cloth took on red from the skirt that was washed in the same tub．那塊布跟裙子在一個盆裡洗染上了紅色。accept punishment without com plaining願受處罰
*Having admitted that he failed to do his part， he was willing to take his medicine and pay for the resulting damage．他承認自己沒有盡到責任，甘願受罰並賠償損失。
*The boy said he was sorry he broke the window and was ready to take his medicine．那個男孩說他打碎了窗戶感到很抱歉，並甘願受罰。get one's revenge報仇
*At last he took his revenge on the enemy．最後，他向敵人報了仇。
*He felt it his duty to take revenge on his uncle for the murder of his father．他感到向他叔叔報殺父之仇是他的責任。do sth． without hurrying不急；慢慢來
*You can take your time writing the article．寫這篇文章你不要搶時間。
*Let's sit down． Take your time and tell me all about it．咱們坐下來，不著急，你慢慢講，把事情全部告訴我。do…in allotted order輪流做…
*Like the other workers， he takes his turn at household chores．就像別的工人一樣，他也輪流做些家務。1．accompany； lead or carry forth into the open air， or from a private to a public place or into society陪伴；帶…出去或到公共場所等
*I am going to take Smith out this evening．今晚我要陪史密斯出去。
*Bob takes his wife out to the theatre every weekend, but my husband hasn't taken me out for months．鮑勃每逢週末都陪同夫人去看戲，可我丈夫有好幾個月沒帶我出門了。
*If you go overseas, will you take the family out with you？假如你出國，你會帶全家一同去嗎？
*The weather is perfect for taking the family out for a walk．這種天氣帶全家出來散步好極了。
2．take from a place where sth． is kept取出
*The students took out their textbooks and started reading．學生們拿出課本，開始閱讀。
*His tooth had such a large hole in it that it had to be taken out．他的牙齒上有個大洞，一定得拔掉。
*The surgeon took out his appendix.外科醫生切除了他的闌尾。
3．purchase；apply for and obtain 領取；申請並得到
*We must take out fire insurance on our home．我們務必要給家產保火災險。
*He took out a licence the day before yesterday．他前天領到了執照。
*As soon as he got married he took out an insurance policy which would grarantee his wife a regular income for the rest of her life,should he die．他一結婚就申請得到一張保險單，保證在他死後他的妻子在晚年有定期的收入。
*Mary and John took out a marriage licence．瑪麗和約翰領了結婚證。
4．remove（stain， colour， etc．）去掉（污漬、顏色等）
*Have you anything that will take out this inkstain from my dress?你有什麼東西可以去掉我衣服上的墨水污漬嗎？
*This liquid is good for taking out stains．這種液體去污漬很靈。
*He took out the pencil marks from his drawing．他擦掉了他的畫上的鉛筆記號。
5．begin to run開始跑
*When the window broke， the boys took out in all directions．窗子打破時，孩子們四處跑開了。
*When the wind blew his hat off，Charlie took out affter it．當帽子被風刮走時，查理跟在後面追。
6．set out； start出發
*He will take out for home next month．他下月啟程回家。
*They took out for the nearest beach．他們出發去最近的一個海灘。
7．take as an equivalent; obtain or receive the value of in another form用（物）抵債
*The firm agreed to take part of the debt out in goods. 這家商行同意用貨物來抵掉一部分債務。
*I owe you ＄50; can I take it out in beet and cigarattes？我欠你 50美元，可以用啤酒和香煙來抵充嗎？1．take the ownership or control of; assume management of or responsibility for接管；接收
*When he retired， his eldest son took over the farm．他退休時，他的長子接管了農場。
*Henry's taken over the running of the family firm from his old father．亨利從年邁的父親手裡接管了自家的商行。
*We will take over thefactory．我們將接管這家工廠。
*The new department head took over yesterday．新的系主任昨天接任。
2．borrow; imitate；adopt借用；模仿；採用
*They have taken over many European ways of life．他們已襲用了許多歐洲的生活方式。do sth． carefully and conscientiously 耗盡心血；費力
*She takes great pdins in educating her children．她耗盡心血教育子女。
*He always takes great pains to do his work well．他總是盡心盡力把工作做好。
*We can see that you've taken pains over your article， but it is too long．我們能看出你在文章上下了不小的功夫，但它還是太長了。participate in參加
*He took part in the sports meet and won two gold medals．他參加了運動會，獲得兩枚金牌。pity; feel sorry for同情
*Mary took pity on the old woman and asked her to live in her own apartment．瑪麗同情那位老人，讓她住在自己的公寓裡。happen發生
*Great changes have taken place in our country since liberation.我國解放以來發生了很大的變化。have satisfaction or enjoyment in 對…滿意；樂意做
*He takes great pleasure in teaching his little sister．他很樂意教他的小妹妹。become owner of佔有；擁有
*You can't take possession of the house until all the papers have been signed．所有文件都簽好之後房子才歸你所有。shelter oneself from danger避難
*He wanted to take refuge in the cellar．他想在地下室裡躲避一下。blame； find fault with責備；挑剔
*He often takes his son to task for not studying hard．他常常責備兒子學習不努力。favor one party over another袒護My brother always takes sides with my sister．我哥哥總是袒護我妹妹。prepare a strategy for dealing with sth．and put it into action採取措施
*We must take steps to prevent this from happening again．我們必須採取措施，以免再發生這種事。
*The factory has taken steps to speed up production．工廠已採取步驟加快生產。
*Theft became such a problem in this town that the police had to take steps to stop it immediately．盜竊行為在這個城裡極為嚴重，警察不得不立即採取措施加以制止。address a public meeting發表演說
*When our representative took the floor，a hush fell over the audience．我們的代表發言時，聽眾席鴉雀無聲。do sth． with ungranted and sometimes improper familiarity冒昧；冒失
*Please excuse me for taking the liberty to write to you．恕我冒昧寫信給你。
*I took the liberty of borrowing your dictionary while you are absent．你不在時我冒昧借用了你的詞典。replace代替；取代
*Plastics have taken the place of many conventional materials．塑料已取代了許多傳統材料。1．begin to apply ordevote oneself to 開始從事；養成（某種習慣）
*Itook to smoking ten years ago．我10年前開始抽煙。
*Some of the plants formerly producing machines have taken to making parts．有些工廠原來生產整部機器，現在開始生產零件。
*If a man once takes to gambling,it's difficult for him to break the habit．一個人一旦染上賭博的習慣，是很難戒掉的。
*I have taken to playing golf at weekends．我養成了在週末打高爾夫球的習慣。
2．be fond of喜歡
*He has really taken to that child．他確實喜歡那孩子。
*I took to stampcollecting last year.我是去年愛上集郵的。
*How has Billy taken to his new school？貝利是如何喜歡上他的新學校的？
*I tried to teach him to type， but he didn't seem to take to．我試圖教他打字，但他似乎對此不感興趣。
*I took to him immediately we met．我們一見面我就喜歡上他了。
3．have recourse to（usn． for safety）求助於（常出於安全原因）
*When the ship was wrecked， the passengers on board took to the life boats．輪船失事時，船上的旅客們乘上了救生艇逃生。
4．go to；betake oneself to去；往
*Thousands of people took to the streets to welcome the returningcombat heroes．成千上萬的人湧上街頭，歡迎歸來的戰鬥英雄們。
*When he is in a bad mood， he usually takes to his room without saymg anything．他情緒不好時，通常去他自己的房間，什麼話也不說。begin to run or run away逃走
*The criminal took to his heels but was soon caught by the police．罪犯逃跑了，但很快就被警察抓了起來。do sth． in turn輪流
*All his children take turns in looking after him．他的孩子輪流照顧他。
*There was only one dictionary so the three students had to take turns using it．只有一本詞典，因此 3個學生只好輪流用。1．allow（ passengers， etc．） to mount； stop and accept停車接納乘客
*The cars took their passengers up outside the hotel．那些汽車在旅館外面接納乘客。
*The bus stopped to take up passengers．公共汽車停下來讓乘客上車。
*The train stops here to take up more passengers，and then goes fast all the way to London. 火車在這裡停下來，再讓一些乘客上車，然後就直抵倫敦。
2．occupy（time， space， etc．）佔有（時間，空間等）
*This work will take up a lot of my time．這項工作將佔去我很多時間。
*I must get rid of this large table;it takes up too much room．我得把這個大桌子拿走，它太佔地方。I'm sorry to have taken up so much of your valuable time．佔用了你那麼多寶貴時間，真抱歉。
3．continue； resume繼續做；接著…講
*I put the telephone down and took up the work again．我放下電話繼續工作。
*She took up her sewing after the visitor had gone．客人走後她繼續做她的針線活。
4．assume（a position， office， atti tude，etc．）擔任；承擔（職位）；採取態度
*When does the new director take up his post? 新的主任什麼時候走馬上任？
*He will take up his new post on October 1．他將在10月1日就任新職。
*The new president took up office yesterday．新總統昨天就職。
*A most aggressive attitude was taken up by the next speaker．第 2個發言人採取了非常放肆的態度。
5．adopt sth． as a profession， hobby， subject for study， etc．從事某種職業；對某事有愛好；從事一項研究或學習
*When he left school he took up journalism．離開學校以後，他就從事了新聞工作。
*Rich people can afford to take up whatever hobbies they like．富人有能力從事他們所喜歡的任何愛好。
*I think I'll take up oil pointing in my spare time．我想我將要在業餘時間練習油畫。
*The scientist has taken up a new subject．這位科學家已開始研究一個新的課題。
6．pull and make tight or shorter;shorten縮緊；減短
*The tailor took up the legs of the trousers. 裁縫把褲子改短了。
7．gather in（a contribution，etc.）； collect募捐；收集（錢等）
*The girls will take up a collection at the end of the concert．這些女孩子在音樂會結束後要募捐。
*All the tickets were taken up at the exit．所有的車票都在出口處被收去了。
8．take away； lift up; raise拿走；拿起；舉起
*The driver has had his license taken up for violating traffic regulations．因為違反交通規則，那個駕駛員的執照被吊銷了。
*He took up the telephone receiver and asked a number. 他拿起電話詢問一個電話號碼。
9．remove by taking in把…吸進去；溶解
*This kind of paper claims to be able to take up more liquid than any other kind．這種紙據說比其它任何紙吸水性都強。
*The vacuum cleaner took up the dirt from the rug．吸塵器把地毯上的灰塵吸掉了。
*10．raise consideration of提出商討；提出考慮
*They decided to take the matter up at the plenary meeting．他們決定在全會上把這件事提出來。
*The question of public housing should be taken up with the Minister whose responsibility it is．公眾的住房問題應該提交負責這項工作的部長考慮。
*He said he would take up my difficulties with the headmaster．他說要把我的問題提出來和校長商量解決。
*The matter will be taken up at the next Party branch meeting．下一次黨支部會議將著手處理此事。
11．arrest逮捕
*The police took him up on a drugs charge．警察以吸毒的罪名逮捕了他。
*Within two hours the arsonist was taken up by the police. 縱火犯在兩小時內就被警察抓住了。
12．establish oneself in在…安居下來
*He took up his permanent residence in Beijing after graduation. 他畢業後在北京定居下來。
13．interrupt by dissent； interrupt andcorrect；rebuke；reprimand （為表示異議等）打斷（某人的話）；打斷並更正；指責；責備
*He took me up short on that point．我講到那個問題時他突然打斷了我的話。
*She said something very absurd and we immediately took her up.她說了些非常荒謬的話，我們立即打斷了她的話。
14．understand理解
*Please don't take me up wrongly.請別誤解我的意思。
15．adopt sb． as a protege提攜；把…當作被保護人；幫助
*Though a busy and successful nowelist， he was willing to take up any promising young writer and give him all the help he could．雖然他是一個很忙而又很有成就的小說家，但他願意提攜任何有前途的青年作家並給予一切可能的幫助。take-home pay
