*I'll take her along with me．我將帶她一道走。believe what sb．says is true 相信某人的話
*I don't take him at his word because I think he's leading us on．我不信他的話，因為我認為他在騙我們。
*You shouldn't take him at his word．你不該信他的話。
*If you say that I can leave all my work to you while I'm out，I'll take you at your word．如果你說我走後把我的所有工作都能交給你，我將相信你的話。1. be seriously affected by； have deep concern or grief over深為…影響；對…非常擔心或悲傷
*He took his brother's death very much to heart．他哥哥的死對他打擊很大。
*Don't take your loss to heart； you can always start again. 不要把失敗放在心上，你總是可以再干的。
*She took her failure in the examination to heart．她因考試不及格而非常傷心。
*He took his friend's advice to heart．朋友對他的勸告對他影響很大。
2．take seriously認真對待
*I hope they will take to heart the warning I have given them. 我希望他們能認真對待我對他們的警告。
*I have not much hope that my words will be taken to heart．他們對我的話是否會認真對待，對此我不抱多大希望。be proud of以…為自豪
*He takes pride in the success of his children.他為孩子們的成功而感到自豪。
*She takes a pride in her library．她以自己的藏書而自豪。assume powers beyond what one should超出個人權力範圍承擔（某事）；擅自
*He took it upon himself to cancel the contract without consulting any of his colleagues．他不同任何同事商量就擅自取消了合同。
*That fellow takes too much upon himself；anyone would think he was the manager．那個傢伙太會自作主張多管事，任何人都會以為他是經理。ta.kin
