5(U)
a. 像人類說話似的聲音 [鳴叫聲] 
b. 隱語,黑話; 方言spend time in talking在談話中度過
*The young lovers talked the night away．這對年輕的情人談了一夜。speak boastingly； make exaggerated statements or excessive claims in order to impress people說大話；吹大牛；言過其實以期引人注目
*He always talked big, but never amounted to anything．他總是誇口，但毫無成就。
*We dislike those who talk big and do nothing．我們不喜歡那些專講大話而不做事的人。
*I don't believe all he says about the profits he is making; ever since I have known him he has liked to talk big．我不相信他說他正在賺錢的那一套話，自從我認識他起，我就知道他愛吹牛。1．make silent by talking louder or longer高聲壓過（別人的話）；使啞口無言
*He tried to argue back but his opponent talked him down．他想反駁，但他的對手高聲壓倒了他的話。
*Such an eloquent man will easily talk us down．這樣一個有口才的人，很容易把我們駁得啞口無言。
2．speak disparagingly of; belittle 說…壞話；貶低
*The hostile newspapers talked down the importance of the Minister's arrival here．持敵對態度的報紙對部長來此訪問的重要性加以貶低。
3．give radio instructions for landing an airplane because of instrument failure or poor visibility（因儀器故障或能見度低）用無線電通訊引導飛機降落
*His flying instruments have all been destroyed by enemy gunfire，so the air traffic controllers will have to talk him．他的飛行器械都給敵人的炮火擊毀了，所以機場導航員只能通過無線電講話引導他降落。
4．use words or ideas that are too easy用太簡單的字或觀念
*The speaker talked down to the students， and they were bored．演講者講的內容太簡單，學生們都聽得不耐煩了。
5．speak in a condescending or superior manner以高人一等的口吻說話
*She talks down to everyone，particularly young people．她對誰講話都擺出高人一等的樣子，特別是對青年人。
*The audience do not like being talked down to．聽眾不喜歡聽人用高人一等的口吻同他們講話。persuade by talking說服（某人）干（某事）
*Can you talk father into buying a new car？你能說服父親買一輛新車嗎？
*A clever salesman can talk a person into buying something he does not really want．一個聰明的售貨員能說服一個人買他並不真正想買的東西。
*At last we talked him into consent．最後我們說服了他，他表示同意。sth． that has become very popular or of great prominence家喻戶曉的事情；大家談論的話題
*Their love affair has become the talk of the town．他倆談戀愛的事成了眾所周知的事情。
*Recent nudity on the New York stage has been the talk of the town.最近紐約舞台上出現裸體的事情已經成為街談巷議的話題。
*His success has become the talk of the town.他的成功已成為大家談論的話題。1．mention談到；說到
*In his lecture，Professor Wang talked of peaceful uses of atomic energy．在講座中，王教授談到了和平利用原子能。
*We have talked of what we shall do next．我們討論了下一步該幹什麼。
*We are just talking of the most exciting book that we have tead recently．我們正在談論最近讀過的一本十分動人的書。
2．debate as a possibility; discuss 討論…之可行性；討論
*The two companies have been talking about a merger．這兩家公司一直在討論合併的可能性。
*What are you talking of？你們正談論什麼？persuade； dissuade sb． from doing sth. 勸阻…不做
*Jim wants to give up his job; can you talk him out of such a foolish idea？吉姆想辭職，你能否勸他放棄這個愚蠢的想法？
*He planned to have a duel with John，but we talked him out of it.他打算和約翰決鬥，但我們勸阻了他。
*Once he has set his mind on a course of action he is not to be talked out of it．一旦他下決心採取某一個行動，誰也說服不了他。
*I'd like to go camping，but my wife's trying to talk me out of it．我想去野營，可是我妻子竭力勸阻我。1．consider； discuss in detail考慮；討論
*Come to my office and we will talk it over．請到我辦公室來討論一下這個問題。
*Jim always talks things over with his parents before he makes an important decision.吉姆在做重要決定之前總是先與父母商量一下。
*I suggest we talk the matter over in earnest．我建議，我們認真討論一下這件事。
2．cause sb．to change his opinion；convince by talking說服（某人）改變立場；說明
*He is very good at talking opponents over to his viewpoing.他善於說服對方改變立場贊成他的觀點。1．persuade； convince勸說；說服At first my friend refused to fall in with the scheme we had suggested， but eventually I managed to talk him round．起初我的朋友不同意我們提出的計劃，但我終於設法說服了他。
*I don't know whether I can talk him round．我不知道我能否使他回心轉意。
2．avoid approaching（a subject）directly兜圈子談（問題）
*He didn't really come to the point；he just talked round it．他其實並沒有講到點子上，而只是在兜圈子。speak to sb．at great length對某人講得太多
*He's been talking my head off．他一直跟我嘮叨不休。talk show
<<可數名詞>>
(電視、廣播節目的) 訪問節目,脫口秀
(節目主持人與上節目者之談話等節目)1．speak to同…談話
*Don't talk to that rough boy any more．不要同那個粗野的男孩再談下去了。
*The teacher is talking to some students on the campus．老師正在校園裡和一些學生談話。
2．reprove責罵
*I'll talk to him when he gets home．他回來時我會教訓他的。
*He talked to them very sharply.他嚴厲地訓斥了他們。
*The boy needs to be talked to．這男孩需要好好教訓一下。1．speak loudly and clearly大聲而清晰地講
*The teacher asked the student to talk up．老師叫那個學生大聲說清楚。
*Please talk up a bit; we can't hear you．請大聲點，我們聽不見你的話。
2．speak without hesitation；speak distinctly and openly坦白地說；直率地講
*If you thought that wasn't fair，why didn't you talk up？ 如果你認為那不公平，為什麼不坦率地說出來？
*George isn't afraid to talk up when he disagrees with the teacher．喬治不同意老師的意見時，就直言不諱。
3．speak in favor of; discuss enthusiastically 為…說好話；讚揚；熱烈討論
*This dictionary was talked up by the students. 這本詞典受到學生們的好評。
*The committee talked up late last night．昨晚委員會討論熱烈，直到深夜。talk-back
