think nothing of?consider; recall考慮；回想
*It's certainly an offer well worth thinking about．這當然是很值得考慮的報價。
*She is thinking about her childhood days．她在回想童年時代的生活。think factory
= think tankrespect greatly對…以高度評價；讚揚
*His students think highly of his teaching. 學生對他的教學十分讚賞。consider unimportant輕視
*They think little of the difficulties and setbacks on their way forward．他們對前進道路上的艱難險阻視若等閒。1．consider； give attention to考慮；關心
*I have many things to think of at the moment．目前，我有許多事情要考慮。
*When I said that, I was not thinking of her feelings．我講那話時，並沒有考慮到她的感情。
*The department leadership is thinking of adding another recording room to the phonetics lab．系領導正在考慮給語音實驗室增加一個錄音室。
*There are many things which have to be thought of before we finally make up our minds to emigrate．在下決心移居國外之前，我們有很多事情不得不考慮。
2．imagine想像
*Can you think of why she should do such a thing？你能想像得出她為什麼幹這樣一件事嗎？
3．have an opinion about； form or have an idea of思索；認為；對某事持某種看法
*You said nothing at the meeting．What were you thinking of then？你在會上一言不發，當時在想些什麼？
*What do you think of my new shoes？你認為我的新鞋子如何？
*They don't think much of his work．他們認為他的工作不怎麼樣。
4．take into account; have in one's mind為…著想；關心
*He always thinks of other people first， never of himself．他總是先想到別人，從不想到自己。
5．remember記得；想起
*I know his face， but I can't think of where I've met him. 我看他面熟，可想不起在哪兒見過他了。
*Will you think of me sometimes？你有時會想起我嗎？
6．consider as a possibility； anticipate認為有一種可能；預料
*I'd never think of asking someone to lend me so much money！我從未想過要向別人借這麼多錢！
*We just wouldn't think of going without you．我們決不會想到把你丟下就走。work out； reason out想出；推想出
*I must think out a way of solving the problem．我必須想出一個解決這個問題的辦法。
*His arguments have obviously been well thought out．他的論點很明顯是經過周密思考而產生的。consider carefully仔細考慮
*I'll think over what he suggested．我將仔細考慮他的建議。
*When you've thought things over，you'll probably realize that my idea is quite good after all．你把情況認真加以思考之後，就可能會意識到，我的想法畢竟是相當不錯的。
*You must think it over before you answer．你得先考慮一下再回答。think piece
