throw off
(1) → v.t. 5a
(2) [~ +off+ n.] 拋掉 <累贅、包袱> ; 斷絕 <與…的> 關係; 甩掉 <追趕者>1．discard； lose or let slip by foolishness or neglect拋棄；因愚蠢或疏忽而失去或放棄
*He has thrown away a good opportunity．他已經失去了一個良好的機會。
*You are throwing away your chance of becoming a success．你在錯過成功的機會。
2．fail to use棄而不用
*My advice was thrown away upon him．我的忠告被他當作耳邊風。
3．use in a foolish or wasteful manner浪費
*You are throwing your money away，buying such useless things．你買這些沒有用的東西是在浪費錢。
*He thinks nothing of throwing away a thousand dollars at the gambling house.他在賭場裡一擲千金滿不在乎。1．straighten挺直
*We should throw back our ahoulders and accept the challenge．我們應該挺起胸膛，接受挑戰。
2．delay the progress or advance of；check；repulsevigorously 推遲；阻止
*His illness threw him back a year at school．他因病耽誤了一年在校學習時間。
*The cold he caught threw back his recovery from rheumatism.感冒拖延了他風濕病痊癒的時間。
3．push back； force to go back to;cause to rely使回到；使依靠
*She has been thrown back on her savings．她又不得不依靠自己的積蓄。
*After this failure to get help we were thrown back upon our own resources. 這次求援失敗後，我們只有回過頭來依靠自己的力量了。delay延誤
*The heavy snow threw the train behind．那場大雪使火車誤了點。1． get rid of擺脫掉
*She finds it difficult to throw off her pursuers．她發現很難擺脫追求她的人。
2．overthrow推翻
*They attempted to throw off the government．他們企圖推翻政府。eject 逐出
*We'll throw him out of the club．我們將把他逐出俱樂部。throw pillow
靠枕
