指著塔
with one's back to the fire 
背向火
b. [含到達之意表示方向; cf. from 1] 迄…,到…,至…,達…
go to the office 
去公司上班
I have often been ~ India. 
我常到印度去
Something dropped to the floor. 
有東西掉到地板上
→ from PLACE to place.
c. 在…方
Their house is to the north of the park. 
他們的房子在公園的北面
2 (變) 成…, (變) 得…
rise to wealth 
變成富有
grow to manhood 
長大成人
The light has changed to red. 
信號燈轉為紅色
3 a. 到…,至…
from beginning to end 
自始至終
count from one to thirty 
從一數到三十
all wet to the skin 
濕透
b. 至…,到…的程度,成…,得…
tear a letter to pieces 
把信撕成碎片
to the best of my belief [knowledge] 
在我所相信 [知道] 的範圍之內,據我所信 [知] 
to that [this] extent 
到那 [這] 個程度
They were killed to the last man. 
他們被殺到最後一個人 [被趕盡殺絕] 
4 
a. 令 (某人) …的是,令 (某人) …地
to my surprise [joy, disappointment, sorrow] 
令我驚訝 [歡喜,失望,傷心] 的是
b. [引導表示結果、效果之片語] 
to one's cost 
對某人有損失[不利]; 歸某人負擔
to no purpose 
白白地,徒然
to the point [purpose] 
適切 [中肯] 地
5 
a. 到…
stay to the end of June 
停留到六月底
put the meeting off to next Saturday 
把集會延期到下星期六
from one to four o'clock 
從一點鐘到四點鐘
It's still about an hour to supper. 
離晚餐時間大約還有一個鐘頭
b. (時刻為) …差 (幾分鐘) ( (美)of,before) 
at (a) quarter to eight 
在八時差一刻 [七點四十五分] 時
It's ten (minutes) to four. 
現在是四時差十分鐘
6 為…,以便…
He came to my rescue. 
他來救我
We sat down to dinner. 
我們坐下來吃晚餐
7 對著…,與…相對著
sit face to face [back to back] 
面對面 [背靠背] 而坐
fight hand to hand 
短兵相接; 肉搏
8 
a. 對…
Listen to me. 
聽我說
I'd like to talk to you. 
我想跟你談談
There can be no answer to this problem. 
對這個問題無法回答 [無計可施] 
b. 為…
drink to (the health of) Mr. Johnson 
為約翰生先生乾杯
Here's to you. [. 
乾杯時之用語] 祝你健康
create a monument to (the memory of) a national hero 
為紀念一位民族英雄而建立一座紀念碑
c. [引導相當於間接受詞之片語] 對…
I gave all of them to him. 
我把它們全都給了他
d. 對…而言,對…
That's very important to me. 
那對我很重要
To her it looked like a rabbit. 
在她看來,它像隻兔子
9 在…,於…,在…之上,加在…
apply soap to a cloth 
把肥皂抹在布上
He put his ear to the door. 
他把耳朵貼在門上
He fastened a shelf to the wall. 
他把擱架裝在牆上
They live next door to us. 
他們住在我們隔壁
Add 25 to 36. 
三十六加上二十五
10 a. 符合…,配合…,依照…的
correspond to 
? 符合…
→ ACCORDING to
made to order 
定制的
to one's taste 
合某人的嗜好 [口味] 
work to a plan 
依照計畫工作
b. 應…
→ rise to the OCCASION
The dog came to my whistle. 
我一吹口哨,狗就來了 [我吹口哨,狗就應聲而來] 
c. 合著…,隨著…
dance to the music 
隨音樂跳舞
11 a. 與… (比較) ,較…,比…
Compared to his brother, he isn't particularly brilliant. 
跟他哥哥[弟弟]比較起來,他並不特別聰穎
Her skill is superior [inferior] to yours. 
她的技術比你的高明 [低劣] 
I prefer walking to driving. 
我喜歡步行甚於駕車
My work is nothing to what you've done. 
跟你所做過的比較起來,我的工作不算什麼
b. 對…,…比…
one penny to the pound 
每磅一便士
→ TEN to one
Reading is to the mind what food is to the body. 
閱讀之於智力如同食物之於身體
12 …的,對…而言的
a key to the door 
門的鑰匙
brother to the King 
國王之弟
I have no right to the use of the land. 
我沒有那塊地的使用權
B [加在動詞原形之前引導不定詞] 
1 [名詞用法] 做…
a. 
To err is human, to forgive divine. 
犯錯乃人之常情,寬恕則是超凡的 [犯錯在人,寬恕在神] 
It is foolish to read such a book. 
讀這樣的書是愚蠢的
b. 
I began to think so. 
我開始那樣想
c. 
The best way is to visit the country. 
最好之方法是訪問該國
2 [形容詞用法] 做…的,做…之用的
He was the first to come and the last to leave. 
他是最早來最後走的人
I have [Thesomewhat在某種程度上
*You are right to a certain extent．在某種程度上你是對的。all without exception全體；一致
*The whole class，to a man，took part in the discussion. 全班每個人都參加了討論。（cooked） to just the proper degree （煮得）恰好
*The food was cooked to a turn and was very delicious. 飯菜烹調得當，非常好吃。apparently顯然
*What he said was to all appearances correct．他所說的顯然是正確的。back and forth來回地
*I saw him walking to and fro in his room at that time．我看見他那時在房間裡來回踱著步。certainly當然
*She is not pretty， to be sure， but she is very intelligent．她固然不漂亮，但她非常聰明。in the first place首先；第一點
*To begin with， there must be close cooperation between them．首先，在他們之間要有密切的合作。of no avail毫無結果
*He worked to no purpose．他只是徒勞而已。
*We spoke to little or no purpose．我們說話作用不大或者毫無作用。as far as I know（usu． used in negative form）就我所知
*To my knowledge， there is no such a saying in Chinese．就我所知，漢語中沒有這種說法。to a standing position站立著；起身
*His wife's call brought him quickly to his feet．他夫人的呼喚使他急忙站起身來。to one's greatest satisfaction盡興地
*They played to their heart's content．他們痛快地玩了一場。in sb.'s opinion某人以為
*To my mind， he will fail in the examination．我認為他考試不會及格的。to sb.'s liking投某人所好；適合某人口味
*The food he cooks is to my taste.他做的飯菜合我的口味。to sb.'s honor是某人的榮譽
*It's greatly to your Creait that you succeeded．取得成功是你莫大的光榮。resulting in sb．'s disappointment 使某人失望
*To her great disappointment，it rained on the day of the picnic．野餐那天下了雨，使她大失所望。in sb.'s presence當某人的面
*I can ever say that to his face.我甚至可以當他的面說那件事。first； for one thing首先；第一；開始
*To start with，I haven't enough reference books．首先，我沒有足夠的參考書。to the opposite effect相反地
*I will come on Monday unless you write me to the contrary．我將於星期一來，除非你寫信叫我不要來。
*I have heard nothing to the contrary．我還沒有聽到任何相反的情況。to the import that； meaning大意是；含意是
*I have received a cable to the effect that someone would come to see me．我收到一封電報，大意是說有人要來看我。entirely完全
*I am very busy and my time is occupied to the full．我很忙，沒有一點空閒時間。to the end到最後；到底
*They fought to the end．他們戰鬥到最後。relevant中肯
*His speech was very long and not to the point．他的演講冗長而且不切題。up to this time直到現在
*I still don't know her name to this day．直到現在我還不知道她的姓名。to-and-fro
