熱使牛奶變酸
4 使<食物等>變質,使…腐敗
Hot weather ~s meat. 
熱天氣使肉腐壞
<<不及物動詞>>
A
1 旋轉
(
→ v.t. A【同義字】) 
a. 轉,旋轉
This tap will not ~. 
這旋塞轉不動
The Ferris wheel is ~ing slowly. 
摩天輪緩緩地轉動著
He ~ed on his heel(s). 
他用腳跟轉身 [急向後轉] 
The earrefuse to listen to對…置之不理；對…置若罔聞
*He has turned a deaf ear to what his parents said．他對父母的話置之不理。oppose（often after earlier support）對…採取敵對態度；反抗
*He turned against his best friends．他對最好的朋友也採取了敵對態度。make a complete turn in order to face in the opposite direction轉身；轉向
*please help me to turn the car around．請幫我將車調過頭來。1．turn in a different direction轉向別處
*Please don't turn your head away while I am talking to you．我和你談話時，請不要把臉轉過去。
2．refuse to admit不許進入
*Hundreds of people were turned away from the theatre．數以百計的人未能獲准進入劇場。return返回
*They walked for two hours and then turned back．他們走了兩小時後又返回來了。turn bridge
旋開橋1．refuse to accept； reject拒絕
*I am afraid your request for a pay rise was turned down again．恐怕你們要增加工資的要求又一次被拒絕了。
2．reduce in speed or volume減弱；調低
*Please turn the radio down； I am trying to sleep．請將收音機音量調小，我想睡覺了。1．deliver送交
*Don't forget to turn in your gun when you leave the army．離開部隊時，別忘了把槍交上來。
2．go to bed睡覺
*I feel very tired and want to turn in now．我覺得很累，想現在就睡。1．enter by making a turn轉入
*There is a strange vehicle turning into our street．有一輛陌生的車子拐入了我們這條街。
2．transform into變成；譯成
*Turn the following Chinese into English．將下列漢語譯成英語。turn of the century
世紀轉換期
(一個世紀之末期與下一個世紀之初期)switch off關掉
*Please turn the lights off when you leave the room. 離開房間時請把燈關掉。1．switch on打開
*Please turn the lights on for me；it's getting dark．天黑了，請幫我打開燈。
2．turn against攻擊；反對
*The dog turned on me and bit me in the leg. 這狗向我撲來，咬了我的腿。1．turn rudely away； refuse to speak to不理睬
*Never turn your back on backward students. 決不能漠視落後的學生。
2．refuse to help 拒絕幫忙
*Don't turn your back on those who really need help．對那些確實需要幫助的人不要拒絕。
*He never turned his back on his neighbors when they needed help.他的鄰居需要幫助時，他從未置之不理。
3．abandon放棄
*He turned his back on the old working method．他放棄了老的工作方法。1．result結果證明
*What he had said turned out false.他的話結果證明是假的。
2．produce生產
*The school has turned out some good scholars．該校培養出了一些優秀的學者。
3．appear出現
*A lot of people turned out for the rally．許多人參加了集會。1．give control to； give ownership to 移交（管理權、業務等）
*Since the original owner was now too old to hold on to his business， he turned it over to his son. 原來的主人因年邁而不能繼續從業，就轉交給他兒子了。
*When the company president resigned， he turned control over to his associate. 公司總裁辭職時，把管理權讓給了副總裁。
2．hand over； turn in（to the police）上交（警察等）
*I turned the thief over to the police．我把竊賊交給了警方。
3．turn upside down翻轉
*The car turned over three times after the crash．撞車後，小汽車翻了3個觔斗。
4．think about carefully考慮
*You'd better turn the matter over．你最好考慮一下此事。1．move so as to face the other way轉臉
*Turning round，Isaw a snake crawling toward me.回過頭時，我看見一條蛇正向我爬來。
2．revolve旋轉
*The earth turns round the sun．地球繞太陽運行。turn signal
