lie in wait for?= lay wait for?埋伏等待…stay in a place（usu．idly and impatiently）在某處等待（通常指無聊地和不耐煩地）
*They waited about for another bus，but none came．他們不耐煩地等著下一輛公共汽車，可是一直沒有車來。
*Where have you been？I've been waiting around for you for more than an hour！你去哪兒了？我已等了你一個多小時！serve food侍候開飯；端菜送飯；（在餐館）當服務員
*The girl earns her pocket money by waiting at table in a restaurant．這女孩在一家餐館當服務員以掙些零花錢。1．serve；attend as a servant侍候；吃飯時作招待
*She waited on us at dinner．她在一旁侍候我們吃飯。
*The old lady does not like to be waited upon，because she thinks she is still capable of taking care of herself．那位老太太不喜歡別人侍候，因為她認為她生活還能自理。
2．follow as a consequence為…結果；隨…而產生
*Success waits on hard work．成功來自於勤奮。
*His whole future waits on the results of the examination．他的整個前程都取決於這次考試的結果。1．defeat by waiting以等待的方式挫敗
*We shall wait the enemy out，and watch them starve．我們將按兵不動，等著敵人斷糧挨餓。
*The enemy are still advancing，but we can wait them out in this valley．敵人還在前進，可我們可以按兵不動，使他們在這山谷裡不戰自敗。
2．await calmly and patiently the end of安靜而耐心地等待…結束
*The storm showed no sign of abating．We'd have to be patient and wait it out．風暴絲毫沒有減弱的跡象，我們只得耐心地等待它過去。1．delay going to bed熬夜等候
*I'll wait up for you tonight．今天晚上我不睡覺也要等你。
*I may be late，but please don't wait up for me．我可能晚回來，你先睡，不要等我。
2．stop and wait for sb．to catch up停下來等候別人趕上去。
*Don't go fast！Wait up for me！別走那麼快，等我一下。
*Hadn't we better wait up for theslower ones？我們是不是等一下後面的人？wait-a-bit
