8『棒球』四壞球上壘
an intentional ~
(戰略性的) 故意送上四壞球使對方上壘
walk of life
(社會上、經濟上的) 地位; 職業
persons from every ~ [all ~s ] of life 
各種行業1．win easily in a race or competition在比賽中輕而易舉地獲勝
*He walked away from all his competitors in the 3，000metre race．在3000米賽跑中，他遙遙領先於所有其他選手。
2．survive（an accident）with little or no injury從（事故中）平安脫身
*How could he walk away from a crash like that without a mark on him？他在那次車禍中怎麼會沒受一點傷而平安脫險的？
*He walked away from the shipwreck．在這次沉船事件中他平安脫險了。1．take and go away with；take away；steal取走；偷走；順手拿走
*Someone got in and walked awaywith the jewels while we were out．我們不在的時候，有人進來順手把珠寶偷走了。
*How can a thief walk off with a safe in broad daylight？一個小偷怎能在光天化日之下將一個保險箱偷走呢？
2．take，get or win easily輕而易舉地獲得或贏得
*He walked away with the election；his majority was about ten thousand．他多得1萬張左右的選票，輕而易舉地贏了這場選舉。
*Our team walked off with the championship．我隊輕而易舉地得了冠軍。
*We expected Peter to walk off with the prize，but he didn't．我們本來指望彼得會輕而易舉地獲獎，可他沒有。1．eat or drink greedily大吃大喝
*He walked into a dinner．他狼吞虎嚥地吃了一頓晚餐。
*The boy walked into a big bowl of chicken soup when the mistress was out visiting a neighbour．那男孩趁女主人出去串門的時候，把一大碗雞湯喝了個精光。
2．scold；attack責罵；申斥；攻擊；毆打
*He walks into us all as if it were our faults．他把我們大家大罵了一頓，好像是我們的過錯。
*I could hear the director walking into Jim for being late again．我可以聽到主任在責罵吉姆又一次遲到。
*Henry walked into his attackers．亨利毫不畏懼地向襲擊他的人衝去。
3．meet with through inattention 由於疏忽而遭到
*Mind you，don't walk into a trap！小心，別上當！way of living；manner in which people live；occupation生活方式；社會階層；行業
*The newsman interviewed people from all walks of life．記者採訪了各界人士。
*The banker did not want his son to marry a girl in a different walk of life．那個銀行家不想讓他兒子和一個不同社會階層的女子結婚。1．get rid of by walking用走路來消除
*I used to walk off my headache．我常常以散步來消除頭痛。
*He tried to walk off the effect of the drink．他試圖以散步來醒酒。
2．depart離開
*My father said no more and walked off．我父親沒有再說下去，轉身離開了。go away without notice不告而別
*He walked his chalks and went to Shanghai．他不辭而別去了上海。1．go on strike罷工
*Building workers walked out during the morning in protest of the sacking of a bricklayer．建築工人上午舉行罷工，抗議解雇一名砌磚工人。
*There's another strike threatening；some of the workers walked out today．又一次罷工迫近了，今天已有一些工人不幹活了。
2．leave in protest退席抗議
*The representatives of the offended country walked out when the opposing speaker took the floor．當對方發言時，受攻擊的國家代表退席以示抗議。
3．be in love談戀愛
*John and Mary are walking out．約翰和瑪麗在談戀愛。abandon；desert遺棄；拋棄
*You can't just walk out on us like this．你不能這樣丟下我們不管。
*Mike just walked out on his wife and family without saying a word．邁克一句話也沒說就丟下妻子兒女不管了。
*She treated him badly，but she never thought he'd walk out on her．她待他很不好，可她從不認為他會拋棄她。1．disregard the wishes or feelings of；treat like a slave；impose upon 無視（某人）的感情或願望；把…當奴隸對待；欺侮
*He would walk over other people to get what he wanted．他會無視別人的意願來達到自己的目的。
*Don't let your husband walk over you like that．別讓你丈夫那樣盛氣凌人對你。
2．defeat easily and by a wide margin輕易地打敗（而且分數相差甚多）；獲勝全不費工夫
*Joans simply walked over Brown in billiards．在檯球比賽中，瓊斯不費吹灰之力贏了布朗。walk shorts
= walking shortsact exactly as you are supposed to；behave properly；obey循規蹈矩；嚴格遵守；服從
*The young teacher took great pains to make his students walk the chalk．那位年輕教師費了好大的勁來使學生們遵守紀律。practise as a student to observe the methods of physicians and surgeons到醫院實習
*You have to walk the hospital for a time as part of your medical course．你必須在醫院實習一段時期，作為醫學課程的一部分。
*Medical students are required to walk the hospital for a period of time before their graduation．醫科大學生畢業前必須到醫院實習一段時間。1．go through（a play，an acting part，etc．）in a perfunctory manner馬馬虎虎地演或念台詞
*He didn't like the script and walked through his part．他不喜歡那個劇本，因此馬馬虎虎地扮演他的角色。
2．deal with or carry out perfunctorily敷衍了事地處理或做完
*He walked through the test．他草草地做完了試驗。walk-in
