<<名詞>>
1 (U)僅用一個顏色的水彩畫法
2 (C)一個顏色的水彩畫,墨畫wash goods
耐洗而不褪色之織物1．remove by washing洗掉
*Can you tell me how I can wash out these stains？你能告訴我怎樣洗掉這些污跡嗎？
*This stain didn't wash out．這個污跡洗不掉。
2．demolish by the action of water 沖掉；沖毀
*The embankment was washed out by the storm．路堤被暴雨沖毀了。
3．spoil by the action of rain，etc．因雨等受影響
*Bad weather has washed the game out．天氣不好影響了比賽。
*Today's football match has been washed out by a sudden downpour．今天的足球賽因突然下了一場大雨而取消了。
4．fail to qualify or continue；be eliminated被淘汰；沒有及格
*He was washed out after one semester．他讀了一個學期就被淘汰了。
5．deplete the strength or vitality of（usu．used in the passive voice）使累極；使精疲力盡（常用被動語態）
*I feel washed out；I shall stop working．我感到累極了，我將不幹了。
*She is washed out after her recent illness．最近她生了一場病，身體極其虛弱。
6．lose color；drain off color退色；因洗滌而掉色
*After the skirt had been cleaned，its bright red was washed out．這條裙子洗過以後，它那淺紅色就退掉了。wash sale
(股票市場為維持買賣興旺的假象而進行的) 虛拋,虛賣1．clean the dishes after a meal飯後洗餐具
*Have the dishes been washed up？餐具洗好了嗎？
*It's your turn to wash up today．今天該你洗碗了。
2．wash one's face and hands；have a wash洗手；洗臉；洗澡
*She washed up before lunch．她洗一洗才吃午飯。
3．exhausted；finished精疲力盡；完蛋
*After a day at the office I feel completely washed up．在辦公室幹了一天下來，我感到精疲力盡。
*Henry and Julie aren't lovers any more；they've washed up．亨利和朱麗已不再相愛，他們的戀愛關係已經結束了。
4．carry to shore將…衝上岸
*The body was washed up the following morning．屍體第2天早上給衝到了岸上。
*The incoming tide washed up cargo from the wrecked ship．上漲的潮水將失事船隻上的貨物衝到了岸邊。Wash, The
