men's [wear and tear
1 損耗; 磨損
Our products must stand ~. 
我們的產品必須經久耐用
2 折磨
the ~ of life 
生活的折磨1．disappear gradually through wear磨損
*The inscriptions on the stones have worn away．石頭上的碑文已經被磨損了。
*The footsteps of thousands of visitors had worn away the steps．台階已經被成千上萬參觀者的腳步磨平了。
2．be reduced until it disappears慢慢地消失
*He could feel pain again as the medicine wore away．藥性消退後，他又感到疼痛了。
*My patience is almost worn away by her endless complaints．她不停的抱怨已使我幾乎無法忍耐了。
3．（of time）pass slowly；（vigour，etc．）fade away（時間）慢慢地消逝；（精力等）衰退
*Don'k wear away your youth in trifles！不要虛度年華。
*The long winter wore away．漫長的冬天過去了。
*Being in prison for many years has wore away the prisoner's resistance．多年呆在監獄裡已經把那個罪犯的反抗精神給消磨掉了。1．reduce or impair by long wearing；erode磨掉；侵蝕
*The soles of my shoes are already worn down．It's time I got a new pair．我的鞋底磨破了，該換雙新鞋了。
*Wind and rain have worn the monument down．風雨將那座紀念碑侵蝕了。
2．exhaust；make or become weaker by constant pressure or attack使衰弱；使精疲力盡
*His strength has been worn down by illness．疾病已使他體質衰弱了。
*Many young mothers appear worn down with hard work，looking after children．許多年輕的母親因為工作辛苦和照料孩子而顯得疲憊不堪。
3．prevail by persistence；overcome 由於堅持而獲勝；克服
*Through perseverance，they gradually wore down opposition to the scheme．通過堅持不懈的努力，他們逐漸克服了實施這項計劃的阻力。
*The general has decided to wear down the enemy's strength by a long slow campaign．將軍決定用持久戰的打法來消耗敵人的力量。wear iron
防磨鐵板; 耐磨護板1．lose power；diminish in effect；disappear失效；效力減少；消失
*He could feel the wound aching again as the effect of the medicine wore off．隨著藥性的漸漸消失，他感到傷口疼痛了。
*My headache isn't serious．It will wear off after an hour or so．我的頭痛不嚴重，一小時左右就會好的。
*His enthusiasm for the plan seems to have worn off；he never speaks about it any more．他對這項計劃的熱情似乎已經消失了，他現在提都不提了。
*His displeasure wore off．他的不愉快心情漸漸消失了。
2．remove（nap，paint，etc．）through continuous pressure，fric tion，etc．磨掉（絨毛、油漆等）
*The nap of your coat is worn off．你外衣上的絨毛都磨光了。
*The brightness of the paint has worn off a little．油漆的光澤已經有些磨損了。1．pass gradually or slowly in time （時間）慢慢地過去；緩緩消逝
*The snow will melt as the day wears on．雪隨著白天時間的消逝而融化。
*As the hours wore on，he grew more and more impatient．時間慢慢地過去，他越來越不耐煩了。
2．continue繼續
*The boys'quarrel wore on all afternoon．孩子們吵吵鬧鬧，持續了整個下午。
*The battle wore on through the night．戰鬥持續了一夜。
3．become angry；irritate；tire激怒；使惱火；使疲倦
*Having to stay indoors all day long is tiresome for the children and wears on their mother's nerves．孩子們整天呆在家裡很厭煩，也使得他們的母親感到焦躁不安。1．tire out；exhaust使精疲力盡；耗盡
*Playing with little children really wears me out！跟小孩子們在一起玩真把我累壞了。
*She keeps wearing herself out for other people．她總是為別人忙得精疲力盡。
*After about an hour，my patience began to wear out．大約一小時以後，我開始有點忍耐不住了。
2．become useless變得無用；用壞
*The machine has worn out．那台機器已經報廢了。
*Children's shoes wear out quickly．孩子們的鞋很快就穿壞。
*The child has worn out his clothes；will you get him another suit？孩子已經把衣服穿破了，你給他再買一套好嗎？
3．consume（time，etc．）tediously 消磨（時間等）
*He has worn out miserable days with patience．他耐心地度過了悲慘的歲月。
*The meeting wore out all afternoon．會議消磨了整個下午的時間。have a man's authority；be the boss of a family or household為一家之主；當家
*He couldn't have the final say，because his wife was the one who wore the trousers in their house．他在家作不了主，因為他家裡是他妻子說了算。1．become thin from use變薄；磨薄
*His old pair of pants has worn thin at the knees．他舊褲子的膝蓋處已經磨薄了。
2．decrease；grow less or less interesting減少；漸漸變得無趣味
*The joke began to wear thin when you heard it too many times．這個笑話聽過好幾遍以後就沒有什麼趣味了。1．continue to be useful or liked for a long time經久耐用；始終令人滿意
*Nylon is easy to wash and wears well too．尼龍既好洗又耐磨。
*Their marriage has worn well．他們的婚姻一直美滿幸福。
2．carry，accept or treat properly 舉止適當；妥善處理
*Murphy has won many honours，but he wears them well．墨菲贏得了很多榮譽，但他對待榮譽謙虛而得體。wear-re.sist.ant
