*He was expected to win in a walk，but he was badly beaten．人們以為他會輕易獲勝，但是他卻被打得一敗塗地。win fame or honor獲得榮譽；成名
*Edison won his spurs as an inventor while young．愛迪生很年輕時就因創造發明而一舉成名。advance by one's efforts憑自己的努力而獲得成功
*He has at length won his way to the head of his profession．他終於憑自己的努力而成為他那一行的帶頭人。be victorous or successful after hard work or difficulty；win or succeed in the end經過艱苦努力和克服了困難而取得成功；勝利；成功
*Although it was a difficult problem，in the end he won out．雖然這個問題很棘手，最後他還是把它解決了。
*Correct ideas will certainly win out against erroneous ones．正確的意見必將戰勝錯誤的意見。
*I know whatever you do you're sure to win through in spite of early difficulties．我知道，不管你做什麼，你最終總會成功的，儘管最初有許多困難。persuade to change sides or opinions說服；把…爭取過來
*They have won over a number of opponents．他們爭取了一些反對者。
*She didn't like me at first，but I was soon able to win her over by being especially considerate．她一開始不喜歡我，可我很快就通過對她特別關心體貼而把她爭取過來了。be successful or victorious戰勝
*We've won the day．我們獲勝了。wince
