*You'll have to take what he says with a grain of salt．他說的話你不可全信。
*with a heavy hand oppressively壓制；苛刻；用高壓手段
*He ruled his household with a heavy hand．他在家裡太專橫了。with power；in force；triumphantly；overbearingly；arbitrarily有權；有勢；得意揚揚；壓制；專橫
*He was capable enough but he carried everything with a high hand that we got to detest him．他相當能幹，但是他太霸道，所以我們討厭他了。merrily；cheerfully愉快；欣然
*He accepted the invitation with a light heart．他欣然接受了這個邀請。
*Our English teacher stepped into the classroom with a light heart．我們的英語老師興高采烈地走進了教室。for the purpose of為了；為了…起見；鑒於；由於
*With a view to improving his ability to speak French，he spent most of his holidays in France．為了提高法語口語能力，他的大部分假期是在法國度過的。
*This subject is one that should be handled with a view to the longrange interests of the country．這是一個應從國家的長遠利益來考慮的問題。with willingness and zeal；with all one's heart or strength；earnestly；heartily甘心情願；熱切；盡心盡力
*She threw herself into the work with a will．她全身心地投入了這項工作。
*Whatever he does，he does it with a will．他不論幹什麼，都盡心盡力。with a will；most willingly甘心情願；十分願意
*I love her with all my heart．我全心全意地愛她。as much as one can盡全力；全力以赴地
*They battled the drought with all their might．In the end，they were rewarded with a bumper harvest．他們全力以赴地與乾旱作鬥爭，終於獲得了豐收。having reference to；intending or purposing目的在於；著眼於
*He reads English every morning with an eye to improving his pronunciation．他每天早晨朗讀英語，目的在於改進自己的發音。
*He constructed his house with an eye to architectural beauty．他建造房屋時著眼於建築之美。reluctantly勉強地
*He accepted the job with an ill grace．他勉強地接受了這工作。with enthusiasm；eager or ready and in the best of spirits for an event熱烈地；熱情地；興高采烈地
*－Will you come to our English evening？
*－I'll be there with bells on．
*－你來參加我們的英語晚會嗎？
*－我很樂意參加。with great or total success；victoriously非常成功；取得好的成績
*He came through the examination with flying colors．他考試取得了優異的成績。
*Our team won the game and returned with flying colors．我們的球隊比賽獲勝而凱旋。politely；willingly；without complaining有禮貌地；心甘情願地；毫不埋怨地
*He accepted the principal's criticism with good grace．他很有禮貌地接受了校長的批評。at a glance；without effort看一眼；一瞥；不費勁
*Anyone with half an eye could see that the young teacher was in love with the girl．任何人一看就知道那位青年教師已愛上那位女孩了。knowing all the circumstances or consequences（usu．used in an unfavorable sense）明知（故犯）
*We punished him because he had made the mistake with his eyes open．因為他是明知故犯，所以我們懲罰了他。concerning關於；說到
*I have nothing to say with reference to this question．關於這個問題我沒有什麼話要講。concerning；with regard to至於；關於
*I have something to say with respect to our business．關於我們的業務，我想說幾句。
*We must plan with respect to the future．我們訂計劃時必須考慮到未來。except除了
*They passed the examination withthe exception of two．除了兩人外，他們考試都通過了。with-
