*If you have what it takes，you can work up to the presidency of the company．如果你有本事，你可以升到公司總裁的地位。
3．stir up；rouse；excite 鼓動起來，激起；使激動
*I can't work up any enthusiasm for the project，I'm afraid．我恐怕對這項計劃鼓不起什麼熱情。
*Let's go out for a walk to work up an appetite．我們出去走走吧，這樣會增加食慾。
*Her words worked him up into a rage．她的話使他大發雷霆。
4．make into sth．； elaborately prepare 精心做成；制訂
*The craftsman is working up the mass of clay into a toy figure．工 匠正把一團泥捏成一個玩具。
