<<名詞>>
[無冠詞]
1 a.『軍』零時,預定行動開始的時間
b. (火箭等的) 發射時刻
(cf. countdown) 
2 決定性的瞬間,危機

1．the exact time when an attack or other military action is supposed to start 發動攻擊的時間；採取軍事行動的時間
*The company was told that their zero hour was 3 a．m．連隊奉命於凌晨3點開始行動。
2．the time when an important decision or change is supposed to come；the time for a dangerous action 做出重要決定或重要變動的時間；關鍵時刻；危急關頭
*It was zero hour and the doctor began the operation on the patient．那是個關鍵的時刻，醫生開始為那個病人動手術了。1．adjust a gun so that it will exactly hit a target；aim at 向…瞄準
*The plane zeroed in on the enemy's arms factory and destroyed it with one bomb．飛機瞄準了敵人的軍工廠，一枚炸彈就把它炸毀了。
2．give full attention to 全神貫注於；集中注意力
*Let's zero in on this problem today．我們今天研究這個問題。
*The children zeroed in on the toy display．孩子們聚精會神地觀看玩具展覽。zero meridian
本初子午線zero population growth
